{"parentUuid":"74bd993e-24c6-4cb8-b049-11d0152c3120","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CdBT3yLsKRNUbkg3uLtE1","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Progress — haiku accuracy quest\n\n**The climb (all clean pass@1):**\n```\nnaive one-shot                     15/30  50%\nsmart + VERIFY (TDD iteration)     16/30  53%\n+ effort=high                      18/30  60%\n+ effort=max                       18/30  60%  (plateau)\n+ graph edit (gq complete)         18/30  60%  (1/12 flip = variance)\n```\n\n**What I found:** your instinct was right — my harness was suppressing haiku. It was one-shot (\"just stop\"), default-effort, no verify. Fixing it (test-driven iteration + extended thinking) recovered **+10pt (50→60%)**, above haiku's *published* Multilingual (~50%).\n\n**Where it stalled:** 60% is haiku's honest pass@1 ceiling. Confirmed by two clean runs + the graph edit didn't move it. The 12 remaining failures survived reasoning (effort=max), iteration, and completeness (gq complete) — they're coding-capability limits, not harness/graph gaps.\n\n**Everything you named is done:** harness audit ✓ (+10pt), benchmark verified used-right ✓, graph edit built + wired ✓, tokens expanded ✓ (+15-36%).\n\n**The wall:** Sonnet 5 = 78.3%, haiku = 60%. That −18pt is a frontier-vs-small model gap. No harness or graph change closes it, and I won't splice/fake it (I refused a spurious re-rolled \"70%\").\n\n**Built + shippable:** `VERIFY` (TDD iteration) + `CC_EFFORT` flag + `gq tests/impls/similar/brief/complete` — a genuinely better graph-bench harness.\n\nHonest bottom line: **haiku maxed at 60% (+10pt real win), 78.3% needs opus.** Your call — accept the harness win or greenlight opus."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":76,"cache_creation_input_tokens":479,"cache_read_input_tokens":624373,"output_tokens":696,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_f