{"parentUuid":"ab1265c2-36cd-4729-957d-754ef2af739e","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CdBTShEdqqsURZEj6hZm6","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**haiku graph vs baseline accuracy: ~0 (noise), measured 3× at matched configs:**\n\n| config (both arms same, only graph differs) | baseline (no graph) | treated (+graph) | Δ |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| sed-naive | 15/27 | 16/28 | **+1** |\n| naive + brief | 15/30 | 15/30 | **+0** |\n| budget-40 | 10/30 | 9/30 | **−1** |\n\n**The graph adds ~0 accuracy** (+1/+0/−1 = noise). It's a navigation/token tool, not an accuracy lever — consistent with everything measured.\n\n**Important caveat:** the 60% (best config) is **treated-only** — I ran smart+VERIFY+effort *with* the graph but never ran the no-graph baseline at that same config. So the 50→60% climb is the **harness** (iteration + effort), not proven to be the graph. To cleanly isolate the graph's contribution at 60%, I'd run the no-graph baseline at smart+VERIFY+effort=high.\n\nWant me to run that paired baseline (~40min) so you get the exact graph-vs-nograph delta at the best config? Expect ~0 based on the 3 matched runs, but it'd close the gap cleanly. Otherwise the answer stands: **graph ≈ +0 accuracy, the tokens are its real win.**"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4004,"cache_read_input_tokens":630736,"output_tokens":1098,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4004,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1098,"cache_read_input_tokens":630736,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4004,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4004},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CdBTSZERoVQ