{"parentUuid":"866d3090-9b06-4cdb-b625-67e2c6c3ed77","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"673ae418-bd81-4d95-94bf-517d121fb717","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0172T8YkCCEj91dpEv3dB1Rc","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t#!/usr/bin/env bash\n2\t# Build the entire-graph NDJSON dump for one repo @ base_commit, on the HOST (native binary).\n3\t# Output: <out>/graph.symbols.ndjson + <out>/graph.edges.ndjson  (fed into the treated container).\n4\tset -uo pipefail\n5\tROOT=\"/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/brain-swebench\"\n6\tPY=\"$ROOT/.venv/bin/python\"; [ -x \"$PY\" ] || PY=python3\n7\t# Canonical provider is `entire graph` (entireio/entire-graph). Override with ENTIRE_GRAPH\n8\t# only for a legacy `entire sem` box. graph emits a richer graph than the old sem (more\n9\t# symbols + relation families), so graphs MUST be built with graph to measure the real tool.\n10\tGRAPH=\"${ENTIRE_GRAPH:-entire graph}\"\n11\trepo=\"$1\"; commit=\"$2\"; out=\"$3\"\n12\tcache=\"$ROOT/repo-cache/$(echo \"$repo\" | tr '/' '__')\"\n13\tmkdir -p \"$out\"\n14\tout=\"$(cd \"$out\" && pwd)\"   # absolutize before we cd into the repo cache\n15\t\n16\tif [ ! -d \"$cache/.git\" ]; then\n17\t  echo \"[clone] $repo -> $cache\"\n18\t  git clone --quiet \"https://github.com/$repo\" \"$cache\" || { echo \"CLONE FAILED\"; exit 1; }\n19\tfi\n20\tcd \"$cache\" || exit 1\n21\tgit fetch --quiet origin \"$commit\" 2>/dev/null || git fetch --quiet --all 2>/dev/null\n22\tgit checkout --quiet \"$commit\" 2>&1 | tail -1 || { echo \"CHECKOUT FAILED $commit\"; exit 1; }\n23\t\n24\techo \"[graph] symbols…\"\n25\t# Capture the provider's stderr to a log (do NOT discard it): an OOM/kill must be diagnosable,\n26\t# and its exit status must be checkable — a killed provider silently shipped a half-graph before.\n27\t$GRAPH symbols --repo \"$cache\" --format ndjson > \"$out/graph.symbols.ndjson\" 2> \"$out/sem_symbols.err\"\n28\tsym_rc=$?\n29\techo \"[graph] edges… (piped through filter_edges.py: caps CALLS fan-out; see that file)\"\n30\t# `entire graph edges` emits every CALLS as a fixed-confidence (0.62) name-collision heuristic,\n31\t# which is quadratic on large repos (10+ GB dumps that OOM graph-query / exhaust Docker disk).\n32\t# filter_edges.py keeps all non-CALLS + any high-conf CALLS + a bounded per-symbol CALLS fan-out.\n33\t# PIPESTATUS lets us fail the instance if `entire graph edges` (not just the filter) exited nonzero.\n34\t$GRAPH edges   --repo \"$cache\" --format ndjson 2> \"$out/sem_edges.err\" \\\n35\t  | \"$PY\" \"$ROOT/filter_edges.py\" > \"$out/graph.edges.ndjson\" 2> \"$out/filter.err\"\n36\t# Snapshot the WHOLE PIPESTATUS array in ONE statement: the first `x=${PIPESTATUS[0]}` assignment\n37\t# is itself a command that RESETS PIPESTATUS (to length 1), so a second `${PIPESTATUS[1]}` would be\n38\t# an unbound-variable error under `set -u`. Copy the array first, then index the copy.\n39\t_ps=(\"${PIPESTATUS[@]}\")\n40\tedges_rc=${_ps[0]}; filter_rc=${_ps[1]}\n41\t\n42\t# grep -c prints \"0\" AND exits 1 on zero matches; a bare `|| echo 0` then appends a SECOND \"0\"\n43\t# (\"0\\n0\"), which breaks the int() parse in validate. Capture grep's own count and default only\n44\t# when grep produced nothing (missing file).\n45\ts=$(grep -c '\"record_type\":\"symbol\"'  \"$out/graph.symbols.ndjson\" 2>/dev/null || true); s=${s:-0}\n46\te=$(grep -c '\"record_type\":\"relation\"' \"$out/graph.edges.ndjson\"   2>/dev/null || true); e=${e:-0}\n47\t\n48\t# Completeness / truncation validation — LOUD, never silent. Compares the provider's own\n49\t# header stats (symbols/relations/completeness_level) to the actual records + the filter's\n50\t# raw relation count, and warns on a nonzero `entire graph`, truncation, or an unsafe graph.\n51\tif ! \"$PY\" \"$ROOT/graph_stats.py\" validate \"$out\" \"$repo\" \"$commit\" \\\n52\t      \"$sym_rc\" \"$edges_rc\" \"$filter_rc\" \"$s\"; then\n53\t  # DELETE the rejected/partial graph data — do NOT leave it on disk. Otherwise the next batch\n54\t  # pass's idempotency check (graph_stats.py `complete` / the treated-arm `-s` guard) would see\n55\t  # present, non-empty files and silently bless this truncated build, shipping it into the treated\n56\t  # arm. With the data files gone the instance reads as \"not built\" and is rebuilt. Keep .err logs.\n57\t  rm -f \"$out/graph.symbols.ndjson\" \"$out/graph.edges.ndjson\"\n58\t  echo \"[done-INCOMPLETE] $repo@${commit:0:8}  symbols=$s edges=$e  -> $out REJECTED+REMOVED (see WARNING above)\"\n59\t  exit 3\n60\tfi\n61\techo \"[done] $repo@${commit:0:8}  symbols=$s edges=$e  -> $out\"\n62\t"}]},"uuid":"abc6cf1f-5bb7-4dfc-a4c3-47ac736d71b8","timestamp":"2026-07-19T13:44:41.410Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/brain-swebench/build_graph.sh","content":"#!/usr/bin/env bash\n# Build the entire-graph NDJSON dump for one repo @ base_commit, on the HOST (native binary).\n# Output: <out>/graph.symbols.ndjson + <out>/graph.edges.ndjson  (fed into the treated container).\nset -uo pipefail\nROOT=\"/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/brain-swebench\"\nPY=\"$ROOT/.venv/bin/python\"; [ -x \"$PY\" ] || PY=python3\n# Canonical provider is `entire graph` (entireio/entire-graph). Override with ENTIRE_GRAPH\n# only for a legacy `entire sem` box. graph emits a richer graph than the old sem (more\n# symbols + relation families), so graphs MUST be built with graph to measure the real tool.\nGRAPH=\"${ENTIRE_GRAPH:-entire graph}\"\nrepo=\"$1\"; commit=\"$2\"; out=\"$3\"\ncache=\"$ROOT/repo-cache/$(echo \"$repo\" | tr '/' '__')\"\nmkdir -p \"$out\"\nout=\"$(cd \"$out\" && pwd)\"   # absolutize before we cd into the repo cache\n\nif [ ! -d \"$cache/.git\" ]; then\n  echo \"[clone] $repo -> $cache\"\n  git clone --quiet \"https://github.com/$repo\" \"$cache\" || { echo \"CLONE FAILED\"; exit 1; }\nfi\ncd \"$cache\" || exit 1\ngit fetch --quiet origin \"$commit\" 2>/dev/null || git fetch --quiet --all 2>/dev/null\ngit checkout --quiet \"$commit\" 2>&1 | tail -1 || { echo \"CHECKOUT FAILED $commit\"; exit 1; }\n\necho \"[graph] symbols…\"\n# Capture the provider's stderr to a log (do NOT discard it): an OOM/kill must be diagnosable,\n# and its exit status must be checkable — a killed provider silently shipped a half-graph before.\n$GRAPH symbols --repo \"$cache\" --format ndjson > \"$out/graph.symbols.ndjson\" 2> \"$out/sem_symbols.err\"\nsym_rc=$?\necho \"[graph] edges… (piped through filter_edges.py: caps CALLS fan-out; see that file)\"\n# `entire graph edges` emits every CALLS as a fixed-confidence (0.62) name-collision heuristic,\n# which is quadratic on large repos (10+ GB dumps that OOM graph-query / exhaust Docker disk).\n# filter_edges.py keeps all non-CALLS + any high-conf CALLS + a bounded per-symbol CALLS fan-out.\n# PIPESTATUS lets us fail the instance if `entire graph edges` (not just the filter) exited nonzero.\n$GRAPH edges   --repo \"$cache\" --format ndjson 2> \"$out/sem_edges.err\" \\\n  | \"$PY\" \"$ROOT/filter_edges.py\" > \"$out/graph.edges.ndjson\" 2> \"$out/filter.err\"\n# Snapshot the WHOLE PIPESTATUS array in ONE statement: the first `x=${PIPESTATUS[0]}` assignment\n# is itself a command that RESETS PIPESTATUS (to length 1), so a second `${PIPESTATUS[1]}` would be\n# an unbound-variable error under `set -u`. Copy the array first, then index the copy.\n_ps=(\"${PIPESTATUS[@]}\")\nedges_rc=${_ps[0]}; filter_rc=${_ps[1]}\n\n# grep -c prints \"0\" AND exits 1 on zero matches; a bare `|| echo 0` then appends a SECOND \"0\"\n# (\"0\\n0\"), which breaks the int() parse in validate. Capture grep's own count and default only\n# when grep produced nothing (missing file).\ns=$(grep -c '\"record_type\":\"symbol\"'  \"$out/graph.symbols.ndjson\" 2>/dev/null || true); s=${s:-0}\ne=$(grep -c '\"record_type\":\"relation\"' \"$out/graph.edges.ndjson\"   2>/dev/null || true); e=${e:-0}\n\n# Completeness / truncation validation — LOUD, never silent. Compares the provider's own\n# header stats (symbols/relations/completeness_level) to the actual records + the filter's\n# raw relation count, and warns on a nonzero `entire graph`, truncation, or an unsafe graph.\nif ! \"$PY\" \"$ROOT/graph_stats.py\" validate \"$out\" \"$repo\" \"$commit\" \\\n      \"$sym_rc\" \"$edges_rc\" \"$filter_rc\" \"$s\"; then\n  # DELETE the rejected/partial graph data — do NOT leave it on disk. Otherwise the next batch\n  # pass's idempotency check (graph_stats.py `complete` / the treated-arm `-s` guard) would see\n  # present, non-empty files and silently bless this truncated build, shipping it into the treated\n  # arm. With the data files gone the instance reads as \"not built\" and is rebuilt. Keep .err logs.\n  rm -f \"$out/graph.symbols.ndjson\" \"$out/graph.edges.ndjson\"\n  echo \"[done-INCOMPLETE] $repo@${commit:0:8}  symbols=$s edges=$e  -> $out REJECTED+REMOVED (see WARNING above)\"\n  exit 3\nfi\necho \"[done] $repo@${commit:0:8}  symbols=$s edges=$e  -> $out\"\n","numLines":62,"startLine":1,"totalLines":62}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"866d3090-9b06-4cdb-b625-67e2c6c3ed77","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"de272aad-c620-4d71-bbdd-27dd2d3dc8af","version":"2.1.201","gitBranch":"main","slug":"quizzical-sniffing-quasar"}
