{"parentUuid":"26b1a4b8-d817-4e62-96ee-e983ad85228c","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"cfe8bd2d-ccce-449a-a216-b8f8291e1ea8","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_016q7THPZzC5vX375QzwbYYS","type":"tool_result","content":"## 3. Uncommitted / unlanded local work\n\n**Checkout** `/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain`, branch `feat/init-agents` @ `d0ba1e06`, **no upstream tracking**, **1 behind / 4 ahead** of `entireio/main`. Remotes: `entireio`=entireio/entire-brain, `origin`=ashtom/entire-brain.\n\n- **3 of the 4 commits ahead are PR #74** (`6b2244a9`, `217d0ad4`, `bdd7ee33`). The only genuinely new work is `d0ba1e06` — **3 files, +221**.\n- **`init-agents`** (2026-07-24): new cobra command `entire-brain init-agents --repo .` in `internal/cli/init_agents.go` (157 L) — writes `<root>/.entire/brain-agent.md` from const `agentGuideDoc`, then upserts a marker-guarded `<!-- entire-brain:begin -->…<!-- entire-brain:end -->` block + `@.entire/brain-agent.md` import into both `AGENTS.md` and `CLAUDE.md`, creating them if absent; idempotent, never clobbers. Test `internal/cli/init_agents_test.go` (63 L, `TestInitAgentsInstallsGuideAndIsIdempotent`). Registered at `internal/cli/root.go:100` under \"Explore the brain:\". Doctrine encoded: brief-first, graph-search-first, one-call-then-act, ≤120-line reads, freshness check, `entire brain remember`.\n- **Quality:** `go build ./...` exit 0; `go test -run TestInitAgents` 1 pass; gofmt + `go vet` clean. **golangci-lint not run** (binary not on PATH).\n- **PR-ready? Code yes, plumbing no.** (1) branch **never pushed** — `git ls-remote --heads entireio` shows no `feat/init-agents`; (2) **stacked on unmerged #74** — a PR against `main` would drag in its 2,668 lines; (3) 1 commit behind main; (4) zero docs — `init-agents` appears nowhere in `README.md` or `docs/`, and PR #73's install guide doesn't mention it.\n- **`git add -A` hazard — 10 untracked entries, none gitignored:**\n  - *Dogfood output:* `.entire/brain-agent.md` (3.2K, byte-identical to `agentGuideDoc`), `AGENTS.md` + `CLAUDE.md` (635B, identical twins). Main tracks neither AGENTS.md nor CLAUDE.md.\n  - *Other tool's output:* `.entire/graph-agent.md` (2.1K) — **stale graph doctrine** (no `graph impact`, no `explain`-pipe, says \"do not run builds\") vs devenv's newer verify-once version.\n  - *Unrelated machine-local regente junk with hardcoded `/Users/suhaan/...` paths:* `.mcp.json`, `.cursor/mcp.json`, `.cursor/rules/regente.mdc`, `.gemini/{settings.json,regente.md}`, `.claude/skills/regente/SKILL.md`, `.codex/skills/regente/SKILL.md`, `.regente/` (2.9 MB, 15 files).\n- **Cleanest path:** cherry-pick `d0ba1e06` onto a fresh branch off `entireio/main` → 3-file/+221 PR, commit only the Go files, add a README/docs line. Decide separately whether the dogfooded `.entire/brain-agent.md` + `AGENTS.md`/`CLAUDE.md` get checked in; gitignore the regente files.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Milestones\n\n**Caveat: there is no master roadmap doc.** M-IDs live only in Go package comments and PR bodies — a repo-wide grep for `P0.M*`/`P1.M*` returns 11 hits total. Authoritative sources are `docs/ga-readiness.md`, `docs/brain_wire_contract.md`, `docs/semantic_brain_plan.md`, `docs/release-blockers.md`, `docs/durable_facts_handover.md`.\n\n### P0 — local brain GA\n`docs/ga-readiness.md:81` verbatim: **\"P0 GA status: gates 1–11 satisfied.\"** Gates are numbered **1–11, not M1..M7**.\n\n| Gate | Status |\n|---|---|\n| 1 module path `entireio/entire-graph` | ✅ |\n| 2 version stamped from tag `v0.1.0` | ✅ |\n| 3 provider schema frozen (ADR 0001, `1.x`, additive-only) | ✅ |\n| 4 brain pins provider (`entire-plugin.yml`) | ✅ |\n| 5 no-egress + deterministic golden coverage (`doctor` `no_egress:true`) | ✅ |\n| 6 `brain_*` MCP contract locked (`additionalProperties:false`) | ✅ |\n| 7 GraphMark regression gate; floor 28/30 languages, 1148 vs 802 | ✅ |\n| 8 Phase-1 local-only boundary frozen (stdio MCP only) | ✅ |\n| 9 blockers B1 + R1–R4 on RC SHA | table says ⏳ verify; §resolved marks ✅ (0 hard integrity flags, 24/24 provenance) — **doc self-conflicts** |\n| 10 aligned tags both repos | table says ⏳ partial; §resolved marks ✅ (both at v0.1.0 on aligned GA SHA) — **doc self-conflicts** |\n| 11 `no_release_claim` resolved | ✅ |\n\n- **P0.M5** — the *only* P0 M-ID that exists anywhere — = standalone install docs, **OPEN as PR #73**, described in its body as \"the last non-code P0 item; code is done + tagged v0.1.0\". **P0.M1–M4 do not appear in any repo text.**\n- **Claim posture:** semantic usefulness **CLAIMABLE** (28/30 top languages, exact-McNemar p<0.05; C# p=0.07 and PHP p=0.18 below sig; 1,148 vs 802 = 91% vs 64%, BH-controlled). Distill wall-clock **NO CLAIM** (only ~2× local proof). Durable-facts-vs-raw **NO CLAIM** (zero active durable facts). Note `docs/eval_ledger.md` (2026-06-18) supersedes `release-blockers.md`: replay-lab clean task no_brain 0/4 → full_brain 4/4, `proof_ready=true`, history-channel correctness now claimable; MCP/Radar/codex-runner/efficiency stay no-claim.\n- **Deferred out of P0:** marketplace/plugin-discovery listing (post-GA); MCP cosmetic divergences (dual vs NDJSON framing, fallback proto `2024-11-05` vs `2025-06-18`, 4 MiB vs 1 MiB frame) → **P2 unified-MCP-surface**.\n\n### P1 — Shared/Hosted Brain (= `semantic_brain_plan.md` §Phase 3)\n| ID | Status |\n|---|---|\n| **M1.1** brain artifact wire contract | ✅ MERGED PR #59 (07-03) — `internal/brainwire`, `BrainSchemaVersion \"1.0\"`, tolerant reader, `CheckCompatibility` |\n| **M1.2** server-side brain store | ❓ **not in this repo** — server half lives in entire-api; `brain_wire_contract.md:180` \"this milestone defines the contract, not the store\". Status unknown from here |\n| **M1.3 / M1.4** canonical encoding + cross-impl manifest signing | ⬜ **NOT STARTED**, forward-referenced only |\n| **M1.5** publish client `entire brain publish` | ✅ MERGED PR #60 (07-03) + re-audit `aff29100` (github.com origins only). Two-gate opt-in per ADR-P1-A; **inert until opt-in set**; paired server endpoint lands separately |\n| **M2.2** merge engine → `internal/factmerge` | ✅ MERGED PR #64 (07-07), ~70 CLI call sites shimmed, zero behavior change |\n| **M2.3/M2.3b** fact-sync runner | ✅ MERGED PR #64 — `internal/factsync` read-merge-CAS + `HTTPServer` adapter + egress redaction |\n| **M2.4** cross-member conflict routing + `Resolve` | ✅ MERGED PR #64 — proof `TestCrossMemberConflictRoutedThenResolvedConverges`. ADR-P1-E: merge runs on the runner, not the API server |\n| **M3.3** remote hosted-brain MCP client | ✅ MERGED PR #64 — `internal/hostedbrain`, drives `POST /repos/{repo_id}/brain/mcp`; +#65 camelCase `oldRef`/`newRef` + 412→`ErrConflict` |\n| **M4–M7** | ❓ **no such IDs in any entire-brain text** |\n\n- PR #64 testing: factmerge+factsync+hostedbrain+brainwire `-race` 60/0; full `internal/cli` 1057/0.\n- **PR #64 explicit deferrals:** live cross-repo round-trip against a running entire-api; the open-proposal-set HTTP transport (model + `Resolve` proven, transport not); wiring `hostedbrain`/`factsync` into user-facing CLI verbs.\n- **In-flight P1:** PR #74 (local git-meta fact store) — the local half of durable facts; **shared publication blocked on the entiredb reserved-ref unblock**, verbatim from the PR body.\n- **Durable facts** (`docs/durable_facts_handover.md`): B0 baseline frozen 06-09; **B1 KIND, B2 stored LOCUS, B3 synthesized outline, B4 audience A/B eval all landed**; **Phase D (embeddings) IN PROGRESS** — fusion tuning \"resolved (no lever)\", default-on + disk cache shipped. Open: `facts gc` should prune `embeddings/` (today only `facts.ndjson`); stronger embedder/cross-encoder rerank only if a measured target justifies. **Closed negatives — do not re-litigate:** expansion, lexical weight tuning, RRF fusion tuning.\n- `docs/pattern_consolidation_plan.md` Phases 0–7 all DONE (2026-06-16).\n\n---\n\n## 5. Parked experiments\n\n**265 remote refs; 112 `codex/*` refs = 56 unique names, mirrored identically (same SHA, zero divergence) on both `entireio` and `origin` — any cleanup must delete twice.** 53 unique names are unmerged into `entireio/main`.\n\n**The count overstates the work.** 44 of the 53 are **one commit each on a single shared codex trunk** off base `5d4b08c3` (2026-07-11 \"Freeze Phase 0A temporal memory evidence\"). 37 have 0–1 unique commits vs the stack tip. \"120 ahead\" = one lineage with ~1 experiment per branch tip, not 120 branches of work.\n\n- **LIVE (<2wk):**\n  - `codex/current-main-source-of-truth` (07-24, 72 ahead, 156 unique) — \"Harden benchmark proof + Brain retrieval contracts\". **The only branch based on current main (`afe7d3f2`)**, own lineage. Most likely the successor to #75.\n  - `codex/benchmark-repair-integration` (07-18) — stack tip, **PR #75**.\n  - The **43-branch 07-17 wave** + 3-branch 07-16 wave — retrieval/brief experiments (`action-relevance-gate-v1`, `brief-git-intent-overlay-v1`, `semantic-test-suggestion-rank-v1`, `stale-index-new-file-bridge-v1`, `product-*` layout/latency/token/MCP-schema-cost tips, `negative-control-*`). **52 of 53 have no PR.** Their content is what PR #75 aggregates.\n- **DELETABLE — subsumed (0 unique commits vs #75 head):** `apfs-capacity-observation-v1`, `negative-control-cache-archive-v1`, `negative-control-cache-bundle-v2`, `negative-control-classifier`, `negative-control-execution-contract-v1`, `negative-control-owner-approval-v1`.\n- **DELETABLE — squash residue:** `full-plan-implementation` (PR #49 MERGED, 36d), `brain-large-repo-bench` (PR #48 MERGED, 41d).\n- **ABANDONED (>2wk):** `brain-distillation-fable` (07-12, PR #70 **CLOSED unmerged**), `brain-phase0b-causal`, `brain-retrieval-fable` (both 07-12).\n- **Separate lineages worth a look:** `agent-v2-semantic-edges` (96 unique, \"absolute file URI privacy rule\"), `agent-v1-product-reconciled` (86 unique, \"pack agent packets incrementally\").\n- **Practical read:** landing PR #75 (or its A/B split) plus cherry-picking the ~44 single-commit tips retires nearly the entire inventory.\n- *Caveat:* branch descriptions are from tip commit subjects only; no per-branch CI or diff review was done.\n\n---\n\n## 6. Open issues\n\n**None — and there never have been any.** `gh issue list --state all` returns `[]`. Issues are enabled (`hasIssuesEnabled:true`) but unused; all work is tracked via PRs and branches. No labels, no themes.\n\n---\n\n## 7. What I'd do next\n\n1. **Merge PR #73** (docs-only, 14/14 green, CLEAN, zero reviewer feedback in 13 days) — closes the last non-code P0 item. **Needs your approval (merge).**\n2. **Unblock PR #74's CI**: split flock into `lock_unix.go`/`lock_windows.go`, `gofmt -w internal/factgitmeta/backend_test.go`, fix the stale blob-key paragraph in the body — three mechanical fixes standing between a 2,668-line feature and a green build. *No approval needed to push fixes; merging does.*\n3. **Split PR #75 into PR-A (75 product files, +17,348) and PR-B (477 benchmark files, +182k)**, rebase A onto `afe7d3f2` and resolve its 9 product conflicts — #75 as-is is unlandable (552 files, 11 conflicts, GitHub won't render the diff). Close #75 once A and B exist. **Closing #75 needs your approval.**\n4. **Decide whether `mined-scale/` (147 files) and `mined-c0701/` (94 files) corpora + generated evidence ledgers belong in git** — this one call shrinks PR-B by ~90% and is the single biggest lever on repo weight. **Your call.**\n5. **Land `init-agents`**: cherry-pick `d0ba1e06` onto a fresh branch off `entireio/main` (3 files, +221, builds/tests/vet clean) and open a standalone PR; add a docs line and gitignore the untracked `.regente/`, `.mcp.json`, `.cursor/`, `.gemini/`, `.claude/skills/`, `.codex/skills/` so no one runs `git add -A`. *Opening the PR needs your approval.*\n6. **Reconcile the three known cleanups**: fix `docs/ga-readiness.md` gates 9 and 10 (table says ⏳, the resolved section says ✅ — pick one); refresh the stale `.entire/graph-agent.md` doctrine copy; delete the 8 subsumed/squash-residue codex branches on **both** remotes.\n\n**Two things nobody has done and everyone is assuming:** the confirmatory benchmark run that all of PR #75's eval hardening exists to enable has **never been executed** (budget-gated), and the Hit@8 0/8→6/8 headline is **not currently reproducible** — fix or explicitly waive that before any of those numbers are cited outside the repo.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"727a2a5c-c5a3-415c-9515-fdee09922256","timestamp":"2026-07-31T03:00:37.840Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"## 3. Uncommitted / unlanded local work\n\n**Checkout** `/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain`, branch `feat/init-agents` @ `d0ba1e06`, **no upstream tracking**, **1 behind / 4 ahead** of `entireio/main`. Remotes: `entireio`=entireio/entire-brain, `origin`=ashtom/entire-brain.\n\n- **3 of the 4 commits ahead are PR #74** (`6b2244a9`, `217d0ad4`, `bdd7ee33`). The only genuinely new work is `d0ba1e06` — **3 files, +221**.\n- **`init-agents`** (2026-07-24): new cobra command `entire-brain init-agents --repo .` in `internal/cli/init_agents.go` (157 L) — writes `<root>/.entire/brain-agent.md` from const `agentGuideDoc`, then upserts a marker-guarded `<!-- entire-brain:begin -->…<!-- entire-brain:end -->` block + `@.entire/brain-agent.md` import into both `AGENTS.md` and `CLAUDE.md`, creating them if absent; idempotent, never clobbers. Test `internal/cli/init_agents_test.go` (63 L, `TestInitAgentsInstallsGuideAndIsIdempotent`). Registered at `internal/cli/root.go:100` under \"Explore the brain:\". Doctrine encoded: brief-first, graph-search-first, one-call-then-act, ≤120-line reads, freshness check, `entire brain remember`.\n- **Quality:** `go build ./...` exit 0; `go test -run TestInitAgents` 1 pass; gofmt + `go vet` clean. **golangci-lint not run** (binary not on PATH).\n- **PR-ready? Code yes, plumbing no.** (1) branch **never pushed** — `git ls-remote --heads entireio` shows no `feat/init-agents`; (2) **