{"parentUuid":"bfb32d1e-3515-404f-9e46-9d76abc0aeee","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"3131e5ed-61e9-4bb3-8ce1-5c8846dda398","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FvKf7nkCC3wPvc2jPig43H","type":"tool_result","content":"########## MATCH[PR #73] len=12942 ##########\nRepo `/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain`. Remotes: `entireio` = github.com/entireio/entire-brain, `origin` = github.com/ashtom/entire-brain. `entireio/main` = `afe7d3f2`. Module path on main still `github.com/ashtom/entire-brain` (go.mod line 1).\n\nContext for PR #75 (`gh pr view 75`): head `codex/benchmark-repair-integration` @ `923b8a91`, base main, **DRAFT**, **CONFLICTING**, 552 files, +199356/-556, 100 commits. Local `git rev-list --left-right --count entireio/main...923b8a91` = **84 behind / 120 ahead**. Title \"Improve Brain brief retrieval and harden its evaluation pipeline\".\n\n---\n\n## (a) PR #73 — `docs/p0m5-install-docs` @ `073ea21e`\n\n`git diff --stat entireio/main...entireio/docs/p0m5-install-docs`:\n```\ndocs/getting-started.md       | 254 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++--\ndocs/release_press_release.md | 222 ++++++++++++++++++++----------------\n2 files changed, 372 insertions(+), 104 deletions(-)\n```\n\n**docs/getting-started.md** — 553 B / 12 lines on main → 11242 B / 250 lines. Cold-start install + first-run guide. Sections (verified by heading grep): Requirements; Install (Quick install with `go install` — step 1 semantic provider `entire-graph`, step 2 the brain; Install from source; Release archive); Verify; First run: build a brain and query it; If you do not have the semantic provider yet; Query the brain; Optional: distill durable facts; Use the brain from an agent; What you get; Further reading. Uses post-rename naming: 13 occurrences of `entire graph`, **0** of `entire sem`.\n\n**docs/release_press_release.md** — 7939 B → 9974 B. Sections: Headline; Customer Promise; What Is Shipped; Proven With Evidence; Known Replay-Lab Outcome; What Must Be Proven Before Public Claims; Blocked Or Access-Dependent; Future Claims We Should Not Make Yet; Release Checklist. Content deltas: adds \"Internal draft … Not for publication\" banner; \"prepares a local brain\" → \"ships a local brain … benchmark-backed semantic code graph\"; adds explicit note \"`entire-sem` was renamed to `entire-graph` after `v0.1.0`. This release targets the `v0.1.0` provider (`entire sem`)\"; **deletes** the old `## Compatibility Note` section; adds a `## Proven With Evidence` section with the brain-bench claim (28/30 languages at exact-McNemar p<0.05, C# p=0.07, PHP p=0.18, overall 1,148 vs 802 = 91% vs 64%, Benjamini-Hochberg control, CI byte-identical-regeneration gate); adds local-only bullet (`ENTIRE_BRAIN_NO_EGRESS` / `ENTIRE_BRAIN_LOCAL_ONLY`).\n\nStatus: OPEN, non-draft, `MEREGEABLE`, **all 14 checks SUCCESS** (release-evidence SKIPPED), **0 reviews**. PR body flags 3 release-owner blockers: module path is `ashtom` not `entireio` so `go install github.com/entireio/entire-brain/...@v0.1.0` will not resolve (I confirmed main's go.mod is still `github.com/ashtom/entire-brain`); `entire plugin install` does not resolve the `requires: sem` provider dep; verify the v0.1.0 archive ships an `entire graph`-answering provider.\n\n## (b) PR #74 — `feat/facts-gitmeta-local` @ `bdd7ee33`\n\n3 commits: `6b2244a9` vendor git-meta exchange engine, `217d0ad4` local git-meta-backed fact store + `facts sync`, `bdd7ee33` serialize Advance to close create-path race.\n\n`git diff --stat entireio/main...entireio/feat/facts-gitmeta-local` — 17 files, +2668/−11:\n```\ngo.mod                                            |  20 +-\ngo.sum                                            |  68 ++-\ninternal/cli/facts_admin_cmd.go                   |   1 +\ninternal/cli/facts_sync_cmd.go                    | 247 +\ninternal/factgitmeta/backend.go                   | 334 +\ninternal/factgitmeta/backend_test.go              | 349 +\ninternal/factgitmeta/gitmeta/apply.go             | 209 +\ninternal/factgitmeta/gitmeta/apply_test.go        |  74 +\ninternal/factgitmeta/gitmeta/commit.go            |  53 +\ninternal/factgitmeta/gitmeta/golden_test.go       | 167 +\ninternal/factgitmeta/gitmeta/materialize.go       | 208 +\ninternal/factgitmeta/gitmeta/serialize.go         | 269 +\ninternal/factgitmeta/gitmeta/target_value_test.go |  86 +\ninternal/factgitmeta/gitmeta/treepath.go          | 128 +\ninternal/factgitmeta/gitmeta/treepath_test.go     | 134 +\ninternal/factgitmeta/gitmeta/types.go             | 252 +\ninternal/factgitmeta/localrepo.go                 |  80 +\n```\ngo.mod adds `go-git/go-git/v6 v6.0.0-alpha.4…`, `go-git/go-billy/v6 v6.0.0-alpha.1…`, bumps `golang.org/x/sys v0.42.0 → v0.45.0`, promotes `muesli/termenv` from indirect to direct, adds indirects (go-winio, ProtonMail/go-crypto, circl, gods, gcfg/v2, ssh_config, cpuid/v2, sha1cd, sergi/go-diff, x/crypto, x/net, x/sync, x/text v0.3.8→v0.37.0).\n\n`internal/factgitmeta/gitmeta/types.go` header: `// Copied verbatim from github.com/entirehq/git-meta-service/internal/gitmeta @ feat/git-meta-service-integration (f3ec153) — do not edit; de-internalize upstream to dedupe (follow-up).`\n\nSeam it fills, verified on main: `internal/factsync/sync.go:45: type Server interface`; only implementation on main is `internal/factsync\n\n########## MATCH[M1.3] len=31654 ##########\n# P1 UNFINISHED MILESTONES — implementation-grade spec\n\nRepo `/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain`, branch `feat/init-agents` (HEAD `d0ba1e06`), `origin/main` = `afe7d3f2`.\n\n## 0. DOC INVENTORY — what actually exists (read, not guessed)\n\n| Asked for | Found |\n|---|---|\n| `docs/brain_wire_contract.md` | READ IN FULL, 194 lines (`wc -l`) |\n| `docs/semantic_brain_plan.md` Phase 3 | READ, lines 1258–1303 (`## Phase 3: Shared And Distributed Brain`), 5 subsections, 1324-line file |\n| ADR-P1-* docs | **DO NOT EXIST.** `find . -iname \"*adr*\" -not -path \"./.git/*\"` → empty. Also empty in `/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-api`, which has only `docs/adr/0001…0005` (none P1-lettered). `grep -rn \"ADR-P1\" --exclude-dir=.git .` → **6 hits, all inline Go comments**: `internal/cli/facts_sync_cmd.go:106` (ADR-P1-E), `internal/cli/publish.go:28,153` (ADR-P1-A), `internal/factsync/egress.go:16` (ADR-P1), `internal/factsync/sync.go:6` (ADR-P1-E), `:64` (ADR-P1-G). Letters A/E/F/G/H/I cited; **no file defines them.** |\n| \"M1.3\", \"M1.4\" | `grep -rn \"M1\\.3\\|M1\\.4\" --exclude-dir=.git .` → **exactly 1 hit repo-wide**: `docs/brain_wire_contract.md:113`. |\n\n**Hard finding: M1.3 and M1.4 have no written spec.** One sentence names them. Everything in (a)/(b) below is derived from that sentence + the code, and I flag which is quote vs derivation.\n\nTest baseline (ran it): `go test ./internal/brainwire/... ./internal/factsync/... ./internal/hostedbrain/... ./internal/factmerge/... -count=1` → **62 passed, 4 packages**. `go build` on the four → exit 0.\n\n---\n\n## (a) M1.3 — CANONICAL ENCODING\n\n### The entire spec text that exists (`brain_wire_contract.md:103–114`, verbatim)\n\n> Reference slices are stored in caller-controlled order and contain no maps, so re-marshaling a decoded `BrainArtifact` with this package's `encoding/json` round-trip is byte-stable (the round-trip test asserts `Marshal(Unmarshal(b)) == b` for canonically-produced bytes). This is a Go-`encoding/json` guarantee, not a cross-implementation one: it relies on Go's HTML escaping, struct field order, `omitempty`, and RFC3339Nano time formatting, and it does not hold for bytes a non-Go producer emitted or for a non-canonical original (e.g. explicit `\"size\":0` or reordered fields). **Do not** sign or content-hash the received artifact bytes directly across implementations. Integrity/signing instead hashes each referenced blob by its `sha256:` digest (already content-addressed); if the manifest itself must be signed cross-implementation, M1.3/M1.4 define an explicit canonical encoding rather than relying on `encoding/json` defaults.\n\nThat sentence names **4 hazards**: HTML escaping, struct field order, `omitempty`, RFC3339Nano. Those are the spec.\n\n### Which types (all of `internal/brainwire/contract.go`, read in full, 180 lines)\n\n| Type | Line | Fields | Omittable fields (`omitempty` today) |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `BrainArtifact` | 41 | 4 | `snapshots`, `overlays`, `facts` |\n| `BrainManifest` | 55 | 7 | `default_branch`, `provider`, `provider_version`, `provider_schema_version` |\n| `ContentRef` | 85 | 4 | `size`, `media_type`, `path` |\n| `SnapshotRef` | 101 | 3 | `tree` |\n| `OverlayRef` | 113 | 4 | `branch` |\n| `FactsRef` | 127 | 2 | — |\n\nConstraint from `contract.go:14-16` + doc:29-30: **\"The JSON tags are the contract\"** — canonicalization must not change a single tag; a tag change needs a major bump.\n\n### Byte-level rules to write (derived — each closes one named hazard)\n\n1. **HTML escaping** → MUST be off. Go default escapes `<`,`>`,`&` → `\\u003c\\u003e\\u0026`. Rule: emit raw UTF-8; use `json.Encoder` + `SetEscapeHTML(false)`, or hand-emit. Reachable fields: `repo_key`, `default_branch`, `branch`, `path`, `media_type`, `provider`.\n2. **Field order** → **lexicographic by JSON tag name** (RFC 8785/JCS rule), not Go declaration order. Declaration order is unreproducible by a non-Go producer that doesn't own the struct. This changes bytes vs today's output (`brain_schema_version` currently emits 4th, would emit 1st).\n3. **`omitempty`** → make omission **normative and exhaustive**: enumerate per field which value is the omitted default (`\"\"`, `0`, `nil`/`len==0`). A producer emitting `\"size\":0` or `\"tree\":\"\"` is non-canonical; the canonicalizer MUST drop them (doc names `\"size\":0` explicitly as the failure case). Empty slices: `[]` and `null` both omit.\n4. **Time** → `GeneratedAt time.Time` currently RFC3339Nano; Go trims trailing fractional zeros, so `12:00:00Z` and `12:00:00.000Z` are the same instant with different bytes. Rule: convert to UTC, fixed fractional policy — recommend truncate-to-second, emit `YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SSZ`, literal `Z` (never `+00:00`). Must state whether sub-second input is truncated (lossy) or an error.\n5. **Numbers** (`size int64`) → decimal integer only; no exponent, no leading zeros, no `+`, `-0` forbidden.\n6. **Strings** → UTF-8; minimal escaping (only `\"`, `\\`, C0 controls; `\\b \\f \\n \\r \\t` short forms, remaining C0 as `\\u00xx` lowercase h","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"cfa3519f-d7e9-4bf7-b346-1d0cce9535ab","timestamp":"2026-08-02T14:14:47.952Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"########## MATCH[PR #73] len=12942 ##########\nRepo `/Users/suhaan/Documents/Coding/entire-brain`. Remotes: `entireio` = github.com/entireio/entire-brain, `origin` = github.com/ashtom/entire-brain. `entireio/main` = `afe7d3f2`. Module path on main still `github.com/ashtom/entire-brain` (go.mod line 1).\n\nContext for PR #75 (`gh pr view 75`): head `codex/benchmark-repair-integration` @ `923b8a91`, base main, **DRAFT**, **CONFLICTING**, 552 files, +199356/-556, 100 commits. Local `git rev-list --left-right --count entireio/main...923b8a91` = **84 behind / 120 ahead**. Title \"Improve Brain brief retrieval and harden its evaluation pipeline\".\n\n---\n\n## (a) PR #73 — `docs/p0m5-install-docs` @ `073ea21e`\n\n`git diff --stat entireio/main...entireio/docs/p0m5-install-docs`:\n```\ndocs/getting-started.md       | 254 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++--\ndocs/release_press_release.md | 222 ++++++++++++++++++++----------------\n2 files changed, 372 insertions(+), 104 deletions(-)\n```\n\n**docs/getting-started.md** — 553 B / 12 lines on main → 11242 B / 250 lines. Cold-start install + first-run guide. Sections (verified by heading grep): Requirements; Install (Quick install with `go install` — step 1 semantic provider `entire-graph`, step 2 the brain; Install from source; Release archive); Verify; First run: build a brain and query it; If you do n