{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-08-02T15:34:15.814Z","sessionId":"de272aad-c620-4d71-bbdd-27dd2d3dc8af","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>wzompd6po</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>REDACTED</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-suhaan-devenv/08c113b1-6073-41d6-9c88-fa9632538501/tasks/wzompd6po.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Dynamic workflow \"Land all remaining P0 and P1 work into entire-brain #75 and entire-api #242 worktrees\" completed</summary>\n<result>{\"brain\":{\"r1\":\"Merge committed as `723eec23`, two parents, clean tree, no AI footers, not pushed.\\n\\n## Per-file resolution (11 conflicts)\\n\\n**1. `docs/getting-started.md`** — took main's 12-line stub verbatim. Did NOT re-inflate. The branch's 14-line `packet_format` paragraph needed no relocation: the same content already exists in `docs/semantic_mcp_guide.md:29-45` (merged clean).\\n\\n**2. `internal/cli/embed_vec_cgo.go`** — struct-field union: main's `brainDir` + branch's `validated`.\\n\\n**3. `internal/cli/facts_read_cmd.go`** — import union `io` (main, used L366/373/476) + `os` (branch, used L60).\\n\\n**4. `internal/cli/mcp.go`** — one call site, both new args: `brainBriefOptions{..., packetFormat: packetFormat, surface: \\\"mcp:brain_brief\\\"}`.\\n\\n**5. `internal/cli/retrieve.go`** — kept the branch's BM25-only fast path (`rankHistoryLexicalFromSource`, skips loading the full index) as the `if` arm; main's calibrated hybrid ranks (`lexicalHistoryIDs`, `rankHistorySemanticHybridRanks`, `calibratedSemanticOnly`) as the `else` arm. Branch's `limit*2` repointed to main's `candidateLimit`.\\n\\n**6. `internal/cli/embed_rank.go`** (8 hunks) — main's structure + branch's helpers:\\n- `factVector`: main's invalid-cache tombstone and `factEmbeddingText(f)`; predicate expressed via the branch's `validSemanticEmbedding` (provably equivalent to `d&gt;0 &amp;&amp; len==d &amp;&amp; vectorHasMagnitude`).\\n- `cand` struct: main's `semanticValid`/`semantic` (subsumes branch's `semHit`).\\n- Query validation: main's `dim` local + branch's one-pass `semanticEmbeddingSquaredNorm` and `lastRun` trace.\\n- Candidate loop: main's NaN-default/`isFinite`/calibration mask + branch's `cosineFloat32WithQueryNorm` and `ValidCandidateVectors` counter.\\n- Ranking: main's gated `semanticOrder` + calibration arm, with the branch's `semanticFusionDepth` cap applied over it.\\n\\n**7. `internal/cli/embed_rank_test.go`** — union; both helper types (`controlledSemanticEmbedder`, `scriptedKNNVectorStore`) and all tests from both sides.\\n\\n**8. `internal/cli/embed_store_test.go`** — union; imports `math`/`os`/`sync`, both test funcs.\\n\\n**9. `internal/cli/agent_surface.go`** — options struct unions `profileJSON`/`packetFormat` with `surface`. In `runBrainBrief` I kept the branch's packet emission + profiling and added main's serve receipt as a `recordReceipt` closure fired **after** a successful emit (so receipts now work for every packet format, not just legacy JSON); `emitBrainBriefReport` restored as the pure renderer, keeping main's `stickyErrorWriter`.\\n\\n**10. `benchmarks/agent-brain/run.py`** (18 hunks) — union. Branch logic kept for: tolerant graph-binary build (repointed to main's `graph_bin` name and the `entire-graph` rename), `runtime_env` plumbing, treatment gating + `user_query`, `execution_identity`/`resolved_model`, `schedule_sha256`, treatment packets, timing/billing hand-off, structural-zero exception path, `is_executed_run`, `duration_metric`. Main-side fixes kept: `validation_commands(task)`, harness-temporal packet fail-closed, `read_isolation_profile`/`read_isolation` + `filesystem_read`, harness delivery + isolation lane, `analysis_excluded` (narrowed to failures before `treatment_started`), `validation_commands`/`temporal_delivery_mode` lint.\\n  - **One place I chose main over the branch:** adherence semantics (hunks 13/15/16). The branch retains adherence-failing rows in arm means (`adherence_failures`); main excludes them (`adherence_excluded`). Main's `test_summarize_excludes_adherence_invalid_runs_from_arm_means` asserts exclusion and is in the merged test file; no branch test asserts retention. Flagging it — it's a methodology decision, not a mechanical merge.\\n\\n**11. `benchmarks/agent-brain/run_test.py`** — union; both appended test classes are disjoint.\\n\\n## Extra fixes required to reach green\\n\\n- `brain_brief_profile_test.go`, `brain_brief_semantic_freshness_test.go`: `semanticIndexOptions{semBinary:}` → `{graphBinary:}` (main's rename; branch-added files auto-merged with the stale field, `go vet` caught it).\\n- `facts_default_retrieval_test.go`: three branch goldens froze pre-calibration behavior. Verified against a pristine `git archive MERGE_HEAD` snapshot that main's `semanticResultMask` is the cause, and that my `semanticFusionDepth` cap is not (uncapped gives the same result). Corpus-closed null now returns 0 instead of \\\"nearest six\\\"; the weak-tail premise no longer inverts; `fact:653adbd42aa9c222acb547d9` no longer clears the gate. **This is a real reachability tightening on the branch's corpus — worth a human look.**\\n- `semantic_relevance_test.go`: main's neutral-query test failed because the branch deliberately removed `\\\"before\\\"` from `genericQueryStopwords` (its `TestRankFactsFusedKeepsTemporalConstraintTerms` depends on that), so `reviews`/`database` now score a real lexical 10. Rewrote the assertion to main's actual intent — no fact admitted on *semantic* evidence alone — rather than \\\"no results\\\".\\n- `facts_eligibility_test.go`: `--read-only-semantic-cache` promises only that the vector cache isn't persisted/pruned; main added `recordServedFacts` to the recall path. Narrowed `treeContentHash` to skip `vitality.ndjson`/`vitality.json`/`vitality.lock` (empirically the only deltas).\\n\\n## Verified\\n\\n- `gofmt -l internal/` → empty\\n- `go build ./...` → clean\\n- `go vet ./...` → clean (whole repo, not just `./internal/...`)\\n- `go test ./... -count=1` → **1629 passed, 0 failed** (9 packages)\\n- `python3 -m unittest run_test` in `benchmarks/agent-brain` → **285 tests, OK**\\n\\nNot done: no push, no other checkout touched. Scratch snapshot of main removed.\",\"r2\":\"Done. Commit `47bd6932`, tree clean, not pushed.\\n\\n## Changed\\n\\n**Cherry-picked (clean, zero conflicts)** — `6b2244a9`, `217d0ad4`, `bdd7ee33` → `666c201b`, `2e4e160e`, `3bd2302d`. All 17 files landed: `internal/factgitmeta/**` (backend.go, localrepo.go, backend_test.go, vendored `gitmeta/` engine + tests), `internal/cli/facts_sync_cmd.go`, the `facts_admin_cmd.go` one-liner, go.mod/go.sum. The new package layout needed no reconciliation.\\n\\n**Fix 1 — Windows build** (`47bd6932`):\\n- `internal/factgitmeta/localrepo.go` — dropped the `syscall` import; `lock()` now calls `lockFileExclusive(f)` / `unlockFile(f)`. File-open, error wrapping, and the unlock-func contract are unchanged. Doc comment updated to point at the two platform files.\\n- `internal/factgitmeta/lock_unix.go` (new, `//go:build !windows`) — `syscall.Flock` LOCK_EX / LOCK_UN, byte-for-byte the previous behavior.\\n- `internal/factgitmeta/lock_windows.go` (new, `//go:build windows`) — `windows.LockFileEx` with `LOCKFILE_EXCLUSIVE_LOCK` over `allBytes = ^uint32(0)`, released by `UnlockFileEx` over the same region. No `LOCKFILE_FAIL_IMMEDIATELY`, so it blocks like `LOCK_EX`; the lock is handle-owned, so the OS releases it on close/crash — same \\\"no stale lock\\\" guarantee. `golang.org/x/sys` was already a **direct** require (v0.45.0), so go.mod/go.sum are untouched.\\n\\n**Fix 2 — gofmt**: `gofmt -w internal/factgitmeta/backend_test.go` reflowed the two one-line concurrent-`Advance` goroutine bodies (~L284) into block form.\\n\\n## Verified (all run, all passed)\\n\\n| Command | Result |\\n|---|---|\\n| `go build ./...` | exit 0 |\\n| `GOOS=windows GOARCH=amd64 go build ./...` | exit 0 |\\n| `go test ./internal/factgitmeta/... -count=1` | 22 passed, 2 packages |\\n| `gofmt -l internal/` | empty |\\n| `go vet ./internal/...` | exit 0 |\\n\\nExtra, beyond the required list:\\n- `GOOS=windows GOARCH=amd64 go vet ./internal/...` → exit 0 (type-checks `lock_windows.go`, which host-vet never sees).\\n- `GOOS=windows GOARCH=amd64 go test -c` on both factgitmeta packages → exit 0, i.e. the Windows **test** binaries compile, not just the library. (A plain `GOOS=windows go test` reports `exec format error` — that is darwin refusing to run a `.exe` after a successful compile, not a failure.)\\n- `go test ./... -count=1` → 1651 passed, 11 packages.\\n- `go\n... (truncated 30882 chars, full result in /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-suhaan-devenv/08c113b1-6073-41d6-9c88-fa9632538501/tasks/wzompd6po.output)</result>\n<diagnostics>Per-agent results: /Users/suhaan/.claude/projects/-Users-suhaan-devenv/de272aad-c620-4d71-bbdd-27dd2d3dc8af/subagents/workflows/wf_0c21e6f9-c1d/journal.jsonl — one {\"type\":\"result\",...} line per completed agent with its full return value.\nIf the result above is empty or unexpected, Read this file BEFORE diagnosing — do not assume agents returned non-empty results.\nTo re-run with edited post-processing: Workflow({scriptPath: '/Users/suhaan/.claude/projects/-Users-suhaan-devenv/de272aad-c620-4d71-bbdd-27dd2d3dc8af/workflows/scripts/p0-p1-completion-wf_0c21e6f9-c1d.js', resumeFromRunId: 'wf_0c21e6f9-c1d'}) — agents whose (prompt, opts) are unchanged replay from cache.</diagnostics>\n<usage><agent_count>10</agent_count><agents_done>10</agents_done><agents_error>0</agents_error><agents_skipped>0</agents_skipped><agents_empty_result>0</agents_empty_result><subagent_tokens>1213650</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>482</tool_uses><duration_ms>4635777</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
