{"parentUuid":"7ec97fbe-60ff-4d2b-89c1-dd76c62f8c30","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Ce5QSoGd9HHVcFmAkeNNg","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_015QKRC46W3yBfvkHc386dGv","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv/p0p1/p0-docs\ngit checkout -b docs/p0-gate-reconcile --quiet 2>/dev/null || git branch -m docs/p0-gate-reconcile\ngit add docs/ga-readiness.md\ngit commit -q -F - <<'EOF'\ndocs: reconcile GA gates 9-10 and record provider compatibility\n\nThe gate table contradicted the document's own evidence: rows 9 and 10 read\n\"pending\" while \"GA cut — resolved\" §1 and §2 record both as satisfied, and the\nsummary line above the table already claimed \"gates 1-11 satisfied\". Mark both\nrows done and cite the resolved section rather than restating the evidence.\n\nGate 10 pinned an aligned v0.1.0 tag pair. entire-graph has since shipped v0.2.0\nand v0.3.0, so the tags are no longer numerically aligned. Record why the gate\nstill holds: v0.3.0 advertises SchemaVersion \"1.1\", the same version cut at GA\nand inside the additive-only 1.x major that ADR 0001 freezes; the emitted\nrecord_type set is unchanged; and the brain consumes only `graph snapshot` and\n`graph doctor`, never `graph search`. No brain-side adaptation is required.\nEOF\ngit push entireio HEAD:docs/p0-gate-reconcile --quiet 2>&1 | tail -2\necho \"pushed: $(git log --oneline -1)\"","description":"Commit and push P0 gate reconcile"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":642,"cache_read_input_tokens":550216,"output_tokens":972,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":367},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":642,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_toke