{"type":"pr-link","sessionId":"de272aad-c620-4d71-bbdd-27dd2d3dc8af","prNumber":84,"prUrl":"https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/84","prRepository":"entireio/entire-brain","timestamp":"2026-08-15T23:39:03.014Z"}
{"type":"pr-link","sessionId":"de272aad-c620-4d71-bbdd-27dd2d3dc8af","prNumber":85,"prUrl":"https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/85","prRepository":"entireio/entire-brain","timestamp":"2026-08-15T23:39:24.468Z"}
{"parentUuid":"4eb60e3c-4f65-4374-926e-a30deb282854","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Ce5R5QB6SNUsxcEpdF5cy","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01PmKYNKS7X6VNp9DchuLG4k","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv/p0p1/p1-new\ngh pr create --repo entireio/entire-brain --base main --head feat/p1-canonical-signing-proposals \\\n  --title \"P1: canonical wire encoding, manifest signing, and the open-proposal transport\" \\\n  --body 'Completes the three P1 items that were specified but never built. Each commit is independent and additive; no existing behavior changes.\n\n## M1.3 — canonical wire encoding (`internal/brainwire/canonical.go`)\n\n`docs/brain_wire_contract.md` names four reasons the current `encoding/json` round-trip is a Go guarantee rather than a cross-implementation one: HTML escaping, struct field order, `omitempty`, and RFC3339Nano formatting. It then defers the fix to \"M1.3/M1.4 define an explicit canonical encoding\". This defines it.\n\n- HTML escaping off, so `repo_key`, `branch`, `path`, `media_type` and `provider` survive as raw UTF-8.\n- Object keys ordered lexicographically by JSON tag (RFC 8785 rule), not Go declaration order, so a non-Go producer can reproduce the bytes without owning the struct.\n- `omitempty` made normative and exhaustive: an explicit `\"size\":0` or `\"tree\":\"\"` is non-canonical and normalizes to omission. This is the failure the contract doc calls out by name.\n- Times normalize to UTC with a fixed fractional policy and a literal `Z`.\n- Integers decimal-only; strings minimally escaped.\n\n`Canonicalize` normalizes foreign bytes, which is the point — the format has to be reachable by a producer that is not this package. **No JSON tag changes**, per `contract.go`: the tags are the contract.\n\n## M1.4 — manifest signing (`internal/brainwire/signing.go`)\n\nEd25519 over the canonical bytes, which is why it depends on M1.3. The envelope carries algorithm, key id, and the canonical-encoding version, so a future encoding revision cannot silently validate against an old signature. `Sign` takes a `crypto.Signer`, so key material never has to transit the API.\n\nPer the contract doc, blobs are already content-addressed, so the signature covers the manifest — and it commits to every referenced blob digest, so swapping a blob invalidates it. That property has its own test rather than being asserted in a comment.\n\n## PR #64 deferrals — open-proposal transport and CLI\n\n#64 landed the proposal model and `Resolve` with a passing convergence test, and explicitly deferred the transport and the user-facing verbs. Both are here:\n\n- `internal/factsync/httpproposals.go` — list, get, apply, resolve, symmetric with the existing fact-set handlers and reusing their 409/412 semantics and egress redaction.\n- `internal/hostedbrain/proposals.go` — the client half.\n- `entire-brain facts proposals {list,show,apply,reject}`.\n\n`facts sync` now publishes the conflicts a sync raised to the shared queue **only when the backend implements `ProposalTransport`**. The local git-meta store does not, so it is a no-op and the default local flow never reaches the network. A publish failure warns rather than failing the sync: the facts have already landed, and an entire-api predating the endpoint must not break a working sync.\n\n## Verification\n\n`go build`, `GOOS=windows GOARCH=amd64 go build`, `go vet ./...`, `gofmt -l` clean; `go test ./...` green across all 9 packages, `internal/brainwire` also under `-race`.\n\nThe server counterpart for the proposal endpoints is entire-api #242.' 2>&1 | tail -3","description":"Open P1 PR"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":654,"cache_read_input_tokens":563213,"output_tokens":1308,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":654,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1308,"cache_read_input_tokens":563213,"cache_creation_input_tokens":654,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":654},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011Ce5R5MYqVcyJtGLXdEAP4","type":"assistant","uuid":"50cecf12-baaf-48ed-8325-d8781d078407","timestamp":"2026-08-15T23:39:22.411Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"f507d58c-285f-4d11-b1d0-201f2a5e172d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/p0p1/p1-new","sessionId":"de272aad-c620-4d71-bbdd-27dd2d3dc8af","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"quizzical-sniffing-quasar"}
