{"parentUuid":"14aea75b-42ea-4821-8b17-8c0a81ae6e74","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Ce8TBXx59oNnjjz6dMGyz","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01EAukASEhuuJr2bifjgFcnQ","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"echo \"=== api #617 ===\"\ngh pr view 617 --repo entirehq/entire-api --json title,state,mergeStateStatus,additions,changedFiles,author,body --jq '\"\\(.title)\\n\\(.state) \\(.mergeStateStatus) +\\(.additions) files=\\(.changedFiles) by=\\(.author.login)\\n---\\n\\(.body[0:700])\"' 2>/dev/null\necho \"\"\necho \"=== is factsrelay on api main already? ===\"\ngh api repos/entirehq/entire-api/contents/internal/factsrelay --jq '.[].name' 2>/dev/null | head -6 || echo \"  (absent on main)\"\necho \"\"\necho \"=== entire-graph open PRs ===\"\ngh pr list --repo entireio/entire-graph --state open --limit 10 --json number,title,author,mergeStateStatus,updatedAt --jq '.[]|\"#\\(.number) [\\(.author.login)] \\(.title[0:56]) \\(.mergeStateStatus) upd=\\(.updatedAt[0:10])\"' 2>/dev/null","description":"Check api 617 + graph open PRs"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1245,"cache_read_input_tokens":579964,"output_tokens":639,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":150},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1245,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":639,"cache_read_input_tokens":579964,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1245,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1245},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011Ce8TBTZuGML632jdqznzN","type":"assistant","uuid":"8db31989-347f-4c8f-951c-0a0f723ff31f","timestamp":"2026-08-17T14:08:36.117Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"f507d58c-285f-4d11-b1d0-201f2a5e172d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/p0p1/p1-new","sessionId":"de272aad-c620-4d71-bbdd-27dd2d3dc8af","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"quizzical-sniffing-quasar"}
{"parentUuid":"8db31989-347f-4c8f-951c-0a0f723ff31f","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"9b632cc4-8ae4-4a21-90b3-b370830204c2","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01EAukASEhuuJr2bifjgFcnQ","type":"tool_result","content":"=== api #617 ===\nfactsrelay: single-row fallback and dead-letter for slow batches\nOPEN CLEAN +554 files=7 by=pfleidi\n---\n## Why\n\nThe facts relay's batch RecordFacts RPC is all-or-nothing at transport, and core applies a batch's sets serially. A batch whose total apply cost exceeds the RPC timeout therefore failed and was retried identically every tick, forever — the wedge behind the 2026-08-14 ap-south-1 incident, where ~6-row batches at ~800ms per cross-region upsert pinned the cluster's p99 for 9+ hours. #616 widened the timeout as immediate mitigation; this PR removes the failure mode: a batch that can't fit the timeout no longer blocks its shard, and a row that can never deliver stops consuming the relay.\n\n## What changed\n\n- On a timeout-shaped batch failure the relay falls back to single-row sends, capped\n\n=== is factsrelay on api main already? ===\nrelay.go\nrelay_test.go\n\n=== entire-graph open PRs ===\n#104 [suhaanthayyil] feat(search): prose retrieval by section, with the bench CLEAN upd=2026-08-17\n#97 [ashtom] feat: add experimental SCIP snapshot export CLEAN upd=2026-08-14","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"16a4c7d4-1146-47c5-86f9-6eba90cd4acb","timestamp":"2026-08-17T14:08:38.817Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"=== api #617 ===\nfactsrelay: single-row fallback and dead-letter for slow batches\nOPEN CLEAN +554 files=7 by=pfleidi\n---\n## Why\n\nThe facts relay's batch RecordFacts RPC is all-or-nothing at transport, and core applies a batch's sets serially. A batch whose total apply cost exceeds the RPC timeout therefore failed and was retried identically every tick, forever — the wedge behind the 2026-08-14 ap-south-1 incident, where ~6-row batches at ~800ms per cross-region upsert pinned the cluster's p99 for 9+ hours. #616 widened the timeout as immediate mitigation; this PR removes the failure mode: a batch that can't fit the timeout no longer blocks its shard, and a row that can never deliver stops consuming the relay.\n\n## What changed\n\n- On a timeout-shaped batch failure the relay falls back to single-row sends, capped\n\n=== is factsrelay on api main already? ===\nrelay.go\nrelay_test.go\n\n=== entire-graph open PRs ===\n#104 [suhaanthayyil] feat(search): prose retrieval by section, with the bench CLEAN upd=2026-08-17\n#97 [ashtom] feat: add experimental SCIP snapshot export CLEAN upd=2026-08-14","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"8db31989-347f-4c8f-951c-0a0f723ff31f","session_id":"f507d58c-285f-4d11-b1d0-201f2a5e172d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/p0p1/p1-new","sessionId":"de272aad-c620-4d71-bbdd-27dd2d3dc8af","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"quizzical-sniffing-quasar"}
