{"parentUuid":"8826a5fc-ddf3-4c4c-bf32-58e7fdde8c50","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Ce8TDggkDQ8PVorjPNcX6","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1025,"cache_read_input_tokens":582319,"output_tokens":2471,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":961},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1025,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2471,"cache_read_input_tokens":582319,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1025,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1025},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011Ce8TDbukiRHddMLrfEdNw","type":"assistant","uuid":"79c4660f-97fd-4b5e-937f-664ed0d5fc6a","timestamp":"2026-08-17T14:09:14.519Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"f507d58c-285f-4d11-b1d0-201f2a5e172d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/p0p1/p1-new","sessionId":"de272aad-c620-4d71-bbdd-27dd2d3dc8af","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"quizzical-sniffing-quasar"}
{"parentUuid":"79c4660f-97fd-4b5e-937f-664ed0d5fc6a","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Ce8TDggkDQ8PVorjPNcX6","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# Status report — 2026-08-17\n\n## P0: closed ✅\n**#84 merged 08-15.** All 11 gates read ✅ on main, zero pending rows. My \"Provider compatibility since the GA cut\" section survives intact at line 81.\n\n**#86 merged 08-16** — big one (+24,051/−8,759, 97 files): made the `release-evidence` job pass on *honest* evidence rather than by loosening the gate. It **withdrew the June bundle** (its treatment arm had read a harness-prepared history excerpt with `used_brain: False`, and the baseline could reach the answer through committed history). Replacement clean-proof: **semantic_history_brain 5/5 vs no_brain 0/5, delta +55.8, zero adherence flags across all 20 cells**, under per-cell deny-first sandbox with the answer scrubbed from blobs *and* commit messages.\n\nThat's a stronger P0 position than when I wrote #84 — the evidence gate now actually runs green.\n\n## entire-brain — 1 open PR\n**#85** (P1: canonical encoding + signing + proposal transport) — **CLEAN, 15 pass / 1 skipping.**\n\nIt was **reviewed** by an automated pass on ashtom's behalf, and **two fix commits were pushed onto my branch** (`c64327e4`, `2d8dd890`). Real bugs it caught in my code:\n- `Canonicalize` accepted **duplicate JSON members** — Go's last-wins decode meant a signature could verify over bytes a first-wins parser in another language reads differently. Now rejected via a token-level decoder.\n- That decoder was **unbounded recursion** — a few MB of `[` was a stack overflow in the entry point for untrusted bytes. Now depth-bounded at 512.\n- **Integers now bounded to ±2^53** — beyond that a double-based JCS verifier re-serializes a different value and signatures fail silently cross-language.\n- `ResolveOpen` didn't pin the proposal ID across CAS retries; prefix ref `prop` matched *every* open proposal; `facts sync` swallowed real publish errors.\n\n**Not merge-ready.** The review flags 5 open design questions and says **items 1 and 2 are worth settling before merge**:\n1. **Accepted settlements don't stick** — the losing member's local facts are never reconciled to a hosted resolution, so their next sync re-raises the same conflict under a fresh ID.\n2. **Local `facts review` has no hosted interlock** — settling a published proposal locally leaves the hosted copy open; a teammate's later apply silently overrides the decision.\n\n## entire-api — 2 open, 1 is ours\n- **#242** (P1 server half) — still **untouched since 07-17**, mergeable `UNKNOWN` (stale). This is the server counterpart #85's client talks to.\n- **#617** `factsrelay` timeout fallback — **not ours.** Different subsystem (relay→core), by pfleidi, fixing the 08-14 ap-south-1 incident where ~6-row batches at ~800ms pinned p99 for 9+ hours.\n\n## git-meta-service\n**#1** — `MERGEABLE` but status **BLOCKED** (needs approval). Brain still carries the vendored copy of this engine until it lands.\n\n## entire-graph — brain unaffected by both open PRs\nLatest release **v0.3.0** (08-14).\n- **#104** (mine, prose retrieval) — OPEN, CLEAN. Touches search only; brain never calls `graph search`.\n- **#97** (ashtom, SCIP export) — OPEN, CLEAN. Adds opt-in `snapshot --format scip`; **native and compact NDJSON explicitly unchanged**, and brain passes `--format ndjson`. No impact.\n\nSchema is still `1.1` at v0.3.0, same record types, additive-only under ADR 0001 — documented on main with the re-check trigger.\n\n## The critical path now\n1. **Decide #85's items 1 & 2** — this is a model question (do hosted settlements get pulled into local facts during sync?), not a bug fix. It's the only thing standing between P1's client half and merge.\n2. **Refresh #242** against api's current main — it's a month stale regardless of #85.\n3. **Unblock git-meta #1** so brain can de-vendor.\n\nItems 1 and 2 are genuinely your design call. Want me to write up the two options for settlement reconciliation so you can pick, or go straight at refreshing #242?"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1025,"cache_read_input_tokens":582319,"output_tokens":2471,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":961},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1025,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2471,"cache_read_input_tokens":582319,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1025,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1025},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011Ce8TDbukiRHddMLrfEdNw","type":"assistant","uuid":"318a4e28-6268-430c-8827-72596cbeb081","timestamp":"2026-08-17T14:09:32.978Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"f507d58c-285f-4d11-b1d0-201f2a5e172d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/p0p1/p1-new","sessionId":"de272aad-c620-4d71-bbdd-27dd2d3dc8af","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"quizzical-sniffing-quasar"}
