{"type":"pr-link","sessionId":"de272aad-c620-4d71-bbdd-27dd2d3dc8af","prNumber":85,"prUrl":"https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/85","prRepository":"entireio/entire-brain","timestamp":"2026-08-17T14:35:37.398Z"}
{"parentUuid":"d209f84e-f6d1-4c5b-9312-fb5aeef4c45a","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Ce8VEWXZthC18WxtNHu9a","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01L3J94s3mCdZPc2QvzAkJsr","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv/p0p1/p1-new\ngh pr comment 85 --repo entireio/entire-brain --body 'Pushed `5b17f2a3` — closes the two findings flagged as worth settling before merge (items 1 and 2). The other three remain open by design; notes below.\n\n## 1. Accepted settlements now stick\n\nSync reads the shared head back and mirrors each settlement into local facts with the same primitives the hosted side ran, so the two cannot drift.\n\nThe decision is **derived from the head** rather than requiring a new server field:\n\n| head state after settlement | read as |\n|---|---|\n| candidate absent, target present (merge) | accept — remove the candidate locally |\n| target superseded, pointing at the candidate | accept — mirror the status locally |\n| anything else | reject — clear the local conflict cross-link only |\n\nFacts are mirrored **before** the queue entry is dropped, so a crash cannot lose the record of what still needs reconciling. A head read that fails only costs this sync'\"'\"'s mirroring: the entry stays queued and the next sync retries.\n\n## 2. Local review is interlocked\n\nA proposal recorded in the shared ledger refuses to settle via `facts review` and names the `facts proposals` command that settles it for everyone. Bulk `--apply-all` / `--reject-all` skips shared entries with a warning rather than failing the batch, so distill'\"'\"'s private backlog — unattributed, never shared — still clears in one command exactly as before.\n\n## On the tests\n\nMutation-verified: reverting either fix fails them.\n\nWorth flagging, because it changed the test design — the **natural sync fixture cannot exercise this defect at all**. In it the local fact is the proposal'\"'\"'s *candidate* and wins the supersede, so nothing needs retiring locally and an assertion written against it passes with the fix reverted. I had exactly that false-confidence test and the mutation run caught it. The settlement test now drives `reconcileLocalProposalQueue` directly and covers merge accept, supersede accept, and reject, so it exercises the **losing** member — the only side the defect affects.\n\n## Still open by design\n\nItems 3, 4 and 5 are untouched: no server-side settled-id tombstone (the ledger stays per-checkout), `distill --force` still rewrites `proposals.ndjson` without the sync-raised backlog, and an orphaned proposal whose facts head is gone is still unremovable. Each needs a server-side or ownership change rather than a client fix, so they read as follow-ups rather than merge blockers.\n\nVerification: `go build`, `GOOS=windows GOARCH=amd64 go build`, `go vet ./...`, `gofmt -l` clean; `go test ./...` green across all 9 packages.' 2>&1 | tail -2","description":"Comment on PR 85 explaining fixes"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1112,"cache_read_input_tokens":658753,"output_tokens":1010,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1112,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1010,"cache_read_input_tokens":658753,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1112,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1112},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011Ce8VEN5p4o7Wppm7d4gWU","type":"assistant","uuid":"71d51445-79d6-4952-8082-5e1d2a816489","timestamp":"2026-08-17T14:35:36.455Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"f507d58c-285f-4d11-b1d0-201f2a5e172d","userType":"external","entrypoint":