{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-08-17T14:35:40.754Z","sessionId":"de272aad-c620-4d71-bbdd-27dd2d3dc8af","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>bm5og7dyk</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>REDACTED</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-suhaan-devenv/f507d58c-285f-4d11-b1d0-201f2a5e172d/tasks/bm5og7dyk.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Background command \"Watch affected package tests\" completed (exit code 0)</summary>\n</task-notification>"}
{"parentUuid":"30881df8-26e9-4ead-92f4-97e2fe863928","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Ce8VFpYovnM6sUnmvphKp","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"P1 is now merge-ready on the brain side. **PR only — nothing merged.**\n\n## What I did\nBoth blockers from the review are closed on **#85** (`5b17f2a3`), plus a comment explaining the design.\n\n**Item 1 — accepted settlements now stick.** Sync reads the shared head back and mirrors each settlement into local facts using the same primitives the hosted side ran, so the two can't drift. The decision is *derived from the head* rather than needing a new server field:\n\n| head state after settlement | read as |\n|---|---|\n| candidate gone, target present (merge) | accept → remove candidate locally |\n| target superseded → candidate | accept → mirror status locally |\n| anything else | reject → clear the cross-link only |\n\nFacts are mirrored **before** the queue entry drops, so a crash can't lose what still needs reconciling.\n\n**Item 2 — local review is interlocked.** A proposal in the shared ledger refuses to settle via `facts review` and names the `facts proposals` command that settles it for everyone. Bulk `--apply-all`/`--reject-all` skips shared entries with a warning rather than failing the batch, so distill's private backlog still clears in one command.\n\n## The part worth your attention\n**Mutation testing caught a false-confidence test of my own.** My first settlement test passed with the fix reverted — because in the natural sync fixture the local fact is the proposal's *candidate* and **wins** the supersede, so nothing needed retiring locally and the assertion was vacuous. The defect only affects the **losing** member. Rewrote it to drive `reconcileLocalProposalQueue` directly across merge-accept, supersede-accept and reject. Now it fails on both accept shapes when reverted.\n\nI'd have shipped a test that proved nothing if I hadn't run the mutation check.\n\n## Verified\n`go build` · `GOOS=windows` cross-build · `go vet ./...` · `gofmt` clean · `go test ./...` **all 9 packages pass**\n\n## State\n- **#85** — brain P1 complete, +6,493/−16, 17 files, CI running. Not merged.\n- Items 3–5 from the review left open deliberately (server-side tombstone, `distill --force` file ownership, orphaned-proposal prune) — each needs a server or ownership change, not a client fix. Called out as follow-ups in the comment.\n- **#242** (api server half) still stale from 07-17 — that's the remaining P1 work, and it's the counterpart #85's client talks to.\n\nWant me to refresh #242 next, same rules — PR only?"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1418,"cache_read_input_tokens":659865,"output_tokens":848,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1418,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":848,"cache_read_input_tokens":659865,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1418,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1418},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011Ce8VFisFKxPvNtT3azStb","type":"assistant","uuid":"c81d4cf9-9bf1-4a3d-ad4f-7bd144e77454","timestamp":"2026-08-17T14:35:50.995Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"f507d58c-285f-4d11-b1d0-201f2a5e172d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/p0p1/p1-new","sessionId":"de272aad-c620-4d71-bbdd-27dd2d3dc8af","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"quizzical-sniffing-quasar"}
