{"parentUuid":"5bcdb074-64f9-43ea-bfda-6bef2c438684","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"bee87439-e2ff-4ab7-9b58-577b5019ead8","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013U5fyACAP2f1Sy4KYrpwLD","type":"tool_result","content":"=== apiTags catalog (tags.go) ===\npackage httpapi\n\nimport \"github.com/danielgtaylor/huma/v2\"\n\n// apiTags is the top-level OpenAPI tag catalog: the ordered, documented list of\n// groups the operations sort into. Declaring it here (rather than letting huma\n// synthesise bare tags from first use) gives every group a description and a\n// deliberate order in the rendered docs. Each operation's own Tags value (set at\n// registration, one per operation) must name one of these — grouping tracks the\n// resource, independent of the access gate that wired the route.\n//\n// Order is reader-facing and the renderer follows this slice, so moving an entry\n// moves the group in the docs: the caller's own surface, then a repo and its\n// sub-resources, then the trail family (roughly the order a trail moves through\n// it, with attachments trailing as an ancillary), then cross-repo rollups and\n// repo configuration, and last the machine-only groups. Anything more precise\n// than that rots the next time a tag is inserted.\n//\n// Only tags on THIS document belong here. The internal admin surface builds its\n// own huma config in NewAdminHandler and never reads apiTags, so declaring its\n// tag here would render an empty group.\nvar apiTags = []*huma.Tag{\n\t{Name: \"me\", Description: \"The authenticated caller's own cross-repo activity, commits, checkpoints, sessions, and recap.\"},\n\t{Name: \"experimental\", Description: \"Residency-aware previews of the caller's surface, served under /experimental. Shapes may change without notice.\"},\n\t{Name: \"preferences\", Description: \"Per-user settings: pinned and recent repos, diff view, and saved filter tabs.\"},\n\t{Name: \"repos\", Description: \"Repository discovery list, metadata, and headline rollups (summary, activity, contributors, agents).\"},\n\t{Name: \"code\", Description: \"Git browsing for a repo: commits, commit detail, branch compare, tree listings, raw file bytes, and branches.\"},\n\t{Name: \"checkpoints\", Description: \"Checkpoint listing, resolution, LLM analysis, transcripts, and per-repo checkpoint status.\"},\n\t{Name: \"sessions\", Description: \"Materialised sessions: listing, detail, transcripts, rename, and the public-share toggle.\"},\n\t{Name: \"overview\", Description: \"Repo dashboard aggregates under /overview: commit and checkpoint stats, contributor breakdowns, and session patterns.\"},\n\t{Name: \"refs\", Description: \"Live ref-change stream for a repo (SSE).\"},\n\t{Name: \"trails\", Description: \"Trails themselves: list, create, read, update, delete, plus per-repo counts, claimed branches, and the body-document ensure.\"},\n\t{Name: \"trail-activity\", Description: \"What has happened on a trail: the merged timeline, the event stream, and who is watching (per trail, plus a repo-wide roll-up).\"},\n\t{Name: \"trail-threads\", Description: \"Conversation on a trail: threads, their messages, and the live thread-event stream.\"},\n\t{Name: \"trail-reviews\", Description: \"Code review on a trail: review state, comments, diffs, reviewed files, and review re-runs.\"},\n\t{Name: \"trail-runs\", Description: \"Runner output on a trail: the latest result per configured runner, monitor results, and manual launches.\"},\n\t{Name: \"trail-gates\", Description: \"Quality gates: repo gate definitions, gate settings, repo-authored monitor definitions, and a trail's gate evaluation.\"},\n\t{Name: \"trail-approvals\", Description: \"Getting a trail landed: approval decisions, merge readiness, and the merge itself.\"},\n\t{Name: \"trail-attachments\", Description: \"Trail attachment blobs: upload intent, completion, retrieval, and deletion.\"},\n\t{Name: \"projects\", Description: \"Project-scoped rollups across the project's repos: summary, repos, activity, and contributors.\"},\n\t{Name: \"experts\", Description: \"Agent-provenance ranking for a repo's code scopes.\"},\n\t{Name: \"git-meta\", Description: \"git-meta-compatible repo metadata read and write (git is the source of truth).\"},\n\t{Name: \"records\", Description: \"Experimental, read-only: schema-described records decoded from a repository's git-meta records store (refs/meta/records/<schema>/main). Shapes may change without notice.\"},\n\t{Name: \"repo-settings\", Description: \"Mutating repo configuration: runner, trail, and public-sharing settings (requires repo push; the gate-enforcement toggle requires manage_settings).\"},\n\t{Name: \"pull-requests\", Description: \"The caller's open pull requests across their repositories.\"},\n\t{Name: \"trails-internal\", Description: \"Service-authed only: editor-document sync behind the trail body editor. The runner ingest routes carry this tag too, but are hidden from the document.\"},\n\t{Name: \"runner-issuer\", Description: \"The runner OIDC issuer's discovery document and JWKS. Machine-consumed.\"},\n}","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"599046b2-7706-4241-8fb9-f355afcf1418","timestamp":"2026-08-17T14:38:36.933Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"=== apiTags catalog (tags.go) ===\npackage httpapi\n\nimport \"github.com/danielgtaylor/huma/v2\"\n\n// apiTags is the top-level OpenAPI tag catalog: the ordered, documented list of\n// groups the operations sort into. Declaring it here (rather than letting huma\n// synthesise bare tags from first use) gives every group a description and a\n// deliberate order in the rendered docs. Each operation's own Tags value (set at\n// registration, one per operation) must name one of these — grouping tracks the\n// resource, independent of the access gate that wired the route.\n//\n// Order is reader-facing and the renderer follows this slice, so moving an entry\n// moves the group in the docs: the caller's own surface, then a repo and its\n// s