{"parentUuid":"84e703cc-6897-443b-ac00-88b2dce13e4c","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Ce8VjYEZm3naUWbZqujqx","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"#242 is now **MERGEABLE** (was CONFLICTING/DIRTY). Recording the interop fork on the PR:"}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1400,"cache_read_input_tokens":686748,"output_tokens":1582,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":108},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1400,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1582,"cache_read_input_tokens":686748,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1400,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1400},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011Ce8VjTgUEsnYuDiwKyfgo","type":"assistant","uuid":"ef3ecc97-d89e-4340-8eae-12be5cc7c154","timestamp":"2026-08-17T14:42:00.220Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"f507d58c-285f-4d11-b1d0-201f2a5e172d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/p0p1/api-242","sessionId":"de272aad-c620-4d71-bbdd-27dd2d3dc8af","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"quizzical-sniffing-quasar"}
{"parentUuid":"ef3ecc97-d89e-4340-8eae-12be5cc7c154","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Ce8VjYEZm3naUWbZqujqx","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01FrLAjkTMevi4wKZRtitsGQ","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv/p0p1/api-242\ngh pr comment 242 --repo entirehq/entire-api --body 'Refreshed onto current `main` (734 commits, **zero conflicts**) and fixed a CI failure this branch had picked up. But verifying it against the brain client surfaced a **hard interop break** that has to be settled before either half can ship.\n\n## Landed here\n\n- `a9709820` — merge current `main`. Clean auto-merge; `go build`, `go vet ./internal/...` clean, `gofmt` clean on this branch'\"'\"'s files, and `brainbuild` / `brainstore` / `brainquery` / `httpapi` tests green.\n- `4234e98e` — declare the `brain` OpenAPI tag. `TestOpenAPITagCatalogInvariants` landed on main after this branch was cut and failed for **all nine** brain operations (publish, facts current/advance, the five proposal routes, remote MCP), because they carried the tag without declaring it in `apiTags`. Grouped with `git-meta` and `records`, since the shared fact set is likewise a git-backed repo metadata store rather than a product read-model.\n\nStatus is now `MERGEABLE` (was `CONFLICTING`/`DIRTY`).\n\n## The interop break\n\nThe server half here and the client half in entire-brain [#85](https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/85) were built independently and **do not agree on the wire at three levels**. As it stands no proposal could be addressed across it.\n\n| | brain client (#85) | this branch |\n|---|---|---|\n| collection path | `/api/v1/repos/{id}/brain/facts/proposals` | `/repos/{repo_id}/brain/proposals` |\n| settle | `POST .../{id}/resolve`, decision in body | `POST .../{id}/apply` and `.../{id}/reject` |\n| proposal id | `sha256(action, candidateID, targetID, branch, proposedBy)`, truncated to **16** hex | `sha256(branch, baseRef, contentRef)`, full **64** hex |\n\nThe id divergence is the fatal one: the two sides derive identity from different inputs *and* different lengths, so a client-computed id can never match a server-stored one.\n\n## Which side should move, and why\n\n**This one.** Three reasons, in order of weight:\n\n1. **ADR-P1-E.** The merge runs on the runner, not the API server. `ProposalStore.Apply` here computes the resolution server-side, which contradicts that. The client is ADR-correct: it computes the resolved fact set and CAS-pushes it with `factsOldRef` / `proposalsOldRef` preconditions, leaving the server as storage plus CAS.\n2. **Path family.** This branch already serves `/brain/facts` and `/brain/facts/advance`. The proposal set is the fact set'\"'\"'s review queue, so `/brain/facts/proposals` is the consistent home — the client already uses it.\n3. **Review state.** The client half has been through review and had its proposal lifecycle hardened (id pinning across CAS retries, reject-as-prune, prefix-ref scoping). The server half is unreviewed.\n\nMechanically that means a `resolve` endpoint accepting `{branch, decision, factsOldRef, data, proposalsOldRef, proposals}` and returning `{factsRef, proposalsRef, changed}`, mapping CAS loss to 412/409 and an unknown id to 404 — the same shape `advanceBrainFacts` already implements against `FactSetStore.Current`/`Advance`. The proposal set needs an equivalent CAS'\"'\"'d-blob seam; the Postgres `ProposalIndex` can stay as a read-model behind it, but it should not be the wire surface.\n\nI have deliberately not rewritten it here: that is an architecture call on which storage seam the queue gets, and picking it unilaterally on an unreviewed branch seemed worse than surfacing it. Happy to implement it the moment the direction is confirmed.' 2>&1 | tail -2","description":"Comment interop fork on 242"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1400,"cache_read_input_tokens":686748,"output_tokens":1582,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":108},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1400,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1582,"cache_read_input_tokens":686748,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1400,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1400},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011Ce8VjTgUEsnYuDiwKyfgo","type":"assistant","uuid":"cc0be223-d925-4a0b-b9f7-95e4e9e89d07","timestamp":"2026-08-17T14:42:17.229Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"f507d58c-285f-4d11-b1d0-201f2a5e172d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/p0p1/api-242","sessionId":"de272aad-c620-4d71-bbdd-27dd2d3dc8af","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"quizzical-sniffing-quasar"}
