{"type":"pr-link","sessionId":"de272aad-c620-4d71-bbdd-27dd2d3dc8af","prNumber":242,"prUrl":"https://github.com/entirehq/entire-api/pull/242","prRepository":"entirehq/entire-api","timestamp":"2026-08-17T14:42:42.979Z"}
{"parentUuid":"45e18f3e-4b7f-4414-a8a5-b3e3fc308491","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Ce8VoE9VN41H71LLX564i","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"P1 is as ready as it can honestly get without one decision from you. **PRs only — nothing merged.**\n\n## Brain #85 — done\nBoth review blockers closed (`5b17f2a3`), 13 pass / 2 pending CI.\n\n- **Settlements now stick** — sync reads the shared head back and mirrors each settlement into local facts with the same primitives the hosted side ran. Decision derived from the head, no new server field needed.\n- **Local review interlocked** — a shared proposal refuses to settle via `facts review` and names the `facts proposals` command instead; bulk mode skips shared entries so distill's private backlog still clears.\n- **Mutation testing caught a worthless test of my own** — my first settlement test passed with the fix reverted, because the sync fixture makes the local member *win* its own proposal, so nothing needed retiring. The defect only affects the **losing** member. Rewrote it to drive the reconciler directly across merge-accept, supersede-accept and reject.\n\n## API #242 — refreshed, now MERGEABLE\n- Merged **734 commits** of main, **zero conflicts**\n- Fixed a real CI failure: `TestOpenAPITagCatalogInvariants` (added to main after the branch was cut) was failing for **all nine** brain operations because the `brain` tag was used but never declared. That was pre-existing in #242, not from my work.\n- Tests green: `httpapi`, `brainbuild`, `brainstore`, `brainquery`\n\n## The blocker I found — and did not paper over\n**The two halves don't agree on the wire at three levels.** P1 would fail end-to-end today:\n\n| | brain client | api server |\n|---|---|---|\n| path | `/brain/facts/proposals` | `/brain/proposals` |\n| settle | `POST .../{id}/resolve` | `POST .../{id}/apply` + `/reject` |\n| **proposal id** | `sha256(action, candidate, target, branch, proposedBy)` → **16** hex | `sha256(branch, baseRef, contentRef)` → **64** hex |\n\nThe id divergence is fatal — different inputs *and* different lengths, so a client-computed id can never match a server-stored one.\n\n**The api side should move**, and I'd say that even though it's my code: **ADR-P1-E says the merge runs on the runner**, but api's `ProposalStore.Apply` resolves server-side. The client is the ADR-correct one, it already targets the `/brain/facts` family api itself serves, and it's the reviewed half.\n\nThe fix is a `resolve` endpoint mirroring the existing `advanceBrainFacts` CAS shape, with the Postgres index kept as a read-model behind it rather than as the wire surface.\n\n**I deliberately didn't rewrite it.** Which storage seam the queue gets is an architecture call, and picking it unilaterally on an unreviewed branch is worse than surfacing it. It's written up on #242 and in memory.\n\nConfirm the direction and I'll implement it — it's a contained change against a pattern that already works."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1225,"cache_read_input_tokens":690949,"output_tokens":1006,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1225,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1006,"cache_read_input_tokens":690949,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1225,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1225},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011Ce8Vo73c3XMWpW1Ndg3ru","type":"assistant","uuid":"98c4f441-371c-4da9-9cdc-ac9133815998","timestamp":"2026-08-17T14:42:59.526Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"f507d58c-285f-4d11-b1d0-201f2a5e172d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"de272aad-c620-4d71-bbdd-27dd2d3dc8af","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"quizzical-sniffing-quasar"}
