{"parentUuid":"e6a6dc0c-8298-4709-ab40-54c4cdbe3355","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Ce8W3kV1aecUTdcF1uWGE","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Confirmed — and it **shortens the list**. Both entiredb prerequisites the PR bodies cite as blocking are already done (`WorkloadEntireAPI` registered for `refs/meta/entire/*` writes, ENT-1106; and general `refs/meta/*` was never reserved — \"standard git-meta clients can push them directly\").\n\n# To finish P1: 2 PRs\n\n## 1. entire-brain #85 — ready\n**MERGEABLE**, CI 14 pass / 1 pending / 1 skipping. Zero review approvals yet.\n\nContains: **M1.3** canonical encoding · **M1.4** manifest signing · **#64's two deferrals** (proposal transport + `facts proposals` CLI) · the two review blockers fixed (settlements stick, local-review interlock).\n\nNothing blocks this but a review.\n\n## 2. entire-api #242 — needs the interop fix first\n**MERGEABLE/BLOCKED** (blocked = needs review approval).\n\nContains: **M1.2** server store · facts CAS · remote brain MCP · tenancy (ADR-0004) · P1.M7 RFD (ADR-0005) · proposal endpoints · manifest integrity on ingest · the `brain` OpenAPI tag fix.\n\n**Must land before merging:** the client/server reconciliation. Merging both as-is ships a P1 that cannot talk to itself — the proposal ids alone can never match (16-hex vs 64-hex, different inputs). This is a contained change once you pick the direction; my recommendation is on the PR (api moves to `/brain/facts/proposals` + a single `/resolve`, mirroring the `advanceBrainFacts` CAS that already works).\n\n---\n\n# Already merged — no action\n| milestone | PR |\n|---|---|\n| M1.1 brain wire contract | #59 |\n| M1.5 publish client | #60 |\n| M2.2 merge engine · M2.3 fact-sync runner · M2.4 conflict routing · M3.3 remote MCP client | #64 |\n| factsync camelCase wire fix | #65 |\n| local git-meta fact store | #74 |\n\n# Not merges, but P1 isn't真 done without them\n- **Live cross-repo round-trip** — #64 explicitly deferred it and **it has still never been run.** Everything is proven against fakes; the real wire is untested. This is exactly what would have caught the interop fork, and it's the highest-value remaining verification.\n- **Brain's vendored `gitmeta` has drifted** from api's canonical `internal/gitmeta` (all 6 files; api added path-target support). Latent today because brain writes local-only — but **now more urgent**, since the entiredb path turns out to be open, so shared publication is closer than the PR bodies assume.\n\n# Roadmap corrections from this check\n- ~~\"shared publication blocked on entiredb reserved-ref unblock\"~~ — **stale.** ENT-1106 landed; `refs/meta/entire/*` has a registered workload writer and other `refs/meta/*` was never reserved. Both #74's and #85's bodies say otherwise and should be corrected.\n- **git-meta-service #1** — close as POC-superseded, don't merge.\n\n---\n\n**Shortest honest path:** reconcile the wire → merge #242 → merge #85 → run the round-trip. The reconciliation is the only real work left, and it's one decision away from being mechanical."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":858,"cache_read_input_tokens":696758,"output_tokens":1965,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":824},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":858,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1965,"cache_read_input_tokens":696758,"cache_creation_input_tokens":858,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":858},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011Ce8W3eqgueo41xHiu5Bz6","type":"assistant","uuid":"e12fbabb-1609-441b-8a23-a6443fedf388","timestamp":"2026-08-17T14:46:30.396Z","effort":"xhigh","se