{"parentUuid":"aac5de51-563b-4d74-8f0e-5871a3240c73","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Ce8ZLdD2yWaU6kk4qgjfX","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Final verification running (the 169s `internal/cli` package is the long pole). Watcher `bdjf7lo38` will report — then I commit and push to #85.\n\nProgress so far this round, all mutation-verified (each fix fails its test when reverted):\n\n**Bugs fixed — the three the reviewer left open, plus one I introduced myself:**\n1. **Silent data loss** — `distill --force` deleted sync-raised cross-member proposals on its final flush. Distill may only drop the proposals it *owns* (unattributed); attributed ones it never regenerates.\n2. **Unremovable orphans** — a proposal whose fact head is gone could be neither accepted nor rejected (the empty-head guard fired before the reject path). Split the guard; added a `FactsUnchanged` prune that CASes the proposal set only, guarded so it can never let an accept skip its fact write.\n3. **Cross-clone resurrection** — the shared ledger is per-checkout, so a second clone republished settled conflicts. Now derived from the shared head, which is identical for every clone.\n4. **A bug I introduced in the last round** — settled entries got pruned even when the head was unreadable, losing the settlement permanently. Now they stay queued until they can actually be mirrored.\n\n**Performance:** `Sync` already computes the post-sync head, so it now returns it — eliminating a full HTTP round-trip per `facts sync` against the hosted backend. Also stopped a needless fact-store write + manifest bump on a no-op reject.\n\n**Accuracy:** after `facts proposals apply`, the member's own local facts now reflect their decision immediately instead of staying stale until the next sync.\n\n**Audited and found sound (no change needed):** the privacy-purge and hosted-settle queue writers — both drop only what they should."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":190,"cache_read_input_tokens":758220,"output_tokens":848,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":256},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":190,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":848,"cache_read_input_tokens":758220,"cache_creation_input_tokens":190,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":190},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011Ce8ZLXRmbe71ZJT5PNymY","type":"assistant","uuid":"6c158e54-5c58-47f8-abfa-31debe91a617","timestamp":"2026-08-17T15:29:25.031Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"f507d58c-285f-4d11-b1d0-201f2a5e172d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/p0p1/p1-new","sessionId":"de272aad-c620-4d71-bbdd-27dd2d3dc8af","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"quizzical-sniffing-quasar"}
