{"parentUuid":"ec5cb810-ed8d-48cc-8f49-24975e46afae","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Ce8ZQCniDDVpxUudRW9tt","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Committing while the final suite finishes (push waits for green):"}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":188,"cache_read_input_tokens":759607,"output_tokens":1320,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":233},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":188,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1320,"cache_read_input_tokens":759607,"cache_creation_input_tokens":188,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":188},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011Ce8ZQ7gdVZUaUf1Qnw34u","type":"assistant","uuid":"ea42ff42-3f2c-42a3-82c9-4b9ecc3e0b76","timestamp":"2026-08-17T15:30:07.075Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"f507d58c-285f-4d11-b1d0-201f2a5e172d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/p0p1/p1-new","sessionId":"de272aad-c620-4d71-bbdd-27dd2d3dc8af","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"quizzical-sniffing-quasar"}
{"parentUuid":"ea42ff42-3f2c-42a3-82c9-4b9ecc3e0b76","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Ce8ZQCniDDVpxUudRW9tt","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01M8feqir5DHWTFAnufbX4Ac","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv/p0p1/p1-new\ngit add -A internal/\ngit commit -q -F - <<'EOF'\nfix(facts): close the proposal-queue lifecycle gaps and drop a sync round-trip\n\nFive defects, each with a test that fails when the fix is reverted.\n\ndistill --force silently deleted cross-member conflicts. The final flush dropped\nthe WHOLE local review queue. Dropping distill's own backlog is right — the rebuild\nregenerates it — but the queue is shared, and conflicts raised by `facts sync` are\nnever regenerated, so they vanished with no trace and no one could review them.\nOwnership is the ProposedBy attribution: distill's entries carry none, sync-raised\nones do. A force rebuild now drops only what it owns.\n\nAn orphaned proposal could not be removed. One whose fact head is gone entirely\ncannot be accepted, and reject was blocked too: the empty-head guard returned before\nthe reject path, and pushing an empty fact set is refused on purpose, so the entry\nsat in every member's open list forever. Reject changes no facts, so the write it\nneeds is the proposal set alone — expressed as FactsUnchanged, which CASes the set\nand leaves the head at factsOldRef. It is rejected outright when paired with accept,\nso it can never become a way to retire a proposal while dropping its merge result.\n\nSettled conflicts came back in a second clone. Publication was suppressed only by\nthe shared-proposal ledger, which lives in one checkout, so another clone of the same\nmember started empty and republished conflicts the team had already resolved. The\nshared head is identical for every clone and a settled conflict is no longer\napplicable to it, so applicability now gates publication regardless of ledger state.\n\nSettled entries could be pruned with nothing to mirror from. Introduced with the\nmirroring itself: with no readable head the entry was still dropped, leaving the\nretired fact active locally and no record left to reconcile it against — the same\ndefect the mirroring exists to close. Such entries now stay queued until they can\nactually be mirrored, and mirroring precedes the prune so a crash retries instead of\nlosing it.\n\nA member's own decision was invisible until their next sync. `facts proposals apply`\nadvanced the hosted head but left local facts stale, so the member who made the call\nkept seeing the pre-settlement state in their own recall. The settlement is now\nmirrored in the same write lock that prunes the local copy.\n\nPerformance: Sync already computes the post-sync fact set, so it returns it. Callers\nneeding the head — to check which proposals are still live, or to mirror settlements\n— use that instead of a second Current, removing a full network round-trip from every\nsync against a hosted backend. A no-op reject no longer rewrites the fact store or\nbumps the source manifest.\n\nAlso audited and left alone: the privacy-purge and hosted-settle queue writers, which\ncorrectly drop only proposals whose facts were deleted, or exactly the settled id.\nEOF\ngit log --oneline -2","description":"Commit all five fixes"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":188,"cache_read_input_tokens":759607,"output_tokens":1320,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":233},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":188,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1320,"cache_read_input_tokens":759607,"cache_creation_input_tokens":188,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":188},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011Ce8ZQ7gdVZUaUf1Qnw34u","type":"assistant","uuid":"eb23a765-1980-42d9-9f5e-27ab35199953","timestamp":"2026-08-17T15:30:20.005Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"f507d58c-285f-4d11-b1d0-201f2a5e172d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/p0p1/p1-new","sessionId":"de272aad-c620-4d71-bbdd-27dd2d3dc8af","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"quizzical-sniffing-quasar"}
