{"parentUuid":"26d7fd1d-ddfc-4d44-82b9-f0379c3ddd75","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Ce8ZtWoxEqC1z8YaR2TvC","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01CL3NWBgaFFmXLNcYB7NN6i","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv/p0p1/p1-new\ngit add internal/cli/brain_brief_git_intent_test.go\ngit commit -q -F - <<'EOF'\ntest(brief): stop the git-intent tests failing on a loaded machine\n\nBoth assertions were sensitive to machine load rather than to the behavior they\ncheck, and one of them failed a full-suite run alongside a -race run on correct code.\n\nThe live operational-recall table drives REAL git through ExecRunner, and the overlay\nis bounded by brainBriefGitIntentTimeout (500 ms) on purpose — it degrades to the\nbaseline instead of letting a slow repo stall a brief. Under load the two git calls\ncan miss that window, so the overlay correctly returns false and a good implementation\nfails the \"did not activate\" assertion. Retry a bounded five times: a single lost\nwindow is absorbed, while an overlay that is actually broken never activates on any\nattempt and still fails (verified by stubbing the promoter to return false).\n\nThe hard-timeout case allowed the 500 ms timeout plus 500 ms of slack, putting the\nwhole budget at 1 s. The claim under test is that the timeout BOUNDS the call, and the\nrunner blocks on ctx.Done(), so a broken bound does not return late — it never returns\n(the package timeout catches that) or waits a wall clock wildly larger than this one.\nSlack therefore only has to exclude that, not measure scheduler wake-up latency.\nEOF\ngit log --oneline -3\necho \"=== FINAL verification (nothing else running) ===\"\n{\necho \"gofmt -s: [$(gofmt -s -l internal/ cmd/ 2>/dev/null | tr '\\n' ' ')]\"\necho \"vet: $(go vet ./... 2>&1|head -2)OK\"\necho \"win: $(GOOS=windows GOARCH=amd64 go build ./... 2>&1|head -1)OK\"\ngo test ./... -count=1 2>&1 | grep -E \"^(ok|FAIL|---)\"\necho \"FINALDONE\"\n} > /tmp/fv2.txt 2>&1\ntail -14 /tmp/fv2.txt","description":"Commit flake fixes and final verify","run_in_background":true},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1195,"cache_read_input_tokens":778926,"output_tokens":856,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1195,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":856,"cache_read_input_tokens":778926,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1195,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1195},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011Ce8ZtPrW27mD1Mzetbfna","type":"assistant","uuid":"b947f2be-5ce5-43dd-8b07-ad51656489b2","timestamp":"2026-08-17T15:36:35.984Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"f507d58c-285f-4d11-b1d0-201f2a5e172d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/p0p1/p1-new","sessionId":"de272aad-c620-4d71-bbdd-27dd2d3dc8af","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"quizzical-sniffing-quasar"}
