{"parentUuid":"ec58fc35-f9c1-42e0-8453-c4d8ab17a445","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Ce8aMWvQSjtLFZUc4Es4R","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Pushed. Documenting it on the PR:"}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1035,"cache_read_input_tokens":782803,"output_tokens":1846,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1035,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1846,"cache_read_input_tokens":782803,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1035,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1035},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011Ce8aMNGkQimC869E9UzQm","type":"assistant","uuid":"9554c67a-5f2a-4314-bd87-7d36135f661d","timestamp":"2026-08-17T15:42:33.510Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"f507d58c-285f-4d11-b1d0-201f2a5e172d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/p0p1/p1-new","sessionId":"de272aad-c620-4d71-bbdd-27dd2d3dc8af","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"quizzical-sniffing-quasar"}
{"parentUuid":"9554c67a-5f2a-4314-bd87-7d36135f661d","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Ce8aMWvQSjtLFZUc4Es4R","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01HbckKr7CoJiT72bDEBbJ7o","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv/p0p1/p1-new\ngh pr comment 85 --repo entireio/entire-brain --body 'Pushed `c7ce1b19` + `f59c760d`. This closes the three review items that were left open by design, fixes a defect I introduced in the previous round, removes a per-sync network round-trip, and de-flakes two load-sensitive brief tests. Every fix has a test that fails when the fix is reverted.\n\n## Review items 3, 4 and 5 — now closed\n\n**4. `distill --force` silently deleted cross-member conflicts.** The final flush dropped the *whole* local review queue. Dropping distill'\"'\"'s own backlog is right — the rebuild regenerates it — but the queue is shared, and conflicts raised by `facts sync` are never regenerated, so they vanished with no trace and nobody could review them. Ownership is the `ProposedBy` attribution (the same rule the publish filter already uses): distill'\"'\"'s entries carry none, sync-raised ones do. A force rebuild now drops only what it owns.\n\n**5. An orphaned proposal could not be removed.** One whose fact head is gone entirely cannot be accepted, and reject was blocked too: the empty-head guard returned before the reject path, and pushing an empty fact set is refused on purpose. Reject changes no facts, so the write it actually needs is the proposal set alone — expressed as `FactsUnchanged`, which CASes the set and leaves the head at `factsOldRef`. Pairing it with accept is refused outright, so it can never become a way to retire a proposal while dropping its merge result.\n\n**3. Settled conflicts came back in a second clone.** Publication was suppressed only by the shared-proposal ledger, which lives in one checkout, so another clone of the same member started empty and republished conflicts the team had already resolved. This did not need the server-side tombstone the review suggested: the shared head is identical for every clone, and a settled conflict is no longer *applicable* to it, so applicability now gates publication regardless of ledger state.\n\n## A defect I introduced in the previous round\n\nMirroring settlements created a way to lose them. With no readable shared head there is nothing to mirror *from*, yet the settled entry was still pruned — leaving the retired fact active locally with no record left to reconcile it against, reintroducing the exact defect the mirroring exists to close. Such entries now stay queued until they can actually be mirrored, and mirroring precedes the prune so a crash retries instead of losing it.\n\n## Performance\n\n`Sync` already computes the post-sync fact set, so it now returns it. Callers needing the head — to check which proposals are still live, or to mirror settlements — use that instead of a second `Current`, **removing a full network round-trip from every sync against a hosted backend**. A no-op reject also no longer rewrites the fact store or bumps the source manifest.\n\n## Accuracy\n\nAfter `facts proposals apply`, the member'\"'\"'s own local facts now reflect their decision immediately, in the same write lock that prunes the local copy. Previously the member who made the call kept seeing the pre-settlement state in their own recall until their next sync.\n\n## Two load-sensitive brief tests\n\n`TestBrainBriefGitIntentLiveShapedOperationalRecall` failed a full-suite run alongside a `-race` run **on correct code**. It drives real git through `ExecRunner`, and the overlay is bounded at 500 ms on purpose — it degrades to the baseline rather than letting a slow repo stall a brief. Under load the two git calls miss that window, the overlay correctly returns false, and the assertion that it *must* activate fails. Now retried a bounded five times; verified it still catches real breakage by stubbing the promoter to return false. The hard-timeout case budgeted `timeout + 500 ms` = 1 s total; since the runner blocks on `ctx.Done()` a broken bound never returns at all rather than returning late, so the slack only has to exclude that.\n\nWorth stating plainly: that 500 ms bound means the git-intent overlay also stops contributing on a loaded machine **in production**, not only in tests. The code comment shows it is a deliberate trade, so I have left the product behavior alone rather than trading latency for it uninvited.\n\n## Audited, no change needed\n\nThe privacy-purge and hosted-settle queue writers both drop only what they should — proposals whose facts were deleted, and exactly the settled id.\n\n## Verification\n\n`gofmt -s`, `go vet ./...`, `GOOS=windows GOARCH=amd64 go build ./...` clean; `go test ./...` green across all 9 packages; `-race` clean on `factsync`, `factmerge`, `brainwire`, `hostedbrain`, `factgitmeta`.\n\n## Correction to this PR'\"'\"'s description\n\nThe body says shared publication is blocked on an entiredb reserved-ref unblock. **That is stale.** `refs/meta/entire/*` has a registered workload writer (`WorkloadEntireAPI`, ENT-1106) and `server/githttp/receive_pack.go` states other `refs/meta/*` paths were never reserved — \"standard git-meta clients can push them directly\". Nothing in entiredb blocks this any more.' 2>&1 | tail -2","description":"Comment all fixes on PR 85"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1035,"cache_read_input_tokens":782803,"output_tokens":1846,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1035,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1846,"cache_read_input_tokens":782803,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1035,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1035},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011Ce8aMNGkQimC869E9UzQm","type":"assistant","uuid":"f9e3ea1f-9f55-4e80-a3e3-790213e0f37d","timestamp":"2026-08-17T15:42:53.767Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"f507d58c-285f-4d11-b1d0-201f2a5e172d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/p0p1/p1-new","sessionId":"de272aad-c620-4d71-bbdd-27dd2d3dc8af","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"quizzical-sniffing-quasar"}
