{"parentUuid":"77447216-a8df-4c78-92ac-9c6e55163574","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Ce8aPTDxc2b5QFzN5NdSb","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01HTHN3KeWtwofP4Nn68wM4x","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv/p0p1/p1-new\nuntil [ \"$(gh pr checks 85 --repo entireio/entire-brain 2>&1 | grep -c pending)\" = \"0\" ]; do sleep 30; done\necho \"=== PR #85 final CI ===\"\ngh pr checks 85 --repo entireio/entire-brain 2>&1 | awk -F'\\t' '{print $2}' | sort | uniq -c | tr '\\n' ' '; echo\ngh pr checks 85 --repo entireio/entire-brain 2>&1 | grep -viE \"\tpass|skipping\" | head -5\ngh pr view 85 --repo entireio/entire-brain --json mergeable,mergeStateStatus --jq '\"\\(.mergeable)/\\(.mergeStateStatus)\"'","description":"Wait for PR 85 CI to go green","run_in_background":true},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1906,"cache_read_input_tokens":783838,"output_tokens":381,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1906,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":381,"cache_read_input_tokens":783838,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1906,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1906},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011Ce8aPL3N3wzFA8BGLbM2N","type":"assistant","uuid":"6809fab1-9c6c-4773-99b8-77aee3862531","timestamp":"2026-08-17T15:43:03.520Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"f507d58c-285f-4d11-b1d0-201f2a5e172d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/p0p1/p1-new","sessionId":"de272aad-c620-4d71-bbdd-27dd2d3dc8af","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"quizzical-sniffing-quasar"}
{"parentUuid":"6809fab1-9c6c-4773-99b8-77aee3862531","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"6ea7d3a7-d6de-4754-be59-1e6360a418a8","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HTHN3KeWtwofP4Nn68wM4x","type":"tool_result","content":"Command running in background with ID: b7o9fvnak. Output is being written to: /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-suhaan-devenv/f507d58c-285f-4d11-b1d0-201f2a5e172d/tasks/b7o9fvnak.output. You will be notified when it completes. To check interim output, use Read on that file path.\nSession cwd remains /Users/suhaan/devenv/p0p1/p1-new; directory changes made by the backgrounded command do not apply to subsequent commands.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"abb33ca6-1620-405d-8e32-66c2f5e93f03","timestamp":"2026-08-17T15:43:03.548Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"backgroundTaskId":"b7o9fvnak","backgroundCwdHint":"Session cwd remains /Users/suhaan/devenv/p0p1/p1-new; directory changes made by the backgrounded command do not apply to subsequent commands."},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"6809fab1-9c6c-4773-99b8-77aee3862531","session_id":"f507d58c-285f-4d11-b1d0-201f2a5e172d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/p0p1/p1-new","sessionId":"de272aad-c620-4d71-bbdd-27dd2d3dc8af","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"quizzical-sniffing-quasar"}
{"parentUuid":"abb33ca6-1620-405d-8e32-66c2f5e93f03","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"total_tokens_reminder","text":"<total_tokens>14907055 tokens left</total_tokens>"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"2421d8b6-34a0-45bc-88a1-0c47995e4196","timestamp":"2026-08-17T15:43:03.576Z","session_id":"f507d58c-285f-4d11-b1d0-201f2a5e172d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/p0p1/p1-new","sessionId":"de272aad-c620-4d71-bbdd-27dd2d3dc8af","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"quizzical-sniffing-quasar"}
{"parentUuid":"2421d8b6-34a0-45bc-88a1-0c47995e4196","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Ce8aQ5exJ7jEwDjXRKnoN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Everything is on **#85** (`+7,065/−27`, 22 files). Waiting on CI to confirm green.\n\n## What landed\n\n**The three review items left open — closed:**\n- **`distill --force` silently deleted cross-member conflicts.** It dropped the whole shared queue; distill may only drop what it *owns* (unattributed entries). Sync-raised ones it never regenerates, so they vanished unreviewed.\n- **Orphaned proposals were unremovable.** Couldn't be accepted (no head) and couldn't be rejected either (the guard fired first). Reject changes no facts, so it now writes only the proposal set via `FactsUnchanged` — refused outright if paired with accept.\n- **Settled conflicts resurrected in a second clone.** This *didn't* need the server-side tombstone the review proposed: the shared head is identical across clones and a settled conflict is no longer applicable to it, so applicability gates publication regardless of the per-checkout ledger.\n\n**A defect I introduced last round:** mirroring created a way to *lose* settlements — with no readable head there's nothing to mirror from, yet the entry was still pruned. Entries now stay queued until they can actually be mirrored.\n\n**Performance:** `Sync` already computes the post-sync head, so it returns it — **removing a full network round-trip from every hosted sync.** Plus no more pointless fact-store write on a no-op reject.\n\n**Accuracy:** `facts proposals apply` now mirrors into the member's own facts immediately, instead of leaving their recall contradicting the decision they just made until the next sync.\n\n## Two things I'd want you to see\n\n**A test failed my verification on correct code, and the root cause is a real product characteristic.** The git-intent overlay is bounded at 500ms by design; under load real git misses that window, the overlay correctly degrades, and a test requiring activation fails. I fixed the test with a bounded retry (and proved it still catches real breakage by stubbing the promoter false) — but **that same bound means the overlay silently stops contributing to retrieval on a loaded machine in production too.** The comment shows it's a deliberate latency trade, so I left the product behavior alone rather than changing it uninvited.\n\n**#85's own description is now wrong.** It claims shared publication is blocked on an entiredb reserved-ref unblock. That's stale — `WorkloadEntireAPI` is registered (ENT-1106) and other `refs/meta/*` paths were never reserved. Corrected in the comment.\n\nEvery fix is mutation-verified: reverting it fails its test. Full suite green across all 9 packages, `-race` clean, Windows cross-build clean.\n\nThe remaining P1 blocker is unchanged and not in brain: **#242's wire disagreement with this client** (paths, settle model, and 16-vs-64-hex proposal ids)."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":582,"cache_read_input_tokens":785744,"output_tokens":938,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":582,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":938,"cache_read_input_tokens":785744,"cache_creation_input_tokens":582,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":582},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011Ce8aPy1MUKTwG8GE48Snk","type":"assistant","uuid":"b926d5b2-1522-4fe3-9d8c-0c9203c81f69","timestamp":"2026-08-17T15:43:20.020Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"f507d58c-285f-4d11-b1d0-201f2a5e172d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/p0p1/p1-new","