{"parentUuid":"65aa3204-a5c3-4112-a4e6-93000d313293","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Ce8aiDzkiif5b6BerzhR4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Confirmed — and this is the **same bug class the reviewer already fixed for duplicate keys**, via a different vector. Two failures:\n\n1. **Fixed point breaks**: the bytes path keeps unknown fields, the struct path drops them → a signature made via one won't verify via the other.\n2. **Field smuggling**: a producer attaches extra fields, the signature covers them, but a verifier decoding into the struct never sees them and still validates. Two implementations disagree on content while both call the signature good.\n\nRejecting is also the precedent already set for the integer bound. Fixing:"}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1424,"cache_read_input_tokens":793984,"output_tokens":1832,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":748},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1424,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1832,"cache_read_input_tokens":793984,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1424,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1424},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011Ce8ai5kAiQR84o92Twtrg","type":"assistant","uuid":"aec88cb1-d4e5-4007-a459-7b6041cc5287","timestamp":"2026-08-17T15:47:26.755Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"f507d58c-285f-4d11-b1d0-201f2a5e172d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/p0p1/p1-new","sessionId":"de272aad-c620-4d71-bbdd-27dd2d3dc8af","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"quizzical-sniffing-quasar"}
{"parentUuid":"aec88cb1-d4e5-4007-a459-7b6041cc5287","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Ce8aiDzkiif5b6BerzhR4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01AEfNYpgFw3qKh4nfX5Lucm","name":"Edit","input":{"replace_all":false,"file_path":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/p0p1/p1-new/internal/brainwire/canonical.go","old_string":"\t// Unknown (newer-minor) fields pass through; only their encoding is\n\t// canonicalized, by encodeValue.\n\tfor k, v := range in {\n\t\tif _, ok := known[k]; ok {\n\t\t\tcontinue\n\t\t}\n\t\tout[k] = v\n\t}\n\treturn out, nil\n}","new_string":"\t// Unknown fields are REJECTED, not passed through. Canonical form exists only to\n\t// be signed and verified, and a field the contract cannot represent must never sit\n\t// inside signed bytes:\n\t//\n\t//   - It breaks the fixed point. Canonicalize keeps such a field, while the struct\n\t//     path (CanonicalUnmarshal then CanonicalMarshal) drops it, so the two produce\n\t//     different bytes for one logical artifact and a signature made through one\n\t//     will not verify through the other.\n\t//   - It allows field smuggling. A producer attaches extra keys, the signature\n\t//     covers them, and a verifier that decodes into BrainArtifact never sees them\n\t//     yet still validates — two implementations disagreeing about the content while\n\t//     both consider the signature good. That is the same confusion class as the\n\t//     duplicate-member rejection above, reached by a different route.\n\t//\n\t// Forward compatibility for READING newer minors is a separate concern, served by\n\t// the tolerant decode path and CheckCompatibility; canonicalization is not that\n\t// path. Per ADR 0001 the 1.x major is additive-only, and a minor that adds a field\n\t// must ship a new Signature.CanonicalEncoding identifier — the same rule the\n\t// integer bound already follows — rather than have old verifiers silently sign\n\t// bytes they cannot interpret.\n\tif len(in) != len(known) {\n\t\tunknown := make([]string, 0, len(in))\n\t\tfor k := range in {\n\t\t\tif _, ok := known[k]; !ok {\n\t\t\t\tunknown = append(unknown, k)\n\t\t\t}\n\t\t}\n\t\tif len(unknown) > 0 {\n\t\t\tsort.Strings(unknown)\n\t\t\treturn nil, fmt.Errorf(\"brainwire: %s: unknown field(s) %v are not part of the canonical encoding; a newer minor must ship a new canonical-encoding identifier\", t.Name, unknown)\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\treturn out, nil\n}"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1424,"cache_read_input_tokens":793984,"output_tokens":1832,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":748},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1424,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1832,"cache_read_input_tokens":793984,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1424,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1424},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011Ce8ai5kAiQR84o92Twtrg","type":"assistant","uuid":"0ca02e0e-4eb7-473d-a3e2-734327835e82","timestamp":"2026-08-17T15:47:35.930Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"f507d58c-285f-4d11-b1d0-201f2a5e172d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/p0p1/p1-new","sessionId":"de272aad-c620-4d71-bbdd-27dd2d3dc8af","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"quizzical-sniffing-quasar"}
