{"parentUuid":"546752c5-0898-46c6-a3a2-0b94e12fd558","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Ce8bCTJyhdRozDJYKyo6p","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"6.2M tamper executions, no failures. Committing the fuzz coverage and the corrected invariant documentation:"}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":540,"cache_read_input_tokens":811015,"output_tokens":1258,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":326},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":540,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1258,"cache_read_input_tokens":811015,"cache_creation_input_tokens":540,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":540},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011Ce8bCHPgPvdrrug1mHdwJ","type":"assistant","uuid":"7d44d854-4520-467e-a1c7-a28e03cea5df","timestamp":"2026-08-17T15:53:42.419Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"f507d58c-285f-4d11-b1d0-201f2a5e172d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/p0p1/p1-new","sessionId":"de272aad-c620-4d71-bbdd-27dd2d3dc8af","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"quizzical-sniffing-quasar"}
{"parentUuid":"7d44d854-4520-467e-a1c7-a28e03cea5df","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Ce8bCTJyhdRozDJYKyo6p","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01G1PhDzy5Ke9W7fVj9X1nUu","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv/p0p1/p1-new\ngofmt -s -l internal/ cmd/ | head -3\ngo vet ./internal/brainwire/ 2>&1 | head -3\ngit add internal/brainwire/\ngit commit -q -F - <<'EOF'\ntest(brainwire): fuzz the canonical encoding and the signature\n\nThree property-based targets over the wire format, ~12M executions with no defect\nfound. They pin the invariants the signing scheme depends on, which unit tests can\nonly sample:\n\n  FuzzCanonicalizeIdempotent    canonical form is a fixed point, and every accepted\n                                output is itself acceptable and valid UTF-8 — so the\n                                encoder can never emit bytes its own decoder rejects\n  FuzzCanonicalMarshalRoundTrip the struct path and the bytes path agree, so a\n                                signature made through one verifies through the other\n  FuzzVerifyRejectsTamper       a signature verifies those bytes and nothing else:\n                                any single-byte mutation, stripped field or appended\n                                trailing data is rejected, by error and never a panic\n\nThe round-trip target is deliberately scoped to artifacts whose keys are all known,\nand the reason is now written down where it will be read. Unknown newer-minor fields\npass through canonicalization ON PURPOSE — ADR 0001 makes 1.x additive-only, so an\nolder verifier has to be able to canonicalize and verify a newer producer's artifact,\nand a fatal unknown key would break exactly that. The struct cannot represent such a\nfield, so re-marshaling necessarily drops it; asserting round-trip equality over those\ninputs would be asserting that tolerance is a bug.\n\nI first read the pass-through as a canonicalization flaw and changed it to reject,\nwhich broke three tests including TestVerifyBytesToleratesUnknownFields. That test\nanswers the concern: the signature is taken over the bytes INCLUDING the unknown\nfields, so an older reader can neither add nor strip what it does not understand and\nstill validate. The behavior was right; the missing piece was a comment saying why,\nand a test scoped to the property that actually holds.\nEOF\ngit push entireio HEAD:feat/p1-canonical-signing-proposals --quiet 2>&1 | tail -1\ngit log --oneline -1\necho \"=== corpus files generated by fuzzing (should NOT be committed) ===\"\ngit status --short | head -5","description":"Commit and push fuzz coverage"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":540,"cache_read_input_tokens":811015,"output_tokens":1258,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":326},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":540,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1258,"cache_read_input_tokens":811015,"cache_creation_input_tokens":540,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":540},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011Ce8bCHPgPvdrrug1mHdwJ","type":"assistant","uuid":"317bdaa5-fa53-4c9d-9f2a-e8e89c9bdcae","timestamp":"2026-08-17T15:53:53.214Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"f507d58c-285f-4d11-b1d0-201f2a5e172d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/p0p1/p1-new","sessionId":"de272aad-c620-4d71-bbdd-27dd2d3dc8af","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"quizzical-sniffing-quasar"}
