{"parentUuid":"dfb91bc9-462c-4b74-9d47-e9208bb964b7","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Ce8bRA6FMNQ58jUFaTGPj","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01RAHoNTVtEHUJAUBmevxKB3","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv/p0p1/p1-new\ngit add internal/factgitmeta/\ngit commit -q -F - <<'EOF'\ndocs(factgitmeta): point the vendored engine at its real upstream\n\nEvery file in the vendored git-meta engine named github.com/entirehq/git-meta-service\nas its source. That repository was a proof of concept and its PR was superseded rather\nthan merged; the shipping implementation now lives in entire-api internal/gitmeta. As\nwritten, the header sends the next person to re-vendor from a dead branch.\n\nRecord where it actually lives, and what has happened since. The two copies have\ndiverged in both directions — entire-api grew path-target support (PathTargetSubtree,\nValidatePathTargetValue) and typed accessors, while this copy carries helpers of its own\nand the older ValidateTargetValue name.\n\nThat divergence is inert today, and the header now says why rather than leaving the\nreader to work it out: this engine only drives the bare LOCAL store at\nrefs/meta/local/main, with no remote, no push or fetch, and no ref entire-api also\nwrites, so no record crosses between the two implementations. It stops being inert as\nsoon as brain exchanges git-meta records with entire-api over a shared ref. Both are\ninternal packages, so neither can import the other and a real dedupe means extracting\nthe engine into a shared module — which is the follow-up the original note gestured at\nwithout saying what it required.\nEOF\ngit push entireio HEAD:feat/p1-canonical-signing-proposals --quiet 2>&1 | tail -1\ngit log --oneline -1\ncat /tmp/fv3.txt 2>/dev/null | tail -14","description":"Commit provenance fix and check verify"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":920,"cache_read_input_tokens":816950,"output_tokens":634,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":920,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":634,"cache_read_input_tokens":816950,"cache_creation_input_tokens":920,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":920},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011Ce8bR1UaXSVVDNPvB6NCo","type":"assistant","uuid":"2a87a9e6-6e1c-4689-b8bb-0c4adf635eab","timestamp":"2026-08-17T15:56:35.618Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"f507d58c-285f-4d11-b1d0-201f2a5e172d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/p0p1/p1-new","sessionId":"de272aad-c620-4d71-bbdd-27dd2d3dc8af","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"quizzical-sniffing-quasar"}
