{"parentUuid":"3eb2332e-2aca-46e9-acb6-a6df049d0651","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"total_tokens_reminder","text":"<total_tokens>14965883 tokens left</total_tokens>"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"f2405c3c-dc2b-4ce7-8b8a-9a4f42092f24","timestamp":"2026-08-17T15:58:27.645Z","session_id":"f507d58c-285f-4d11-b1d0-201f2a5e172d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/p0p1/p1-new","sessionId":"de272aad-c620-4d71-bbdd-27dd2d3dc8af","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"quizzical-sniffing-quasar"}
{"parentUuid":"f2405c3c-dc2b-4ce7-8b8a-9a4f42092f24","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Ce8baEtENA4L3B5KDr3ma","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Everything's on **#85** now. Local suite fully green; waiting on CI for the last two pushes.\n\n## This round\n\n**Fuzzed the wire format** — 12M+ executions across three property targets, since a byte-level codec used for signing is exactly where sampling-based unit tests miss things:\n- canonical form is a **fixed point**, and every accepted output is re-acceptable and valid UTF-8\n- the **struct path and bytes path agree**, so a signature made through one verifies through the other\n- a signature verifies those bytes and **nothing else** — any flipped byte, stripped field, or appended data is rejected by error, never a panic\n\nNo defects found. That's a real result for code that had none of this coverage.\n\n**I was wrong about a bug, and reverted myself.** My round-trip fuzzer flagged that `Canonicalize` passes unknown fields through while the struct path drops them. I read that as a canonicalization flaw plus a smuggling vector and changed it to reject — which broke three tests, one named `TestVerifyBytesToleratesUnknownFields`. That test answers the concern directly: the signature covers the unknown fields, so an older reader can neither add nor strip what it doesn't understand and still validate. The pass-through is **load-bearing** for ADR 0001's additive-only 1.x — a fatal unknown key would stop an older verifier validating a newer producer's artifact.\n\nSo I reverted, scoped my fuzzer to the property that actually holds, and wrote the reasoning into the code — the missing piece was never behavior, it was a comment explaining why.\n\n**Fixed a documentation defect with teeth:** all 10 vendored `gitmeta` files named the *proof-of-concept* repo as their upstream. That PR was superseded, not merged; the shipping engine is in entire-api. As written it would send the next person to re-vendor from a dead branch. The header now records the real source, the two-way divergence since (api grew path-target support), and why it's currently inert — brain's engine only drives the bare local store at `refs/meta/local/main`, with no ref entire-api also writes.\n\n**Verified inert, not assumed:** I checked for remotes/push/fetch in `factgitmeta` before calling the drift harmless."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":668,"cache_read_input_tokens":820914,"output_tokens":731,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":668,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":731,"cache_read_input_tokens":820914,"cache_creation_input_tokens":668,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":668},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011Ce8ba5yhT3TLNn3WqRC7U","type":"assistant","uuid":"fd2e0a3e-1fce-4499-be13-24718a3b5a0f","timestamp":"2026-08-17T15:58:44.576Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"f507d58c-285f-4d11-b1d0-201f2a5e172d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/p0p1/p1-new","sessionId":"de272aad-c620-4d71-bbdd-27dd2d3dc8af","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"quizzical-sniffing-quasar"}
