{"type":"pr-link","sessionId":"de272aad-c620-4d71-bbdd-27dd2d3dc8af","prNumber":85,"prUrl":"https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/85","prRepository":"entireio/entire-brain","timestamp":"2026-08-17T16:21:32.023Z"}
{"parentUuid":"d95a6dbf-033d-449b-8f84-2ac427d0fac9","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Ce8dLMGJEQhN7e3HRrauH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# entire-brain P1 is clean and ready — #85 is `MERGEABLE/CLEAN`, CI 15/15\n\n`+7,463/−57` across 33 files. Every fix is mutation-verified: revert it and its test fails.\n\n## Bugs fixed\n| | |\n|---|---|\n| **Silent data loss** | `distill --force` deleted sync-raised cross-member conflicts it can never regenerate |\n| **Unremovable orphans** | a proposal with no fact head could be neither accepted nor rejected — stuck in every member's list forever |\n| **Cross-clone resurrection** | a second clone republished conflicts the team had already settled |\n| **Lost settlements** | *(mine, from the prior round)* entries were pruned even when there was nothing to mirror from |\n\n## Performance\n`Sync` already computes the post-sync head, so it returns it — **removing a full network round-trip from every hosted sync**. Plus no more needless fact-store write on a no-op reject.\n\n## Accuracy\n`facts proposals apply` now mirrors into the member's own facts immediately, instead of leaving their recall contradicting the decision they just made.\n\n## Robustness\nThree fuzz targets over the wire format, **12M+ executions**, no defects — fixed-point, struct/bytes agreement, and tamper rejection. Plus two load-sensitive brief tests de-flaked (one had failed my own verification on correct code).\n\n## Two things I'd want you to read\n**I was wrong once and reverted myself.** I read `Canonicalize`'s unknown-field pass-through as a flaw and made it reject — breaking `TestVerifyBytesToleratesUnknownFields`, which exists precisely to pin that behavior. The signature already covers unknown fields, so nothing can be smuggled or stripped, and the pass-through is what lets an older verifier validate a newer producer under ADR 0001. Behavior was right; the missing piece was a comment saying why, which I added.\n\n**A latent trap defused:** all 10 vendored `gitmeta` files cited the *proof-of-concept* repo as upstream. That PR was superseded, not merged — the real engine is in entire-api. Anyone re-vendoring would have pulled from a dead branch. Header now records the true source, the two-way drift since, and why it's inert today (verified: local-only store, no remote, no shared ref).\n\n## Left deliberately alone, flagged not hidden\nThe git-intent overlay's 500ms bound means it **also stops contributing to retrieval on a loaded machine in production** — the code shows that's a deliberate latency trade, so I didn't change product behavior uninvited.\n\n**Remaining P1 blocker is unchanged and not in brain:** #242's wire disagreement with this client — paths, settle model, and 16-vs-64-hex proposal ids."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":979,"cache_read_input_tokens":822910,"output_tokens":934,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":979,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":934,"cache_read_input_tokens":822910,"cache_creation_input_tokens":979,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":979},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011Ce8dL9aau98Zrfj2abZfN","type":"assistant","uuid":"cf299b1f-11dd-44fe-b4c2-1345ecb99c54","timestamp":"2026-08-17T16:21:49.661Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"f507d58c-285f-4d11-b1d0-201f2a5e172d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/p0p1/p1-new","sessionId":"de272aad-c620-4d71-bbdd-27dd2d3dc8af","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"quizzical-sniffing-quasar"}
{"parentUuid":"cf299b1f-11dd-44fe-b4c2-1345ecb99c54","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"goal_status","met":true,"condition":"fix all bugs and rpoblems and slowign down and accorchay in engite brain make it a clean ready p1 add all changes to pr 85","reason":"entire-brain #85 is MERGEABLE/CLEAN with CI 15/15 passing, containing +7,463/-57 across 33 files. Fixed bugs: (1) silent data loss in `distill --force` deleting sync-raised conflicts, (2) unremovable orphaned proposals, (3) cross-clone resurrection of settled conflicts, (4) lost settlements from unavailable heads. Performance: removed per-sync network round-trip by returning computed head from Sync(). Accuracy: facts proposals apply now mirrors immediately. Robustness: 12M+ fuzz executions on wire format with no defects found. Every fix is mutation-verified. All changes pushed to PR #85 per condition.","iterations":1,"durationMs":3972099,"tokens":84217},"type":"attachment","uuid":"8cf37e31-9f66-494a-bce8-b7ffe26a1f6c","timestamp":"2026-08-17T16:21:57.237Z","session_id":"f507d58c-285f-4d11-b1d0-201f2a5e172d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/p0p1/p1-new","sessionId":"de272aad-c620-4d71-bbdd-27dd2d3dc8af","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"quizzical-sniffing-quasar"}
