{"parentUuid":"bc7acc07-064d-42a3-8454-d78f69fa71a7","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"008251ba-5894-4079-a812-8e401d59a62b","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BktH2QkM14b6tNCFxagPvB","type":"tool_result","content":"=== what repo-not-found error does the facts handler map? ===\n91:\t\t\treturn nil, huma.Error404NotFound(\"repo not found\")\n160:\t\treturn nil, huma.Error404NotFound(\"repo not found\")\n176:\tdeclareErrors(&currentOp, http.StatusNotFound)\n188:\tdeclareErrors(&advanceOp, http.StatusPreconditionFailed, http.StatusNotFound)","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"97a898db-4b09-4237-bb6e-701eab084047","timestamp":"2026-08-17T17:35:09.947Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"=== what repo-not-found error does the facts handler map? ===\n91:\t\t\treturn nil, huma.Error404NotFound(\"repo not found\")\n160:\t\treturn nil, huma.Error404NotFound(\"repo not found\")\n176:\tdeclareErrors(&currentOp, http.StatusNotFound)\n188:\tdeclareErrors(&advanceOp, http.StatusPreconditionFailed, http.StatusNotFound)","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"bc7acc07-064d-42a3-8454-d78f69fa71a7","session_id":"f507d58c-285f-4d11-b1d0-201f2a5e172d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/p0p1/api-242","sessionId":"de272aad-c620-4d71-bbdd-27dd2d3dc8af","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"quizzical-sniffing-quasar"}
{"parentUuid":"97a898db-4b09-4237-bb6e-701eab084047","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"nested_memory","path":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/p0p1/api-242/CLAUDE.md","content":{"path":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/p0p1/api-242/CLAUDE.md","type":"Project","content":"# entire-api — agent notes\n\nPer-jurisdiction Go service: HTTP API + two NATS workers (repo-activity,\nuser-activity) over two Postgres stores (`repo`, `usr` schemas). See\n[README.md](./README.md) for architecture and [CONTRIBUTING.md](./CONTRIBUTING.md)\nfor build/test.\n\n## Conventions an agent must not get wrong\n\n- **Database migrations use a UTC-timestamp version, never a hand-picked\n  integer.** Create them with `scripts/new-migration.sh <repo|user> <name>` →\n  `internal/store/migrations/<store>/YYYYMMDDHHMMSS_<name>.sql`. goose tracks by\n  the filename's version number and silently skips any version `≤` the current\n  DB version, so two PRs picking the same next integer (e.g. both `016_…`) make\n  one migration vanish with no error. Leave the existing `001…0NN` files as-is.\n  Full rationale: [CONTRIBUTING.md](./CONTRIBUTING.md#database-migrations).\n- **Never renumber or edit an already-merged migration** — add a new\n  (timestamped) one. They're applied in every environment.\n- **Run `mise run build`, `mise run vet`, `mise run lint` before pushing.**\n  Integration tests (`mise run test:integration`) need Docker and self-skip\n  without `ACTIVITY_TEST_DATABASE_URL`; plain `mise run test` stays unit-only.\n\n## Testing cross-cell behaviour\n\n`internal/multicellular` is the cross-jurisdiction suite — several real cells\n(embedded NATS + real Postgres each) driven over real transport; the only CI suite\nthat's cross-cell, real-transport, and real-store at once. See its README for the DSL.\n\nAdd or extend a scenario there when a change affects behaviour that only appears\nwhen ≥2 cells (placements) interact, or depends on an event crossing cells: activity\nforwarding (origin / `repo_group` keying, dedup, the `/me` pull gate), settings\nfan-out (`settingsrelay` / `settingsconsumer` / `mirrorlifecycle`), placement-\ndependent `/me` resolution, or any NATS consumer / cross-cell event / fan-out flag.\nSingle-cell behaviour stays in the `httpapi` / `store` / `test:pipeline` suites.\n\nNew scenarios: wire events only (`cell.Receives` / `cell.API` / `w.Settle`), and\nmutation-verify — revert the fix it guards and confirm it fails.\n","contentDiffersFromDisk":false},"displayPath":"CLAUDE.md"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"66ee7139-76e6-4be8-a1fc-d8be7ffcf2b0","timestamp":"2026-08-17T17:35:10.047Z","session_id":"f507d58c-285f-4d11-b1d0-201f2a5e172d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/p0p1/api-242","sessionId":"de272aad-c620-4d71-bbdd-27dd2d3dc8af","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"quizzical-sniffing-quasar"}
