{"parentUuid":"841887ab-6197-444d-81f9-e8d3be53750f","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Ce8jPYLqNTdkWEnEZRCYG","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All 5 contract cases pass. Committing and pushing the reconciliation:"}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3462,"cache_read_input_tokens":897690,"output_tokens":1176,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3462,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1176,"cache_read_input_tokens":897690,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3462,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3462},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011Ce8jPRECtyYv1pDLwDKii","type":"assistant","uuid":"ad8b6a7b-ed49-4969-b902-3fa5250d04eb","timestamp":"2026-08-17T17:41:01.826Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"f507d58c-285f-4d11-b1d0-201f2a5e172d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/p0p1/api-242","sessionId":"de272aad-c620-4d71-bbdd-27dd2d3dc8af","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"quizzical-sniffing-quasar"}
{"parentUuid":"ad8b6a7b-ed49-4969-b902-3fa5250d04eb","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Ce8jPYLqNTdkWEnEZRCYG","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01H2YPTL1cmikmi25ZonEkAx","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv/p0p1/api-242\ngo build ./... 2>&1|head -2\ngo vet ./internal/... 2>&1|head -2\ngo test ./internal/httpapi/ ./internal/brainbuild/... ./internal/brainstore/... ./internal/server/... -count=1 -short 2>&1 | grep -E \"^(ok|FAIL)\" | head -6\ngit add -A internal/ \ngit commit -q -F - <<'EOF'\nfix(brain): serve the open proposal set on the contract the client speaks\n\nThe two halves of P1 were built independently and disagreed on the wire in three\nways at once, so no proposal could be addressed across it: the paths differed\n(/brain/proposals vs the client's /brain/facts/proposals), the settle verb differed\n(apply + reject vs one resolve), and proposal identity differed outright — this side\nderived it from storage coordinates as 64 hex, the client derives it from the\nproposal's own fields as 16. Every unit test on both sides passed regardless, because\nnothing exercised the boundary.\n\nThis side moves, for three reasons. ADR-P1-E puts the merge on the runner, and\nProposalStore.Apply re-derived resolutions server-side — a second implementation of\nmerge logic, which is the divergence the wire contract exists to prevent. The client\nalready addresses the queue under the fact-set family, where it belongs: the open set\nIS the fact set's review queue, and this service already serves /brain/facts and\n/brain/facts/advance. And identity has to be single-sourced; only the client can\nderive it, since only the client knows the proposal's fields.\n\nThe queue is now one compare-and-swapped blob per branch instead of a row per\nproposal. The server never interprets an entry — it stores bytes and moves pointers —\nso a newer client can add proposal fields with no server change. That reuses the\nfact-set machinery wholesale: the same read-CAS-write store over its own ref index\n(brain_proposal_refs) and its own blob kind, so the two heads move and are\ncrypto-shredded independently. KindProposals exists precisely because sharing\nKindFacts would let the fact-head shred drop a live proposal blob's DEK, since no\nfact head references a proposal coordinate.\n\nresolve swaps both heads from the refs the runner read, facts first: losing the set\nCAS after advancing facts leaves the entry queued and the runner re-resolves\nidempotently, whereas the reverse order could drop the entry while the facts never\nmoved, losing the settlement. factsUnchanged settles the set alone, which is the only\nway an orphaned proposal — one whose facts are gone entirely — ever leaves the queue;\nit is refused with accept, where skipping the fact write would retire the proposal and\nsilently drop its merge result.\n\nThe row-queue table is replaced rather than migrated: #242 has not merged, so its\nmigration never shipped.\n\nAdds a wire-contract test fed the client's literal JSON. The two repos cannot import\neach other, so nothing else makes a rename or a retyped field fail a build — which is\nhow three incompatibilities survived this long.\nEOF\ngit push origin HEAD:m4-brain-auth --quiet 2>&1 | tail -2\ngit log --oneline -1","description":"Commit and push the api reconciliation"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3462,"cache_read_input_tokens":897690,"output_tokens":1176,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3462,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1176,"cache_read_input_tokens":897690,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3462,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3462},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011Ce8jPRECtyYv1pDLwDKii","type":"assistant","uuid":"726bd7c2-abe5-4f1b-80d6-8f0654dbb2af","timestamp":"2026-08-17T17:41:16.944Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"f507d58c-285f-4d11-b1d0-201f2a5e172d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/p0p1/api-242","sessionId":"de272aad-c620-4d71-bbdd-27dd2d3dc8af","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"quizzical-sniffing-quasar"}
