{"type":"pr-link","sessionId":"de272aad-c620-4d71-bbdd-27dd2d3dc8af","prNumber":242,"prUrl":"https://github.com/entirehq/entire-api/pull/242","prRepository":"entirehq/entire-api","timestamp":"2026-08-17T17:42:56.487Z"}
{"parentUuid":"b23950ae-6724-447c-af6a-b58e8a2c27a3","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Ce8jWoaZXxhxnoCFx1w2x","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01AbtCiQWEWxjnuvjvuhkoZY","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/devenv/p0p1/api-242\ngh pr comment 242 --repo entirehq/entire-api --body 'Pushed `6934692d` — the wire reconciliation. This side moves to the contract the brain client speaks, so the two halves of P1 can actually talk.\n\n## What was broken\n\nThree incompatibilities at once, and **every unit test on both sides passed** because nothing exercised the boundary:\n\n| | brain client | this side (before) |\n|---|---|---|\n| path | `/brain/facts/proposals` | `/brain/proposals` |\n| settle | `POST .../{id}/resolve` | `POST .../{id}/apply` + `/reject` |\n| proposal id | `sha256(action, candidate, target, branch, proposedBy)` → 16 hex | `sha256(branch, baseRef, contentRef)` → 64 hex |\n\nThe id divergence alone meant no proposal could ever be addressed across the wire.\n\n## Why this side moved\n\n1. **ADR-P1-E puts the merge on the runner.** `ProposalStore.Apply` re-derived resolutions server-side — a second implementation of merge logic, which is exactly the divergence the wire contract exists to prevent.\n2. **The queue belongs under the fact-set family.** The open set *is* the fact set’s review queue, and this service already serves `/brain/facts` and `/brain/facts/advance`.\n3. **Identity has to be single-sourced.** Only the client knows a proposal’s fields, so only the client can derive its id.\n\n## What changed\n\nThe queue is now **one compare-and-swapped blob per branch** rather than a row per proposal. The server never interprets an entry — it stores bytes and moves pointers — so a newer client can add proposal fields with no server change.\n\nThat reuses the fact-set machinery wholesale: the same read-CAS-write store over its own ref index (`brain_proposal_refs`) and its own blob kind. `KindProposals` exists precisely because sharing `KindFacts` would let the fact-head shred drop a **live proposal blob’s DEK**, since no fact head references a proposal coordinate.\n\n`resolve` swaps both heads from the refs the runner read, **facts first**: losing the set CAS after advancing facts leaves the entry queued and the runner re-resolves idempotently, whereas the reverse order could drop the entry while the facts never moved — losing the settlement outright.\n\n`factsUnchanged` settles the set alone. It is the only way an orphaned proposal — one whose facts are gone entirely — ever leaves the queue, and it is refused with `accept`, where skipping the fact write would retire the proposal while silently dropping its merge result.\n\nThe row-queue table is **replaced rather than migrated**: this PR has not merged, so its migration never shipped.\n\n## Guarding it\n\nAdded a wire-contract test fed the client’s **literal JSON**. The two repos cannot import each other, so nothing else makes a rename or a retyped field fail a build — which is how three incompatibilities survived this long. It covers the publish body, the resolve body, the orphan-prune variant, and both response envelopes.\n\nOne matching fix went to the client (entire-brain `c0ae25e6`): this service answers **503** when the hosted brain is disabled, but the client only treated 404/501 as an absent queue, so a brain-disabled deployment failed a sync whose facts had already landed instead of degrading to the local queue.\n\nVerification: `go build ./...`, `go vet ./internal/...`, `gofmt -s` clean; `httpapi`, `brainbuild`, `brainstore`, `brainquery`, `server` tests green, including `TestOpenAPITagCatalogInvariants`.\n\n**Still not verified end-to-end.** Both halves now agree on paper and the contract test pins the shapes, but the live cross-repo round-trip that #64 deferred has still never been run. That is the last thing standing between this and a P1 anyone should trust.' 2>&1 | tail -2","description":"Comment the reconciliation on 242"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":592,"cache_read_input_tokens":902539,"output_tokens":1399,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":592,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1399,"cache_read_input_tokens":902539,"cache_creation_input_tokens":592,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":592},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011Ce8jWfYsSyt2aTxqTxggE","type":"assistant","uuid":"db07d08d-b715-4e39-a992-66a9ae65d010","timestamp":"2026-08-17T17:42:55.367Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"f507d58c-285f-4d11-b1d0-201f2a5e172d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/p0p1/api-242","sessionId":"de272aad-c620-4d71-bbdd-27dd2d3dc8af","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"quizzical-sniffing-quasar"}
