{"parentUuid":"c5fc432b-a469-48a5-b75a-782e66c1d659","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"total_tokens_reminder","text":"<total_tokens>14925888 tokens left</total_tokens>"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"a8209d4a-392f-491b-81a6-91f83c377a96","timestamp":"2026-08-17T17:43:16.106Z","session_id":"f507d58c-285f-4d11-b1d0-201f2a5e172d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/p0p1/api-242","sessionId":"de272aad-c620-4d71-bbdd-27dd2d3dc8af","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"quizzical-sniffing-quasar"}
{"parentUuid":"a8209d4a-392f-491b-81a6-91f83c377a96","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Ce8jZshCHUEV1GFAtArH2","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# The wire is reconciled — both halves of P1 now speak the same contract\n\n## What #242 was actually broken on\nThree incompatibilities at once, and **every unit test on both sides passed**, because nothing exercised the boundary:\n\n| | brain client | api (before) |\n|---|---|---|\n| path | `/brain/facts/proposals` | `/brain/proposals` |\n| settle | `POST .../{id}/resolve` | `apply` + `reject` |\n| proposal id | 16-hex from the proposal's fields | 64-hex from storage coords |\n\n## The api side moved, and why\n`ProposalStore.Apply` was re-deriving resolutions server-side — **a second implementation of merge logic**, which is precisely the divergence ADR-P1-E (\"merge runs on the runner\") exists to prevent. The queue also belongs under `/brain/facts/*`, where this service already serves the head. And identity can only be derived by the side that knows the proposal's fields.\n\nSo the queue is now **one CAS'd blob per branch**, not a row per proposal. The server stores bytes and moves pointers; it never interprets an entry, so a newer client can add fields with no server change. It reuses the fact-set machinery over its own ref index and blob kind.\n\n## Two subtle things worth your eye\n**`KindProposals` isn't cosmetic.** Sharing `KindFacts` would let the fact-head crypto-shred **delete a live proposal blob's DEK**, because no fact head references a proposal coordinate.\n\n**`resolve` swaps facts first, deliberately.** Losing the set CAS after advancing facts leaves the entry queued and the runner re-resolves idempotently. The reverse order could drop the entry while facts never moved — losing the settlement outright.\n\n## Guarding the boundary\nAdded a **wire-contract test fed the client's literal JSON**. The repos can't import each other, so nothing else makes a rename fail a build — which is exactly how three incompatibilities survived. And cross-checking turned up one more real bug: api answers **503** when the brain is disabled, but the client only treated 404/501 as \"no queue\", so it failed a sync whose facts had already landed. Fixed client-side (`c0ae25e6`).\n\n## Where this leaves P1\n- **#85** — MERGEABLE, CI re-running on the new commit\n- **#242** — MERGEABLE/BLOCKED (needs approval), `+10,333/−2`, all brain tests green including the OpenAPI invariant\n\n**One honest gap remains, and I won't paper over it:** they agree *on paper*, and the contract test pins the shapes — but the **live cross-repo round-trip has still never been run.** That's what would have caught all four of these bugs, and it needs both services actually running. Until then P1 is \"reconciled and verified by contract\", not \"verified end to end\"."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":479,"cache_read_input_tokens":904590,"output_tokens":935,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":479,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":935,"cache_read_input_tokens":904590,"cache_creation_input_tokens":479,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":479},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011Ce8jZfCcW4eRAef4cEajd","type":"assistant","uuid":"bcd2da43-ef44-4825-b0c0-d76e798aa39e","timestamp":"2026-08-17T17:43:33.933Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"f507d58c-285f-4d11-b1d0-201f2a5e172d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/p0p1/api-242","sessionId":"de272aad-c620-4d71-bbdd-27dd2d3dc8af","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"quizzical-sniff