{"parentUuid":"5e4299a0-0b28-4ce2-b8eb-b178c20b491e","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CeAPkRLRRs5oYPst3HTys","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Got it — **\"Semantic Reasoning Layer — Roadmap\"** (suhaan@entire.io, last modified 2026-07-10, \"As of July 2026\"). Read in full, and cross-checked against the live repos.\n\n# P2 as the doc defines it\n\n**Unified memory, one MCP surface** — the chokepoint. Linear: *Unified, Pluggable Agent Memory* (High), compressed target **Sep–Nov 2026**. Gate: P1 transport + auth.\n\n**Done when** one MCP tool returns unified results across code *and* knowledge, and only **one search engine and one embedding backbone** remain in production.\n\n| M | What | Target | Issues |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| **M1** | Converge code-search into one engine | 2026-09-30 | COR-786 (RFD), COR-787 (ship) |\n| **M2** | Converge knowledge onto one embedding backbone | 2026-10-31 | COR-788 |\n| **M3** | Brain + code-search + knowledge behind one MCP surface | 2026-11-30 | COR-789 |\n| **M4** | Retire duplicates, prove no regression | — | COR-790 |\n\n**The score that motivates it:** 4 search systems live or half-live (entire-search, librarian, peregrine, brain), **3 embedding backbones** (Cohere 1536, nomic 768, and none), **≥2 tree-sitter extractors**.\n\n# Sync report — the doc is a month stale in 9 places\n\n**Ⓐ The big one, and it's good news for P2.M1.** The doc treats \"converge code search\" as an unstarted RFD. But the convergence mechanism is **already built on both sides**:\n- entire-graph **#97** adds `snapshot --format scip` (open, draft)\n- peregrine really does reserve `SymbolSource::Scip = 1` and `SymbolPrecision::Semantic = 1` — I read `src/symbols/types.rs:112-122`\n\nSo the RFD's \"pick one direction\" question is largely **answered by construction**: entire-graph feeds peregrine's symbol overlay. M1 is closer to a wiring task than a decision.\n\n**Ⓑ Stale P1 facts:**\n| doc says | reality |\n|---|---|\n| P0 \"GA wrapper in progress\" | **P0 closed** — #84 merged 08-15, all 11 gates ✅ |\n| P1 client = entire-brain **#65** | #65 merged 07-13 (camelCase fix). Client is now **#85** |\n| #242 ≈ +8,532 lines | **+10,333 across 67 files** — and I rewrote its whole proposal surface |\n| Trail #243, 0 findings, risk 62% | stale — #242 changed substantially since that review |\n| P1 \"one step from prod\" | wire now **reconciled + live round-trip verified**; still awaiting merge |\n| `entire-sem` | renamed **entire-graph** (v0.2.0, v0.3.0 shipped) |\n| `brain-bench` | renamed **GraphMark** |\n\n**Ⓒ ADR-P1-D's blocker is gone.** The doc points storage at EntireDB. The reserved-ref obstacle both PR bodies cite no longer exists — `WorkloadEntireAPI` is registered for `refs/meta/entire/*` (ENT-1106), and other `refs/meta/*` paths were never reserved.\n\n**Ⓓ The tracking is dead.** The doc's own closing note: COR-781…803 were created 2026-07-01 and are **Canceled in Linear**. P2 has no live tracking today.\n\n# One strategic input for P2.M2\n\nM2 assumes the answer is *one embedding backbone*. But entire-graph **#104** just measured **94.74 vs mem0's 93.83 on LoCoMo (all 1,540 questions)** with **zero embeddings** — tree-sitter sections plus BM25. That's a real data point that the convergence answer for code+prose may be **fewer embeddings, not one backbone**. Worth landing before COR-788 is written, since it changes the question.\n\n# What I'd do next\n1. **Reactivate COR-781…803** — P2 can't be tracked while its issues are canceled\n2. **Refresh the doc's P1 section** — wrong PR link, stale line counts, dead blocker, renamed repos\n3. **Land #97 + #104**, then write COR-786 with the SCIP path as the leading option rather than an open question\n\nWant me to produce the corrected P1/P2 sections as a doc update, or go land the two entire-graph PRs that unblock M1?"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1303,"cache_read_input_tokens":955854,"output_tokens":2915,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1377},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1303,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2915,"cache_read_input_tokens":955854,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1303,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1303},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CeAPkJMUfsXUPWuCcKDWx","type":"assistant","uuid":"e9c8c513-64bd-4913-a66f-53e000916efe","timestamp":"2026-08-18T14:45:15.535Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"f507d58c-285f-4d11-b1d0-201f2a5e172d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"de272aad-c620-4d71-bbdd-27dd2d3dc8af","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"quizzical-sniffing-quasar"}
