{"type":"pr-link","sessionId":"de272aad-c620-4d71-bbdd-27dd2d3dc8af","prNumber":242,"prUrl":"https://github.com/entirehq/entire-api/pull/242","prRepository":"entirehq/entire-api","timestamp":"2026-08-18T17:56:04.776Z"}
{"parentUuid":"effee8b0-5388-4e98-ae6b-860537131c9f","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_011CeAeMNXbsaSbdSDrwBTBy","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# The brain roadmap, phase by phase\n\nThe arc in one line: **make one brain → share it → make it the only memory → make it compound → coordinate fleets on it → cross repo walls → turn it all into decisions.**\n\n---\n\n## 🟢 P0 — GA the local brain *(✅ done, closed 08-15)*\n**The foundation.** The local brain already worked; P0 was making it something the rest can *depend* on — not new build, but freeze-and-tag.\n\n- **entire-graph** (was entire-sem): parses code into symbols + a 30-type relation graph (CALLS, EXTENDS, DATA_FLOWS…) with tree-sitter. Zero vectors.\n- **entire-brain**: durable, branch-scoped, provenance-anchored facts + ~33 local MCP tools agents query.\n- **GraphMark** (was brain-bench): the CI regression gate across ~30 languages.\n\nWhat \"done\" meant: schema frozen (additive-only 1.x), both repos tagged v0.1.0, MCP contract locked, benchmark wired as a required floor, install docs. All 11 gates read ✅ on main today.\n\n**Why it's first:** every later phase trusts this contract. You can't share, converge, or mine a thing whose schema still moves.\n\n---\n\n## 🔵 P1 — Shared / hosted brain *(built + wire-verified, awaiting merge)*\n**The differentiator.** Lift the brain off the laptop: one member's agent learns something, every teammate's agent can read it.\n\n- **M1** server-side store — content-addressed, encrypted per-object (AES-256-GCM, KMS-wrapped), **crypto-shred** on retract so a removed fact is provably unreadable\n- **M2** sync — read-merge-CAS on a branch head; lost race = 412, re-read, re-merge; tamper-evident hash-chained audit log\n- **M3** remote MCP query — a teammate queries the shared brain with no local clone\n- **M4** auth/tenancy — SpiceDB org→project→repo cascade, fail-closed twice\n\nKey design rule (ADR-P1-E): **the merge runs on the runner, never the server.** The server stores bytes and moves pointers. That rule is exactly what the wire reconciliation I just did restored — the api side had drifted into server-side merging.\n\nCurrent truth: client (#85) and server (#242) agree on the wire, live round-trip passes, activation is one env var (`ENTIRE_BRAIN_HOSTED_ENABLED=true`), rollback is unsetting it. Needs merges.\n\n---\n\n## 🧩 Keystone — semantic index tied to VCS *(between P1 and P2)*\nNot a \"P\" but the hinge: persist **entity deltas onto checkpoints** and build a git-native index, so \"which checkpoints changed entity X?\" is answered from the index, not by re-parsing. Ties meaning to git history permanently. Everything from P2 on assumes this exists.\n\n---\n\n## 🟣 P2 — Unified memory, one MCP surface *(Sep–Nov 2026)*\n**The chokepoint.** Today the company runs **4 search systems** (brain, entire-search, librarian, peregrine), **3 embedding backbones** (Cohere-1536, nomic-768, none), and **2+ tree-sitter extractors**. P2 collapses that:\n\n- **M1** one code-search engine — the mechanism already exists: entire-graph exports SCIP (#97), peregrine reserved the `SymbolSource::Scip` slot. One extractor feeds both; peregrine = find-text-fast, brain = understand-structure\n- **M2** one embedding backbone for knowledge — though #104's result (beating mem0 with *zero* embeddings) suggests the real answer may be \"fewer embeddings,\" worth deciding with data\n- **M3** one MCP tool over code + knowledge + brain — every agent (Claude Code, Codex, Cursor, Droid, Gemini) queries the *same* memory\n- **M4** retire the duplicates\n\n**Why it matters:** it's the surface everything downstream registers on. No convergence → every later phase multiplies the fragmentation.\n\n---\n\n## 🟡 Reasoning capture *(companion to P2, Oct–Dec 2026)*\n**Makes memory compound.** Agents capture transcripts, not reasoning — so understanding restarts every run. This writes agent reasoning back as **structured, queryable facts**: a record schema per checkpoint/trail, review findings written back as durable facts, and a provenance graph (decision → task → PR → review).\n\nDone when: a second run *reuses* the first run's reasoning instead of re-deriving it.\n\n---\n\n## 🟠 P3 — Coordinated agents *(Nov 2026–Feb 2027)*\n**Fleets without collisions.** Two agents editing the same function today collide silently.\n\n- **entity-level claims/leases** — claim a *symbol*, not a file, with expiry\n- **pre-merge conflict detection** — warned before the merge, not after\n- **signed handovers** — structured data the next agent auto-hydrates via MCP\n- **scheduler** — ready tasks auto-dispatch to sandboxes; presence/read-receipts so a dead claim gets reclaimed\n\nGate: P1's durable state + P2's one surface. Runs parallel with P4.\n\n---\n\n## 🔴 P4 — Cross-repo federation *(Jan–Mar 2027)*\n**Break the repo wall.** An agent in repo A surfaces reasoning from repo B; a capability registry routes tasks to the best-fit agent. Cross-org authz rides the existing SpiceDB/MCP gating. Parallel with P3.\n\n---\n\n## ⭐ P5 — Behavioral intelligence *(north star, Jan–Jun 2027)*\n**The payoff: retained behavior becomes decisions.** Every prompt, session, and outcome is already captured as checkpoints — P5 mines it:\n\n- **prompt intelligence** — score a prompt before it runs; a best-prompt library mined from real checkpoints so the org's best prompting becomes everyone's baseline\n- **fit modeling** — who/which agent succeeds on what, from history not vibes\n- **auto-routing** — send work to the best-fit agent or person\n- **org dashboards** — leadership watches the org learn\n\nCame from the Salesforce ask; it's what makes the memory layer a *product*. Explicit first step: merge efforts with Alisha's MemoryRecords (same checkpoint stream, same territory) rather than building a third parallel system.\n\n---\n\n## The logic of the ordering\n```\nP0 trust the contract\n └─ P1 share it            ← the linchpin; everything needs durable shared state\n     └─ keystone: tie meaning to git\n         └─ P2 one surface  ← the chokepoint; all tools register here\n             ├─ reasoning capture (compound)\n             ├─ P3 coordinate ┐ parallel\n             └─ P4 federate  ┘\n                 └─ P5 decisions (north star)\n```\nGoverning constraint throughout: **no new infrastructure** — everything rides entiredb, checkpoint_remote, snapshotstore/crypt, SpiceDB, the jurisdiction forwarder.\n\nWhere you actually are: **P0 done, P1 one approval away, keystone unstarted (its Linear issues are canceled — needs reactivating), P2's M1 mechanism already half-built.**"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":853599,"cache_read_input_tokens":22123,"output_tokens":2481,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":853599,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2481,"cache_read_input_tokens":22123,"cache_creation_input_tokens":853599,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":853599},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":{"cache_miss_reason":{"type":"previous_message_not_found"}}},"requestId":"req_011CeAeMCqwZ1kUdumMmuZjS","type":"assistant","uuid":"feb15611-7e0f-4b0e-98e2-4725b81df63d","timestamp":"2026-08-18T17:57:11.544Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"f507d58c-285f-4d11-b1d0-201f2a5e172d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"de272aad-c620-4d71-bbdd-27dd2d3dc8af","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"quizzical-sniffing-quasar"}
