{"parentUuid":"744ba756-069b-491e-8182-0e55d2ca4b55","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"533fa54c-53b9-4246-8592-71abf1c78776","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The session progressed through a sequence of explicit user requests around the entire-brain project:\n   - Get up to date on entireio/entire-brain and report where things stand\n   - Enumerate all open brain-related PRs across repos (brain, api, etc.)\n   - \"now add everything to complete p1 and p0 to pr 75 and 242\" — build all remaining P0 and P1 work into entire-brain PR #75 and entire-api PR #242\n   - Wrap up all of P0, update all docs to date, merge all entire-brain PRs that should be merged, observe entire-graph changes (latest = PR #104) and whether brain needs to adapt\n   - \"make fully ready for p1\" — close the review blockers on #85 (**mid-turn user correction: \"only pr remmeber\" — open/update PRs only, NEVER merge without explicit approval**)\n   - Goal (session Stop hook, since cleared): \"fix all bugs and problems and slowing down and accuracy in entire brain make it a clean ready p1 add all changes to pr 85\"\n   - \"then keep on going and fix fully\" — continue hunting bugs (led to fuzzing, provenance fixes)\n   - \"then udapte 242 and veified ocne merged p1 fully done\" — implement the wire reconciliation on #242\n   - \"then do it fully hoyl\" — actually run the live cross-repo round-trip end to end\n   - \"ok what is the p2 plan make sure u have the google doc and are completely synced\" — retrieve the roadmap Google Doc and sync it against reality\n   - **Current/final request: \"explain to me each p of the brain\"** — explain each phase (P0 through P5) of the Semantic Reasoning Layer roadmap, in plain text (no tools)\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Semantic Reasoning Layer roadmap: P0 (GA local brain) → P1 (shared/hosted brain) → P2 (unified memory, one MCP surface) → P3 (coordinated agents) → P4 (cross-repo federation) → P5 (behavioral intelligence, north star); plus Keystone (semantic index tied to VCS) and Reasoning Capture tracks\n   - P1 architecture: fact-set head = content-addressed blob behind a compare-and-swap ref per (repo_key, branch); ADR-P1-E: the merge runs on the runner, server is storage+CAS only; ADR-P1-A: two-gate opt-in for hosted egress; crypto-shred via per-object DEKs (KindFacts vs KindProposals separation so shred paths can't cross)\n   - M1.3 canonical wire encoding: no HTML escaping, lexicographic key order (RFC 8785), normative omitempty, UTC-Z time, ±2^53 integers, duplicate-member rejection, 512-depth bound; unknown-field pass-through is DELIBERATE (additive-only 1.x, signature covers unknown fields — TestVerifyBytesToleratesUnknownFields pins both directions)\n   - M1.4 manifest signing: ed25519 over canonical bytes, Signature envelope (alg, key id, canonical-encoding version), commits to every referenced blob digest\n   - Open-proposal set: one CAS'd blob per branch (NOT row-per-proposal); client-derived proposal ids (sha256 over action/candidate/target/branch/proposedBy, 16 hex); resolve swaps facts first then proposal set; FactsUnchanged prune path for orphans (reject-only)\n   - Wire contract: `/api/v1/repos/{id}/brain/facts/proposals[/{id}[/resolve]]`; 412 = CAS loss, 404/501/503 = queue unsupported (client degrades to local queue)\n   - Mutation-verified testing (revert fix → test must fail); Go fuzzing (12M+ execs over canonical encoding + signing); live cross-repo round-trip test gated on ENTIRE_BRAIN_BIN\n   - Shared-proposal ledger (per-checkout) + shared-head applicability (cross-clone) for settlement dedup; settlement mirroring into local facts\n   - P2 plan: converge 4 search systems / 3 embedding backbones / 2+ tree-sitter extractors into one engine + one backbone + one MCP surface; peregrine SymbolSource::Scip + SymbolPrecision::Semantic reserved slots; entire-graph #97 SCIP export = producer side\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - **Google Doc \"Semantic Reasoning Layer - Roadmap.docx\"** (Drive fileId `REDACTED`, suhaan@entire.io, modified 2026-07-10) — the P0–P5 roadmap; read in full. P2 = Unified, Pluggable Agent Memory, Sep–Nov 2026, M1 COR-786/787 (converge code search, 2026-09-30), M2 COR-788 (one embedding backbone, 2026-10-31), M3 COR-789 (single MCP surface, 2026-11-30), M4 COR-790 (retire duplicates). Doc's own closing note: COR-781..803 are Canceled in Linear. Landscape: entirehq/mcp (James, hosted connector), librarian (Alex), entire-search (Alisha), peregrine (Evis), Alisha's MemoryRecords.\n   - **Worktrees** (never the main checkouts): `/Users/suhaan/devenv/p0p1/p1-new` (branch `feat/p1-canonical-signing-proposals` = PR #85), `/Users/suhaan/devenv/p0p1/api-242` (branch pushed to `m4-brain-auth` = PR #242)\n   - **entire-brain internal/brainwire/canonical.go** — M1.3; `CanonicalMarshal`, `Canonicalize`, `CanonicalUnmarshal`; field tables per type; unknown-field pass-through documented as load-bearing:\n     ```go\n     // Unknown (newer-minor) fields pass through; only their encoding is\n     // canonicalized... deliberate and load-bearing for the additive-only 1.x\n     // contract in ADR 0001... signature is taken over these bytes INCLUDING\n     // the unknown fields\n     ```\n   - **entire-brain internal/brainwire/signing.go** — M1.4; `Sign/Verify/VerifyBytes/VerifyCanonical`, `Signature` envelope, `ReferencedDigests`, `Ed25519Signer`\n   - **entire-brain internal/brainwire/canonical_fuzz_test.go** — 3 fuzz targets + `canonicalHasUnknownKeys` scope helper + `mustFuzzSigner`\n   - **entire-brain internal/cli/facts_sync_cmd.go** — settlement mirroring: `settledHostedAsAccept` (derives accept from head state: merge→candidate gone; supersede→target superseded by candidate), `applySettlementLocally`, `proposalStillOpenAgainst` (cross-clone guard), `readSharedFactHead`, `reconcileLocalProposalQueue(brainDir, branch, hosted, hostedFacts, now)` with `canMirror` guard (no head → keep entries queued); publish filter: ProposedBy-attributed + not in ledger + still open against head; uses `res.Facts` from Sync to skip a network read\n   - **entire-brain internal/factsync/sync.go** — `Result.Facts []factmerge.Record` added, populated on all 3 return paths (`Facts: merged`)\n   - **entire-brain internal/factsync/proposals.go** — `ResolveProposalRequest.FactsUnchanged bool`; `ResolveOpen` headGone split: Accept fails loudly, Reject prunes via FactsUnchanged\n   - **entire-brain internal/factsync/httpproposals.go** — client transport; `resolveRequestBody` with `FactsUnchanged bool json:\"factsUnchanged,omitempty\"`; guard factsUnchanged-only-with-reject; 503 added to unsupported statuses on list+publish paths\n   - **entire-brain internal/cli/facts_admin_cmd.go** — hosted interlock in `runFactsReview` (isShared via ledger → refuse targeted settle / skip in bulk with `deferred` count), `bulkDecisionVerb`/`targetedDecisionVerb`\n   - **entire-brain internal/cli/distill_cmd.go** — force+final flush now retains ProposedBy-attributed proposals (sync-raised) and drops only unattributed (distill-owned)\n   - **entire-brain internal/cli/facts_proposals_cmd.go** — `pruneLocalProposalCopy(ctx, opts, branch, decision, settled)` now mirrors the settlement into local facts inside the write lock before pruning\n   - **entire-brain internal/cli/facts_settlement_test.go** — `TestReconcileLocalQueuePullsSettlementIntoLocalFacts` (drives reconciler directly; merge-accept/supersede-accept/reject), `TestFactsReviewRefusesToSettleSharedProposalLocally`, `TestFactsReviewBulkSkipsSharedButSettlesPrivate`, `TestProposalStillOpenAgainstDetectsSettlements`, `TestReconcileKeepsSettledEntryWhenHeadUnavailable`, `TestFactsProposalsApplyMirrorsIntoLocalFactsImmediately`\n   - **entire-brain internal/factsync/orphan_prune_test.go** — `orphanServer`/`countingServer` fakes; orphan prune, accept-refusal, `TestSyncResultCarriesMergedFacts` (exactly one Current call)\n   - **entire-brain internal/cli/brain_brief_git_intent_test.go** — de-flaked: bounded 5-attempt retry on overlay activation (real git under 500ms product timeout degrades under load); hard-timeout slack widened to `2*timeout+2s`\n   - **entire-brain internal/factgitmeta/gitmeta/*.go (10 files)** — provenance headers corrected: real upstream is entire-api internal/gitmeta (POC repo superseded); drift documented as inert (local-only, refs/meta/local/main)\n   - **entire-api internal/store/migrations/repo/20260817120000_brain_proposal_refs.sql** — replaced row-queue migration; CAS head table mirroring brain_fact_refs (repo_key, branch, current_ref, version), no DELETE grant\n   - **entire-api internal/brainstore/store.go** — `KindProposals = \"proposals\"` added with shred-safety rationale\n   - **entire-api internal/brainbuild/fact_sync.go** — `ProposalSetRef` (\"proposals-\" prefix), `FactSetStore.kind` field, `NewProposalSetStore`, `setRef` dispatcher\n   - **entire-api internal/brainbuild/fact_ref_index_pg.go** — parameterized by `table`+`kind` (compile-time constants `factRefsTable`/`proposalRefsTable` only), `NewPgProposalRefIndex`; stale brain_fact_proposals clause removed from shred query\n   - **entire-api internal/httpapi/brain_proposals.go** — fully rewritten to client contract: `brainProposal{ID string; Proposal json.RawMessage}` (opaque), list/get/publish/resolve handlers, facts-first ordering in resolve, `brainProposalStoreError` (412/404/500), `registerBrainProposals` (pull reads, push writes)\n   - **entire-api internal/httpapi/brain_proposals_test.go** — rewritten; includes `TestProposalWireContractMatchesBrainClient` fed the client's literal JSON (publish body, resolve body, factsUnchanged variant, list + resolve response envelopes)\n   - **entire-api internal/httpapi/router.go + authz.go** — `RepoActivityDeps.repoExists repoExister` test seam + `repoExisterOrStore()`; deps.Proposals now `*brainbuild.FactSetStore`\n   - **entire-api internal/httpapi/brain_roundtrip_test.go** — THE live round-trip: real brain binary (ENTIRE_BRAIN_BIN) against real router via httptest.NewServer; jwksAuth + fakeReaderRW push grant + fakeRepoExister; sync via http backend, server-seeded proposal read back by client (`prop-roundtrip01`), `lastJSONObject` extractor. PASSES.\n   - **entire-api internal/httpapi/tags.go** — added `brain` tag to apiTags (fixed TestOpenAPITagCatalogInvariants for all nine brain operations)\n   - **Memory files**: `p0-p1-completion-worktrees.md`, `p1-client-server-interop-fork.md` (+ MEMORY.md pointers)\n   - **peregrine src/symbols/types.rs:112-122** (read-only verification): `SymbolSource { TreeSitter = 0, Scip = 1 }`, `SymbolPrecision { Syntax = 0, Semantic = 1 }` — confirms P2.M1 convergence slots are real\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - **Force-push nearly clobbered Thomas's work on #73**: `--force-with-lease` rejected it (branch had moved to 9dd3581d). Lesson: always fetch + re-baseline before pushing to shared branches.\n   - **Wrong org slugs**: entireio/entire-api 404 — api/db/io live under entirehq.\n   - **False-confidence settlement test (caught by mutation testing)**: my first test passed with the fix reverted because the natural sync fixture makes the local member WIN its own proposal (nothing to retire locally). Rewrote to drive `reconcileLocalProposalQueue` directly across the losing side's three shapes.\n   - **Bug I introduced then fixed**: settled entries were pruned even when the shared head was unreadable, losing the settlement permanently — added `canMirror` guard (entries stay queued until mirrorable); mutation-verified with a compiling mutation (`canMirror := true`) after the first mutation failed to compile.\n   - **I was wrong about unknown-field pass-through**: changed Canonicalize to reject unknown fields; broke 3 tests including `TestVerifyBytesToleratesUnknownFields` which pins it deliberately (signature covers unknown fields both directions; additive-only 1.x requires old verifiers to verify newer producers). Reverted, documented the rationale in code, scoped my fuzz target to all-known-keys inputs.\n   - **Wire fork between #85 and #242** (three simultaneous incompatibilities: paths, settle verbs, id derivation 16 vs 64 hex) — every unit test on both sides passed because nothing crossed the boundary. Fixed by moving api to the client's contract; guarded with the literal-JSON contract test.\n   - **Client/server status mismatch**: api 503s when hosted brain disabled; client only treated 404/501 as unsupported → failed a sync whose facts had landed. Client now treats 503 as ErrProposalQueueUnsupported.\n   - **Live round-trip found a 500 panic**: `checkRepoPermission` nil-dereferenced `deps.Store` on the ALLOW path (every existing authz test asserts denials only, which short-circuit before the store). Added the `repoExists repoExister` seam.\n   - **lastJSONLine parser bug in my own test**: CLI pretty-prints JSON multi-line; single-line matcher returned `{}` silently. Replaced with `lastJSONObject` (first `{` to last `}`).\n   - **Flaky test failed my verification on correct code**: `TestBrainBriefGitIntentLiveShapedOperationalRecall` drives real git under the product's deliberate 500ms overlay bound; under load the overlay correctly degrades and the must-activate assertion fails. Fixed with bounded 5-attempt retry; proved detection preserved by stubbing promoter false. Noted product implication: overlay silently stops contributing under load in production too (left alone deliberately).\n   - **TestOpenAPITagCatalogInvariants failure on #242**: \"brain\" tag used but undeclared (invariant landed on main after branch cut) — declared in apiTags.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Completed P0: gates 9/10 reconciled + provider-compatibility section (PR #84, merged 08-15; main gate table all ✅)\n   - Completed P1 client