n   - \"so all rbain prs merged good? only api pr pnding?\"\n   - \"get updat eto dat now and give me a cleans tatus report\"\n   - \"git emt serive was implemnted in api; that waa a poc repo\"\n   - \"k now give list\"\n   - \"make fully ready fro p1 ready\"\n   - \"only pr remmeber\" (mid-turn — **PRs only, never merge without explicit approval**)\n   - \"list all tha tneed to be merged for p1 to finish\"\n   - \"/goal fix all bugs and rpoblems and slowign down and accorchay in engite brain make it a clean ready p1 add all changes to pr 85\" (goal since cleared)\n   - \"then keep on goigna d fix fully\"\n   - \"give all prs- fully ready>\"\n   - \"no give lsit fo prs pendign to be merged for fullv erfie dp1 as u fixed eveyrthign right\"\n   - \"then udapte 242 and veified ocne merged p1 fully done\"\n   - \"then do it fully hoyl\"\n   - \"ok what is the p2 plan make sure u have the google doc and are ompeclty synced\"\n   - \"epxlain to me eahc p of the brain\" (current request; local-command caveat noted /model set to Fable 5)\n   \n   Standing constraints (from this + prior compacted session): **PR only — never merge/publish without explicit per-action approval; NO AI/Claude/session footers or Co-Authored-By on commits; no cheating/fabrication of results; work in fresh worktrees, never the main checkouts; never force-push over others' work (use --force-with-lease)**.\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - **Answer the current question: explain each P (P0–P5) of the brain roadmap** (plain text)\n   - Awaiting user approval to merge #85 (entire-brain, MERGEABLE/CLEAN) and #242 (entire-api, MERGEABLE/BLOCKED = needs review approval) — both ready, merge is user's call\n   - P2 housekeeping surfaced but not started: reactivate canceled Linear issues COR-781..803; update the roadmap doc's stale P1 section (wrong PR link #65→#85, +8,532→+10,333, entire-sem→entire-graph, brain-bench→GraphMark, entiredb blocker gone, P0 closed); land graph #97/#104 ahead of COR-786\n   - Optional follow-ups noted along the way: de-vendor brain's gitmeta into a shared module (both copies are internal/, needs extraction); close git-meta-service #1 as POC-superseded (needs user ok)\n\n8. Current Work:\n   Immediately before this summary, the user asked \"epxlain to me eahc p of the brain\" — a plain-text explanation of each phase of the Semantic Reasoning Layer roadmap, right after I had read the Google Doc (\"Semantic Reasoning Layer - Roadmap.docx\") in full and delivered the P2 sync report. All context needed is in hand from the doc read: P0 (GA the local brain: entire-sem/graph provider, entire-brain facts + ~33 MCP tools, brain-bench/GraphMark CI gate, M1–M5 finish work — now CLOSED per my verification), P1 (shared/hosted brain: server store M1, CAS sync M2, remote MCP query M3, auth/tenancy M4 — now built, reconciled, live-round-trip verified, two PRs awaiting merge), Keystone (semantic index tied to VCS: entity deltas in checkpoint metadata, git-native entity→checkpoint index, transparency-log causality), P2 (unified memory/one MCP surface: converge 4 search systems + 3 embedding backbones into one engine/backbone/surface, M1–M4, COR-786..790), Reasoning Capture track (record schema, write-back, provenance graph, COR-791..794), P3 (coordinated agents: entity claims/leases, pre-merge conflict detection, signed handovers, scheduler, presence, COR-795..800), P4 (cross-repo federation: federated discovery, cross-org authz, capability registry, COR-801..803), P5 north star (behavioral intelligence: prompt-quality classifier, best-prompt library, fit modeling, auto-routing, feedback dashboards — align with Alisha's MemoryRecords first).\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Answer the user's direct question in plain text: explain each P of the brain roadmap (P0, P1, keystone, P2, reasoning-capture, P3, P4, P5) — what each phase is, its gate, its milestones, and its CURRENT verified status where I have fresher ground truth than the doc (P0 closed via #84; P1 code-complete and round-trip-verified awaiting merge of #85/#242; P2 planned with its M1 largely answered by the peregrine SCIP slots + graph #97; P3–P5 planned with canceled Linear tracking that needs reactivation). Direct quote of the task: \"epxlain to me eahc p of the brain\".\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /Users/suhaan/.claude/projects/-Users-suhaan-devenv/de272aad-c620-4d71-bbdd-27dd2d3dc8af.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened."},"isVisibleInTranscriptOnly":true,"isCompactSummary":true,"uuid":"747ff69a-6758-404d-849d-e9f79ad1f047","timestamp":"2026-08-18T18:00:03.267Z","session_id":"f507d58c-285f-4d11-b1d0-201f2a5e172d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"de272aad-c620-4d71-bbdd-27dd2d3dc8af","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"quizzical-sniffing-quasar"}
