{"parentUuid":"4d211b7e-779a-437f-a377-30b68d565ee1","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_011CeAfU7UYZb49NtFtnJD4G","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_011XtdfdJB4sVibbwpmNjCTS","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Scout entire-graph diff schema","subagent_type":"general-purpose","model":"sonnet","prompt":"READ-ONLY scout of /Users/suhaan/devenv/entire-graph (a Go repo, the `entire graph` CLI). Use rtk-prefixed commands where possible (e.g. `rtk grep`, or plain grep is fine). DO NOT edit anything.\n\nQuestions:\n1. `entire graph diff --base A --head B --json` — find the implementation. What EXACTLY is the JSON output schema? (added/removed/modified entities? entity ids/names/kinds/file:line? relations too?) Paste the Go struct(s) that define the diff output.\n2. Is there a stable entity identity across commits (an entity ID/fingerprint that survives file moves/renames), or is identity just name+file+kind? Where computed?\n3. Is there any existing code mapping entities→commits/checkpoints or any index persisted per-commit? (search: checkpoint, commit, history, index, delta)\n4. What is SchemaVersion of graph output currently, and where is the diff command registered (file:line)?\n5. Does the graph have a programmatic Go API brain could import, or is CLI+JSON the only integration surface? (check go.mod module name + whether internal/ hides everything)\n\nReport in caveman-ultra compressed style: max ~40 lines, file:line for every claim, paste only the key structs. No prose padding."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":222,"cache_read_input_tokens":84691,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":222},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CeAfU4Rz8MrqAUSKVbbon","type":"assistant"