{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-08-18T18:12:42.793Z","sessionId":"de272aad-c620-4d71-bbdd-27dd2d3dc8af","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>ab691a79ea6350449</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>REDACTED</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-suhaan-devenv/f507d58c-285f-4d11-b1d0-201f2a5e172d/tasks/ab691a79ea6350449.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Scout entire-graph diff schema\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>Report:\n\n**1. `entire graph diff` impl + schema**\n`internal/cli/root.go:52` → `runDiff` (root.go:662) → parses `--base/--head`/paths → `analyzeAndPrint` (root.go:704) → `sem.AnalyzeGitRangeWithOptions` (`internal/sem/analyze.go:41`) → returns `sem.Result`, JSON via `json.MarshalIndent` (root.go:718-725, `--json` flag).\n\nStructs (`internal/sem/model.go:11-59`):\n```go\ntype Entity struct {\n    Kind, Name, Signature string\n    StartLine, EndLine    int\n    BodyHash, Fingerprint string\n    Local bool `json:\"-\"`\n}\ntype EntityChange struct {\n    Type, Kind, Name                        string  // type: added/removed/modified/renamed/moved\n    OldName, NewName                        string\n    OldSignature, NewSignature              string\n    OldPath, NewPath                        string\n    BeforeStartLine, AfterStartLine         int\n    DependentsCount                         float64... int\n    Similarity                              float64\n    Reconciliation string // \"RENAMED\" | \"MOVED\" | \"RECONCILED_FROM\"\n}\ntype FileChange struct {\n    Path, OldPath, Status, Language string\n    Changes []EntityChange\n}\ntype Result struct {\n    Checkpoint string\n    Base, Head string\n    Files      []FileChange\n    Warnings   []ProviderWarning\n}\n```\nNo relation (call-graph edge) diffing — only entity-level file/kind/name/signature/line changes. `analyze` command is literally `runAnalyze = runDiff` (root.go:658-660), same output.\n\n**2. Entity identity**: NOT a stable persisted ID. `Fingerprint` = `hash(normalize(entityFingerprintSource(entity, block)))`, sha256 truncated to 16 hex chars (parser.go:7576-7590, computed at parse time in every language parser, e.g. parser.go:3186). Fingerprint source = signature-with-name-stripped (single-line) or body-minus-first-line (multi-line) — content-based, no file path baked in. Cross-commit matching happens live inside one diff call via `similarity()` (analyze.go:855-862: fingerprint match=1.0, bodyHash match=0.97, else jaccard(signature)) and `bestRename`/reconciliation groups (analyze.go:380-397 \"MOVED\", 505-516 \"RENAMED\") keyed by git's own `--find-renames` groups (gitutil/git.go:352) + entity-level fallback matching (analyze.go:794-825, cascading matchClass/matchUnique on {signature,bodyHash,fingerprint}). So identity = name+file+kind AND, when that breaks (rename/move), content fingerprint/bodyHash recomputed per-diff-call — nothing is stored to reuse across separate CLI invocations.\n\n**3. No entity→commit/checkpoint history index.** `AnalyzeCheckpoint` (analyze.go:424) just resolves checkpoint→commit via `git log --grep=Entire-Checkpoint:` (gitutil/git.go:61-71, no index, greps refs live) then does a normal 1-commit diff. `records_cache.go` (internal/sem) is a symbols/edges/snapshot NDJSON cache keyed by **HEAD tree hash** (records_cache.go:19-38) purely to skip re-parsing — not a history/delta index, no per-entity commit log anywhere.\n\n**4. SchemaVersion**: `internal/sem/provider.go:34` — `SchemaVersion = \"1.1\"` — but this only appears on `snapshot`/`symbols`/`edges` provider-record output (provider.go:136,275,456,669: `format_version`/`schema_version` fields on those structs). `diff`'s `sem.Result` (model.go:53) has NO schema_version field at all — unversioned. `diff` registered: `internal/cli/root.go:52` (dispatch), handler `root.go:662`.\n\n**5. CLI+JSON only — no Go API for brain.** Module = `github.com/entireio/entire-graph` (go.mod:1). All logic lives under `internal/cli/`, `internal/sem/`, `internal/gitutil/` (internal/ has cli, sem, gitutil, filedigest, bench — ls confirmed) — Go's `internal/` visibility rule means only code inside this module tree can import `sem`/`gitutil`. `cmd/` has only `entire-graph/main.go` and `graph-bench/main.go`, both thin wrappers calling `cli.Execute`. Nothing exported outside `internal/`. So brain (a separate repo/module) has zero programmatic import surface — must shell out to the `entire-graph` binary and parse stdout JSON, same as any other consumer.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>65498</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>25</tool_uses><duration_ms>79156</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
