{"parentUuid":"ab58ae7d-68f3-48f9-89cb-69eb6db7baa3","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_011CeAfcr9JsBB1dWnApHHKg","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Lpvg6mrobVFGdXFTuUP64a","name":"mcp__claude_ai_Google_Drive__read_file_content","input":{"fileId":"1sVWKzuP_sQGpf7l8M2Yf_hgJE2kOgHvW"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3364,"cache_read_input_tokens":90767,"output_tokens":195,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":93},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3364,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":195,"cache_read_input_tokens":90767,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3364,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3364},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CeAfcoMsy9CmDHNiuoCD2","type":"assistant","uuid":"5e0420f0-5b92-4d86-b289-909f46886b2d","timestamp":"2026-08-18T18:12:54.905Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"f507d58c-285f-4d11-b1d0-201f2a5e172d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"de272aad-c620-4d71-bbdd-27dd2d3dc8af","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"quizzical-sniffing-quasar"}
{"parentUuid":"5e0420f0-5b92-4d86-b289-909f46886b2d","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"d72b9eed-39e6-4651-8098-6928de58d291","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Lpvg6mrobVFGdXFTuUP64a","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"fileContent\":\"# ð§  The Semantic Reasoning Layer: Roadmap\\n\\nTurn the local brain into a shared reasoning substrate that a fleet of agents builds on. Git preserves change, but it does not preserve meaning. This initiative gives every agent persistent, shared, pluggable memory tied to git history, so humans and agents can reason and build in parallel without colliding.\\n\\nInitiative: [Semantic Reasoning Layer](https://linear.app/entirehq/initiative/semantic-reasoning-layer-e043385c2167) (Linear, Active) · Vision: [entire.io/vision](https://entire.io/vision) · As of: July 2026\\n\\nThe arc: ð¢ P0 finish the brain, then ðµ P1 host it, then ð£ P2 unify memory behind one surface, then ð  P3 coordinate fleets and ð´ P4 federate across repos in parallel, all feeding ⭐ P5, the north star: behavioral intelligence, where retained behavior becomes decisions (best-agent routing, prompt quality per person, a best-prompt library).\\n\\nGoverning constraint: no new infrastructure. The whole arc rides entire.io's existing rails (entiredb, checkpoint\\\\_remote, snapshotstore and snapshotcrypt, authz and SpiceDB, the jurisdiction forwarder). Each milestone ports proven parts onto the brain model rather than building storage or crypto from scratch.\\n\\n## ð Timeline at a glance\\n\\nTarget: the whole roadmap complete by end of March 2027. The schedule below is the compressed plan to hit that date. The dates run tight and in parallel from P2 onward.\\n\\n| Phase | Focus | Window | Status |\\n| :-: | :-: | :-: | :-: |\\n| ð¢ P0 GA the local brain | Harden entire-sem, brain, MCP surface, bench | Jul to Aug 2026 | Ships today, GA wrapper in progress |\\n| ðµ P1 Shared / hosted brain | Server store, sync, remote query, auth | Now, ship Aug 2026 | Built and tested on clones, one step from prod |\\n| ð§© Keystone: semantic index tied to VCS | Entity deltas, git-native index, causality | Aug to Sep 2026 | Planned |\\n| ð£ P2 Unified memory, one MCP surface | Converge search, one backbone, one surface | Sep to Nov 2026 | Planned |\\n| ð¡ Reasoning capture, compounding memory | Record schema, write-back, provenance graph | Oct to Dec 2026 | Planned |\\n| ð  P3 Coordinated agents | Claims, conflict detection, handovers, scheduler | Nov 2026 to Feb 2027 | Planned |\\n| ð´ P4 Cross-repo federation | Federated discovery, capability registry | Jan to Mar 2027 | Planned |\\n| ⭐ P5 Behavioral intelligence (north star) | Prompt quality, best-prompt library, fit, auto-routing | Jan to Jun 2027 | Planned |\\n\\nThe March 2027 target covers the enabling phases (P0 through P4). The P5 north star starts as soon as P2's surface and P3's coordination land, and runs to June 2027. Linear milestone dates now match the compressed schedule.\\n\\n## ð¢ P0, GA the local brain\\n\\nWhat it is. The foundation the whole initiative stands on. The local brain already runs, so P0 is finish work and release hygiene, not new build. There is no gate here. Everything ships today, but nothing is formally tagged, so P0 is the wrapper that makes it something the rest of the arc can depend on.\\n\\nThe pieces, all live today.\\n\\nentire-sem is the semantic provider. It parses code into symbols and relations with tree-sitter, and it uses no vectors anywhere in the stack.\\n\\nentire-brain is the local brain. It holds durable, branch-scoped, provenance-anchored facts, plus a local MCP surface of about 33 tools that agents query.\\n\\nbrain-bench is the CI gate. It benchmarks the extractor against a reference tool across roughly 30 languages and fails the build on regression or drift.\\n\\nThe milestones.\\n\\nM1, harden and GA entire-sem. Version-stamp it and freeze the schema so everything downstream can trust the contract.\\n\\nM2, close the brain blockers. Ship the local brain with honest claims, no overreach.\\n\\nM3, GA the MCP surface for both plugins. Harden the local tool surface for the Claude Code and Codex plugins.\\n\\nM4, brain-bench as the automated eval gate. Make the benchmark a required regression floor.\\n\\nM5, release logistics. The release checklist, the compatibility matrix, and distribution.\\n\\nFoundation build tracked in Linear: [Semantic Index Tied to VCS History](https://linear.app/entirehq/project/semantic-index-tied-to-vcs-history-ea453fa387e2) (Urgent). This is the piece that persists entity-level meaning onto checkpoints and a git-native index, so meaning is stored with git history and not re-parsed on demand. Done when entire and MCP can answer \\\"which checkpoints changed entity X\\\" from the index.\\n\\nEntity deltas in checkpoint metadata (target 2026-08-15): [COR-781](https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-781/spike-map-semantic-extractor-snapshot-checkpoint-metadata-schema) spike the schema, then [COR-782](https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-782/embed-entity-deltas-into-the-checkpoint-metadata-write-path) embed the deltas into the write path.\\n\\nGit-native entity to checkpoint index (target 2026-09-15): [COR-783](https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-783/build-the-git-native-entity-checkpoint-index) build the index, [COR-784](https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-784/mcp-tool-query-checkpointssessions-by-semantic-entity) expose it as an MCP tool.\\n\\nTransparency-log semantic causality (target 2026-09-30): [COR-785](https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-785/tie-transparency-log-events-to-semantic-causality) tie ref-change events to the session and entities that caused them.\\n\\n## ðµ P1, shared / hosted brain ⭐\\n\\nWhat it is. The differentiator. P1 lifts the brain off the laptop into a shared, server-side, multi-tenant service, so one member's agent learns something and every other member's agent can read it. The gate is the P0 schema-freeze plus a namespace, and it deliberately relaxes the local-only guardrail. All four parts are built and DB-tested on clone branches, race-clean, and awaiting merge.\\n\\nThe milestones.\\n\\nM1, server-side brain store. Content-addressed and authz-gated, encrypted at rest. Every artifact gets a fresh per-object key, AES-256-GCM, KMS-wrapped, bound to the repo and artifact, with crypto-shred of the key on retract so a removed fact becomes provably unreadable.\\n\\nM2, sync protocol over checkpoint\\\\_remote and entiredb. Durable facts sync under compare-and-swap on the branch head. The tenancy key is the injective slug@ULID, a lost race returns 412, and every advance appends to a tamper-evident hash-chained log.\\n\\nM3, multi-machine shared query. A remote MCP transport over HTTP, so a teammate's agent queries the shared brain without a local clone. The facts tools serve now. Direction: this endpoint becomes the backend of a brain surface on entirehq/mcp (the one hosted connector), not a second standalone connector.\\n\\nM4, auth and tenancy. Multi-tenant isolation on the org, project, repo SpiceDB cascade, with two independent fail-closed layers.\\n\\nWhat P1 rides and reuses (locked in after the landscape review).\\n\\nTransport: entirehq/mcp. James's hosted connector already solves OAuth, per-principal token exchange, tenancy, and discovery for about 60 tools. The brain registers a tool surface there; M3's endpoint is that surface's backend. No second connector, no duplicate auth plumbing.\\n\\nStorage direction: EntireDB. Blobs onto objstore, the fact CAS onto refstore, the audit log onto rsl, aligned with the git-meta move. This work is owned in decentralized-architecture, with the brain as its first customer and forcing function. The organizing rule: the brain owns the what and the when; decentralized-architecture owns the shared rails, because a capability with many consumers lives with the platform, not inside one product.\\n\\nEncryption honesty. Per-object DEKs and crypto-shred exist because the current store is one bucket shared across tenants (separate orgs). In-repo or in EntireDB under the repo's own trust boundary, that need mostly falls away, so the crypto layer is a property of where the data sits, not of the data.\\n\\nHardening state. Both PRs went through a 4-angle cleanup pass (reuse, simplification, efficiency, altitude): one shared AWS store builder, no double-hashing on the publish path, narrowed validation interface, egress-toggle warning parity with the CLI. Trail re-review pending on the latest push.\\n\\nLinks. [entire-api PR \\\\#242](https://github.com/entirehq/entire-api/pull/242) is the store, sync, remote MCP, and tenancy, roughly +8,532 lines. [entire-brain PR \\\\#65](https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/65) is the client wire fixes. [Trail \\\\#243](https://entire.io/gh/entirehq/entire-api/trails/243) is entire.io's own AI review, with 0 open findings and risk around 62%.\\n\\nWhere the storage is headed. The brain is in-repo by design already, keyed by repo, branch, and commit, and the hosted service exists only for the shared, authed query that a file in one clone cannot serve. The store rides the session-share stack today (S3 plus KMS) because that was the fastest proven path to ship P1, but the target is to push it down into EntireDB so it inherits resiliency and replication for free: the artifact blobs onto objstore, the fact-set CAS onto refstore, the audit log onto rsl. The one piece EntireDB does not cover yet is encryption at rest with a per-object key and crypto-shred, and that only matters because the current store is shared across tenants, meaning separate orgs in one bucket. In-repo, under the repo's own trust boundary, that need mostly falls away, so the direction is to ride EntireDB and add per-object encrypt and shred there only if a shared store still requires it.\\n\\n### ð Shipping P1, staging to production\\n\\nThe path is staging-first and reversible, so nothing turns on by accident.\\n\\nMerge [PR \\\\#242](https://github.com/entirehq/entire-api/pull/242) and [PR \\\\#65](https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/65) into main, one approval each.\\n\\nStaging deploys automatically. The brain migrations (brain\\\\_deks, brain\\\\_overlay\\\\_branches, brain\\\\_fact\\\\_refs, brain\\\\_fact\\\\_advances) apply on deploy and are additive only.\\n\\nEnable on staging. Set ENTIRE\\\\_BRAIN\\\\_HOSTED\\\\_ENABLED=true on the US and EU staging cells.\\n\\nSmoke test on partial.to. Publish a brain, advance a fact-set under CAS, and read it back over the remote MCP transport.\\n\\nPromote to production. Set the same one env var on the US and EU prod cells. That is the activation.\\n\\nRollback is instant. Unset the flag and every endpoint fails closed to 503, with data left sealed and dormant.\\n\\nThe only new setting is ENTIRE\\\\_BRAIN\\\\_HOSTED\\\\_ENABLED=true. Everything else is reused, since the brain shares session-share's already-live ENTIRE\\\\_SNAPSHOT\\\\_CIPHER=aws, its S3 bucket, and its KMS key, so there is no new bucket, key, IAM policy, or AWS credential. Until the flag is set, the endpoints fail closed to 503, so merging ships the code dormant on production.\\n\\n## ðº️ The landscape: what already exists, and how the plan converges it\\n\\nFour systems already live in this space. The plan does not route around them, it converges onto them. This is grounded in a full read of each codebase.\\n\\nentirehq/mcp (James). A hosted, multi-tenant, stateless remote MCP proxy: about 60 tools over four upstreams, Streamable HTTP, OAuth resource server with per-principal token exchange, all authorization downstream in SpiceDB. It stores nothing. It is the one hosted MCP transport, and it is architected to add tool surfaces. Decision: the brain does not ship its own standalone MCP connector. The hosted brain is an upstream data service, exposed as a brain surface on this server. P1.M3's transport work becomes the backend that surface calls.\\n\\nlibrarian (Alex). A knowledge-indexing and hybrid-search service over team communications and docs: Slack threads, Linear issues, GitHub PRs and issues, markdown. Postgres plus pgvector, its own 768-dim embedding stack (nomic-embed-text on Ollama), RRF fusion, no S3, no code, no sessions. Its roadmap heads toward an entity graph and synthesized views over the same checkpoint stream the brain distills. Librarian is the who-and-why half of team memory (comms); the brain is the what-and-where half (code, keyed to git). The facts and synthesis layer must be negotiated between the two, plus Alisha's MemoryRecords, before either builds further.\\n\\nentire-search (Alisha, deployed, serves entire.io search today). Product-entity search: checkpoint transcript chunks, commits, PRs. Cohere embed-v4.0 (1536-dim) with vectors in Turbopuffer, BM25 plus ANN with a tier system, SpiceDB ACL fan-out. It deliberately strips code before indexing. Near-zero overlap with the brain: different corpus, different store. The seam is checkpoints, which both consume; a distilled brain fact is a better search document than a raw transcript chunk, a future feed-in, not a conflict.\\n\\nperegrine (Evis, staging, prod target July). Trigram lexical code search, the Zoekt replacement: regex and full-text over source at platform scale, one index file per repo on S3, plus a tree-sitter symbol layer (15 languages, definition and reference extraction, query-time go-to-def). Zero embeddings. The one real duplication in the landscape: entire-sem and peregrine both maintain per-language tree-sitter extractors. Peregrine has no typed relation graph (its only edge is an untyped ref-to-def link) while entire-sem emits a 30-type relation graph (CALLS, EXTENDS, IMPLEMENTS, DATA\\\\_FLOWS). Peregrine reserved explicit extension slots (SymbolSource::Scip, SymbolPrecision::Semantic) for a higher-precision external symbol producer. Decision to pursue: entire-sem feeds peregrine's symbol overlay, one extractor serving both, with peregrine the find-text-fast engine and the brain the understand-structure engine.\\n\\nAlisha's MemoryRecords (Agent Improvement Engine). The sharpest overlap in the company: it derives memory from the same checkpoint stream the brain distills facts from, the descriptive and prescriptive halves of one problem. It also sits directly under the P5 north star (prompt quality, fit, routing), and Alisha owns the deployed semantic search too, so she holds two seats at the convergence table. Decision: align with Alisha before building the facts layer or P5 further; P5 should merge efforts, not add a third parallel one.\\n\\nThe score that motivates P2: four search systems live or half-live, three embedding backbones (Cohere 1536, nomic 768, and none), and at least two tree-sitter extractors. P2's converge-code-search RFD ([COR-786](https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-786/decision-rfd-converge-code-search-on-one-engine-deprecate-duplicates)) and one-backbone milestone ([COR-788](https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-788/unify-knowledge-code-artifact-indexes-on-one-embedding-backbone)) are exactly this cleanup.\\n\\n## ð£ P2, unified memory, one MCP surface\\n\\nWhat it is. The chokepoint. Today retrieval and knowledge are fragmented across several parallel code-search efforts and two parallel knowledge systems. P2 converges them into one shared memory on one embedding backbone, exposed through MCP, so every agent (Claude Code, Codex, Droid, Cursor, Gemini) queries the same thing with the same tools. The gate is P1 transport plus auth, and it is the surface every downstream tool registers on. Done when one MCP tool returns unified results across code and knowledge, and only one search engine and one embedding backbone remain in production.\\n\\nTracked in Linear: [Unified, Pluggable Agent Memory](https://linear.app/entirehq/project/unified-pluggable-agent-memory-eaf5762e7339) (High, compressed target Sep to Nov 2026).\\n\\nM1, converge code-search into one engine (target 2026-09-30). [COR-786](https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-786/decision-rfd-converge-code-search-on-one-engine-deprecate-duplicates) is the RFD that picks one direction, and [COR-787](https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-787/ship-the-converged-code-search-service) ships the converged code-search service.\\n\\nM2, converge knowledge into one backbone (target 2026-10-31). [COR-788](https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-788/unify-knowledge-code-artifact-indexes-on-one-embedding-backbone) unifies the knowledge and code-artifact indexes on one embedding backbone.\\n\\nM3, expose brain plus code-search plus knowledge behind one MCP surface (target 2026-11-30). [COR-789](https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-789/single-mcp-shared-memory-tool-over-code-knowledge-semantic-index) is the single MCP shared-memory tool.\\n\\nM4, retire duplicates and prove no regression. [COR-790](https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-790/retire-duplicate-search-and-knowledge-paths) decommissions the superseded search and knowledge paths once the unified surface is in production.\\n\\n## ð¡ Reasoning capture and compounding memory\\n\\nWhat it is. The companion to P2 that makes memory compound. Agents capture transcripts, not reasoning, and the reasoning surfaces we have emit prose that gets overwritten, so understanding restarts every run. This captures agent reasoning as structured, queryable facts written back into shared memory, so a later run inherits what an earlier one learned. It rides on the unified surface and the keystone entity deltas. Done when a second agent run reuses the first run's structured reasoning rather than re-deriving it, and a provenance query returns the decision cascade.\\n\\nTracked in Linear: [Reasoning Capture and Compounding Memory](https://linear.app/entirehq/project/reasoning-capture-and-compounding-memory-db95c0b2ef1c) (High, target Oct to Dec 2026).\\n\\nM1, structured reasoning-record schema (target 2026-10-31). [COR-791](https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-791/design-the-structured-reasoning-record-schema-rfd) designs the schema, [COR-792](https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-792/persist-reasoning-records-per-checkpointtrail) persists a record per checkpoint and trail.\\n\\nM2, write-back from reasoning surfaces (target 2026-11-30). [COR-793](https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-793/write-back-review-findings-durable-semantic-facts) has review findings write durable semantic facts back into memory.\\n\\nM3, provenance graph (target 2026-12-31). [COR-794](https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-794/provenance-graph-over-decisions-tasks-prs-reviews) builds a queryable graph of decision to task to PR to review.\\n\\n## ð  P3, coordinated agents\\n\\nWhat it is. Let fleets of agents build in parallel without colliding. Today agents cannot coordinate, so two agents editing the same function silently collide. P3 adds entity-level ownership, conflict detection before merge, structured handovers, and a scheduler over ready tasks. The gate is P1 durable state plus the P2 one surface, and it runs in parallel with P4. Done when two agents editing the same entity get a pre-merge conflict warning, a ready task auto-dispatches, and a handover auto-hydrates into the next agent's context.\\n\\nTracked in Linear: [Semantic Collision-Free Parallel Agents](https://linear.app/entirehq/project/semantic-collision-free-parallel-agents-e20ca0e40e08) (High, compressed target Nov 2026 to Feb 2027).\\n\\nM1, entity claims and leases (target 2026-11-30). [COR-795](https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-795/spike-evaluate-the-coordination-substrate-task-dag-handovers) evaluates the substrate, [COR-796](https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-796/entity-level-claimlease-primitive-claim-a-symbol-expiry) builds the claim primitive so an agent claims a symbol rather than a whole file, with expiry and sweep.\\n\\nM2, pre-merge conflict detection (target 2026-12-31). [COR-797](https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-797/pre-merge-semantic-conflict-detection-over-concurrent-claims) warns when two agents touch the same entity before the changes merge.\\n\\nM3, signed handovers and auto-hydration (target 2027-01-31). [COR-798](https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-798/structured-handover-schema-mcp-auto-hydration) makes handovers structured data the next agent auto-loads via MCP.\\n\\nM4, scheduler to sandboxes (target 2027-02-28). [COR-800](https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-800/scheduler-auto-dispatch-ready-tasks-to-sandboxes) auto-dispatches ready tasks into sandboxes.\\n\\nM5, presence and read-receipts. [COR-799](https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-799/agent-presence-read-receipt-messaging) adds agent presence and read-receipt messaging so an idle claim holder can be nudged or reclaimed.\\n\\n## ð´ P4, cross-repo federation\\n\\nWhat it is. Break the repo boundary. Git-native discovery stops at the repo edge, so an agent cannot find who reasoned about similar code elsewhere, and there is no registry to route a task to the right agent. P4 shares reasoning across repos and orgs, and adds a capability registry so tasks route by capability. The gate is P1 durable state plus the P2 one surface, and it runs in parallel with P3. Done when an agent working in repo A surfaces relevant reasoning from repo B, and tasks route to an agent by declared capability.\\n\\nTracked in Linear: [Cross-Repo Shared Reasoning](https://linear.app/entirehq/project/cross-repo-shared-reasoning-0f9532a0d661) (Medium, compressed target Jan to Mar 2027).\\n\\nM1, cross-repo semantic index and query (target 2027-02-28). [COR-801](https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-801/cross-repo-semantic-discovery-over-the-federated-index) queries the semantic index across repos over the federated index and mirror pipeline.\\n\\nM2, cross-org authz. [COR-802](https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-802/spike-cross-org-authz-for-shared-reasoning) defines the authorization model for sharing reasoning across orgs, building on the existing MCP and SpiceDB gating.\\n\\nM3, agent capability registry (target 2027-03-31). [COR-803](https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-803/agent-capability-registry-discovery) registers agents by capability so a task resolves to the best-fit agent.\\n\\n## ⭐ P5, behavioral intelligence: the north star\\n\\nWhat it is. The payoff the whole arc builds toward: turn retained behavior into decisions. Every prompt, session, and outcome is already captured as checkpoints; P5 mines that record. It came from the Salesforce ask and it is what makes the memory layer a product, not plumbing. The gate is the P2 one surface plus P3 coordinated execution.\\n\\nWhat it delivers.\\n\\nPrompt intelligence. Score a prompt's quality before it runs, from retained outcome signal. See which people write prompts that succeed. Surface a curated best-prompt library of exemplars mined from real checkpoints, so the org's best prompting becomes everyone's baseline.\\n\\nFit modeling. Who, or which agent or model, succeeds on what kind of task, from history instead of vibes.\\n\\nAuto-routing. Send a task to the agent or person most likely to do it well, with P4's capability registry supplying the candidates.\\n\\nFeedback loop and org dashboards. Outcomes flow back into the models; leadership watches the org learn.\\n\\nAlignment first. Alisha's MemoryRecords (Agent Improvement Engine) mines the same checkpoint stream toward the same territory, and she owns the deployed semantic search. P5 starts with a merge-of-efforts conversation, not a third parallel build. The brain brings what the others lack: facts with provenance anchors tied to commits, and brain-bench's eval discipline as the pattern for scoring the prompt-quality classifier.\\n\\nTracked in Linear: [P5 · Behavioral Intelligence (North Star)](https://linear.app/entirehq/project/p5-behavioral-intelligence-north-star-1bb9991bc853) (High, target Jan to Jun 2027).\\n\\nM1, prompt-quality classifier (target 2027-02-28): score prompts from outcome signal (checkpoint success, iteration count, review outcomes).\\n\\nM2, per-person profiles and the best-prompt library (target 2027-03-31): which employees write prompts that succeed, and the best of their prompts, curated from real checkpoints.\\n\\nM3, agent and person to task fit (target 2027-04-30): the fit model over checkpoint history.\\n\\nM4, auto-routing (target 2027-05-31): route work to the best-fit agent or person.\\n\\nM5, feedback loop and org dashboards (target 2027-06-30): close the loop, show the learning.\\n\\n## ð Full tracking table\\n\\nEvery issue links to Linear. Priorities are U (urgent), H (high), M (medium).\\n\\n| Phase | Milestone (target) | Issue | Pri |\\n| :-: | :-: | :-: | :-: |\\n| ð¢ P0 Keystone | Entity deltas in checkpoint metadata (2026-08-15) | [COR-781](https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-781/spike-map-semantic-extractor-snapshot-checkpoint-metadata-schema) Spike: extractor snapshot to metadata schema | U |\\n| ð¢ P0 Keystone | Entity deltas in checkpoint metadata (2026-08-15) | [COR-782](https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-782/embed-entity-deltas-into-the-checkpoint-metadata-write-path) Embed entity deltas into the write path | U |\\n| ð¢ P0 Keystone | Git-native entity to checkpoint index (2026-09-15) | [COR-783](https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-783/build-the-git-native-entity-checkpoint-index) Build the git-native index | H |\\n| ð¢ P0 Keystone | Git-native entity to checkpoint index (2026-09-15) | [COR-784](https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-784/mcp-tool-query-checkpointssessions-by-semantic-entity) MCP tool: query by entity | H |\\n| ð¢ P0 Keystone | Transparency-log semantic causality (2026-09-30) | [COR-785](https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-785/tie-transparency-log-events-to-semantic-causality) Tie events to causality | M |\\n| ð£ P2 Unified memory | Converge code search (2026-09-30) | [COR-786](https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-786/decision-rfd-converge-code-search-on-one-engine-deprecate-duplicates) RFD: converge code search | H |\\n| ð£ P2 Unified memory | Converge code search (2026-09-30) | [COR-787](https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-787/ship-the-converged-code-search-service) Ship converged code-search | H |\\n| ð£ P2 Unified memory | Unified knowledge backbone (2026-10-31) | [COR-788](https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-788/unify-knowledge-code-artifact-indexes-on-one-embedding-backbone) Unify indexes on one backbone | H |\\n| ð£ P2 Unified memory | Single MCP surface (2026-11-30) | [COR-789](https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-789/single-mcp-shared-memory-tool-over-code-knowledge-semantic-index) Single MCP shared-memory tool | H |\\n| ð£ P2 Unified memory | Single MCP surface (2026-11-30) | [COR-790](https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-790/retire-duplicate-search-and-knowledge-paths) Retire duplicate paths | M |\\n| ð¡ Reasoning capture | Record schema (2026-10-31) | [COR-791](https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-791/design-the-structured-reasoning-record-schema-rfd) Design the record schema | H |\\n| ð¡ Reasoning capture | Record schema (2026-10-31) | [COR-792](https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-792/persist-reasoning-records-per-checkpointtrail) Persist records per checkpoint | H |\\n| ð¡ Reasoning capture | Write-back (2026-11-30) | [COR-793](https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-793/write-back-review-findings-durable-semantic-facts) Write-back findings to facts | H |\\n| ð¡ Reasoning capture | Provenance graph (2026-12-31) | [COR-794](https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-794/provenance-graph-over-decisions-tasks-prs-reviews) Provenance graph | M |\\n| ð  P3 Coordinated agents | Claims and leases (2026-11-30) | [COR-795](https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-795/spike-evaluate-the-coordination-substrate-task-dag-handovers) Spike: coordination substrate | H |\\n| ð  P3 Coordinated agents | Claims and leases (2026-11-30) | [COR-796](https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-796/entity-level-claimlease-primitive-claim-a-symbol-expiry) Entity-level claim primitive | H |\\n| ð  P3 Coordinated agents | Pre-merge conflict detection (2026-12-31) | [COR-797](https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-797/pre-merge-semantic-conflict-detection-over-concurrent-claims) Pre-merge conflict detection | H |\\n| ð  P3 Coordinated agents | Handovers and auto-hydration (2027-01-31) | [COR-798](https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-798/structured-handover-schema-mcp-auto-hydration) Structured handover schema | H |\\n| ð  P3 Coordinated agents | Handovers and auto-hydration (2027-01-31) | [COR-799](https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-799/agent-presence-read-receipt-messaging) Presence and read-receipts | M |\\n| ð  P3 Coordinated agents | Scheduler to sandboxes (2027-02-28) | [COR-800](https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-800/scheduler-auto-dispatch-ready-tasks-to-sandboxes) Scheduler to sandboxes | M |\\n| ð´ P4 Federation | Cross-repo discovery (2027-02-28) | [COR-801](https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-801/cross-repo-semantic-discovery-over-the-federated-index) Cross-repo semantic discovery | M |\\n| ð´ P4 Federation | Cross-repo discovery (2027-02-28) | [COR-802](https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-802/spike-cross-org-authz-for-shared-reasoning) Spike: cross-org authz | M |\\n| ð´ P4 Federation | Capability registry (2027-03-31) | [COR-803](https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-803/agent-capability-registry-discovery) Agent capability registry | M |\\n| ⭐ P5 North star | Prompt-quality classifier (2027-02-28) | milestone (issues to be scoped) | H |\\n| ⭐ P5 North star | Per-person profiles + best-prompt library (2027-03-31) | milestone (issues to be scoped) | H |\\n| ⭐ P5 North star | Agent and person to task fit (2027-04-30) | milestone (issues to be scoped) | H |\\n| ⭐ P5 North star | Auto-routing (2027-05-31) | milestone (issues to be scoped) | H |\\n| ⭐ P5 North star | Feedback loop + org dashboards (2027-06-30) | milestone (issues to be scoped) | H |\\n\\nTotals: 8 Linear projects under the initiative (the five arc projects plus P0, P1, and P5), 29 milestones, 23 scoped issues (COR-781 through COR-803); P0, P1, and P5 carry milestones with issues to be scoped.\\n\\n## Architecture decisions\\n\\nADR-1, schema freeze. The brain wire schema is major.minor, additive minors, tolerant readers. From P0.\\n\\nADR-P1-A, opt-in egress. Hosted publish is never implicit. It is gated on an explicit entire brain publish plus ENTIRE\\\\_BRAIN\\\\_ALLOW\\\\_HOSTED.\\n\\nADR-P1-C, branch build model. A default push builds a baseline, a feature branch builds an overlay, merge promotes it, delete garbage-collects it.\\n\\nADR-P1-D, platform target. The post-refactor mirror and decentralized architecture. Treat interfaces as a moving target. The intent is for the brain store to ride entiredb (objstore for blobs, refstore for the fact CAS, rsl for the audit log), with per-object encryption and crypto-shred as the one capability that still needs a home.\\n\\n## Critical path\\n\\nP0 finishes the brain. P1 is the linchpin, since store, sync, query, and auth unblock everything else. The keystone semantic index and unified memory land next, and the P2 single MCP surface is the chokepoint every downstream tool registers on. Reasoning capture builds on the record schema and the unified surface. Coordinated agents and cross-repo federation both need P1 plus the one surface, and they run in parallel.\\n\\n## ð Links\\n\\nInitiative: [Semantic Reasoning Layer](https://linear.app/entirehq/initiative/semantic-reasoning-layer-e043385c2167)\\n\\nVision: [entire.io/vision](https://entire.io/vision)\\n\\nP1 store and sync: [entire-api PR \\\\#242](https://github.com/entirehq/entire-api/pull/242)\\n\\nP1 client: [entire-brain PR \\\\#65](https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/65)\\n\\nP1 review: [Trail \\\\#243](https://entire.io/gh/entirehq/entire-api/trails/243)\\n\\nKeystone: [Semantic Index Tied to VCS History](https://linear.app/entirehq/project/semantic-index-tied-to-vcs-history-ea453fa387e2)\\n\\n[Unified, Pluggable Agent Memory](https://linear.app/entirehq/project/unified-pluggable-agent-memory-eaf5762e7339)\\n\\n[Reasoning Capture and Compounding Memory](https://linear.app/entirehq/project/reasoning-capture-and-compounding-memory-db95c0b2ef1c)\\n\\n[Semantic Collision-Free Parallel Agents](https://linear.app/entirehq/project/semantic-collision-free-parallel-agents-e20ca0e40e08)\\n\\n[Cross-Repo Shared Reasoning](https://linear.app/entirehq/project/cross-repo-shared-reasoning-0f9532a0d661)\\n\\n[P5 · Behavioral Intelligence (North Star)](https://linear.app/entirehq/project/p5-behavioral-intelligence-north-star-1bb9991bc853)\\n\\nLandscape repos read for the convergence calls: entirehq/mcp, entirehq/librarian, entirehq/entire-search, entirehq/peregrine\\n\\nOne housekeeping note. The initiative is Active. The 23 Linear issues above (COR-781 through COR-803) were created on 2026-07-01 and are currently in a Canceled state in Linear, so they nee\"}"}]},"uuid":"36437a3d-c65c-4361-a937-3eacdf0a0553","timestamp":"2026-08-18T18:12:55.744Z","toolUseResult":"{\"fileContent\":\"# ð§  The Semantic Reasoning Layer: Roadmap\\n\\nTurn the local brain into a shared reasoning substrate that a fleet of agents builds on. Git preserves change, but it does not preserve meaning. This initiative gives every agent persistent, shared, pluggable memory tied to git history, so humans and agents can reason and build in parallel without colliding.\\n\\nInitiative: [Semantic Reasoning Layer](https://linear.app/entirehq/initiative/semantic-reasoning-layer-e043385c2167) (Linear, Active) · Vision: [entire.io/vision](https://entire.io/vision) · As of: July 2026\\n\\nThe arc: ð¢ P0 finish the brain, then ðµ P1 host it, then ð£ P2 unify memory behind one surface, then ð  P3 coordinate fleets and ð´ P4 federate across repos in parallel, all feeding ⭐ P5, the north star: behavioral intelligence, where retained behavior becomes decisions (best-agent routing, prompt quality per person, a best-prompt library).\\n\\nGoverning constraint: no new infrastructure. The whole arc rides entire.io's existing rails (entiredb, checkpoint\\\\_remote, snapshotstore and snapshotcrypt, authz and SpiceDB, the jurisdiction forwarder). Each milestone ports proven parts onto the brain model rather than building storage or crypto from scratch.\\n\\n## ð Timeline at a glance\\n\\nTarget: the whole roadmap complete by end of March 2027. The schedule below is the compressed plan to hit that date. The dates run tight and in parallel from P2 onward.\\n\\n| Phase | Focus | Window | Status |\\n| :-: | :-: | :-: | :-: |\\n| ð¢ P0 GA the local brain | Harden entire-sem, brain, MCP surface, bench | Jul to Aug 2026 | Ships today, GA wrapper in progress |\\n| ðµ P1 Shared / hosted brain | Server store, sync, remote query, auth | Now, ship Aug 2026 | Built and tested on clones, one step from prod |\\n| ð§© Keystone: semantic index tied to VCS | Entity deltas, git-native index, causality | Aug to Sep 2026 | Planned |\\n| ð£ P2 Unified memory, one MCP surface | Converge search, one backbone, one surface | Sep to Nov 2026 | Planned |\\n| ð¡ Reasoning capture, compounding memory | Record schema, write-back, provenance graph | Oct to Dec 2026 | Planned |\\n| ð  P3 Coordinated agents | Claims, conflict detection, handovers, scheduler | Nov 2026 to Feb 2027 | Planned |\\n| ð´ P4 Cross-repo federation | Federated discovery, capability registry | Jan to Mar 2027 | Planned |\\n| ⭐ P5 Behavioral intelligence (north star) | Prompt quality, best-prompt library, fit, auto-routing | Jan to Jun 2027 | Planned |\\n\\nThe March 2027 target covers the enabling phases (P0 through P4). The P5 north star starts as soon as P2's surface and P3's coordination land, and runs to June 2027. Linear milestone dates now match the compressed schedule.\\n\\n## ð¢ P0, GA the local brain\\n\\nWhat it is. The foundation the whole initiative stands on. The local brain already runs, so P0 is finish work and release hygiene, not new build. There is no gate here. Everything ships today, but nothing is formally tagged, so P0 is the wrapper that makes it something the rest of the arc can depend on.\\n\\nThe pieces, all live today.\\n\\nentire-sem is the semantic provider. It parses code into symbols and relations with tree-sitter, and it uses no vectors anywhere in the stack.\\n\\nentire-brain is the local brain. It holds durable, branch-scoped, provenance-anchored facts, plus a local MCP surface of about 33 tools that agents query.\\n\\nbrain-bench is the CI gate. It benchmarks the extractor against a reference tool across roughly 30 languages and fails the build on regression or drift.\\n\\nThe milestones.\\n\\nM1, harden and GA entire-sem. Version-stamp it and freeze the schema so everything downstream can trust the contract.\\n\\nM2, close the brain blockers. Ship the local brain with honest claims, no overreach.\\n\\nM3, GA the MCP surface for both plugins. Harden the local tool surface for the Claude Code and Codex plugins.\\n\\nM4, brain-bench as the automated eval gate. Make the benchmark a required regression floor.\\n\\nM5, release logistics. The release checklist, the compatibility matrix, and distribution.\\n\\nFoundation build tracked in Linear: [Semantic Index Tied to VCS History](https://linear.app/entirehq/project/semantic-index-tied-to-vcs-history-ea453fa387e2) (Urgent). This is the piece that persists entity-level meaning onto checkpoints and a git-native index, so meaning is stored with git history and not re-parsed on demand. Done when entire and MCP can answer \\\"which checkpoints changed entity X\\\" from the index.\\n\\nEntity deltas in checkpoint metadata (target 2026-08-15): [COR-781](https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-781/spike-map-semantic-extractor-snapshot-checkpoint-metadata-schema) spike the schema, then [COR-782](https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-782/embed-entity-deltas-into-the-checkpoint-metadata-write-path) embed the deltas into the write path.\\n\\nGit-native entity to checkpoint index (target 2026-09-15): [COR-783](https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-783/build-the-git-native-entity-checkpoint-index) build the index, [COR-784](https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-784/mcp-tool-query-checkpointssessions-by-semantic-entity) expose it as an MCP tool.\\n\\nTransparency-log semantic causality (target 2026-09-30): [COR-785](https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-785/tie-transparency-log-events-to-semantic-causality) tie ref-change events to the session and entities that caused them.\\n\\n## ðµ P1, shared / hosted brain ⭐\\n\\nWhat it is. The differentiator. P1 lifts the brain off the laptop into a shared, server-side, multi-tenant service, so one member's agent learns something and every other member's agent can read it. The gate is the P0 schema-freeze plus a namespace, and it deliberately relaxes the local-only guardrail. All four parts are built and DB-tested on clone branches, race-clean, and awaiting merge.\\n\\nThe milestones.\\n\\nM1, server-side brain store. Content-addressed and authz-gated, encrypted at rest. Every artifact gets a fresh per-object key, AES-256-GCM, KMS-wrapped, bound to the repo and artifact, with crypto-shred of the key on retract so a removed fact becomes provably unreadable.\\n\\nM2, sync protocol over checkpoint\\\\_remote and entiredb. Durable facts sync under compare-and-swap on the branch head. The tenancy key is the injective slug@ULID, a lost race returns 412, and every advance appends to a tamper-evident hash-chained log.\\n\\nM3, multi-machine shared query. A remote MCP transport over HTTP, so a teammate's agent queries the shared brain without a local clone. The facts tools serve now. Direction: this endpoint becomes the backend of a brain surface on entirehq/mcp (the one hosted connector), not a second standalone connector.\\n\\nM4, auth and tenancy. Multi-tenant isolation on the org, project, repo SpiceDB cascade, with two independent fail-closed layers.\\n\\nWhat P1 rides and reuses (locked in after the landscape review).\\n\\nTransport: entirehq/mcp. James's hosted connector already solves OAuth, per-principal token exchange, tenancy, and discovery for about 60 tools. The brain registers a tool surface there; M3's endpoint is that surface's backend. No second connector, no duplicate auth plumbing.\\n\\nStorage direction: EntireDB. Blobs onto objstore, the fact CAS onto refstore, the audit log onto rsl, aligned with the git-meta move. This work is owned in decentralized-architecture, with the brain as its first customer and forcing function. The organizing rule: the brain owns the what and the when; decentralized-architecture owns the shared rails, because a capability with many consumers lives with the platform, not inside one product.\\n\\nEncryption honesty. Per-object DEKs and crypto-shred exist because the current store is one bucket shared across tenants (separate orgs). In-repo or in EntireDB under the repo's own trust boundary, that need mostly falls away, so the crypto layer is a property of where the data sits, not of the data.\\n\\nHardening state. Both PRs went through a 4-angle cleanup pass (reuse, simplification, efficiency, altitude): one shared AWS store builder, no double-hashing on the publish path, narrowed validation interface, egress-toggle warning parity with the CLI. Trail re-review pending on the latest push.\\n\\nLinks. [entire-api PR \\\\#242](https://github.com/entirehq/entire-api/pull/242) is the store, sync, remote MCP, and tenancy, roughly +8,532 lines. [entire-brain PR \\\\#65](https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/65) is the client wire fixes. [Trail \\\\#243](https://entire.io/gh/entirehq/entire-api/trails/243) is entire.io's own AI review, with 0 open findings and risk around 62%.\\n\\nWhere the storage is headed. The brain is in-repo by design already, keyed by repo, branch, and commit, and the hosted service exists only for the shared, authed query that a file in one clone cannot serve. The store rides the session-share stack today (S3 plus KMS) because that was the fastest proven path to ship P1, but the target is to push it down into EntireDB so it inherits resiliency and replication for free: the artifact blobs onto objstore, the fact-set CAS onto refstore, the audit log onto rsl. The one piece EntireDB does not cover yet is encryption at rest with a per-object key and crypto-shred, and that only matters because the current store is shared across tenants, meaning separate orgs in one bucket. In-repo, under the repo's own trust boundary, that need mostly falls away, so the direction is to ride EntireDB and add per-object encrypt and shred there only if a shared store still requires it.\\n\\n### ð Shipping P1, staging to production\\n\\nThe path is staging-first and reversible, so nothing turns on by accident.\\n\\nMerge [PR \\\\#242](https://github.com/entirehq/entire-api/pull/242) and [PR \\\\#65](https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/65) into main, one approval each.\\n\\nStaging deploys automatically. The brain migrations (brain\\\\_deks, brain\\\\_overlay\\\\_branches, brain\\\\_fact\\\\_refs, brain\\\\_fact\\\\_advances) apply on deploy and are additive only.\\n\\nEnable on staging. Set ENTIRE\\\\_BRAIN\\\\_HOSTED\\\\_ENABLED=true on the US and EU staging cells.\\n\\nSmoke test on partial.to. Publish a brain, advance a fact-set under CAS, and read it back over the remote MCP transport.\\n\\nPromote to production. Set the same one env var on the US and EU prod cells. That is the activation.\\n\\nRollback is instant. Unset the flag and every endpoint fails closed to 503, with data left sealed and dormant.\\n\\nThe only new setting is ENTIRE\\\\_BRAIN\\\\_HOSTED\\\\_ENABLED=true. Everything else is reused, since the brain shares session-share's already-live ENTIRE\\\\_SNAPSHOT\\\\_CIPHER=aws, its S3 bucket, and its KMS key, so there is no new bucket, key, IAM policy, or AWS credential. Until the flag is set, the endpoints fail closed to 503, so merging ships the code dormant on production.\\n\\n## ðº️ The landscape: what already exists, and how the plan converges it\\n\\nFour systems already live in this space. The plan does not route around them, it converges onto them. This is grounded in a full read of each codebase.\\n\\nentirehq/mcp (James). A hosted, multi-tenant, stateless remote MCP proxy: about 60 tools over four upstreams, Streamable HTTP, OAuth resource server with per-principal token exchange, all authorization downstream in SpiceDB. It stores nothing. It is the one hosted MCP transport, and it is architected to add tool surfaces. Decision: the brain does not ship its own standalone MCP connector. The hosted brain is an upstream data service, exposed as a brain surface on this server. P1.M3's transport work becomes the backend that surface calls.\\n\\nlibrarian (Alex). A knowledge-indexing and hybrid-search service over team communications and docs: Slack threads, Linear issues, GitHub PRs and issues, markdown. Postgres plus pgvector, its own 768-dim embedding stack (nomic-embed-text on Ollama), RRF fusion, no S3, no code, no sessions. Its roadmap heads toward an entity graph and synthesized views over the same checkpoint stream the brain distills. Librarian is the who-and-why half of team memory (comms); the brain is the what-and-where half (code, keyed to git). The facts and synthesis layer must be negotiated between the two, plus Alisha's MemoryRecords, before either builds further.\\n\\nentire-search (Alisha, deployed, serves entire.io search today). Product-entity search: checkpoint transcript chunks, commits, PRs. Cohere embed-v4.0 (1536-dim) with vectors in Turbopuffer, BM25 plus ANN with a tier system, SpiceDB ACL fan-out. It deliberately strips code before indexing. Near-zero overlap with the brain: different corpus, different store. The seam is checkpoints, which both consume; a distilled brain fact is a better search document than a raw transcript chunk, a future feed-in, not a conflict.\\n\\nperegrine (Evis, staging, prod target July). Trigram lexical code search, the Zoekt replacement: regex and full-text over source at platform scale, one index file per repo on S3, plus a tree-sitter symbol layer (15 languages, definition and reference extraction, query-time go-to-def). Zero embeddings. The one real duplication in the landscape: entire-sem and peregrine both maintain per-language tree-sitter extractors. Peregrine has no typed relation graph (its only edge is an untyped ref-to-def link) while entire-sem emits a 30-type relation graph (CALLS, EXTENDS, IMPLEMENTS, DATA\\\\_FLOWS). Peregrine reserved explicit extension slots (SymbolSource::Scip, SymbolPrecision::Semantic) for a higher-precision external symbol producer. Decision to pursue: entire-sem feeds peregrine's symbol overlay, one extractor serving both, with peregrine the find-text-fast engine and the brain the understand-structure engine.\\n\\nAlisha's MemoryRecords (Agent Improvement Engine). The sharpest overlap in the company: it derives memory from the same checkpoint stream the brain distills facts from, the descriptive and prescriptive halves of one problem. It also sits directly under the P5 north star (prompt quality, fit, routing), and Alisha owns the deployed semantic search too, so she holds two seats at the convergence table. Decision: align with Alisha before building the facts layer or P5 further; P5 should merge efforts, not add a third parallel one.\\n\\nThe score that motivates P2: four search systems live or half-live, three embedding backbones (Cohere 1536, nomic 768, and none), and at least two tree-sitter extractors. P2's converge-code-search RFD ([COR-786](https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-786/decision-rfd-converge-code-search-on-one-engine-deprecate-duplicates)) and one-backbone milestone ([COR-788](https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-788/unify-knowledge-code-artifact-indexes-on-one-embedding-backbone)) are exactly this cleanup.\\n\\n## ð£ P2, unified memory, one MCP surface\\n\\nWhat it is. The chokepoint. Today retrieval and knowledge are fragmented across several parallel code-search efforts and two parallel knowledge systems. P2 converges them into one shared memory on one embedding backbone, exposed through MCP, so every agent (Claude Code, Codex, Droid, Cursor, Gemini) queries the same thing with the same tools. The gate is P1 transport plus auth, and it is the surface every downstream tool registers on. Done when one MCP tool returns unified results across code and knowledge, and only one search engine and one embedding backbone remain in production.\\n\\nTracked in Linear: [Unified, Pluggable Agent Memory](https://linear.app/entirehq/project/unified-pluggable-agent-memory-eaf5762e7339) (High, compressed target Sep to Nov 2026).\\n\\nM1, converge code-search into one engine (target 2026-09-30). [COR-786](https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-786/decision-rfd-converge-code-search-on-one-engine-deprecate-duplicates) is the RFD that picks one direction, and [COR-787](https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-787/ship-the-converged-code-search-service) ships the converged code-search service.\\n\\nM2, converge knowledge into one backbone (target 2026-10-31). [COR-788](https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-788/unify-knowledge-code-artifact-indexes-on-one-embedding-backbone) unifies the knowledge and code-artifact indexes on one embedding backbone.\\n\\nM3, expose brain plus code-search plus knowledge behind one MCP surface (target 2026-11-30). [COR-789](https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-789/single-mcp-shared-memory-tool-over-code-knowledge-semantic-index) is the single MCP shared-memory tool.\\n\\nM4, retire duplicates and prove no regression. [COR-790](https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-790/retire-duplicate-search-and-knowledge-paths) decommissions the superseded search and knowledge paths once the unified surface is in production.\\n\\n## ð¡ Reasoning capture and compounding memory\\n\\nWhat it is. The companion to P2 that makes memory compound. Agents capture transcripts, not reasoning, and the reasoning surfaces we have emit prose that gets overwritten, so understanding restarts every run. This captures agent reasoning as structured, queryable facts written back into shared memory, so a later run inherits what an earlier one learned. It rides on the unified surface and the keystone entity deltas. Done when a second agent run reuses the first run's structured reasoning rather than re-deriving it, and a provenance query returns the decision cascade.\\n\\nTracked in Linear: [Reasoning Capture and Compounding Memory](https://linear.app/entirehq/project/reasoning-capture-and-compounding-memory-db95c0b2ef1c) (High, target Oct to Dec 2026).\\n\\nM1, structured reasoning-record schema (target 2026-10-31). [COR-791](https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-791/design-the-structured-reasoning-record-schema-rfd) designs the schema, [COR-792](https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-792/persist-reasoning-records-per-checkpointtrail) persists a record per checkpoint and trail.\\n\\nM2, write-back from reasoning surfaces (target 2026-11-30). [COR-793](https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-793/write-back-review-findings-durable-semantic-facts) has review findings write durable semantic facts back into memory.\\n\\nM3, provenance graph (target 2026-12-31). [COR-794](https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-794/provenance-graph-over-decisions-tasks-prs-reviews) builds a queryable graph of decision to task to PR to review.\\n\\n## ð  P3, coordinated agents\\n\\nWhat it is. Let fleets of agents build in parallel without colliding. Today agents cannot coordinate, so two agents editing the same function silently collide. P3 adds entity-level ownership, conflict detection before merge, structured handovers, and a scheduler over ready tasks. The gate is P1 durable state plus the P2 one surface, and it runs in parallel with P4. Done when two agents editing the same entity get a pre-merge conflict warning, a ready task auto-dispatches, and a handover auto-hydrates into the next agent's context.\\n\\nTracked in Linear: [Semantic Collision-Free Parallel Agents](https://linear.app/entirehq/project/semantic-collision-free-parallel-agents-e20ca0e40e08) (High, compressed target Nov 2026 to Feb 2027).\\n\\nM1, entity claims and leases (target 2026-11-30). [COR-795](https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-795/spike-evaluate-the-coordination-substrate-task-dag-handovers) evaluates the substrate, [COR-796](https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-796/entity-level-claimlease-primitive-claim-a-symbol-expiry) builds the claim primitive so an agent claims a symbol rather than a whole file, with expiry and sweep.\\n\\nM2, pre-merge conflict detection (target 2026-12-31). [COR-797](https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-797/pre-merge-semantic-conflict-detection-over-concurrent-claims) warns when two agents touch the same entity before the changes merge.\\n\\nM3, signed handovers and auto-hydration (target 2027-01-31). [COR-798](https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-798/structured-handover-schema-mcp-auto-hydration) makes handovers structured data the next agent auto-loads via MCP.\\n\\nM4, scheduler to sandboxes (target 2027-02-28). [COR-800](https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-800/scheduler-auto-dispatch-ready-tasks-to-sandboxes) auto-dispatches ready tasks into sandboxes.\\n\\nM5, presence and read-receipts. [COR-799](https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-799/agent-presence-read-receipt-messaging) adds agent presence and read-receipt messaging so an idle claim holder can be nudged or reclaimed.\\n\\n## ð´ P4, cross-repo federation\\n\\nWhat it is. Break the repo boundary. Git-native discovery stops at the repo edge, so an agent cannot find who reasoned about similar code elsewhere, and there is no registry to route a task to the right agent. P4 shares reasoning across repos and orgs, and adds a capability registry so tasks route by capability. The gate is P1 durable state plus the P2 one surface, and it runs in parallel with P3. Done when an agent working in repo A surfaces relevant reasoning from repo B, and tasks route to an agent by declared capability.\\n\\nTracked in Linear: [Cross-Repo Shared Reasoning](https://linear.app/entirehq/project/cross-repo-shared-reasoning-0f9532a0d661) (Medium, compressed target Jan to Mar 2027).\\n\\nM1, cross-repo semantic index and query (target 2027-02-28). [COR-801](https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-801/cross-repo-semantic-discovery-over-the-federated-index) queries the semantic index across repos over the federated index and mirror pipeline.\\n\\nM2, cross-org authz. [COR-802](https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-802/spike-cross-org-authz-for-shared-reasoning) defines the authorization model for sharing reasoning across orgs, building on the existing MCP and SpiceDB gating.\\n\\nM3, agent capability registry (target 2027-03-31). [COR-803](https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-803/agent-capability-registry-discovery) registers agents by capability so a task resolves to the best-fit agent.\\n\\n## ⭐ P5, behavioral intelligence: the north star\\n\\nWhat it is. The payoff the whole arc builds toward: turn retained behavior into decisions. Every prompt, session, and outcome is already captured as checkpoints; P5 mines that record. It came from the Salesforce ask and it is what makes the memory layer a product, not plumbing. The gate is the P2 one surface plus P3 coordinated execution.\\n\\nWhat it delivers.\\n\\nPrompt intelligence. Score a prompt's quality before it runs, from retained outcome signal. See which people write prompts that succeed. Surface a curated best-prompt library of exemplars mined from real checkpoints, so the org's best prompting becomes everyone's baseline.\\n\\nFit modeling. Who, or which agent or model, succeeds on what kind of task, from history instead of vibes.\\n\\nAuto-routing. Send a task to the agent or person most likely to do it well, with P4's capability registry supplying the candidates.\\n\\nFeedback loop and org dashboards. Outcomes flow back into the models; leadership watches the org learn.\\n\\nAlignment first. Alisha's MemoryRecords (Agent Improvement Engine) mines the same checkpoint stream toward the same territory, and she owns the deployed semantic search. P5 starts with a merge-of-efforts conversation, not a third parallel build. The brain brings what the others lack: facts with provenance anchors tied to commits, and brain-bench's eval discipline as the pattern for scoring the prompt-quality classifier.\\n\\nTracked in Linear: [P5 · Behavioral Intelligence (North Star)](https://linear.app/entirehq/project/p5-behavioral-intelligence-north-star-1bb9991bc853) (High, target Jan to Jun 2027).\\n\\nM1, prompt-quality classifier (target 2027-02-28): score prompts from outcome signal (checkpoint success, iteration count, review outcomes).\\n\\nM2, per-person profiles and the best-prompt library (target 2027-03-31): which employees write prompts that succeed, and the best of their prompts, curated from real checkpoints.\\n\\nM3, agent and person to task fit (target 2027-04-30): the fit model over checkpoint history.\\n\\nM4, auto-routing (target 2027-05-31): route work to the best-fit agent or person.\\n\\nM5, feedback loop and org dashboards (target 2027-06-30): close the loop, show the learning.\\n\\n## ð Full tracking table\\n\\nEvery issue links to Linear. Priorities are U (urgent), H (high), M (medium).\\n\\n| Phase | Milestone (target) | Issue | Pri |\\n| :-: | :-: | :-: | :-: |\\n| ð¢ P0 Keystone | Entity deltas in checkpoint metadata (2026-08-15) | [COR-781](https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-781/spike-map-semantic-extractor-snapshot-checkpoint-metadata-schema) Spike: extractor snapshot to metadata schema | U |\\n| ð¢ P0 Keystone | Entity deltas in checkpoint metadata (2026-08-15) | [COR-782](https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-782/embed-entity-deltas-into-the-checkpoint-metadata-write-path) Embed entity deltas into the write path | U |\\n| ð¢ P0 Keystone | Git-native entity to checkpoint index (2026-09-15) | [COR-783](https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-783/build-the-git-native-entity-checkpoint-index) Build the git-native index | H |\\n| ð¢ P0 Keystone | Git-native entity to checkpoint index (2026-09-15) | [COR-784](https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-784/mcp-tool-query-checkpointssessions-by-semantic-entity) MCP tool: query by entity | H |\\n| ð¢ P0 Keystone | Transparency-log semantic causality (2026-09-30) | [COR-785](https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-785/tie-transparency-log-events-to-semantic-causality) Tie events to causality | M |\\n| ð£ P2 Unified memory | Converge code search (2026-09-30) | [COR-786](https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-786/decision-rfd-converge-code-search-on-one-engine-deprecate-duplicates) RFD: converge code search | H |\\n| ð£ P2 Unified memory | Converge code search (2026-09-30) | [COR-787](https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-787/ship-the-converged-code-search-service) Ship converged code-search | H |\\n| ð£ P2 Unified memory | Unified knowledge backbone (2026-10-31) | [COR-788](https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-788/unify-knowledge-code-artifact-indexes-on-one-embedding-backbone) Unify indexes on one backbone | H |\\n| ð£ P2 Unified memory | Single MCP surface (2026-11-30) | [COR-789](https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-789/single-mcp-shared-memory-tool-over-code-knowledge-semantic-index) Single MCP shared-memory tool | H |\\n| ð£ P2 Unified memory | Single MCP surface (2026-11-30) | [COR-790](https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-790/retire-duplicate-search-and-knowledge-paths) Retire duplicate paths | M |\\n| ð¡ Reasoning capture | Record schema (2026-10-31) | [COR-791](https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-791/design-the-structured-reasoning-record-schema-rfd) Design the record schema | H |\\n| ð¡ Reasoning capture | Record schema (2026-10-31) | [COR-792](https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-792/persist-reasoning-records-per-checkpointtrail) Persist records per checkpoint | H |\\n| ð¡ Reasoning capture | Write-back (2026-11-30) | [COR-793](https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-793/write-back-review-findings-durable-semantic-facts) Write-back findings to facts | H |\\n| ð¡ Reasoning capture | Provenance graph (2026-12-31) | [COR-794](https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-794/provenance-graph-over-decisions-tasks-prs-reviews) Provenance graph | M |\\n| ð  P3 Coordinated agents | Claims and leases (2026-11-30) | [COR-795](https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-795/spike-evaluate-the-coordination-substrate-task-dag-handovers) Spike: coordination substrate | H |\\n| ð  P3 Coordinated agents | Claims and leases (2026-11-30) | [COR-796](https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-796/entity-level-claimlease-primitive-claim-a-symbol-expiry) Entity-level claim primitive | H |\\n| ð  P3 Coordinated agents | Pre-merge conflict detection (2026-12-31) | [COR-797](https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-797/pre-merge-semantic-conflict-detection-over-concurrent-claims) Pre-merge conflict detection | H |\\n| ð  P3 Coordinated agents | Handovers and auto-hydration (2027-01-31) | [COR-798](https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-798/structured-handover-schema-mcp-auto-hydration) Structured handover schema | H |\\n| ð  P3 Coordinated agents | Handovers and auto-hydration (2027-01-31) | [COR-799](https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-799/agent-presence-read-receipt-messaging) Presence and read-receipts | M |\\n| ð  P3 Coordinated agents | Scheduler to sandboxes (2027-02-28) | [COR-800](https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-800/scheduler-auto-dispatch-ready-tasks-to-sandboxes) Scheduler to sandboxes | M |\\n| ð´ P4 Federation | Cross-repo discovery (2027-02-28) | [COR-801](https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-801/cross-repo-semantic-discovery-over-the-federated-index) Cross-repo semantic discovery | M |\\n| ð´ P4 Federation | Cross-repo discovery (2027-02-28) | [COR-802](https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-802/spike-cross-org-authz-for-shared-reasoning) Spike: cross-org authz | M |\\n| ð´ P4 Federation | Capability registry (2027-03-31) | [COR-803](https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-803/agent-capability-registry-discovery) Agent capability registry | M |\\n| ⭐ P5 North star | Prompt-quality classifier (2027-02-28) | milestone (issues to be scoped) | H |\\n| ⭐ P5 North star | Per-person profiles + best-prompt library (2027-03-31) | milestone (issues to be scoped) | H |\\n| ⭐ P5 North star | Agent and person to task fit (2027-04-30) | milestone (issues to be scoped) | H |\\n| ⭐ P5 North star | Auto-routing (2027-05-31) | milestone (issues to be scoped) | H |\\n| ⭐ P5 North star | Feedback loop + org dashboards (2027-06-30) | milestone (issues to be scoped) | H |\\n\\nTotals: 8 Linear projects under the initiative (the five arc projects plus P0, P1, and P5), 29 milestones, 23 scoped issues (COR-781 through COR-803); P0, P1, and P5 carry milestones with issues to be scoped.\\n\\n## Architecture decisions\\n\\nADR-1, schema freeze. The brain wire schema is major.minor, additive minors, tolerant readers. From P0.\\n\\nADR-P1-A, opt-in egress. Hosted publish is never implicit. It is gated on an explicit entire brain publish plus ENTIRE\\\\_BRAIN\\\\_ALLOW\\\\_HOSTED.\\n\\nADR-P1-C, branch build model. A default push builds a baseline, a feature branch builds an overlay, merge promotes it, delete garbage-collects it.\\n\\nADR-P1-D, platform target. The post-refactor mirror and decentralized architecture. Treat interfaces as a moving target. The intent is for the brain store to ride entiredb (objstore for blobs, refstore for the fact CAS, rsl for the audit log), with per-object encryption and crypto-shred as the one capability that still needs a home.\\n\\n## Critical path\\n\\nP0 finishes the brain. P1 is the linchpin, since store, sync, query, and auth unblock everything else. The keystone semantic index and unified memory land next, and the P2 single MCP surface is the chokepoint every downstream tool registers on. Reasoning capture builds on the record schema and the unified surface. Coordinated agents and cross-repo federation both need P1 plus the one surface, and they run in parallel.\\n\\n## ð Links\\n\\nInitiative: [Semantic Reasoning Layer](https://linear.app/entirehq/initiative/semantic-reasoning-layer-e043385c2167)\\n\\nVision: [entire.io/vision](https://entire.io/vision)\\n\\nP1 store and sync: [entire-api PR \\\\#242](https://github.com/entirehq/entire-api/pull/242)\\n\\nP1 client: [entire-brain PR \\\\#65](https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/65)\\n\\nP1 review: [Trail \\\\#243](https://entire.io/gh/entirehq/entire-api/trails/243)\\n\\nKeystone: [Semantic Index Tied to VCS History](https://linear.app/entirehq/project/semantic-index-tied-to-vcs-history-ea453fa387e2)\\n\\n[Unified, Pluggable Agent Memory](https://linear.app/entirehq/project/unified-pluggable-agent-memory-eaf5762e7339)\\n\\n[Reasoning Capture and Compounding Memory](https://linear.app/entirehq/project/reasoning-capture-and-compounding-memory-db95c0b2ef1c)\\n\\n[Semantic Collision-Free Parallel Agents](https://linear.app/entirehq/project/semantic-collision-free-parallel-agents-e20ca0e40e08)\\n\\n[Cross-Repo Shared Reasoning](https://linear.app/entirehq/project/cross-repo-shared-reasoning-0f9532a0d661)\\n\\n[P5 · Behavioral Intelligence (North Star)](https://linear.app/entirehq/project/p5-behavioral-intelligence-north-star-1bb9991bc853)\\n\\nLandscape repos read for the convergence calls: entirehq/mcp, entirehq/librarian, entirehq/entire-search, entirehq/peregrine\\n\\nOne housekeeping note. The initiative is Active. The 23 Linear issues above (COR-781 through COR-803) were created on 2026-07-01 and are currently in a Canceled state in Linear, so they nee\"}","mcpMeta":{"structuredContent":{"fileContent":"# ð§  The Semantic Reasoning Layer: Roadmap\n\nTurn the local brain into a shared reasoning substrate that a fleet of agents builds on. Git preserves change, but it does not preserve meaning. This initiative gives every agent persistent, shared, pluggable memory tied to git history, so humans and agents can reason and build in parallel without colliding.\n\nInitiative: [Semantic Reasoning Layer](https://linear.app/entirehq/initiative/semantic-reasoning-layer-e043385c2167) (Linear, Active) · Vision: [entire.io/vision](https://entire.io/vision) · As of: July 2026\n\nThe arc: ð¢ P0 finish the brain, then ðµ P1 host it, then ð£ P2 unify memory behind one surface, then ð  P3 coordinate fleets and ð´ P4 federate across repos in parallel, all feeding ⭐ P5, the north star: behavioral intelligence, where retained behavior becomes decisions (best-agent routing, prompt quality per person, a best-prompt library).\n\nGoverning constraint: no new infrastructure. The whole arc rides entire.io's existing rails (entiredb, checkpoint\\_remote, snapshotstore and snapshotcrypt, authz and SpiceDB, the jurisdiction forwarder). Each milestone ports proven parts onto the brain model rather than building storage or crypto from scratch.\n\n## ð Timeline at a glance\n\nTarget: the whole roadmap complete by end of March 2027. The schedule below is the compressed plan to hit that date. The dates run tight and in parallel from P2 onward.\n\n| Phase | Focus | Window | Status |\n| :-: | :-: | :-: | :-: |\n| ð¢ P0 GA the local brain | Harden entire-sem, brain, MCP surface, bench | Jul to Aug 2026 | Ships today, GA wrapper in progress |\n| ðµ P1 Shared / hosted brain | Server store, sync, remote query, auth | Now, ship Aug 2026 | Built and tested on clones, one step from prod |\n| ð§© Keystone: semantic index tied to VCS | Entity deltas, git-native index, causality | Aug to Sep 2026 | Planned |\n| ð£ P2 Unified memory, one MCP surface | Converge search, one backbone, one surface | Sep to Nov 2026 | Planned |\n| ð¡ Reasoning capture, compounding memory | Record schema, write-back, provenance graph | Oct to Dec 2026 | Planned |\n| ð  P3 Coordinated agents | Claims, conflict detection, handovers, scheduler | Nov 2026 to Feb 2027 | Planned |\n| ð´ P4 Cross-repo federation | Federated discovery, capability registry | Jan to Mar 2027 | Planned |\n| ⭐ P5 Behavioral intelligence (north star) | Prompt quality, best-prompt library, fit, auto-routing | Jan to Jun 2027 | Planned |\n\nThe March 2027 target covers the enabling phases (P0 through P4). The P5 north star starts as soon as P2's surface and P3's coordination land, and runs to June 2027. Linear milestone dates now match the compressed schedule.\n\n## ð¢ P0, GA the local brain\n\nWhat it is. The foundation the whole initiative stands on. The local brain already runs, so P0 is finish work and release hygiene, not new build. There is no gate here. Everything ships today, but nothing is formally tagged, so P0 is the wrapper that makes it something the rest of the arc can depend on.\n\nThe pieces, all live today.\n\nentire-sem is the semantic provider. It parses code into symbols and relations with tree-sitter, and it uses no vectors anywhere in the stack.\n\nentire-brain is the local brain. It holds durable, branch-scoped, provenance-anchored facts, plus a local MCP surface of about 33 tools that agents query.\n\nbrain-bench is the CI gate. It benchmarks the extractor against a reference tool across roughly 30 languages and fails the build on regression or drift.\n\nThe milestones.\n\nM1, harden and GA entire-sem. Version-stamp it and freeze the schema so everything downstream can trust the contract.\n\nM2, close the brain blockers. Ship the local brain with honest claims, no overreach.\n\nM3, GA the MCP surface for both plugins. Harden the local tool surface for the Claude Code and Codex plugins.\n\nM4, brain-bench as the automated eval gate. Make the benchmark a required regression floor.\n\nM5, release logistics. The release checklist, the compatibility matrix, and distribution.\n\nFoundation build tracked in Linear: [Semantic Index Tied to VCS History](https://linear.app/entirehq/project/semantic-index-tied-to-vcs-history-ea453fa387e2) (Urgent). This is the piece that persists entity-level meaning onto checkpoints and a git-native index, so meaning is stored with git history and not re-parsed on demand. Done when entire and MCP can answer \"which checkpoints changed entity X\" from the index.\n\nEntity deltas in checkpoint metadata (target 2026-08-15): [COR-781](https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-781/spike-map-semantic-extractor-snapshot-checkpoint-metadata-schema) spike the schema, then [COR-782](https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-782/embed-entity-deltas-into-the-checkpoint-metadata-write-path) embed the deltas into the write path.\n\nGit-native entity to checkpoint index (target 2026-09-15): [COR-783](https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-783/build-the-git-native-entity-checkpoint-index) build the index, [COR-784](https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-784/mcp-tool-query-checkpointssessions-by-semantic-entity) expose it as an MCP tool.\n\nTransparency-log semantic causality (target 2026-09-30): [COR-785](https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-785/tie-transparency-log-events-to-semantic-causality) tie ref-change events to the session and entities that caused them.\n\n## ðµ P1, shared / hosted brain ⭐\n\nWhat it is. The differentiator. P1 lifts the brain off the laptop into a shared, server-side, multi-tenant service, so one member's agent learns something and every other member's agent can read it. The gate is the P0 schema-freeze plus a namespace, and it deliberately relaxes the local-only guardrail. All four parts are built and DB-tested on clone branches, race-clean, and awaiting merge.\n\nThe milestones.\n\nM1, server-side brain store. Content-addressed and authz-gated, encrypted at rest. Every artifact gets a fresh per-object key, AES-256-GCM, KMS-wrapped, bound to the repo and artifact, with crypto-shred of the key on retract so a removed fact becomes provably unreadable.\n\nM2, sync protocol over checkpoint\\_remote and entiredb. Durable facts sync under compare-and-swap on the branch head. The tenancy key is the injective slug@ULID, a lost race returns 412, and every advance appends to a tamper-evident hash-chained log.\n\nM3, multi-machine shared query. A remote MCP transport over HTTP, so a teammate's agent queries the shared brain without a local clone. The facts tools serve now. Direction: this endpoint becomes the backend of a brain surface on entirehq/mcp (the one hosted connector), not a second standalone connector.\n\nM4, auth and tenancy. Multi-tenant isolation on the org, project, repo SpiceDB cascade, with two independent fail-closed layers.\n\nWhat P1 rides and reuses (locked in after the landscape review).\n\nTransport: entirehq/mcp. James's hosted connector already solves OAuth, per-principal token exchange, tenancy, and discovery for about 60 tools. The brain registers a tool surface there; M3's endpoint is that surface's backend. No second connector, no duplicate auth plumbing.\n\nStorage direction: EntireDB. Blobs onto objstore, the fact CAS onto refstore, the audit log onto rsl, aligned with the git-meta move. This work is owned in decentralized-architecture, with the brain as its first customer and forcing function. The organizing rule: the brain owns the what and the when; decentralized-architecture owns the shared rails, because a capability with many consumers lives with the platform, not inside one product.\n\nEncryption honesty. Per-object DEKs and crypto-shred exist because the current store is one bucket shared across tenants (separate orgs). In-repo or in EntireDB under the repo's own trust boundary, that need mostly falls away, so the crypto layer is a property of where the data sits, not of the data.\n\nHardening state. Both PRs went through a 4-angle cleanup pass (reuse, simplification, efficiency, altitude): one shared AWS store builder, no double-hashing on the publish path, narrowed validation interface, egress-toggle warning parity with the CLI. Trail re-review pending on the latest push.\n\nLinks. [entire-api PR \\#242](https://github.com/entirehq/entire-api/pull/242) is the store, sync, remote MCP, and tenancy, roughly +8,532 lines. [entire-brain PR \\#65](https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/65) is the client wire fixes. [Trail \\#243](https://entire.io/gh/entirehq/entire-api/trails/243) is entire.io's own AI review, with 0 open findings and risk around 62%.\n\nWhere the storage is headed. The brain is in-repo by design already, keyed by repo, branch, and commit, and the hosted service exists only for the shared, authed query that a file in one clone cannot serve. The store rides the session-share stack today (S3 plus KMS) because that was the fastest proven path to ship P1, but the target is to push it down into EntireDB so it inherits resiliency and replication for free: the artifact blobs onto objstore, the fact-set CAS onto refstore, the audit log onto rsl. The one piece EntireDB does not cover yet is encryption at rest with a per-object key and crypto-shred, and that only matters because the current store is shared across tenants, meaning separate orgs in one bucket. In-repo, under the repo's own trust boundary, that need mostly falls away, so the direction is to ride EntireDB and add per-object encrypt and shred there only if a shared store still requires it.\n\n### ð Shipping P1, staging to production\n\nThe path is staging-first and reversible, so nothing turns on by accident.\n\nMerge [PR \\#242](https://github.com/entirehq/entire-api/pull/242) and [PR \\#65](https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/65) into main, one approval each.\n\nStaging deploys automatically. The brain migrations (brain\\_deks, brain\\_overlay\\_branches, brain\\_fact\\_refs, brain\\_fact\\_advances) apply on deploy and are additive only.\n\nEnable on staging. Set ENTIRE\\_BRAIN\\_HOSTED\\_ENABLED=true on the US and EU staging cells.\n\nSmoke test on partial.to. Publish a brain, advance a fact-set under CAS, and read it back over the remote MCP transport.\n\nPromote to production. Set the same one env var on the US and EU prod cells. That is the activation.\n\nRollback is instant. Unset the flag and every endpoint fails closed to 503, with data left sealed and dormant.\n\nThe only new setting is ENTIRE\\_BRAIN\\_HOSTED\\_ENABLED=true. Everything else is reused, since the brain shares session-share's already-live ENTIRE\\_SNAPSHOT\\_CIPHER=aws, its S3 bucket, and its KMS key, so there is no new bucket, key, IAM policy, or AWS credential. Until the flag is set, the endpoints fail closed to 503, so merging ships the code dormant on production.\n\n## ðº️ The landscape: what already exists, and how the plan converges it\n\nFour systems already live in this space. The plan does not route around them, it converges onto them. This is grounded in a full read of each codebase.\n\nentirehq/mcp (James). A hosted, multi-tenant, stateless remote MCP proxy: about 60 tools over four upstreams, Streamable HTTP, OAuth resource server with per-principal token exchange, all authorization downstream in SpiceDB. It stores nothing. It is the one hosted MCP transport, and it is architected to add tool surfaces. Decision: the brain does not ship its own standalone MCP connector. The hosted brain is an upstream data service, exposed as a brain surface on this server. P1.M3's transport work becomes the backend that surface calls.\n\nlibrarian (Alex). A knowledge-indexing and hybrid-search service over team communications and docs: Slack threads, Linear issues, GitHub PRs and issues, markdown. Postgres plus pgvector, its own 768-dim embedding stack (nomic-embed-text on Ollama), RRF fusion, no S3, no code, no sessions. Its roadmap heads toward an entity graph and synthesized views over the same checkpoint stream the brain distills. Librarian is the who-and-why half of team memory (comms); the brain is the what-and-where half (code, keyed to git). The facts and synthesis layer must be negotiated between the two, plus Alisha's MemoryRecords, before either builds further.\n\nentire-search (Alisha, deployed, serves entire.io search today). Product-entity search: checkpoint transcript chunks, commits, PRs. Cohere embed-v4.0 (1536-dim) with vectors in Turbopuffer, BM25 plus ANN with a tier system, SpiceDB ACL fan-out. It deliberately strips code before indexing. Near-zero overlap with the brain: different corpus, different store. The seam is checkpoints, which both consume; a distilled brain fact is a better search document than a raw transcript chunk, a future feed-in, not a conflict.\n\nperegrine (Evis, staging, prod target July). Trigram lexical code search, the Zoekt replacement: regex and full-text over source at platform scale, one index file per repo on S3, plus a tree-sitter symbol layer (15 languages, definition and reference extraction, query-time go-to-def). Zero embeddings. The one real duplication in the landscape: entire-sem and peregrine both maintain per-language tree-sitter extractors. Peregrine has no typed relation graph (its only edge is an untyped ref-to-def link) while entire-sem emits a 30-type relation graph (CALLS, EXTENDS, IMPLEMENTS, DATA\\_FLOWS). Peregrine reserved explicit extension slots (SymbolSource::Scip, SymbolPrecision::Semantic) for a higher-precision external symbol producer. Decision to pursue: entire-sem feeds peregrine's symbol overlay, one extractor serving both, with peregrine the find-text-fast engine and the brain the understand-structure engine.\n\nAlisha's MemoryRecords (Agent Improvement Engine). The sharpest overlap in the company: it derives memory from the same checkpoint stream the brain distills facts from, the descriptive and prescriptive halves of one problem. It also sits directly under the P5 north star (prompt quality, fit, routing), and Alisha owns the deployed semantic search too, so she holds two seats at the convergence table. Decision: align with Alisha before building the facts layer or P5 further; P5 should merge efforts, not add a third parallel one.\n\nThe score that motivates P2: four search systems live or half-live, three embedding backbones (Cohere 1536, nomic 768, and none), and at least two tree-sitter extractors. P2's converge-code-search RFD ([COR-786](https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-786/decision-rfd-converge-code-search-on-one-engine-deprecate-duplicates)) and one-backbone milestone ([COR-788](https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-788/unify-knowledge-code-artifact-indexes-on-one-embedding-backbone)) are exactly this cleanup.\n\n## ð£ P2, unified memory, one MCP surface\n\nWhat it is. The chokepoint. Today retrieval and knowledge are fragmented across several parallel code-search efforts and two parallel knowledge systems. P2 converges them into one shared memory on one embedding backbone, exposed through MCP, so every agent (Claude Code, Codex, Droid, Cursor, Gemini) queries the same thing with the same tools. The gate is P1 transport plus auth, and it is the surface every downstream tool registers on. Done when one MCP tool returns unified results across code and knowledge, and only one search engine and one embedding backbone remain in production.\n\nTracked in Linear: [Unified, Pluggable Agent Memory](https://linear.app/entirehq/project/unified-pluggable-agent-memory-eaf5762e7339) (High, compressed target Sep to Nov 2026).\n\nM1, converge code-search into one engine (target 2026-09-30). [COR-786](https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-786/decision-rfd-converge-code-search-on-one-engine-deprecate-duplicates) is the RFD that picks one direction, and [COR-787](https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-787/ship-the-converged-code-search-service) ships the converged code-search service.\n\nM2, converge knowledge into one backbone (target 2026-10-31). [COR-788](https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-788/unify-knowledge-code-artifact-indexes-on-one-embedding-backbone) unifies the knowledge and code-artifact indexes on one embedding backbone.\n\nM3, expose brain plus code-search plus knowledge behind one MCP surface (target 2026-11-30). [COR-789](https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-789/single-mcp-shared-memory-tool-over-code-knowledge-semantic-index) is the single MCP shared-memory tool.\n\nM4, retire duplicates and prove no regression. [COR-790](https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-790/retire-duplicate-search-and-knowledge-paths) decommissions the superseded search and knowledge paths once the unified surface is in production.\n\n## ð¡ Reasoning capture and compounding memory\n\nWhat it is. The companion to P2 that makes memory compound. Agents capture transcripts, not reasoning, and the reasoning surfaces we have emit prose that gets overwritten, so understanding restarts every run. This captures agent reasoning as structured, queryable facts written back into shared memory, so a later run inherits what an earlier one learned. It rides on the unified surface and the keystone entity deltas. Done when a second agent run reuses the first run's structured reasoning rather than re-deriving it, and a provenance query returns the decision cascade.\n\nTracked in Linear: [Reasoning Capture and Compounding Memory](https://linear.app/entirehq/project/reasoning-capture-and-compounding-memory-db95c0b2ef1c) (High, target Oct to Dec 2026).\n\nM1, structured reasoning-record schema (target 2026-10-31). [COR-791](https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-791/design-the-structured-reasoning-record-schema-rfd) designs the schema, [COR-792](https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-792/persist-reasoning-records-per-checkpointtrail) persists a record per checkpoint and trail.\n\nM2, write-back from reasoning surfaces (target 2026-11-30). [COR-793](https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-793/write-back-review-findings-durable-semantic-facts) has review findings write durable semantic facts back into memory.\n\nM3, provenance graph (target 2026-12-31). [COR-794](https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-794/provenance-graph-over-decisions-tasks-prs-reviews) builds a queryable graph of decision to task to PR to review.\n\n## ð  P3, coordinated agents\n\nWhat it is. Let fleets of agents build in parallel without colliding. Today agents cannot coordinate, so two agents editing the same function silently collide. P3 adds entity-level ownership, conflict detection before merge, structured handovers, and a scheduler over ready tasks. The gate is P1 durable state plus the P2 one surface, and it runs in parallel with P4. Done when two agents editing the same entity get a pre-merge conflict warning, a ready task auto-dispatches, and a handover auto-hydrates into the next agent's context.\n\nTracked in Linear: [Semantic Collision-Free Parallel Agents](https://linear.app/entirehq/project/semantic-collision-free-parallel-agents-e20ca0e40e08) (High, compressed target Nov 2026 to Feb 2027).\n\nM1, entity claims and leases (target 2026-11-30). [COR-795](https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-795/spike-evaluate-the-coordination-substrate-task-dag-handovers) evaluates the substrate, [COR-796](https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-796/entity-level-claimlease-primitive-claim-a-symbol-expiry) builds the claim primitive so an agent claims a symbol rather than a whole file, with expiry and sweep.\n\nM2, pre-merge conflict detection (target 2026-12-31). [COR-797](https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-797/pre-merge-semantic-conflict-detection-over-concurrent-claims) warns when two agents touch the same entity before the changes merge.\n\nM3, signed handovers and auto-hydration (target 2027-01-31). [COR-798](https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-798/structured-handover-schema-mcp-auto-hydration) makes handovers structured data the next agent auto-loads via MCP.\n\nM4, scheduler to sandboxes (target 2027-02-28). [COR-800](https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-800/scheduler-auto-dispatch-ready-tasks-to-sandboxes) auto-dispatches ready tasks into sandboxes.\n\nM5, presence and read-receipts. [COR-799](https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-799/agent-presence-read-receipt-messaging) adds agent presence and read-receipt messaging so an idle claim holder can be nudged or reclaimed.\n\n## ð´ P4, cross-repo federation\n\nWhat it is. Break the repo boundary. Git-native discovery stops at the repo edge, so an agent cannot find who reasoned about similar code elsewhere, and there is no registry to route a task to the right agent. P4 shares reasoning across repos and orgs, and adds a capability registry so tasks route by capability. The gate is P1 durable state plus the P2 one surface, and it runs in parallel with P3. Done when an agent working in repo A surfaces relevant reasoning from repo B, and tasks route to an agent by declared capability.\n\nTracked in Linear: [Cross-Repo Shared Reasoning](https://linear.app/entirehq/project/cross-repo-shared-reasoning-0f9532a0d661) (Medium, compressed target Jan to Mar 2027).\n\nM1, cross-repo semantic index and query (target 2027-02-28). [COR-801](https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-801/cross-repo-semantic-discovery-over-the-federated-index) queries the semantic index across repos over the federated index and mirror pipeline.\n\nM2, cross-org authz. [COR-802](https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-802/spike-cross-org-authz-for-shared-reasoning) defines the authorization model for sharing reasoning across orgs, building on the existing MCP and SpiceDB gating.\n\nM3, agent capability registry (target 2027-03-31). [COR-803](https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-803/agent-capability-registry-discovery) registers agents by capability so a task resolves to the best-fit agent.\n\n## ⭐ P5, behavioral intelligence: the north star\n\nWhat it is. The payoff the whole arc builds toward: turn retained behavior into decisions. Every prompt, session, and outcome is already captured as checkpoints; P5 mines that record. It came from the Salesforce ask and it is what makes the memory layer a product, not plumbing. The gate is the P2 one surface plus P3 coordinated execution.\n\nWhat it delivers.\n\nPrompt intelligence. Score a prompt's quality before it runs, from retained outcome signal. See which people write prompts that succeed. Surface a curated best-prompt library of exemplars mined from real checkpoints, so the org's best prompting becomes everyone's baseline.\n\nFit modeling. Who, or which agent or model, succeeds on what kind of task, from history instead of vibes.\n\nAuto-routing. Send a task to the agent or person most likely to do it well, with P4's capability registry supplying the candidates.\n\nFeedback loop and org dashboards. Outcomes flow back into the models; leadership watches the org learn.\n\nAlignment first. Alisha's MemoryRecords (Agent Improvement Engine) mines the same checkpoint stream toward the same territory, and she owns the deployed semantic search. P5 starts with a merge-of-efforts conversation, not a third parallel build. The brain brings what the others lack: facts with provenance anchors tied to commits, and brain-bench's eval discipline as the pattern for scoring the prompt-quality classifier.\n\nTracked in Linear: [P5 · Behavioral Intelligence (North Star)](https://linear.app/entirehq/project/p5-behavioral-intelligence-north-star-1bb9991bc853) (High, target Jan to Jun 2027).\n\nM1, prompt-quality classifier (target 2027-02-28): score prompts from outcome signal (checkpoint success, iteration count, review outcomes).\n\nM2, per-person profiles and the best-prompt library (target 2027-03-31): which employees write prompts that succeed, and the best of their prompts, curated from real checkpoints.\n\nM3, agent and person to task fit (target 2027-04-30): the fit model over checkpoint history.\n\nM4, auto-routing (target 2027-05-31): route work to the best-fit agent or person.\n\nM5, feedback loop and org dashboards (target 2027-06-30): close the loop, show the learning.\n\n## ð Full tracking table\n\nEvery issue links to Linear. Priorities are U (urgent), H (high), M (medium).\n\n| Phase | Milestone (target) | Issue | Pri |\n| :-: | :-: | :-: | :-: |\n| ð¢ P0 Keystone | Entity deltas in checkpoint metadata (2026-08-15) | [COR-781](https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-781/spike-map-semantic-extractor-snapshot-checkpoint-metadata-schema) Spike: extractor snapshot to metadata schema | U |\n| ð¢ P0 Keystone | Entity deltas in checkpoint metadata (2026-08-15) | [COR-782](https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-782/embed-entity-deltas-into-the-checkpoint-metadata-write-path) Embed entity deltas into the write path | U |\n| ð¢ P0 Keystone | Git-native entity to checkpoint index (2026-09-15) | [COR-783](https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-783/build-the-git-native-entity-checkpoint-index) Build the git-native index | H |\n| ð¢ P0 Keystone | Git-native entity to checkpoint index (2026-09-15) | [COR-784](https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-784/mcp-tool-query-checkpointssessions-by-semantic-entity) MCP tool: query by entity | H |\n| ð¢ P0 Keystone | Transparency-log semantic causality (2026-09-30) | [COR-785](https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-785/tie-transparency-log-events-to-semantic-causality) Tie events to causality | M |\n| ð£ P2 Unified memory | Converge code search (2026-09-30) | [COR-786](https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-786/decision-rfd-converge-code-search-on-one-engine-deprecate-duplicates) RFD: converge code search | H |\n| ð£ P2 Unified memory | Converge code search (2026-09-30) | [COR-787](https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-787/ship-the-converged-code-search-service) Ship converged code-search | H |\n| ð£ P2 Unified memory | Unified knowledge backbone (2026-10-31) | [COR-788](https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-788/unify-knowledge-code-artifact-indexes-on-one-embedding-backbone) Unify indexes on one backbone | H |\n| ð£ P2 Unified memory | Single MCP surface (2026-11-30) | [COR-789](https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-789/single-mcp-shared-memory-tool-over-code-knowledge-semantic-index) Single MCP shared-memory tool | H |\n| ð£ P2 Unified memory | Single MCP surface (2026-11-30) | [COR-790](https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-790/retire-duplicate-search-and-knowledge-paths) Retire duplicate paths | M |\n| ð¡ Reasoning capture | Record schema (2026-10-31) | [COR-791](https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-791/design-the-structured-reasoning-record-schema-rfd) Design the record schema | H |\n| ð¡ Reasoning capture | Record schema (2026-10-31) | [COR-792](https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-792/persist-reasoning-records-per-checkpointtrail) Persist records per checkpoint | H |\n| ð¡ Reasoning capture | Write-back (2026-11-30) | [COR-793](https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-793/write-back-review-findings-durable-semantic-facts) Write-back findings to facts | H |\n| ð¡ Reasoning capture | Provenance graph (2026-12-31) | [COR-794](https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-794/provenance-graph-over-decisions-tasks-prs-reviews) Provenance graph | M |\n| ð  P3 Coordinated agents | Claims and leases (2026-11-30) | [COR-795](https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-795/spike-evaluate-the-coordination-substrate-task-dag-handovers) Spike: coordination substrate | H |\n| ð  P3 Coordinated agents | Claims and leases (2026-11-30) | [COR-796](https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-796/entity-level-claimlease-primitive-claim-a-symbol-expiry) Entity-level claim primitive | H |\n| ð  P3 Coordinated agents | Pre-merge conflict detection (2026-12-31) | [COR-797](https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-797/pre-merge-semantic-conflict-detection-over-concurrent-claims) Pre-merge conflict detection | H |\n| ð  P3 Coordinated agents | Handovers and auto-hydration (2027-01-31) | [COR-798](https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-798/structured-handover-schema-mcp-auto-hydration) Structured handover schema | H |\n| ð  P3 Coordinated agents | Handovers and auto-hydration (2027-01-31) | [COR-799](https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-799/agent-presence-read-receipt-messaging) Presence and read-receipts | M |\n| ð  P3 Coordinated agents | Scheduler to sandboxes (2027-02-28) | [COR-800](https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-800/scheduler-auto-dispatch-ready-tasks-to-sandboxes) Scheduler to sandboxes | M |\n| ð´ P4 Federation | Cross-repo discovery (2027-02-28) | [COR-801](https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-801/cross-repo-semantic-discovery-over-the-federated-index) Cross-repo semantic discovery | M |\n| ð´ P4 Federation | Cross-repo discovery (2027-02-28) | [COR-802](https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-802/spike-cross-org-authz-for-shared-reasoning) Spike: cross-org authz | M |\n| ð´ P4 Federation | Capability registry (2027-03-31) | [COR-803](https://linear.app/entirehq/issue/COR-803/agent-capability-registry-discovery) Agent capability registry | M |\n| ⭐ P5 North star | Prompt-quality classifier (2027-02-28) | milestone (issues to be scoped) | H |\n| ⭐ P5 North star | Per-person profiles + best-prompt library (2027-03-31) | milestone (issues to be scoped) | H |\n| ⭐ P5 North star | Agent and person to task fit (2027-04-30) | milestone (issues to be scoped) | H |\n| ⭐ P5 North star | Auto-routing (2027-05-31) | milestone (issues to be scoped) | H |\n| ⭐ P5 North star | Feedback loop + org dashboards (2027-06-30) | milestone (issues to be scoped) | H |\n\nTotals: 8 Linear projects under the initiative (the five arc projects plus P0, P1, and P5), 29 milestones, 23 scoped issues (COR-781 through COR-803); P0, P1, and P5 carry milestones with issues to be scoped.\n\n## Architecture decisions\n\nADR-1, schema freeze. The brain wire schema is major.minor, additive minors, tolerant readers. From P0.\n\nADR-P1-A, opt-in egress. Hosted publish is never implicit. It is gated on an explicit entire brain publish plus ENTIRE\\_BRAIN\\_ALLOW\\_HOSTED.\n\nADR-P1-C, branch build model. A default push builds a baseline, a feature branch builds an overlay, merge promotes it, delete garbage-collects it.\n\nADR-P1-D, platform target. The post-refactor mirror and decentralized architecture. Treat interfaces as a moving target. The intent is for the brain store to ride entiredb (objstore for blobs, refstore for the fact CAS, rsl for the audit log), with per-object encryption and crypto-shred as the one capability that still needs a home.\n\n## Critical path\n\nP0 finishes the brain. P1 is the linchpin, since store, sync, query, and auth unblock everything else. The keystone semantic index and unified memory land next, and the P2 single MCP surface is the chokepoint every downstream tool registers on. Reasoning capture builds on the record schema and the unified surface. Coordinated agents and cross-repo federation both need P1 plus the one surface, and they run in parallel.\n\n## ð Links\n\nInitiative: [Semantic Reasoning Layer](https://linear.app/entirehq/initiative/semantic-reasoning-layer-e043385c2167)\n\nVision: [entire.io/vision](https://entire.io/vision)\n\nP1 store and sync: [entire-api PR \\#242](https://github.com/entirehq/entire-api/pull/242)\n\nP1 client: [entire-brain PR \\#65](https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/65)\n\nP1 review: [Trail \\#243](https://entire.io/gh/entirehq/entire-api/trails/243)\n\nKeystone: [Semantic Index Tied to VCS History](https://linear.app/entirehq/project/semantic-index-tied-to-vcs-history-ea453fa387e2)\n\n[Unified, Pluggable Agent Memory](https://linear.app/entirehq/project/unified-pluggable-agent-memory-eaf5762e7339)\n\n[Reasoning Capture and Compounding Memory](https://linear.app/entirehq/project/reasoning-capture-and-compounding-memory-db95c0b2ef1c)\n\n[Semantic Collision-Free Parallel Agents](https://linear.app/entirehq/project/semantic-collision-free-parallel-agents-e20ca0e40e08)\n\n[Cross-Repo Shared Reasoning](https://linear.app/entirehq/project/cross-repo-shared-reasoning-0f9532a0d661)\n\n[P5 · Behavioral Intelligence (North Star)](https://linear.app/entirehq/project/p5-behavioral-intelligence-north-star-1bb9991bc853)\n\nLandscape repos read for the convergence calls: entirehq/mcp, entirehq/librarian, entirehq/entire-search, entirehq/peregrine\n\nOne housekeeping note. The initiative is Active. The 23 Linear issues above (COR-781 through COR-803) were created on 2026-07-01 and are currently in a Canceled state in Linear, so they nee"}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"5e0420f0-5b92-4d86-b289-909f46886b2d","session_id":"f507d58c-285f-4d11-b1d0-201f2a5e172d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"de272aad-c620-4d71-bbdd-27dd2d3dc8af","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"quizzical-sniffing-quasar"}
