{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-08-18T18:13:31.292Z","sessionId":"de272aad-c620-4d71-bbdd-27dd2d3dc8af","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>af10446c036d6e3ff</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_01Utx3xghPjH9tQN2WbBhRWH</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-suhaan-devenv/f507d58c-285f-4d11-b1d0-201f2a5e172d/tasks/af10446c036d6e3ff.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Scout brain provenance + gitmeta\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>Confirmed: it's the session's *latest* checkpoint at distill time, not the checkpoint that actually introduced the fact — coarse, session-level, not per-checkpoint-delta.\n\n## Report (p0p1/p1-new, entire-brain, read-only scout)\n\n**1. gitmeta engine** — vendored PoC copy, `internal/factgitmeta/gitmeta/`, doc header says re-vendor from `entire-api` instead (types.go:1-18).\n- Targets (`types.go:57-63`): `commit`, `change-id`, `branch`, `path`, `project`. This copy lacks entire-api's `PathTargetSubtree`/typed path helpers (types.go:9-11).\n- Ops (`apply.go:50-64`): `set`, `rm`, `list:push`, `list:rm`, `set:add`, `set:rm`, `cas` (CAS is engine-level unconditional-set; precondition checked by caller).\n- Ref: single hardcoded `refs/meta/local/main` (`backend.go:46`), no remote/push/fetch — explicitly called out as inert until brain exchanges records with entire-api over a shared ref (types.go:11-18).\n- brain's only user of this engine: `internal/factgitmeta/backend.go` — a `factsync.Server` seam storing one head pointer + one NDJSON blob per (repo,branch) under a `project` target, key prefix `brain:facts:` (backend.go:1-30). Not entity-keyed — one blob holds the whole fact set.\n\n**2. Fact record schema** — `internal/factmerge/record.go:20-49`:\n```go\ntype Record struct {\n    ID           string    `json:\"id\"`          // sha256(normalized text + sorted paths)\n    Paths        []string  `json:\"paths\"`\n    Kind         string    `json:\"kind,omitempty\"`\n    Locus        []string  `json:\"locus,omitempty\"` // code identifiers/paths (WHERE)\n    Text         string    `json:\"text\"`\n    Branch       string    `json:\"branch\"`\n    Origin       string    `json:\"origin\"`\n    Status       string    `json:\"status\"`\n    Confidence   string    `json:\"confidence,omitempty\"`\n    Provenance   []Anchor  `json:\"provenance\"` // &gt;=1\n    RelatedIDs   []string  `json:\"related_ids,omitempty\"`\n    SupersededBy string    `json:\"superseded_by,omitempty\"`\n    CreatedAt    time.Time `json:\"created_at\"`\n    UpdatedAt    time.Time `json:\"updated_at\"`\n}\ntype Anchor struct {\n    SessionID, Commit, CheckpointID, TurnID, Transcript string\n    Line     int\n    Verified bool\n}\n```\nProvenance DOES carry `Commit` and `CheckpointID` fields — but populated only from `session.LatestCheckpoint` at distill time (`distill_cmd.go:921`), i.e. the session's checkpoint-at-distill-time, not the checkpoint that introduced the underlying change. `Locus` is the closest thing to entity anchoring — free-text code identifiers/paths, not resolved graph symbol IDs.\n\n**3. Checkpoint ingestion** — yes, but at transcript/session level, not entity level. `export.go` reads checkpoint git refs directly: `v2MainRef=\"refs/entire/checkpoints/v2/main\"`, `v1MainRef/v1OriginRef=\"refs/heads|remotes/origin/entire/checkpoints/v1\"`, `checkpointRefPrefix=\"refs/entire/checkpoints/\"` (export.go:40-45), walks commit messages for checkpoint IDs (`checkpointIDsFromCommitMessages`, export.go:735) and builds an author index (`buildCheckpointAuthorIndex`, export.go:765). `distill_cmd.go` and `episodes.go:187` consume `session.LatestCheckpoint` as the anchor. No per-checkpoint entity-delta ingestion exists.\n\n**4. Entity→history mapping: none found.** No cochange/co-change/co_change hits in non-test Go. `git log`/plumbing.CommitIter usage exists in exactly two places, both repo-level not entity-level: `seed.go:944-1010` (`buildSeedHistoryBaseline`/`buildSeedHistoryCoverage`, shells `git log --reverse --format=...` to build a session-vs-commit date-coverage gap report) and `export.go` (checkpoint ref/commit-message walking for session export). Neither indexes \"which commits/checkpoints touched entity X.\" Brain does not read the entire-graph's co-change signal at all — the only graph integration is symbol/doctor snapshotting (see Q6), not relational/co-change queries.\n\n**5. `internal/cli/export.go`** (3576 lines / 127K) — `entire brain export`: writes an agent-reviewable snapshot of Entire session history (Short/Long at export.go:104-105) — dumps transcripts per session into `sessions/`/`branches/` dirs with a manifest, resolving checkpoints via git checkpoint refs (v1 git-branch + v2 git-refs backends) and commit-message-embedded checkpoint IDs. It touches git history directly (shells to `git`/uses go-git) to enumerate checkpoint commits, detect default branch, and build author/branch indices — it does NOT compute entity-level diffs.\n\n**6. Brain→`entire graph` shell-out points** (only two, both symbol-snapshot ingestion, not query):\n- `internal/cli/semantic.go:946` — `runner.Run(ctx, repoDir, graphBinary, \"graph\", \"doctor\", \"--json\")` inside `runSemanticDoctor` (semantic.go:940), gates on `no_egress`/`network_required` flags.\n- `internal/cli/semantic_stream.go:371` — `args := []string{\"graph\", \"snapshot\", \"--repo\", repoDir, \"--format\", \"ndjson\", \"--no-network\"}`, invoked via `streamer.Stream` (semantic_stream.go:426) inside `streamSemanticSnapshot`.\n- `graphBinary` defaults to `\"entire\"` (semantic.go:308,325), overridable via `--graph-binary`.\n- These build brain's own local semantic/symbol index (`entire graph snapshot`) — no `graph impact`/`graph neighbors`/`graph diff` calls anywhere in brain; co-change and callers/callees graph relations are unused by brain today.\n\n**Bottom line for the keystone plan**: nothing here currently maps entity→checkpoint. gitmeta engine supports arbitrary `commit`/`change-id`/`branch`/`path` targets and `list:push`/`set:add` ops that would suit an entity→checkpoint index, but it's a single inert local ref (`refs/meta/local/main`) storing one project-wide blob, not per-entity keys — building the keystone means either (a) minting new git-meta keys under `path` or a new `entity` scheme and writing them per-checkpoint, or (b) extending `factmerge.Anchor` to carry graph symbol IDs (currently only free-text `Locus`) and populating it per-checkpoint-delta rather than per-session-latest-checkpoint as today.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>76194</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>31</tool_uses><duration_ms>110729</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
