{"parentUuid":"77fb0955-4078-4730-bd57-122b1924b7ee","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_011CeAfgQU5YU9cBDmkJu3zA","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Brain scout is back too — key takeaways while the last scout (cli checkpoint write path) finishes:\n\n- **Nothing maps entity→checkpoint today.** Facts do carry provenance anchors with `Commit` and `CheckpointID` fields, but they're filled with the session's *latest* checkpoint at distill time — not the checkpoint that actually made the change. Coarse, session-level.\n- **The vendored git-meta engine is a ready-made store for the index**: it supports `commit`/`branch`/`path`/`project` targets and list/set push ops on a local ref (`refs/meta/local/main`) — exactly the shape an entity→checkpoint index wants — but brain currently uses it for one project-wide facts blob only, and it's local-only (inert until it exchanges with entire-api).\n- **Brain never calls `graph diff` today** — its only graph integrations are `snapshot` (symbol ingestion) and `doctor`. So the Keystone wiring (diff per checkpoint → index write) is genuinely new code, but both ends already exist.\n\nOne scout to go, then the composed plan + your decision questions."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4690,"cache_read_input_tokens":107509,"output_tokens":489,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":118},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4690,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":489,"cache_read_input_tokens":107509,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4690,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4690},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CeAfgMjsjycfz6x98M