{"parentUuid":"b93134d0-267f-482d-a529-6312b27b0489","isSidechain":false,"type":"system","subtype":"stop_hook_summary","hookCount":2,"hookInfos":[{"command":"sh -c 'if ! command -v entire >/dev/null 2>&1; then exit 0; fi; exec entire hooks claude-code stop'","durationMs":47},{"command":"node \"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/stop-review-gate-hook.mjs\"","durationMs":70}],"hookErrors":[],"hookAdditionalContext":[],"preventedContinuation":false,"stopReason":"","hasOutput":false,"level":"suggestion","timestamp":"2026-08-18T18:13:43.229Z","uuid":"ee399a82-f604-47fd-8495-53278f2397e5","toolUseID":"49a627ab-3ac4-468b-ad16-ad922ce5e85c","session_id":"f507d58c-285f-4d11-b1d0-201f2a5e172d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"de272aad-c620-4d71-bbdd-27dd2d3dc8af","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"quizzical-sniffing-quasar"}
{"parentUuid":"ee399a82-f604-47fd-8495-53278f2397e5","isSidechain":false,"type":"system","subtype":"turn_duration","durationMs":11828,"messageCount":124,"pendingBackgroundAgentCount":1,"timestamp":"2026-08-18T18:13:43.230Z","uuid":"c298204b-a73b-4905-b192-4b66c582df16","isMeta":false,"userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"de272aad-c620-4d71-bbdd-27dd2d3dc8af","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"quizzical-sniffing-quasar"}
{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-08-18T18:13:46.940Z","sessionId":"de272aad-c620-4d71-bbdd-27dd2d3dc8af","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>a8c8f3f5a22b14c6d</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_01Cn6PmfaoZXca2Sta1N1C2W</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-suhaan-devenv/f507d58c-285f-4d11-b1d0-201f2a5e172d/tasks/a8c8f3f5a22b14c6d.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Scout cli checkpoint metadata\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>## Checkpoint metadata scout report (READ-ONLY, no edits made)\n\n**1. Where a checkpoint commit is created / metadata schema**\n- Persistent checkpoint tree is written by `treeWriter` in `cmd/entire/cli/checkpoint/persistent.go` (commit built there); triggered from `ManualCommitStrategy.CondenseSession` at `cmd/entire/cli/strategy/manual_commit_condensation.go:225`, called from git `post-commit` hook via `PostCommit` at `cmd/entire/cli/strategy/manual_commit_hooks.go:879`.\n- Metadata format: **JSON files inside the checkpoint tree**, not commit trailers (trailers only carry the checkpoint ID pointer). Root `metadata.json` = `CheckpointSummary` (aggregated); per-session `&lt;n&gt;/metadata.json` = `Metadata` struct. Read back via `readCommittedMetadataFromCheckpointTree` at `cmd/entire/cli/checkpoint/persistent.go:1643` — plain `json.Unmarshal`, no strict-mode decoder.\n- Real struct lives in `api/checkpoint/metadata.go:318` `type Metadata struct` (re-exported into `checkpoint` pkg via alias in `cmd/entire/cli/checkpoint/aliases.go:19`). Key fields: `CheckpointID, SessionID, Strategy, CreatedAt, Branch, FilesTouched []string, Agent, Model, TurnID, TokenUsage *types.TokenUsage, Summary *Summary, Attribution *Attribution, Kind, ReviewSkills, InvestigateRunID/Topic`. `Attribution` (`api/checkpoint/metadata.go:551`) is **aggregate line-count stats only** (AgentLines/HumanAdded/etc., no per-symbol data).\n- Commit message trailer: `Entire-Checkpoint: &lt;id&gt;` via `AppendCheckpointTrailer`, `cmd/entire/cli/trailers/trailers.go:238`.\n\n**2. Extension point for new metadata fields**\n- `Metadata` is a plain Go struct decoded with vanilla `json.Unmarshal` (no `DisallowUnknownFields` — that's only used in `settings.go` for `.entire/settings.json`, unrelated). Adding a new `omitempty` field is safe: old readers ignore it, new readers default-zero it on old data.\n- Existing extension precedent: `WriteOptions.MetadataDir` (`api/checkpoint/metadata.go:77`) — \"a directory containing additional metadata files to copy\" into the session dir, already used for task/subagent metadata (`copyMetadataDir`, `persistent.go:2218`). Same mechanism could drop an `entity_deltas.json` file per checkpoint without touching the struct at all.\n- Write path is a request-union (`WriteSession`, `BackfillSummary`, `BackfillAttribution`, …) — a new `BackfillEntityDelta` request type would follow the same pattern used for `Attribution` (computed post-commit, backfilled async).\n\n**3. Base/head SHAs available at checkpoint-creation time**\n- Yes. `SessionState.BaseCommit` (session start commit) and `AttributionBaseCommit` are tracked in `strategy` state; `headCommitHash`/`newHead` = HEAD after the user's commit, captured in `PostCommit` (`manual_commit_hooks.go:955` `newHead := head.Hash().String()`) and threaded through `condenseOpts.headCommitHash` (`manual_commit_condensation.go:104,347`). Attribution already diffs `attrBase` tree vs `headCommit` tree (`manual_commit_condensation.go:845-940`) — same base+head pair an entity-diff tool would need.\n\n**4. Existing entity/symbol/semantic capture** — none found. Grep for entity/symbol/semantic/sem/graph across `checkpoint/`, `strategy/`, `api/checkpoint/` returned only false positives (\"identity\", \"symlink\"). No entity-delta concept exists today.\n\n**5. `why`/`blame`/`investigate`** (all CLI-native, not external binaries; `entire labs` just advertises them — `cmd/entire/cli/labs.go:17`):\n- `blame` (`cmd/entire/cli/attribution.go:142`, hidden): git-blame-style **line** attribution enriched with checkpoint metadata (agent/model/session per line). Reads git blame + checkpoint `Attribution`.\n- `why` (`attribution.go:171`): explains a specific line — commit, checkpoint, prompt, session behind it. Same data source as `blame`.\n- `investigate` (`cmd/entire/cli/investigate_bridge.go`, subpackage `investigate/`): spawns a multi-agent investigation into a topic/issue, not code-entity-scoped.\n- None answer \"which checkpoint touched function/type X\" — they're line-range/file-scoped via git blame, not symbol-scoped.\n\n**6. Hook/plugin point for an external binary at checkpoint-write time**\n- Git hooks are CLI-managed shell wrappers calling `entire &lt;hookname&gt;` on PATH: `prepare-commit-msg, commit-msg, post-commit, post-rewrite, pre-push` (`cmd/entire/cli/strategy/hooks.go:32,177-235`). `post-commit` → `PostCommit` → `CondenseSession` is the natural insertion point (already has base+head SHAs, already async-backfills `Attribution`/`Summary`). No existing generic \"run external tool at checkpoint write\" plugin API — would need a new hook step or a `BackfillEntityDelta` write-request analogous to `BackfillAttribution`.\n\nKey files: `api/checkpoint/metadata.go`, `cmd/entire/cli/checkpoint/persistent.go`, `cmd/entire/cli/checkpoint/aliases.go`, `cmd/entire/cli/strategy/manual_commit_condensation.go`, `cmd/entire/cli/strategy/manual_commit_hooks.go`, `cmd/entire/cli/strategy/hooks.go`, `cmd/entire/cli/attribution.go`, `docs/architecture/sessions-and-checkpoints.md`.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>116159</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>34</tool_uses><duration_ms>134848</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
