positives (\"identity\", \"symlink\"). No entity-delta concept exists today.\n\n**5. `why`/`blame`/`investigate`** (all CLI-native, not external binaries; `entire labs` just advertises them — `cmd/entire/cli/labs.go:17`):\n- `blame` (`cmd/entire/cli/attribution.go:142`, hidden): git-blame-style **line** attribution enriched with checkpoint metadata (agent/model/session per line). Reads git blame + checkpoint `Attribution`.\n- `why` (`attribution.go:171`): explains a specific line — commit, checkpoint, prompt, session behind it. Same data source as `blame`.\n- `investigate` (`cmd/entire/cli/investigate_bridge.go`, subpackage `investigate/`): spawns a multi-agent investigation into a topic/issue, not code-entity-scoped.\n- None answer \"which checkpoint touched function/type X\" — they're line-range/file-scoped via git blame, not symbol-scoped.\n\n**6. Hook/plugin point for an external binary at checkpoint-write time**\n- Git hooks are CLI-managed shell wrappers calling `entire &lt;hookname&gt;` on PATH: `prepare-commit-msg, commit-msg, post-commit, post-rewrite, pre-push` (`cmd/entire/cli/strategy/hooks.go:32,177-235`). `post-commit` → `PostCommit` → `CondenseSession` is the natural insertion point (already has base+head SHAs, already async-backfills `Attribution`/`Summary`). No existing generic \"run external tool at checkpoint write\" plugin API — would need a new hook step or a `BackfillEntityDelta` write-request analogous to `BackfillAttribution`.\n\nKey files: `api/checkpoint/metadata.go`, `cmd/entire/cli/checkpoint/persistent.go`, `cmd/entire/cli/checkpoint/aliases.go`, `cmd/entire/cli/strategy/manual_commit_condensation.go`, `cmd/entire/cli/strategy/manual_commit_hooks.go`, `cmd/entire/cli/strategy/hooks.go`, `cmd/entire/cli/attribution.go`, `docs/architecture/sessions-and-checkpoints.md`.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>116159</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>34</tool_uses><duration_ms>134848</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"},"uuid":"a0820439-1b3c-42de-8d70-22c2a612cfe1","timestamp":"2026-08-18T18:13:46.988Z","permissionMode":"bypassPermissions","origin":{"kind":"task-notification"},"promptSource":"system","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"de272aad-c620-4d71-bbdd-27dd2d3dc8af","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"quizzical-sniffing-quasar"}
{"parentUuid":"a0820439-1b3c-42de-8d70-22c2a612cfe1","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_011CeAfhZZZ7jkCEFNiupmWJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3143,"cache_read_input_tokens":112199,"output_tokens":5611,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":3565},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3143,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":5611,"cache_read_input_tokens":112199,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3143,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3143},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CeAfhWnsBvvrgnAgCUv6G","type":"assistant","uuid":"431fbf78-7af7-4e6a-b0f0-8bdb985c0f23","timestamp":"2026-08-18T18:14:50.652Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"f507d58c-285f-4d11-b1d0-201f2a5e172d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"de272aad-c620-4d71-bbdd-27dd2d3dc8af","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"quizzical-sniffing-quasar"}
{"parentUuid":"431fbf78-7af7-4e6a-b0f0-8bdb985c0f23","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_011CeAfhZZZ7jkCEFNiupmWJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All three scouts are back — I have the full picture. Here's the composed Keystone plan (the between-P1-and-P2 work), explained simply, then the decisions I need from you.\n\n## What the Keystone is, in one sentence\n\nEvery checkpoint gets a small record of **which functions/classes/types it changed** (\"entity deltas\"), plus a reverse index so anyone — CLI or agent via MCP — can ask **\"show me every checkpoint that ever touched function X\"** and get an instant answer instead of re-parsing git history.\n\n## What the scouts found (why this is very buildable)\n\n- **The delta producer exists**: `entire graph diff` already outputs exactly the needed list (added/removed/modified/renamed per entity). Only gap: its JSON is unversioned — must be stamped before we persist it.\n- **The attach point exists**: checkpoints store metadata as JSON files in the checkpoint tree, safely extensible, and the cli already has an async \"backfill\" pattern (used for attribution stats) we can copy for entity deltas. Base+head SHAs are already in hand at checkpoint time.\n- **The index store exists**: brain's git-meta engine supports per-commit keys and list-append ops — the exact shape for an entity→checkpoint index — currently unused for this.\n- **Nothing connects them today**: brain never calls `graph diff`; fact provenance anchors to \"latest checkpoint at distill time\" (coarse), and `why`/`blame` are line-based, not symbol-based. The Keystone is the missing wiring, not new machinery.\n\n## The plan (3 PRs + 1 deferral)\n\n1. **entire-graph PR (tiny):** stamp a `schema_version` on `graph diff` output → this frozen schema *is* the COR-781 spike deliverable.\n2. **entire-brain PR (the bulk):** index builder that walks existing checkpoint history, runs `graph diff` per checkpoint, and writes deltas + the reverse entity→checkpoint index. Backfill command + kept fresh by `watch`/session-end (deterministic, zero tokens — slots straight into the daemon plan). Query CLI + the MCP tool \"query checkpoints by entity\" (COR-783/784). Bonus fix: distill starts anchoring facts to the checkpoint that actually made the change.\n3. **cli PR (small, separate):** at checkpoint write, async-backfill `entity_deltas.json` into the checkpoint tree (copying the attribution pattern; silent skip if the graph binary is absent) — COR-782. This makes deltas travel with checkpoints to hosted.\n4. **Defer COR-785** (tying server-side ref-change events to causes) — needs entiredb/hosted rails.\n\nDecided technically (no question needed): entity identity key = `path + kind + name`, with rename/move chaining from graph diff's rename records — content fingerprints change on every edit so they can't be the durable key."}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3143,"cache_read_input_tokens":112199,"output_tokens":5611,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":3565},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3143,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":5611,"cache_read_input_tokens":112199,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3143,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3143},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CeAfhWnsBvvrgnAgCUv6G","type":"assistant","uuid":"c297356b-2d0a-4eca-8a68-0c7b3b0563e4","timestamp":"2026-08-18T18:15:02.446Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"f507d58c-285f-4d11-b1d0-201f2a5e172d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"de272aad-c620-4d71-bbdd-27dd2d3dc8af","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"quizzical-sniffing-quasar"}
{"parentUuid":"c297356b-2d0a-4eca-8a68-0c7b3b0563e4","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_011CeAfhZZZ7jkCEFNiupmWJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_019ApXAGzVjTSLxkBUbJgoAx","name":"AskUserQuestion","input":{"questions":[{"question":"Should I build the brain-side index and the cli-side write-path in parallel, or brain first? Plain terms: the brain PR alone already delivers the whole feature for all EXISTING history (it can compute deltas for any old checkpoint after the fact). The cli PR makes NEW checkpoints carry their deltas at write time so they travel to hosted. The cli repo is another team's surface, so its PR will sit in review longer.","header":"Build split","multiSelect":false,"options":[{"label":"Both in parallel (Recommended)","description":"I orchestrate agents on brain + graph + cli PRs simultaneously. Full keystone (COR-781/782/783/784) in one push; cli PR reviewed separately at its own pace."},{"label":"Brain first, cli later","description":"Ship index + MCP query now with zero cli changes (daemon keeps new checkpoints indexed). Do the cli write-path embed as a follow-up once the brain side is proven."},{"label":"CLI write-path first","description":"Roadmap-literal order: land COR-781/782 (deltas in checkpoint metadata) before building the index. Slowest to a usable feature."}]},{"question":"Where should the entity→checkpoint index live? Plain terms: 'git-native' means the index is stored inside git itself (under special refs via the git-meta engine), so it clones/syncs with the repo and lines up with James's git-meta direction — but reads are a bit slower. A local file index (SQLite/NDJSON in .git/) is faster and simpler but stays on one machine and isn't what the roadmap promised.","header":"Index home","multiSelect":false,"options":[{"label":"git-meta + local cache (Recommended)","description":"git-meta refs are the source of truth (roadmap-faithful, syncs later via git-meta service); a small derived local cache makes queries fast. Rebuildable either way."},{"label":"git-meta only","description":"Purest git-native. Simpler (one store), queries acceptable but slower on big repos."},{"label":"Local index only","description":"Fastest to build and query, but not git-native — diverges from the roadmap and doesn't travel with clones; would need migrating later."}]},{"question":"Include COR-785 (transparency-log causality) in this push? Plain terms: it ties server-side ref-change events (the audit log of who moved what ref) back to the session + entities that caused them. It's the lowest-priority keystone piece, needs the hosted/entiredb side, and the keystone's done-when ('which checkpoints changed entity X, from the index') doesn't require it.","header":"COR-785 scope","multiSelect":false,"options":[{"label":"Defer it (Recommended)","description":"Ship the index + MCP tool now; pick up COR-785 after P1 (#85/#242) is merged and the hosted rails are live."},{"label":"Include it now","description":"Complete the whole keystone milestone in one push; adds server-side work and a dependency on unmerged P1 pieces."}]}]},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3143,"cache_read_input_tokens":112199,"output_tokens":5611,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":3565},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3143,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":5611,"cache_read_input_tokens":112199,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3143,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3143},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CeAfhWnsBvvrgnAgCUv6G","type":"assistant","uuid":"51ab6202-6507-47b6-811c-a54eca53ba8e","timestamp":"2026-08-18T18:15:15.006Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"f507d58c-285f-4d11-b1d0-201f2a5e172d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"de272aad-c620-4d71-bbdd-27dd2d3dc8af","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"quizzical-sniffing-quasar"}
{"parentUuid":"51ab6202-6507-47b6-811c-a54eca53ba8e","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"e6b5e022-e7cd-4069-aff9-03c6e0d48323","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","content":"The user doesn't want to proceed with this tool use. The tool use was rejected (eg. if it was a file edit, the new_string was NOT written to the file). To tell you how to proceed, the user said:\nThe user wants to clarify these questions.\n    This means they may have additional information, context or questions for you.\n    Take their response into account and then reformulate the questions if appropriate.\n    Start by asking them what they would like to clarify.\n\n    Questions asked:\n- \"Should I build the brain-side index and the cli-side write-path in parallel, or brain first? Plain terms: the brain PR alone already delivers the whole feature for all EXISTING history (it can compute deltas for any old checkpoint after the fact). The cli PR makes NEW checkpoints carry their deltas at write time so they travel to hosted. The cli repo is another team's surface, so its PR will sit in review longer.\"\n  Answer: Both in parallel (Recommended)\n- \"Where should the entity→checkpoint index live? Plain terms: 'git-native' means the index is stored inside git itself (under special refs via the git-meta engine), so it clones/syncs with the repo and lines up with James's git-meta direction — but reads are a bit slower. A local file index (SQLite/NDJSON in .git/) is faster and simpler but stays on one machine and isn't what the roadmap promised.\"\n  Answer: git-meta + local cache (Recommended)\n- \"Include COR-785 (transparency-log causality) in this push? Plain terms: it ties server-side ref-change events (the audit log of who moved what ref) back to the session + entities that caused them. It's the lowest-priority keystone piece, needs the hosted/entiredb side, and the keystone's done-when ('which checkpoints changed entity X, from the index') doesn't require it.\"\n  (No answer provided)","is_error":true,"tool_use_id":"toolu_019ApXAGzVjTSLxkBUbJgoAx"}]},"uuid":"7a025feb-0dea-48f4-a218-e4b7f3c24893","timestamp":"2026-08-18T18:28:29.572Z","toolUseResult":"Error: The user doesn't want to proceed with this tool use. The tool use was rejected (eg. if it was a file edit, the new_string was NOT written to the file). To tell you how to proceed, the user said:\nThe user wants to clarify these questions.\n    This means they may have additional information, context or questions for you.\n    Take their response into account and then reformulate the questions if appropriate.\n    Start by asking them what they would like to clarify.\n\n    Questions asked:\n- \"Should I build the brain-side index and the cli-side write-path in parallel, or brain first? Plain terms: the brain PR alone already delivers the whole feature for all EXISTING history (it can compute deltas for any old checkpoint after the fact). The cli PR makes NEW checkpoints carry their deltas at write time so they travel to hosted. The cli repo is another team's surface, so its PR will sit in review longer.\"\n  Answer: Both in parallel (Recommended)\n- \"Where should the entity→checkpoint index live? Plain terms: 'git-native' means the index is stored inside git itself (under special refs via the git-meta engine), so it clones/syncs with the repo and lines up with James's git-meta direction — but reads are a bit slower. A local file index (SQLite/NDJSON in .git/) is faster and simpler but stays on one machine and isn't what the roadmap promised.\"\n  Answer: git-meta + local cache (Recommended)\n- \"Include COR-785 (transparency-log causality) in this push? Plain terms: it ties server-side ref-change events (the audit log of who moved what ref) back to the session + entities that caused them. It's the lowest-priority keystone piece, needs the hosted/entiredb side, and the keystone's done-when ('which checkpoints changed entity X, from the index') doesn't require it.\"\n 