{"parentUuid":"432edac6-9ce0-4310-ae12-77eb1cb4ed82","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_011CeAhGQqDnmVypCVyGBGzF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01LuKc5JsqVeRGtpiHU62LMF","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"CLI PR: checkpoint entity deltas","subagent_type":"general-purpose","model":"opus","prompt":"Implement COR-782 in /Users/suhaan/devenv/cli-keystone (git worktree of entireio/cli, branch feat/checkpoint-entity-deltas, clean, off origin/main). Use rtk where possible. Work ONLY in this worktree. This is another team's surface: smallest complete change, match local idiom exactly.\n\nGOAL: when a persistent checkpoint is condensed, compute WHICH CODE ENTITIES (functions/classes/types) changed between the session's base commit and head, and write that as `entity_deltas.json` into the checkpoint tree's per-session dir — so entity deltas travel with checkpoints.\n\nFROZEN SCHEMA (write EXACTLY this; other repos build to the same contract — do not rename fields):\n{\n  \"schema_version\": \"1.0\",\n  \"producer\": \"entire-graph\",\n  \"producer_version\": \"<graph binary version if it reports one, else omit>\",\n  \"base\": \"<full sha>\", \"head\": \"<full sha>\",\n  \"computed_at\": \"<RFC3339 UTC>\",\n  \"entities\": [ { \"change\": \"added|removed|modified|renamed|moved\",\n    \"kind\": \"...\", \"name\": \"...\", \"old_name\": \"<omitempty>\",\n    \"path\": \"...\", \"old_path\": \"<omitempty>\",\n    \"signature\": \"<omitempty>\", \"old_signature\": \"<omitempty>\",\n    \"start_line\": 0, \"fingerprint\": \"<omitempty>\" } ]\n}\nSource data: shell out to the external graph binary — the cli already has kubectl-style external-command resolution (`entire-<name>` on PATH → resolve `entire-graph`). Run: `entire-graph graph diff --base <base> --head <head> --json` (also try `--repo <dir>`; check the binary's help in code comments only — at runtime just pass base/head and cwd=repo). Its output: Result{Files []FileChange{Path, OldPath, Changes []EntityChange{Type, Kind, Name, OldName, NewName, OldSignature, NewSignature, OldPath, NewPath, AfterStartLine}}}. Map: Type→change, NewName||Name→name, OldName→old_name (renamed only), NewPath||file Path→path, OldPath→old_path (moved only), NewSignature→signature, OldSignature→old_signature, AfterStartLine→start_line.\n\nWHERE TO HOOK IN (scouted for you, verify as you go):\n- CondenseSession: cmd/entire/cli/strategy/manual_commit_condensation.go:225, invoked from PostCommit (manual_commit_hooks.go:879); head sha captured at manual_commit_hooks.go:955; session base = SessionState.BaseCommit / AttributionBaseCommit; attribution already diffs base-tree vs head-tree at manual_commit_condensation.go:845-940 — use the SAME base+head pair attribution uses.\n- Write mechanism — follow the EXISTING pattern, pick whichever is cleaner after reading both: (a) `WriteOptions.MetadataDir` (api/checkpoint/metadata.go:77, copyMetadataDir persistent.go:2218) drops extra files into the session dir; or (b) a new backfill request in the write-request union mirroring BackfillAttribution (async, post-commit). Attribution's async backfill is the precedent for not blocking the hook.\n\nHARD CONSTRAINTS:\n1. The git hook path must NEVER get slower or fail because of this: hard timeout (~10s) on the graph subprocess, and ANY error (binary absent, timeout, bad json) = silent skip, checkpoint proceeds identically. There is a known hook-latency sensitivity in this repo.\n2. Default OFF behind a gate. Inspect how this repo gates experimental features (experimental/ gate, settings, env) and use the idiomatic one (suggest env ENTIRE_ENTITY_DELTAS=1 or settings key if that's the local pattern). Document the gate in the code where it's read.\n3. Test isolation rules (enforced in this repo): never real CWD .git / ~/.config/entire / keychain — use testutil.InitRepo + ENTIRE_CONFIG_DIR; t.Parallel() unless mutating process-global state; subprocess tests set ENTIRE_TOKEN_STORE=file.\n4. Tests: fake `entire-graph` as a PATH stub script emitting canned diff JSON; assert entity_deltas.json lands in the checkpoint tree with the frozen schema; assert silent-skip when the stub is absent/hangs/errors. \n5. Gate: `mise run check` must pass (that is the repo's pre-commit gate).\n6. Commit on the branch, normal message, NO AI footers / NO Co-Authored-By. Do NOT push.\n\nReport caveman-ultra compressed: gate chosen, hook point chosen (a or b + why in one line), files changed w/ line refs, test names, check-gate result, commit sha. Max 25 lines."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1121,"cache_read_input_tokens":128004,"output_tokens":8463,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":3303},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1121,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":8463,"cache_read_input_tokens":128004,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1121,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1121},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CeAhGMssm9WDkJYgn8jbJ","type":"assistant","uuid":"34366802-ec32-473a-aa50-754bf9a4d0b0","timestamp":"2026-08-18T18:35:36.938Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"f507d58c-285f-4d11-b1d0-201f2a5e172d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"de272aad-c620-4d71-bbdd-27dd2d3dc8af","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"quizzical-sniffing-quasar"}
