antUUID":"34366802-ec32-473a-aa50-754bf9a4d0b0","session_id":"f507d58c-285f-4d11-b1d0-201f2a5e172d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"de272aad-c620-4d71-bbdd-27dd2d3dc8af","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"quizzical-sniffing-quasar"}
{"parentUuid":"9d5f226e-24f1-4776-a3da-ca6f541ec952","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_011CeAhGQqDnmVypCVyGBGzF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01C6rS5uzrraNY9krCem6jnA","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Brain PR: entity-checkpoint index","subagent_type":"general-purpose","model":"opus","prompt":"Implement the keystone entity→checkpoint index (COR-783 + COR-784) in /Users/suhaan/devenv/p0p1/brain-keystone (git worktree of entireio/entire-brain, branch feat/entity-checkpoint-index, clean, off origin/main). Use rtk where possible. Work ONLY in this worktree. This is the bulk PR — take the time to do it completely.\n\nGOAL: brain can answer \"which checkpoints/sessions changed entity X\" from a persisted git-native index, without re-parsing. Deliver: (1) index builder + backfill over existing checkpoint history, (2) query CLI, (3) MCP tool, (4) freshness wiring, (5) fact-provenance upgrade.\n\nFROZEN CONTRACT (shared with a parallel cli PR — do not deviate):\n- Per-checkpoint delta doc schema_version \"1.0\": {\"schema_version\":\"1.0\",\"producer\":\"entire-graph\",\"producer_version\":opt,\"base\":sha,\"head\":sha,\"computed_at\":RFC3339-UTC,\"entities\":[{\"change\":\"added|removed|modified|renamed|moved\",\"kind\",\"name\",\"old_name\"?,\"path\",\"old_path\"?,\"signature\"?,\"old_signature\"?,\"start_line\",\"fingerprint\"?}]}\n- Entity index key: \"<path>#<kind>#<name>\" (post-change path/name).\n- git-meta keys (via the EXISTING vendored engine internal/factgitmeta/gitmeta, local ref refs/meta/local/main per backend.go:46): FORWARD target=commit <sha>, key \"brain:entities\", op set, value = compact delta doc JSON. REVERSE target=project, key \"brain:entity:<entitykey>\", op list:push, value = <commit sha>. RENAME/MOVE alias: target=project, key \"brain:entity-alias:<old-entitykey>\", op set, value = <new-entitykey>.\n\nSCOUTED FACTS (verify as you go):\n- Delta source: shell the graph binary — reuse brain's existing pattern: graphBinary defaults to \"entire\" (internal/cli/semantic.go:308,325), runner.Run invocation at semantic.go:946, streaming pattern semantic_stream.go:371. Command: `<graphBinary> graph diff --base <parent> --head <sha> --json` run with repo cwd. Output structs: Result{Base,Head,Files []FileChange{Path,OldPath,Changes []EntityChange{Type,Kind,Name,OldName,NewName,OldSignature,NewSignature,OldPath,NewPath,AfterStartLine}}}; newer graph versions add \"schema_version\":\"1.1\" — TOLERATE its absence (older binaries).\n- Checkpoint enumeration: export.go already walks checkpoint refs: v2MainRef=\"refs/entire/checkpoints/v2/main\", v1 refs, prefix \"refs/entire/checkpoints/\" (export.go:40-45), checkpointIDsFromCommitMessages (export.go:735), author index (export.go:765). Reuse/refactor — do not duplicate ref-walking logic.\n- gitmeta engine ops: set/list:push/set:add etc at internal/factgitmeta/gitmeta/apply.go:50-64; targets commit/change-id/branch/path/project at types.go:57-63. Existing user: internal/factgitmeta/backend.go (facts head blob) — follow its transaction/locking discipline.\n- Fact provenance today: internal/factmerge/record.go:20-49 — Anchor{SessionID,Commit,CheckpointID,...}; distill fills it from session.LatestCheckpoint at distill_cmd.go:921 (COARSE — the fix below).\n\nBUILD:\n1. New package internal/entityindex: builder that, given a set of checkpoint commits, computes parent→commit graph diffs (skip merge commits' extra parents: first-parent diff), maps to the frozen doc, writes forward+reverse+alias git-meta records. Idempotent: a commit already having \"brain:entities\" is skipped. Track a high-water mark so incremental runs are cheap.\n2. Local cache: derived, REBUILDABLE reverse map (entitykey → []{commit, checkpointID, sessionID}) persisted under the brain dir (follow how brain stores other derived indexes), invalidated by the git-meta ref tip. Queries hit the cache; cache miss/stale → rebuild from git-meta.\n3. CLI: `entities backfill [--branch <b>] [--limit N]` (walk history, build), `entities history <query>` (match entitykey by substring/name; print checkpoints+sessions, --json support), `entities show <commit|checkpoint-id>` (print that checkpoint's delta doc). Follow existing cobra command idiom in internal/cli.\n4. Freshness: add a deterministic (zero-token) step to the watch tick refresh and the session-end hook path that indexes any new checkpoint commits since the high-water mark. Follow how watch composes its deterministic steps (watch.go watchSteps) — keep it cheap and failure-silent like the other steps.\n5. MCP tool (COR-784): add a tool to the MCP surface (agent_surface.go) named consistently with the existing ~33 tools: query checkpoints/sessions by semantic entity (input: entity query + optional branch; output: matching entities with their checkpoint/session lists). Wire it to the same query path as `entities history`.\n6. Provenance upgrade in distill: when the index has data, resolve each new fact's Locus identifiers against the reverse index to find the checkpoint that actually introduced/modified the matching entity, and use THAT for Anchor.Commit/CheckpointID; fall back to session.LatestCheckpoint exactly as today when no match. Keep this bounded and non-breaking (distill must not slow meaningfully or fail if index absent).\n\nVERIFY (non-negotiable):\n- Unit tests with a FAKE runner for graph output (brain has a runner seam — use it), covering: build, idempotent re-run, rename alias chaining, reverse query, cache rebuild, provenance fallback.\n- One live e2e gated on real binary availability (feature-detect: exec `entire graph capabilities --json`; skip if unavailable): temp git repo, real commits touching a known function, backfill, `entities history` returns the right commits.\n- MUTATION-VERIFY the two most load-bearing behaviors (e.g. comment out the reverse-index write → query test must FAIL; break the provenance resolution → its test must FAIL). State in your report which mutations you ran.\n- `go build ./... && go test ./...` green.\nCommit on the branch (split into a few logical commits fine), normal messages, NO AI footers / NO Co-Authored-By. Do NOT push.\n\nReport caveman-ultra compressed: packages/files added w/ line counts, command names, MCP tool name, mutation results, test summary, commit shas. Max 30 lines."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1121,"cache_read_input_tokens":128004,"output_tokens":8463,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":3303},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1121,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":8463,"cache_read_input_tokens":128004,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1121,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1121},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CeAhGMssm9WDkJYgn8jbJ","type":"assistant","uuid":"b5a0ff21-e591-4b8b-84ce-92f3dc98bdf8","timestamp":"2026-08-18T18:36:06.161Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"f507d58c-285f-4d11-b1d0-201f2a5e172d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"de272aad-c620-4d71-bbdd-27dd2d3dc8af","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"quizzical-sniffing-quasar"}
