{"parentUuid":"3a533535-c756-455f-821b-2f04c054bb5f","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_011CeAkk3pJnxMfppnoEDddy","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The **brain PR — the bulk of the keystone — is done**, and it's a strong result:\n\n- New `internal/entityindex` package + `entities backfill|history|show` commands + MCP tool `brain_entity_history`, freshness wired into both the watch tick and session-end (bounded to 10 commits/90s, failure-silent), and the distill provenance fix (facts now anchor to the checkpoint that actually changed the matching entity, with the old behavior as fallback).\n- **Mutation-verified**, which is what makes me believe it: removing the reverse-index write broke 9 tests, breaking provenance resolution broke exactly its test while the fallback test kept passing, and ignoring the cache pin broke the rebuild test. All restored, re-verified green.\n- The **live e2e actually ran** against a real repo + real graph binary: history for `ChargeCard` returned exactly the 2 commits that touched it and excluded the unrelated one. Full suite 2,454 tests green.\n- One design realization worth knowing: git-meta rejects `/` inside key segments, so entity keys are hex-encoded inside the index keys (single source of truth in one helper). This is internal to the index — the shared `entity_deltas.json` schema is untouched, so the cli PR is unaffected.\n\nScoreboard: **graph ✅ done, brain ✅ done, cli ⏳ still building.** Once cli reports, I run the adversarial verification pass across all three, then push and open the PRs."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2184,"cache_read_input_tokens":141532,"output_tokens":864,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":376},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2184,"ephem