{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-08-18T19:44:15.245Z","sessionId":"de272aad-c620-4d71-bbdd-27dd2d3dc8af","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>a3b4a8e6a3e9b42ea</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>REDACTED</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-suhaan-devenv/f507d58c-285f-4d11-b1d0-201f2a5e172d/tasks/a3b4a8e6a3e9b42ea.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"CLI PR: checkpoint entity deltas\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>COR-782 done in `/Users/suhaan/devenv/cli-keystone` on `feat/checkpoint-entity-deltas`.\n\n**Gate**: `settings.IsEntityDeltasEnabled` — `entity_deltas` settings key + `ENTIRE_ENTITY_DELTAS=1|true` env override, off by default. Copied verbatim from the local `IsImageExternalizationEnabled` precedent (env-first, `mergeRawBool` so `settings.local.json` can enable/kill it).\n\n**Hook point: (a) MetadataDir** — zero changes to `api/checkpoint` or any store; the existing `WriteOptions.MetadataDir` → `copyMetadataDir` path already drops files into the per-session dir and is shared by both git backends (`gitRefsStore` embeds the same `treeWriter`). (b) would have meant a new WriteRequest + dispatch case in every store. Verified the stop-time transcript backfill does **not** clear the session dir, so the file survives.\n\n**Files**\n- `cmd/entire/cli/strategy/entity_deltas.go` (new, 300 lines) — frozen schema types, `stageEntityDeltas` (gate → base/head/repoDir resolve → produce → stage temp dir), `computeEntityDeltas` (LookPath `entire-graph`, 10s `context.WithTimeout` + `WaitDelay`, `cmd.Output()`), `entityDeltaFromChange`, `normalizeEntityChange`, `discardEntityDeltas`.\n- `cmd/entire/cli/strategy/manual_commit_condensation.go` +7 lines: `MetadataDir: stageEntityDeltas(ctx, logCtx, repo, o, attrBase)` at :412 in the `writeOpts` literal (same `attrBase` attribution uses), `defer discardEntityDeltas(writeOpts.MetadataDir)` at :434.\n- `cmd/entire/cli/settings/settings.go` +26: `EntityDeltas` field :149, merge :989, `IsEntityDeltasEnabled` :1398.\n- Tests: `strategy/entity_deltas_test.go`, `settings/settings_entity_deltas_test.go`.\n\n**Two deviations worth flagging**\n1. Argv is `entire-graph diff --base … --head … --repo … --json`, **not** `entire-graph graph diff …`. The `graph` token is the plugin name, which `resolvePlugin` strips before exec; the binary's own switch has no `graph` case (confirmed in `entire-graph/internal/cli/root.go:52`). Documented in-code.\n2. The producer emits `signature_changed`/`body_changed`, which are outside the frozen enum, so they fold to `modified` (unknown future types too). Verified against `entire-graph/internal/sem/model.go` — that's also where the exact JSON tags came from. `producer_version` is decoded from an optional top-level `version`; the current binary emits none, so it's omitted. `Fingerprint` has no producer source, always omitted.\n\n**Tests** (13 + 6): `TestStageEntityDeltas_{DisabledIsNoOp, WritesFrozenSchema, ProducerAbsentSkips, ProducerErrorSkips, ProducerBadJSONSkips, ProducerHangIsKilled, EmptyRangeSkips}`, `TestCondenseSession_{WritesEntityDeltasIntoCheckpointTree, ProducerAbsentLeavesCheckpointIntact}`, `TestEntityDeltasFromDiff_NeverNil`, `TestEntityDeltaFromChange_{NameAndPathFallbacks, OldFieldsAreChangeScoped}`, `TestNormalizeEntityChange`, plus `TestIsEntityDeltasEnabled_*` / `TestEntireSettings_EntityDeltasJSONTag`. PATH-stub producer is a `#!/bin/sh` script (matches `explain_test.go`), Windows-skipped; `setupGitRepo`/`testutil.InitRepo` + `t.Chdir` + `ENTIRE_CONFIG_DIR`; `t.Parallel()` on the pure mapping tests only.\n\n**Two things I had to chase**\n- `maintidx` on `CondenseSession` was already sitting *exactly* at the threshold (MI 20) before my change, so any addition tripped it — including comment lines, which count toward LOC. Held it at 20 by inlining the call into the struct literal and keeping the comment to one line. No refactor of their function.\n- The full `./...` run flaked twice on my tree (`TestAttach_DiscoversExternalAgents`, `TestExternalCommand_SigintReachesPlugin` — both timing/subprocess tests in `cmd/entire/cli`). Isolated A/B says it's machine load, not me: strategy package 54.9s/55.3s mine vs 51.9s base (= my tests' own ~3s), and `cmd/entire/cli` 108.8s with the gate live vs 107.4s with it short-circuited. Shortened the hang stub from `sleep 60` to `sleep 10` to stop leaving long-lived orphans.\n\n**Gate**: `mise run check` exit 0 (fmt + lint 0 issues + `test:ci` with `-race -tags=integration` + Vogon canary 4/4). **Commit**: `0837a9426`, no AI footers, not pushed.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>252033</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>147</tool_uses><duration_ms>4118252</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
