{"parentUuid":"1bb7d030-9353-47a8-bea6-45b18735abd0","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_011CeAnbkN5uZb1PeBS9dB3P","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All three builds are done. Now the doctrine step: adversarial verification before anything gets pushed — three skeptics, told to refute, one per risk surface. One thing I already flagged for the cli skeptic: the builder chose a **synchronous** staging path with a 10s producer timeout inside the post-commit hook (gate default-off softens it, but a 10s worst-case hook stall when enabled needs scrutiny — hook latency burned this repo before)."}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2480,"cache_read_input_tokens":147795,"output_tokens":6218,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1970},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2480,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":6218,"cache_read_input_tokens":147795,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2480,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2480},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CeAnbeuupc7hUm52PB56i","type":"assistant","uuid":"fc256b58-b22d-4967-a786-e6863a751b46","timestamp":"2026-08-18T19:44:52.562Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"f507d58c-285f-4d11-b1d0-201f2a5e172d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"de272aad-c620-4d71-bbdd-27dd2d3dc8af","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"quizzical-sniffing-quasar"}
{"parentUuid":"fc256b58-b22d-4967-a786-e6863a751b46","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_011CeAnbkN5uZb1PeBS9dB3P","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01XqtYU2FwdArgYHFCDymbmF","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Skeptic: brain PR review","subagent_type":"general-purpose","model":"opus","prompt":"ADVERSARIAL REVIEW. Default verdict: the code is WRONG until you independently verify otherwise. You are reviewing a teammate-agent's work before it becomes a PR; your job is to find real defects, not to praise. Use rtk where possible. READ-ONLY — do not fix anything.\n\nWorktree /Users/suhaan/devenv/p0p1/brain-keystone (entire-brain, branch feat/entity-checkpoint-index, 3 commits off origin/main: 6355c07c factgitmeta MetaStore, 97c7935e internal/entityindex, 5de2688c cli/MCP/freshness/provenance). `git log --oneline origin/main..HEAD` then review the FULL diff of each commit.\n\nClaimed design (verify, don't trust): entity→checkpoint index over git-meta ref refs/meta/local/main; forward key commit/<sha> \"brain:entities\" = delta doc {\"schema_version\":\"1.0\",...}; reverse project \"brain:entity:<hex(path#kind#name)>\" list:push sha; alias \"brain:entity-alias:<hex>\"; HWM \"brain:entities-head:<hex(branch)>\" advances only when a pass leaves nothing unindexed; --limit picks NEWEST unindexed converging backwards; first-parent diffs; unknown change types fold to \"modified\"; distill provenance resolves fact Locus→introducing checkpoint w/ fallback to LatestCheckpoint (no-index/no-match/>5-entity ambiguity); watch+session-end freshness bounded 10 commits/90s failure-silent; NEW shared MetaStore serializes fact-head writer + index writer on one lockfile.\n\nHUNT SPECIFICALLY:\n1. MetaStore refactor REGRESSION risk: the pre-existing facts Backend (internal/factgitmeta/backend.go) now shares lock+CAS with the index writer. Deadlock? Lock ordering? Behavior change for existing facts sync/tests? Compare old vs new code paths line by line.\n2. HWM correctness: can a failure path advance the HWM past unindexed commits (silent permanent gap)? Can bounded passes livelock or re-scan the same window forever? What happens on branch switch / rebase / force-move of checkpoint refs?\n3. Reverse-index consistency: partial-failure between forward write and reverse push — what state results, is it repaired on re-run (idempotency claim)?\n4. Provenance: can the new anchor pick a checkpoint from a DIFFERENT branch/session than the fact's? Off-by-one (parent vs commit)? Does fallback truly preserve today's behavior byte-for-byte?\n5. Freshness step: prove it cannot block or fail the session-end hook / watch tick (panic path? unbounded git walk before the 10-commit cap applies?).\n6. applyBatch replacing State.Apply clone-per-mutation: aliasing bugs from shared references?\n7. Run: `go build ./... && go vet ./...` and `go test ./internal/entityindex/ ./internal/cli/ ./internal/factgitmeta/ ./internal/factsync/ ./internal/factmerge/` — full output pass/fail. If quick, run the whole suite.\n8. Tests that assert nothing (would pass with the feature deleted)? Spot-check 3 by inspection.\n\nReport caveman-ultra: verdict per hunt item (REFUTED-A-DEFECT w/ file:line + failure scenario, or VERIFIED-OK w/ the evidence that convinced you), test-run results, and a final ship/no-ship call. Max 35 lines."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2480,"cache_read_input_tokens":147795,"output_tokens":6218,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1970},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2480,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":6218,"cache_read_input_tokens":147795,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2480,"cache_crea