: 6355c07c factgitmeta MetaStore, 97c7935e internal/entityindex, 5de2688c cli/MCP/freshness/provenance). `git log --oneline origin/main..HEAD` then review the FULL diff of each commit.\n\nClaimed design (verify, don't trust): entity→checkpoint index over git-meta ref refs/meta/local/main; forward key commit/<sha> \"brain:entities\" = delta doc {\"schema_version\":\"1.0\",...}; reverse project \"brain:entity:<hex(path#kind#name)>\" list:push sha; alias \"brain:entity-alias:<hex>\"; HWM \"brain:entities-head:<hex(branch)>\" advances only when a pass leaves nothing unindexed; --limit picks NEWEST unindexed converging backwards; first-parent diffs; unknown change types fold to \"modified\"; distill provenance resolves fact Locus→introducing checkpoint w/ fallback to LatestCheckpoint (no-index/no-match/>5-entity ambiguity); watch+session-end freshness bounded 10 commits/90s failure-silent; NEW shared MetaStore serializes fact-head writer + index writer on one lockfile.\n\nHUNT SPECIFICALLY:\n1. MetaStore refactor REGRESSION risk: the pre-existing facts Backend (internal/factgitmeta/backend.go) now shares lock+CAS with the index writer. Deadlock? Lock ordering? Behavior change for existing facts sync/tests? Compare old vs new code paths line by line.\n2. HWM correctness: can a failure path advance the HWM past unindexed commits (silent permanent gap)? Can bounded passes livelock or re-scan the same window forever? What happens on branch switch / rebase / force-move of checkpoint refs?\n3. Reverse-index consistency: partial-failure between forward write and reverse push — what state results, is it repaired on re-run (idempotency claim)?\n4. Provenance: can the new anchor pick a checkpoint from a DIFFERENT branch/session than the fact's? Off-by-one (parent vs commit)? Does fallback truly preserve today's behavior byte-for-byte?\n5. Freshness step: prove it cannot block or fail the session-end hook / watch tick (panic path? unbounded git walk before the 10-commit cap applies?).\n6. applyBatch replacing State.Apply clone-per-mutation: aliasing bugs from shared references?\n7. Run: `go build ./... && go vet ./...` and `go test ./internal/entityindex/ ./internal/cli/ ./internal/factgitmeta/ ./internal/factsync/ ./internal/factmerge/` — full output pass/fail. If quick, run the whole suite.\n8. Tests that assert nothing (would pass with the feature deleted)? Spot-check 3 by inspection.\n\nReport caveman-ultra: verdict per hunt item (REFUTED-A-DEFECT w/ file:line + failure scenario, or VERIFIED-OK w/ the evidence that convinced you), test-run results, and a final ship/no-ship call. Max 35 lines.","outputFile":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-suhaan-devenv/f507d58c-285f-4d11-b1d0-201f2a5e172d/tasks/ac95c739ddd0c956e.output","canReadOutputFile":true},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"23eb5db1-acb8-46d2-8f38-c0bc6285e517","session_id":"f507d58c-285f-4d11-b1d0-201f2a5e172d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"de272aad-c620-4d71-bbdd-27dd2d3dc8af","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"quizzical-sniffing-quasar"}
{"parentUuid":"a83e2604-7878-416a-8ef3-7dbf581dbd7d","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_011CeAnbkN5uZb1PeBS9dB3P","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Fif1z8hi1ZgZZ1kwMocBqe","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Skeptic: cli PR review","subagent_type":"general-purpose","model":"opus","prompt":"ADVERSARIAL REVIEW. Default verdict: WRONG until you independently verify. Find real defects; do not fix. Use rtk. READ-ONLY.\n\nWorktree /Users/suhaan/devenv/cli-keystone (entireio/cli, branch feat/checkpoint-entity-deltas, single commit 0837a9426 off origin/main). Review the full diff.\n\nClaimed design (verify, don't trust): gated (settings `entity_deltas` + env ENTIRE_ENTITY_DELTAS, default OFF) entity-delta capture at checkpoint condense: stageEntityDeltas (cmd/entire/cli/strategy/entity_deltas.go) LookPaths `entire-graph`, runs `entire-graph diff --base <attrBase> --head <head> --repo <dir> --json` w/ 10s timeout, maps to frozen schema doc, stages temp dir via WriteOptions.MetadataDir → lands as entity_deltas.json in the checkpoint per-session dir; ANY error = silent skip; defer discardEntityDeltas cleans temp dir; manual_commit_condensation.go +7 lines.\n\nHUNT SPECIFICALLY:\n1. HOOK LATENCY — the critical one. stageEntityDeltas runs SYNCHRONOUSLY inside CondenseSession, which runs in the git post-commit hook. With the gate ON, worst case adds 10s to every commit. Trace the exact call path and time budget; compare to how Attribution handles the same problem (async backfill?). Is sync-with-10s-cap acceptable here, or a defect vs the repo's own latency discipline? Give a measured or code-traced answer, not vibes. Also: does the 10s timeout actually kill the subprocess on all paths (WaitDelay semantics), or can it leak/hang the hook?\n2. Gate default: prove OFF by default on every path (settings absent, settings.local, env unset/empty/0). Can `mergeRawBool` or the merge order accidentally enable it?\n3. Failure modes: producer absent / errors / emits garbage JSON / emits 100MB — silent skip in ALL cases? Any path where the checkpoint write itself fails or the temp dir leaks (defer ordering vs early returns)?\n4. Correctness of the invocation: `entire-graph diff` (no `graph` token) — verify against /Users/suhaan/devenv/graph-keystone (the binary's arg parsing at internal/cli/root.go) that this argv actually works, including `--repo`. Would the WRONG argv fail silently forever (gate on + no deltas ever + no signal)? Is there any logging when skipped?\n5. Schema fidelity: compare the emitted doc field-by-field against this frozen contract: {\"schema_version\":\"1.0\",\"producer\":\"entire-graph\",\"producer_version\"?,\"base\",\"head\",\"computed_at\" RFC3339-UTC,\"entities\":[{\"change\":\"added|removed|modified|renamed|moved\",\"kind\",\"name\",\"old_name\"?,\"path\",\"old_path\"?,\"signature\"?,\"old_signature\"?,\"start_line\",\"fingerprint\"?}]} — names, omitempty, enum folding (signature_changed/body_changed→modified), UTC.\n6. Multi-session checkpoints: MetadataDir applies to WHICH session dir when several sessions condense? Could deltas attach to the wrong session or get dropped for all-but-one?\n7. Tests honest? Would TestCondenseSession_WritesEntityDeltasIntoCheckpointTree pass if stageEntityDeltas were stubbed to no-op? Spot-check the strongest 3 tests for vacuity.\n8. Run: `cd /Users/suhaan/devenv/cli-keystone && go build ./... && go test ./cmd/entire/cli/strategy/ ./cmd/entire/cli/settings/` — report results (skip full mise check, already run by builder).\n\nReport caveman-ultra: per hunt item REFUTED-A-DEFECT (file:line + concrete failure scenario) or VERIFIED-OK (evidence), test results, ship/no-ship. Max 35 lines."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2480,"cache_read_input_tokens":147795,"output_tokens":6218,"output_tokens_details":