"kind\",\"name\",\"old_name\"?,\"path\",\"old_path\"?,\"signature\"?,\"old_signature\"?,\"start_line\",\"fingerprint\"?}]}\n\nThree implementations:\nA. /Users/suhaan/devenv/graph-keystone (branch feat/diff-schema-version, commit b6ddbb7): the PRODUCER — `entire graph diff --json` output (sem.Result, internal/sem/model.go). Diff vs origin/main.\nB. /Users/suhaan/devenv/cli-keystone (branch feat/checkpoint-entity-deltas, commit 0837a9426): CONSUMER→WRITER — cmd/entire/cli/strategy/entity_deltas.go parses A's output, writes the doc.\nC. /Users/suhaan/devenv/p0p1/brain-keystone (branch feat/entity-checkpoint-index): CONSUMER→WRITER — internal/entityindex/graphdiff.go + doc.go parse A's output, write the doc into git-meta.\n\nCHECK, field by field, with the actual Go structs + JSON tags side by side:\n1. B and C parse A's output using the SAME field names A actually emits (Type/Kind/Name/OldName/NewName/OldSignature/NewSignature/OldPath/NewPath/AfterStartLine + file-level Path/OldPath — pull the real JSON tags from A's model.go, including whether A emits lowercase/camel/exact-case tags). Any field B or C reads that A never emits (silent always-zero)? Any A field with omitempty that B/C assume present?\n2. B's doc vs C's doc: identical field names, identical omitempty decisions, identical change-enum folding (incl. signature_changed/body_changed→modified and unknown→modified), identical time format (RFC3339 UTC \"Z\"), identical name/path fallback rules (NewName||Name, NewPath||file Path). Produce a table: field | B behavior | C behavior | MATCH/MISMATCH.\n3. A's new schema_version/producer_version fields: additive-only (no removed/renamed fields in the diff)? Do B and C both TOLERATE their absence (old binary) and presence (new binary)?\n4. Invocation drift: B execs `entire-graph diff ...` directly; C execs `entire graph diff ...` via the entire CLI plugin dispatch. Verify BOTH argv forms reach the same handler with the same flags (A's root.go arg parsing + the plugin-name-stripping behavior), including --repo handling and cwd assumptions.\n5. If any mismatch found: state the concrete interop failure it causes and which side should move (contract says the frozen doc wins).\n\nReport caveman-ultra: the field table, per-check ALIGNED/MISMATCH w/ file:line evidence, final verdict. Max 40 lines.","outputFile":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-suhaan-devenv/f507d58c-285f-4d11-b1d0-201f2a5e172d/tasks/aed1cceaa8097ad9e.output","canReadOutputFile":true},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"c11f2712-8d0c-4df3-b29e-7b1575aacaf1","session_id":"f507d58c-285f-4d11-b1d0-201f2a5e172d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"de272aad-c620-4d71-bbdd-27dd2d3dc8af","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"quizzical-sniffing-quasar"}
