{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-08-18T19:47:28.650Z","sessionId":"de272aad-c620-4d71-bbdd-27dd2d3dc8af","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>a7fe2c00d403812c8</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>REDACTED</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-suhaan-devenv/f507d58c-285f-4d11-b1d0-201f2a5e172d/tasks/a7fe2c00d403812c8.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Verify entire-graph diff argv\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>## VERIFIED — argv works exactly as specified\n\n**Repo:** `/Users/suhaan/devenv/graph-keystone` (source), built binary at `/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-suhaan-devenv/de272aad-c620-4d71-bbdd-27dd2d3dc8af/scratchpad/entire-graph`\n\n### 1. Dispatch — direct token, no `graph` prefix, no argv[0] rewriting\n`internal/cli/root.go:41` `Run(ctx, opts, args)` — plain `switch args[0]` (line 71), `case \"diff\": return runDiff(...)`. No cobra, no os.Args[0]/plugin-env dispatch rewriting anywhere in root.go. `cmd/entire-graph/main.go:1-19` — `main()` just calls `cli.Execute(version, os.Args[1:])`. Comment at top of main.go: \"Once built as executable named `entire-graph`, the parent Entire CLI dispatches it when a user runs `entire graph`\" — i.e. the `graph` token is stripped by the **parent `entire` CLI's** plugin dispatcher, not by this binary. Called directly, `entire-graph diff ...` is correct — no `graph` token needed/accepted.\n\n### 2. Flags — exact match\n`internal/cli/root.go` `parseDiffFlags` (~line 605) + `parseCommonFlags`: `--base` (default `HEAD~1`), `--head` (default `HEAD`), `--repo` (defaults to git-root of cwd via `resolveRepo`, root.go:709), `--json` (bool, from `parseCommonFlags`). All optional, no required flags, no shorthand. Unknown flags rejected non-zero (verified live, see below). `--` separator supported for literal path args.\n\n### 3. JSON shape — `internal/sem/model.go:82-97`\n```go\ntype Result struct {\n  Checkpoint      string            `json:\"checkpoint,omitempty\"`\n  Base            string            `json:\"base\"`\n  Head            string            `json:\"head\"`\n  Files           []FileChange      `json:\"files\"`\n  Warnings        []ProviderWarning `json:\"warnings,omitempty\"`\n  SchemaVersion   string            `json:\"schema_version\"`\n  ProducerVersion string            `json:\"producer_version,omitempty\"`\n}\ntype FileChange struct {\n  Path string `json:\"path\"`; OldPath string `json:\"old_path,omitempty\"`\n  Status string `json:\"status\"`; Language string `json:\"language,omitempty\"`\n  Changes []EntityChange `json:\"changes\"`\n}\ntype EntityChange struct {\n  Type string `json:\"type\"`; Kind string `json:\"kind\"`; Name string `json:\"name\"`\n  OldName,NewName string `json:\"old_name,omitempty\"/\"new_name,omitempty\"`\n  OldSignature,NewSignature string `json:\"old_signature,omitempty\"/\"new_signature,omitempty\"`\n  OldPath,NewPath string `json:\"old_path,omitempty\"/\"new_path,omitempty\"`\n  BeforeStartLine,AfterStartLine int `json:\"before_start_line,omitempty\"/\"after_start_line,omitempty\"`\n  DependentsCount int `json:\"dependents_count\"`; Similarity float64 `json:\"similarity,omitempty\"`\n  Reconciliation string `json:\"reconciliation,omitempty\"`\n}\n```\n**NO top-level `version` field** — it's `schema_version` (observed `\"1.1\"`) + `producer_version` (`\"dev\"` for this unversioned build). Files ARE under `files` key with `path`/`changes` (also `old_path` when renamed, omitempty). Change tag names confirmed exactly as asked, PLUS `before_start_line`, `dependents_count`, `similarity`, `reconciliation` (not asked but present).\n\n**`type` enum** — exactly 6 values, grep-verified `internal/sem/analyze.go`: `added`, `removed`, `renamed`, `moved`, `signature_changed`, `body_changed`. No `\"modified\"` value exists.\n\n### 4. Stdout purity\n`printResult` (root.go, final func) is the ONLY stdout writer on the diff path — JSON via `json.MarshalIndent` or text via `sem.WriteText`. `--progress` output (if passed) goes to **stderr** (`diffProgressLine`, root.go ~830). Live-verified: stderr was empty on a real run, stdout was pure JSON from byte 0.\n\n### 5. Exit codes\nSuccess = 0 (including zero-diff case, `files:null`). Non-zero (1) on: bad repo path (`chdir: no such file or directory`), unknown flag (rejected by name with helpful message, not silently swallowed as a path — this was a deliberate anti-footgun fix per code comment in `parseDiffFlags`). No index/cache is required for `diff` — it re-parses from git objects each run; the tree-hash record cache (`sem.LoadProviderRecords`) only applies to `snapshot`/`symbols`/`edges` modes, NOT `diff`.\n\n### 6. Live run — `cli-keystone` (real repo), `--base origin/main --head HEAD`\n- Cold: **exit 0, 4.51s**, 32,076 bytes JSON, 5 files changed, clean parse.\n- Repeat run (still no cache for diff): **~3.5-4.5s** each time — consistent, well under a 10s budget for this repo size, but note **no caching exists for `diff` itself** so cost is per-invocation.\n- `files:null` (not `[]`) when base==head, `warnings` key omitted when empty (omitempty).\n\n### PATH / version\n`which entire-graph` → **not found** (exit 127) — not on `$PATH` on this machine. No system install exists; only the just-built binary at the scratchpad path and the repo's own `entire-graph` binary artifact (`/Users/suhaan/devenv/graph-keystone/entire-graph`, 76MB, untested/unverified which version — the source in this checkout builds and runs correctly as shown above).</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>69914</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>15</tool_uses><duration_ms>87982</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
