{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-08-18T19:49:53.278Z","sessionId":"de272aad-c620-4d71-bbdd-27dd2d3dc8af","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>aed1cceaa8097ad9e</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_01RcbkQmQZThDwtoRU8fewat</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-suhaan-devenv/f507d58c-285f-4d11-b1d0-201f2a5e172d/tasks/aed1cceaa8097ad9e.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Skeptic: cross-PR contract\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>ADVERSARIAL CONTRACT CHECK — verdict: MISMATCH (confirmed, not \"disagree until proven aligned\" — proven disagree)\n\n**A's real Result (graph-keystone internal/sem/model.go:82-99, EntityChange:54-72)**: NOT the frozen doc shape. Result={Checkpoint,Base,Head,Files[],Warnings,SchemaVersion=\"1.1\"(json:\"schema_version\"),ProducerVersion(json:\"producer_version,omitempty\")}. FileChange={Path,OldPath,Status,Language,Changes[]}. EntityChange={Type,Kind,Name,OldName,NewName,OldSignature,NewSignature,OldPath,NewPath,BeforeStartLine,AfterStartLine(both omitempty),DependentsCount,Similarity,Reconciliation}. **No \"entities\",\"producer\",\"computed_at\" anywhere in A** — those 3 doc fields are pure B/C invention, not sourced from A. **EntityChange has no Fingerprint field** (only the separate Entity type does, not exposed in diff output).\n\n**Field table (doc-level, B=cli-keystone entity_deltas.go, C=brain-keystone graphdiff.go/doc.go):**\n\n| field | B | C | verdict |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| schema_version | const \"1.0\" | const \"1.0\" | ALIGNED |\n| producer | const \"entire-graph\" | const \"entire-graph\" | ALIGNED |\n| producer_version | reads A key `\"version\"` (entity_deltas.go:93) — **A never emits this key**, always \"\" | never reads A's `producer_version`; instead stuffs A's `schema_version` into it (graphdiff.go:96-98) — always \"1.1\", wrong semantics | **MISMATCH** — both wrong, differently |\n| change enum fold | body/sig_changed→modified (entity_deltas.go:301-307) | same (graphdiff.go:169-182) | ALIGNED |\n| name/path fallback | NewName\\|\\|Name, NewPath\\|\\|file.Path | identical | ALIGNED |\n| old_name | set **only** when Change==\"renamed\" (entity_deltas.go:287-292) | set whenever OldName≠resolved name, **any** change type (graphdiff.go:141-144) | **MISMATCH** — a moved+renamed entity (A sets OldName+NewName on Type=\"moved\", analyze.go:392-394) loses old_name in B, kept in C |\n| start_line | `AfterStartLine`, **no fallback** (entity_deltas.go:282) | `AfterStartLine`, falls back to `BeforeStartLine` if 0 (graphdiff.go:145-150) | **MISMATCH** — every `removed` entity: A's `removedChange()` (analyze.go:555-563) sets only BeforeStartLine, AfterStartLine stays 0/omitted → B writes `start_line:0` for all removals, C writes the real line |\n| fingerprint | never set | reads A key `\"fingerprint\"` — A never emits it at EntityChange level | both always-empty (vestigial), but C's field is a phantom read of a key A never has (check-1 violation) |\n| computed_at | time.Now().UTC().Format(RFC3339) | same | ALIGNED |\n\n**Per-check:**\n1. **MISMATCH** — B's `version`↔A's `producer_version` key mismatch (silent always-zero); C's `Fingerprint`↔A never emits it at EntityChange level (silent always-zero, both sides).\n2. **MISMATCH** — old_name drop (moved+renamed) and start_line-on-removal, both above, evidenced file:line.\n3. **Additive-confirmed**: `git diff origin/main..HEAD -- model.go` = +11/-0 only. Both tolerate absence (Go zero-value decode) fine, but C's presence-handling misassigns schema_version→producer_version (a new-field bug, not an absence bug).\n4. **ALIGNED mechanically**: B execs `entire-graph diff …` (LookPath, argv[0]=\"diff\") — direct match to root.go:70. C execs `entire graph diff …`; plugin.go resolvePlugin (no built-in \"graph\" cobra cmd found — verified) strips \"graph\", forwards `[\"diff\",...]` to `entire-graph` — same argv[0]=\"diff\", same handler. Confirmed no collision. One asymmetry: B passes explicit `--repo` + `cmd.Dir`; C passes neither `--repo` flag nor visible `cmd.Dir` in graphdiff.go, relying on `ENTIRE_REPO_ROOT` env (plugin.go:169, from outer `entire`'s cwd) — not provably broken from these 2 files alone, but a fragility C should harden with explicit `--repo`.\n\n**Contract says frozen doc wins → which side moves:**\n- B: fix `graphDiffResult.Version` json tag `\"version\"`→`\"producer_version\"`; add BeforeStartLine fallback for start_line on removal; carry old_name whenever OldName≠Name regardless of change bucket.\n- C: stop assigning A's `schema_version` into `delta.ProducerVersion`; decode A's actual `producer_version` key instead; drop the dead `Fingerprint` read or note it's currently unpopulatable given A's schema.\n\nFiles: `/Users/suhaan/devenv/graph-keystone/internal/sem/model.go`, `/Users/suhaan/devenv/graph-keystone/internal/sem/analyze.go`, `/Users/suhaan/devenv/graph-keystone/internal/cli/root.go`, `/Users/suhaan/devenv/cli-keystone/cmd/entire/cli/strategy/entity_deltas.go`, `/Users/suhaan/devenv/cli-keystone/cmd/entire/cli/plugin.go`, `/Users/suhaan/devenv/p0p1/brain-keystone/internal/entityindex/graphdiff.go`, `/Users/suhaan/devenv/p0p1/brain-keystone/internal/entityindex/doc.go`.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>118986</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>24</tool_uses><duration_ms>249515</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
