{"parentUuid":"8c327b5e-d699-400f-96dd-79b8e5b56291","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_011CeAo2cvJnoWie54waUGcQ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The contract checker earned its keep — **it found exactly the fork class that bit #85/#242, three real mismatches** between the two doc writers before anything shipped:\n\n1. **`producer_version` is broken on both sides, differently**: the cli reads a `\"version\"` key the graph never emits (always empty), and the brain stuffs the graph's `schema_version` (\"1.1\") into it (wrong meaning). Both should read the graph's actual new `producer_version` field.\n2. **`old_name` drops on moved+renamed entities in the cli** (it only carries old_name for `renamed`, but the graph legitimately sets a new name on `moved` too). The brain's behavior — carry old_name whenever it differs — is right; contract amended to that, cli moves.\n3. **`start_line` is 0 for every removed entity in the cli** (removals only have a *before* line; cli doesn't fall back to it, brain does). Brain right, cli moves.\n\nPlus one hardening item for the brain: its graph invocation relies on an inherited env var for repo targeting instead of passing the repo explicitly — works today (the live e2e passed), fragile tomorrow.\n\nThe graph PR itself came back clean: purely additive (+11/−0 on the model), and both argv styles provably reach the same handler.\n\nI'm holding the fixes until the other two skeptics (brain deep-review, cli deep-review) report, so each repo gets one consolidated fix pass instead of churn."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2762,"cache_read_input_tokens":157715,"output_tokens":1737,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1263},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2762,"ephemeral_5m