{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-08-18T19:51:54.872Z","sessionId":"de272aad-c620-4d71-bbdd-27dd2d3dc8af","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>ac7fa37feec50e1d4</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_01Fif1z8hi1ZgZZ1kwMocBqe</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-suhaan-devenv/f507d58c-285f-4d11-b1d0-201f2a5e172d/tasks/ac7fa37feec50e1d4.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Skeptic: cli PR review\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>**Build/test: `go build ./...` OK; `go test ./cmd/entire/cli/strategy/ ./cmd/entire/cli/settings/` → 1070 passed, exit 0.**\n\n**1. HOOK LATENCY — REFUTED-A-DEFECT (ship-blocker).** Measured, real `entire-graph` built from graph-keystone against cli-keystone: HEAD~1 → **3.48/3.51/3.50s** (3 runs, no caching — `diff` has no record cache); ~5 commits 5.15s; ~50 commits **11.86s (&gt;10s cap → produces nothing, ever)**; ~200 commits 21.98s/2.1MB. Path: `hooks_git_cmd.go:266 PostCommit` → `manual_commit_hooks.go:1394 CondenseSession` → `manual_commit_condensation.go:409` sync, **once per session**, no hook-wide deadline → N sessions = N×3.5s serial on every commit. Repo's own discipline says otherwise: `execx.SpawnDetached` fire-and-forget already used for analytics (`telemetry/detached.go:93`) and trail-cache refresh (`trail_context_cache.go:330`); neither used here. Worse, `agent/codex/lifecycle.go:94` sets a **2s** hard session-end budget (`lifecycle.go:1097`) — a 3.5s producer can only ever burn the whole budget and yield nothing.\n**1b. Kill semantics — VERIFIED-OK-with-gap.** Stdout(`Output()`)/Stderr are non-`*os.File` → pipes → `WaitDelay=2s` genuinely applies; bounded ≈12s, no hang. But no `Setpgid`: `checkpoint/remote/command_cancel_unix.go killProcessGroupOnCancel` exists for exactly this and is not used → grandchildren orphan.\n\n**2. Gate default OFF — VERIFIED-OK.** `mergeRawBool` (settings.go:1013-1019) writes only when key present; absent/local-enable/local-disable all covered by tests; env matches only `\"1\"`/`\"true\"`. Nit: env can only *enable* — no `=0` kill switch.\n\n**3. Failure modes — REFUTED-A-DEFECT ×2.** (a) **No output size cap**: `cmd.Output()` buffers unbounded and the result is committed verbatim to `entire/checkpoints/v1` per checkpoint per session forever; signatures embed whole struct bodies incl. comments (measured 686KB @50 commits, 2.1MB @200). (b) \"ANY error = silent skip\" is **false after staging**: `persistent.go:648-651 copyMetadataDir` error → `applySessionWrite` → `store.Write` → `CondenseSession` returns error → **whole checkpoint dropped** (`condenseAndUpdateState` Warn+false). Defer ordering VERIFIED-OK (no early return between literal and `defer`; staging failure self-cleans at entity_deltas.go:200).\n\n**4. Invocation — argv VERIFIED-OK; observability REFUTED-A-DEFECT.** Ran it: `entire-graph diff --base X --head Y --repo D --json` → exit 0, pure JSON on stdout, no `graph` token needed (`internal/cli/root.go` switches on `args[0]`). But every skip is `logging.Debug` and default level is **Info** (`logging/logger.go:238`), `entire-graph` is **not on PATH** on this machine and nothing installs it, and `entire doctor` has no probe → gate-on yields no deltas and **no signal, indefinitely**.\n\n**5. Schema fidelity — REFUTED-A-DEFECT ×3.** (a) `producer_version` is **never populated**: `entity_deltas.go:93` decodes `json:\"version\"`, but the producer's real top-level keys are `[base, files, head, producer_version, schema_version]` (verified live) → field always omitted; test `entity_deltas_test.go:129` asserts NotContains, enshrining it. (b) `graphFileChange.OldPath` (line 99) is decoded and **never read** → a renamed *file* whose entities are `body_changed` lands as `modified` with no `old_path`. (c) `removed` entities always get `start_line: 0` — producer emits `after_start_line` omitempty and `before_start_line` for removals, which isn't decoded. Rest OK: field names/omitempty match, enum folding correct against the real 6-value producer enum, `computed_at` RFC3339 UTC.\n\n**6. Multi-session — placement VERIFIED-OK, scope REFUTED-A-DEFECT.** MetadataDir is per-`CondenseSession` call → lands in that session's numbered dir (`persistent.go:640-651`); no cross-session drop/mixup. But the deltas are raw `base..head` git-range-scoped with **no filtering by `sessionData.FilesTouched`/`allAgentFiles`**, unlike attribution — so on a multi-session or human-edited commit, every session's `entity_deltas.json` contains the other sessions' and the human's entities. Also N× identical duplicated producer runs.\n\n**7. Tests — one vacuous, one blind spot.** `TestCondenseSession_WritesEntityDeltasIntoCheckpointTree` **would fail** if stubbed to no-op (asserts the tree file + 6 entities) — honest. `TestStageEntityDeltas_ProducerHangIsKilled` is **vacuous**: shortens the deadline to 200ms but only asserts `elapsed &lt; 30s` against a `sleep 10` stub — passes with the timeout entirely broken. **No test asserts the producer argv** (the stub ignores args), so a wrong argv would pass everything. `TestStageEntityDeltas_WritesFrozenSchema` tests a hand-written fixture whose keys diverge from the real producer — exactly how defect 5a survived.\n\n**VERDICT: NO-SHIP.** Default-off makes it non-urgent, but as built the feature is broken on its own terms: `producer_version` dead, file-rename provenance lost, no deltas at all past ~50-commit ranges, 3.5s+ synchronous cost per session per commit against a repo that already has the async and process-group primitives it needed.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>112603</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>39</tool_uses><duration_ms>385644</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
