{"parentUuid":"5b6f40be-277e-4df8-9746-6a2a062e2025","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_011CeAoBcKqmTZWbUArhfyBf","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Jq87T5bQGAgoqnwTi3YLZ7","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Fix cli PR: async + contract","subagent_type":"general-purpose","model":"opus","prompt":"FIX PASS in /Users/suhaan/devenv/cli-keystone (entireio/cli, branch feat/checkpoint-entity-deltas, commit 0837a9426 = the feature you're fixing; base origin/main). Use rtk. An adversarial review measured real defects; fix ALL of them. The feature: gated entity-delta capture writing entity_deltas.json into the checkpoint tree per session.\n\nDEFECTS TO FIX (all confirmed with evidence — do not re-litigate):\n\nARCHITECTURE (the big one):\n1. stageEntityDeltas runs SYNCHRONOUSLY in the post-commit hook via WriteOptions.MetadataDir (manual_commit_condensation.go:409): measured 3.5s per session per commit, serial across sessions; agent/codex/lifecycle.go:94 has a 2s session-end budget so it can NEVER succeed there; >10s ranges produce nothing ever. REWORK to the repo's own async discipline: compute + write AFTER the hook returns, via a detached process — the repo already ships the primitives: execx.SpawnDetached fire-and-forget (used by telemetry/detached.go:93 and trail_context_cache.go:330) and the write-request union has the BackfillAttribution precedent (api/checkpoint/metadata.go) for post-hoc writes into a checkpoint. Study how BackfillAttribution's write is applied, add a BackfillEntityDeltas request following it exactly, and trigger the compute+backfill through a detached `entire` subcommand invocation (hidden cmd, mirror how other detached work re-enters the CLI). The hook path's ONLY new cost must be spawning the detached process. Raise the producer timeout to 120s (nobody waits now).\n2. A staging/copy failure currently FAILS THE WHOLE CHECKPOINT: persistent.go:648-651 copyMetadataDir error propagates out of CondenseSession. With the backfill rework this must become structurally impossible: backfill errors are logged and dropped, never fail or block checkpoint creation. Prove with a test: backfill write erroring leaves the checkpoint intact.\n3. Subprocess hygiene: no Setpgid — use the existing killProcessGroupOnCancel (checkpoint/remote/command_cancel_unix.go) pattern so producer grandchildren die with the timeout. Cap producer output read at 8MB; over-cap = skip with a log line (docs get committed to the checkpoint branch forever — 2.1MB was measured on a 200-commit range).\n\nCONTRACT/SCHEMA (frozen doc wins):\n4. producer_version dead: decode the producer's REAL top-level key `producer_version` (verified live: keys are [base, files, head, producer_version, schema_version]) — not `version`. Populate doc's producer_version from it (omitempty).\n5. start_line 0 on removals: decode `before_start_line` and use it when `after_start_line` absent/0 (producer emits only before_start_line for removed entities).\n6. old_name dropped on moved+renamed: carry old_name whenever producer OldName differs from the resolved name, ANY change type (not just \"renamed\").\n7. File-level OldPath is decoded but never used: when an entity has no entity-level OldPath but its file has OldPath (renamed file), emit old_path from the file level.\n8. Multi-session scope bleed: deltas are raw base..head, so every session's doc contains other sessions'/human entities. Filter mapped entities to the session's own files (sessionData.FilesTouched / the same set attribution scopes by — match attribution's scoping exactly). Sessions with no intersecting files skip the producer run entirely.\n\nOBSERVABILITY/GATE:\n9. Every skip is logging.Debug but default level is Info → gate-on + missing binary = silent forever. Log ONE Info line per condense when the gate is on but the producer is unavailable; keep per-entity noise at Debug.\n10. Env gate: support explicit disable — ENTIRE_ENTITY_DELTAS=0/false force-disables even if settings enable it (mirror how other env overrides in settings.go handle tri-state, if a precedent exists; else document env-set-empty = fall through to settings).\n\nTESTS (close the vacuities):\n11. TestStageEntityDeltas_ProducerHangIsKilled asserts elapsed<30s with a 200ms deadline and sleep-10 stub — vacuous. Make it assert elapsed < ~2s (deadline 200ms, stub sleeps 10s) so a broken timeout FAILS.\n12. No test asserts the producer argv — make the PATH stub record its argv to a file and assert base/head/--repo/--json exactly.\n13. The frozen-schema test uses a hand-written fixture that diverged from the real producer (that's how defect 4 survived). Regenerate the fixture from the REAL producer's output shape: build the real binary from /Users/suhaan/devenv/graph-keystone (go build ./cmd/entire-graph) into a temp dir, run one real diff in a scratch repo, capture its JSON as the fixture (commit the captured fixture, not the binary). Add a comment in the fixture file naming the producer commit it was captured from.\n14. New tests for: backfill-error-leaves-checkpoint-intact (item 2), session-file filtering (item 8), before_start_line fallback, old_name-on-moved, file-level old_path, output-size cap skip.\n\nVERIFY: `mise run check` green (that's fmt+lint+test:ci -race). Keep the gate default OFF. Amend into a clean commit history on the branch (feel free to reset and re-commit as one or two logical commits), normal messages, NO AI footers/Co-Authored-By. Do NOT push.\n\nReport caveman-ultra: per defect # = what you did + file:line, test names added, check result, final commit sha(s). Max 30 lines."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4360,"cache_read_input_tokens":160477,"output_tokens":4096,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1704},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_t