ducer_version, schema_version]) — not `version`. Populate doc's producer_version from it (omitempty).\n5. start_line 0 on removals: decode `before_start_line` and use it when `after_start_line` absent/0 (producer emits only before_start_line for removed entities).\n6. old_name dropped on moved+renamed: carry old_name whenever producer OldName differs from the resolved name, ANY change type (not just \"renamed\").\n7. File-level OldPath is decoded but never used: when an entity has no entity-level OldPath but its file has OldPath (renamed file), emit old_path from the file level.\n8. Multi-session scope bleed: deltas are raw base..head, so every session's doc contains other sessions'/human entities. Filter mapped entities to the session's own files (sessionData.FilesTouched / the same set attribution scopes by — match attribution's scoping exactly). Sessions with no intersecting files skip the producer run entirely.\n\nOBSERVABILITY/GATE:\n9. Every skip is logging.Debug but default level is Info → gate-on + missing binary = silent forever. Log ONE Info line per condense when the gate is on but the producer is unavailable; keep per-entity noise at Debug.\n10. Env gate: support explicit disable — ENTIRE_ENTITY_DELTAS=0/false force-disables even if settings enable it (mirror how other env overrides in settings.go handle tri-state, if a precedent exists; else document env-set-empty = fall through to settings).\n\nTESTS (close the vacuities):\n11. TestStageEntityDeltas_ProducerHangIsKilled asserts elapsed<30s with a 200ms deadline and sleep-10 stub — vacuous. Make it assert elapsed < ~2s (deadline 200ms, stub sleeps 10s) so a broken timeout FAILS.\n12. No test asserts the producer argv — make the PATH stub record its argv to a file and assert base/head/--repo/--json exactly.\n13. The frozen-schema test uses a hand-written fixture that diverged from the real producer (that's how defect 4 survived). Regenerate the fixture from the REAL producer's output shape: build the real binary from /Users/suhaan/devenv/graph-keystone (go build ./cmd/entire-graph) into a temp dir, run one real diff in a scratch repo, capture its JSON as the fixture (commit the captured fixture, not the binary). Add a comment in the fixture file naming the producer commit it was captured from.\n14. New tests for: backfill-error-leaves-checkpoint-intact (item 2), session-file filtering (item 8), before_start_line fallback, old_name-on-moved, file-level old_path, output-size cap skip.\n\nVERIFY: `mise run check` green (that's fmt+lint+test:ci -race). Keep the gate default OFF. Amend into a clean commit history on the branch (feel free to reset and re-commit as one or two logical commits), normal messages, NO AI footers/Co-Authored-By. Do NOT push.\n\nReport caveman-ultra: per defect # = what you did + file:line, test names added, check result, final commit sha(s). Max 30 lines.","outputFile":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-suhaan-devenv/f507d58c-285f-4d11-b1d0-201f2a5e172d/tasks/a2ce260f93dd41028.output","canReadOutputFile":true},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"def201a2-e5ac-4f74-9fb0-9221921bb1f5","session_id":"f507d58c-285f-4d11-b1d0-201f2a5e172d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"de272aad-c620-4d71-bbdd-27dd2d3dc8af","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"quizzical-sniffing-quasar"}
{"parentUuid":"80994e35-a11e-41c4-b878-ac4698331ce6","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"queued_command","prompt":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>ac95c739ddd0c956e</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_01XqtYU2FwdArgYHFCDymbmF</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-suhaan-devenv/f507d58c-285f-4d11-b1d0-201f2a5e172d/tasks/ac95c739ddd0c956e.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Skeptic: brain PR review\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>Repo clean (overlay probes never touched it). Full suite green.\n\n---\n\n# ADVERSARIAL REVIEW — feat/entity-checkpoint-index — **NO-SHIP**\n\n**Build/vet/test:** `go build ./...` ✅ · `go vet ./...` ✅ · targeted 5 pkgs **2396 pass** ✅ · full suite **2455 pass, 12 pkgs** ✅. Green ≠ correct: 3 defects proven live via `go test -overlay` probes (repo untouched).\n\n**1. MetaStore \"refactor\" — VERIFIED-OK (no regression) but the commit message is false.**\n`internal/factgitmeta/backend.go` is **not in the diff** (0 deletions across all 3 commits). Nothing was \"lifted out\" — `store.go` is a copy-paste of Advance's read/commit/CAS loop and a byte-identical clone of `state()` (backend.go:275 ≡ store.go:137). Facts path unchanged ⇒ no regression (factgitmeta/factsync/factmerge tests pass). Serialization is real only because both call `openLocalRepo(gitDir).lock()` → same `factgitmeta.lock`. No deadlock: no nesting path exists today. **Latent:** `unix.Flock(LOCK_EX)` is per-FD, so any future nested Backend+MetaStore call self-deadlocks, unkillable.\n\n**2. HWM — REFUTED-A-DEFECT (proven).** `build.go:255` `complete := !truncated &amp;&amp; !walkCapped &amp;&amp; Failed==0` ignores `CheckpointsOnly`, and `HighWaterKey` (doc.go:154) isn't namespaced by mode. Probe: `backfill --checkpoints-only` → `indexed=1 skipped=1 highwater=bbbb…` (tip). Next **default** pass → `scanned=0 indexed=0`, commit `aaaa…` **permanently unindexed**, `Commits(\"a.go#function#Alpha\")==[]`. Silent permanent gap; only `--full` recovers. `TestBuildCheckpointsOnlySkipsPlainCommits` (:335) asserts nothing about HWM. No livelock found; branch-switch/rebase/prune fallback (`build.go:367`) is sound.\n\n**3. Reverse-index consistency — VERIFIED-OK.** Forward+reverse+alias+HWM ship in **one** `store.Update` = one ref CAS ⇒ no partial state. Pre-CAS re-check (`build.go:288`) drops whole groups, so a concurrent writer can't duplicate list appends. Kill mid-pass writes nothing.\n\n**4. Provenance — REFUTED-A-DEFECT (two).**\n(a) **Breaks `entire brain verify`.** `verify_cmd.go:427` requires `session.LatestCheckpoint == anchor.CheckpointID`; distill previously always set exactly that. Sharpening rewrites CheckpointID ⇒ falls to `bySession[0]` → **STALE** (\"session is now exported at checkpoint X\"), and `snapshotSourceTranscriptPath` (:498) needs `SessionID &amp;&amp; CheckpointID` to match → transcript mismatch → **STALE/ORPHANED**. Every sharpened fact downgrades. Untested.\n(b) **No session/branch scoping.** `entities_provenance.go:69` iterates the *whole* cache; `anchorFor` picks the globally newest checkpoint-bearing occurrence. A fact from session S can get session S′/another branch's checkpoint while `anchor.SessionID` keeps S (only Commit+CheckpointID are overwritten, :158-161) — an anchor pair that never existed. Privacy is safe (gates key off SessionID/Transcript). Also: `byPath` lookup (:151) has **no** ambiguity guard, unlike `byName`; \"introducing\" is actually *newest*; `at` is `%aI` (author date), wrong under rebase.\n\n**5. Freshness — REFUTED-A-DEFECT (three).** Cannot *fail* a hook/tick ✅ (both callers only warn; no panic path). But:\n(a) **Cannot be bounded.** `MetaStore.Update` → `unix.Flock(LOCK_EX)` blocks forever; the 90s `ctx` (`entities_cmd.go:741`) cannot interrupt it. Contended lock = hung session-end hook.\n(b) **The 10-commit cap applies after the walk.** No HWM ⇒ `git log --first-parent --max-count=20000 &lt;tip&gt;` with full `%B` bodies + full git-meta `State()` materialize, **every tick**. With `Limit=10` a big repo always sets `truncated` ⇒ HWM **never** advances ⇒ ~2000 ticks to converge, each re-walking all 20000.\n(c) **Derived cache poisoning (proven).** `entityCommitMetadata` swallows git errors (`entities_cmd.go:623 continue`), `rebuildEntityIndexCache` persists the empty join pinned to the current MetaTip, `loadEntityIndexView:523` then trusts it. Probe: after one failed `git log --no-walk`, all checkpoint/session joins are lost, **still served after git recovers** (`rebuilt=false`), and `newEntityProvenanceResolver` returns nil ⇒ distill silently reverts to coarse anchoring with no warning.\n\n**6. applyBatch — VERIFIED-OK.** Top-of-func clone is deep for Lists/Sets (state.go:30-35); `dropKeyTombstone`'s `in[:0]` only ever mutates that fresh copy; `&amp;candidate` in `observe` is a per-call copy. One divergence from `Apply`: the in-place string-update path (state.go:43-46) `continue`s **without** `dropKeyTombstone`, unlike `Apply` (apply.go:62). Needs a tombstone+string coexisting for one key — not shown reachable.\n\n**8. Tests that assert nothing (3 spot-checks).** `TestEntityProvenanceResolvesToTheChangingCheckpoint` (:342) — fixture's `LatestCheckpoint == entityFixtureCkptB` == the resolved value, so it passes with the whole feature deleted-and-fallback; the *sharpening* case (resolved ≠ latest) is never exercised, which is why the verify regression is invisible. `TestBuildCheckpointsOnlySkipsPlainCommits` (:335) — no HWM assertion (defect #2 lives here). `TestApplyBatchMatchesReferenceApply` (:531) — starts from `gitmeta.State{}`, so neither the in-place-update path nor tombstones nor pre-existing lists are covered.\n\n**Verdict: NO-SHIP.** Blockers: #2 (silent permanent index gap), #4a (regresses a shipped verify surface), #5c (self-poisoning cache). #5a/#5b make the \"bounded, token-free tick\" claim untrue in practice.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>145362</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>38</tool_uses><duration_ms>410213</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>","commandMode":"task-notification","timestamp":"2026-08-18T19:52:01.080Z"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"dfdddd6e-5ea0-4f22-ab73-b112cd6cacc3","timestamp":"2026-08-18T19:52:01.080Z","session_id":"f507d58c-285f-4d11-b1d0-201f2a5e172d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"de272aad-c620-4d71-bbdd-27dd2d3dc8af","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"quizzical-sniffing-quasar"}
