{"parentUuid":"1b86e27d-58eb-4984-829b-10ba4b84774a","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_011CeAoGE2nkRdS8ZUBRJwHd","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7386,"cache_read_input_tokens":164837,"output_tokens":5324,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":2465},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":7386,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":5324,"cache_read_input_tokens":164837,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7386,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":7386},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CeAoGBDctmkYGatNZUJxk","type":"assistant","uuid":"1bcab67b-acaa-42a6-a939-cb196ac3bdbb","timestamp":"2026-08-18T19:53:43.069Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"f507d58c-285f-4d11-b1d0-201f2a5e172d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"de272aad-c620-4d71-bbdd-27dd2d3dc8af","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"quizzical-sniffing-quasar"}
{"parentUuid":"1bcab67b-acaa-42a6-a939-cb196ac3bdbb","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_011CeAoGE2nkRdS8ZUBRJwHd","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01FuNNC9RrmHc2t74soeLHNG","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Fix brain PR: cursors+provenance","subagent_type":"general-purpose","model":"opus","prompt":"FIX PASS in /Users/suhaan/devenv/p0p1/brain-keystone (entire-brain, branch feat/entity-checkpoint-index, 3 commits off origin/main). Use rtk. An adversarial review PROVED these defects live (overlay probes); fix all. Do not re-litigate findings.\n\nSTRUCTURAL FIX 1 — replace the single high-water mark with a CONTIGUOUS INDEXED WINDOW:\nDefects it kills: (a) build.go:255 `complete := !truncated && !walkCapped && Failed==0` ignores CheckpointsOnly and HighWaterKey (doc.go:154) isn't mode-namespaced → a `--checkpoints-only` pass advances HWM to tip and plain commits before it are PERMANENTLY unindexed (proven). (b) Freshness tick with Limit=10 on a big repo: `git log --first-parent --max-count=20000` full-%B walk + full gitmeta State() EVERY tick, always truncated, HWM never advances, ~2000 ticks each re-walking 20000 commits.\nNew model: persist TWO cursors (one record, same git-meta location discipline): floor + tip of one contiguous fully-indexed range. Ticks extend tip forward (walk ONLY tip..branch-head — O(new commits)); backfill extends floor backward (`--limit` chunks converge backward, floor only moves when a chunk fully lands). `--checkpoints-only` NEVER moves cursors (it's a filtered convenience pass; document that). Idempotency: inside window → skip without reading full State(); use per-commit forward-key presence checks only at the window edges. Add tests: checkpoints-only leaves cursors untouched then default pass indexes what it skipped (the exact proven scenario: probe was backfill --checkpoints-only then default pass → scanned=0, commit aaaa unindexed); tick on repo-with-new-commits walks only the delta (assert via fake runner call count).\n\nSTRUCTURAL FIX 2 — provenance sharpening must not lie and must not break verify:\n(a) PROVEN regression: verify_cmd.go:427 requires session.LatestCheckpoint == anchor.CheckpointID; sharpened anchors fall to bySession[0] → STALE, and snapshotSourceTranscriptPath (:498) mismatches → STALE/ORPHANED. Teach verify to accept any checkpoint belonging to the anchor's session (resolve against the session's checkpoint set, and resolve the transcript path for THAT checkpoint), preserving current behavior for latest-checkpoint anchors byte-for-byte. Add the missing test case: sharpened fact (resolved ≠ latest) passes verify as VERIFIED not STALE.\n(b) Scoping: entities_provenance.go:69 iterates the whole cache; anchorFor can pair the fact's SessionID with ANOTHER session/branch's Commit+CheckpointID (:158-161) — an anchor that never existed. Constrain sharpening to checkpoints OF THE FACT'S OWN SESSION (same SessionID) on the fact's branch; anything else → fallback unchanged. Within-session semantics: the newest same-session checkpoint whose deltas touch the locus entity. Add ambiguity guard to the byPath lookup (:151) mirroring byName's >5 guard. Use committer date %cI not author date %aI for `at`.\nSTRUCTURAL FIX 3 — freshness tick must be truly non-blocking and the cache must not self-poison:\n(a) MetaStore.Update takes unix.Flock(LOCK_EX) which blocks forever; the 90s ctx (entities_cmd.go:741) cannot interrupt it → contended lock hangs the session-end hook. Add a non-blocking TryLock path (LOCK_EX|LOCK_NB) used by the freshness tick: contention → skip this tick silently (best-effort freshness). Backfill/CLI keep blocking behavior. Test: hold the lock, run the tick with a deadline, assert it returns promptly without indexing.\n(b) PROVEN cache poisoning: entityCommitMetadata swallows git errors (entities_cmd.go:623 continue), rebuildEntityIndexCache persists the empty join pinned to current MetaTip, loadEntityIndexView:523 serves it forever; provenance resolver silently nil. Fix: distinguish \"commit genuinely absent\" from \"git failed\" — on git failure, abort the rebuild WITHOUT persisting (serve previous cache or rebuild next call), log one warning. Test: fail git once, assert next call rebuilds and serves the real join (the proven scenario).\n\nCONTRACT FIXES (frozen doc wins, cross-checked against the real producer):\n4. graphdiff.go:96-98 stuffs the producer's schema_version (\"1.1\") into delta.ProducerVersion — wrong. Decode the producer's REAL top-level `producer_version` key (new graph builds emit it, omitempty) into ProducerVersion; tolerate absence.\n5. Drop the phantom EntityChange-level `fingerprint` read (producer never emits it at that level) or keep the doc field with a comment that no current producer populates it — no phantom decode.\n6. Harden the graph invocation: pass the repo explicitly (--repo <dir> — the producer accepts it; verified live) instead of relying on inherited ENTIRE_REPO_ROOT env.\n\nSMALLER:\n7. state.go:43-46 in-place string-update path `continue`s without dropKeyTombstone, diverging from Apply (apply.go:62) — make identical; extend TestApplyBatchMatchesReferenceApply to start from a NON-empty state including a tombstone+string coexisting on one key and pre-existing lists.\n8. Commit honesty: commit 6355c07c's message claims backend.go was refactored onto MetaStore — it wasn't (store.go duplicates the CAS loop; backend.go untouched; serialization only via the shared lockfile). When you rewrite history (fine to reset/re-commit the branch cleanly), make the message state the truth, and add a code comment on the duplication + the latent per-FD flock self-deadlock if Backend and MetaStore ever nest.\n9. The sharpening test fixture sets LatestCheckpoint == the resolved checkpoint, so it passes with the feature deleted — make the primary test exercise resolved ≠ latest (and keep a separate fallback test).\n\nVERIFY: re-run the three original mutations (reverse-index write removed; anchorFor always-fallback; cache tip-pin ignored) plus TWO new ones (cursor-advance-on-checkpoints-only re-introduced → test fails; cache-persist-on-git-error re-introduced → test fails). Full `go test ./...` green, gofmt/vet clean. Re-run the live e2e (it feature-detects the graph binary). Clean commit history, normal messages, NO AI footers. Do NOT push.\n\nReport caveman-ultra: per fix # = done+file:line, new test names, mutation results (5), suite result, final shas. Max 30 lines."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7386,"cache_read_input_tokens":164837,"output_tokens":5324,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":2465},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":7386,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":5324,"cache_read_input_tokens":164837,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7386,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":7386},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CeAoGBDctmkYGatNZUJxk","type":"assistant","uuid":"d4b5cc8d-82ef-4330-a2eb-15b3aaa1256c","timestamp":"2026-08-18T19:54:13.164Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"f507d58c-285f-4d11-b1d0-201f2a5e172d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"de272aad-c620-4d71-bbdd-27dd2d3dc8af","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"quizzical-sniffing-quasar"}
