{"parentUuid":"151cb0cb-9397-4281-875a-c14b7393dfb1","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_011CeArDk8o61fZNgfe32vYT","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"CLI fixer is done — all 14 defects addressed, with the architecture pivot landed (detached `__entity_deltas` child process + a proper backfill write request across all four store backends, hook cost reduced to a process spawn) and live-verified end-to-end with the real producer. `mise run check` green.\n\nThe rework introduced a lot of *new* surface (hidden command, job files, per-repo flock, a write request implemented in four stores) — that gets its own skeptic now, without waiting for the brain fixer:"}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2441,"cache_read_input_tokens":178778,"output_tokens":2094,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":534},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2441,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2094,"cache_read_input_tokens":178778,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2441,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2441},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CeArDg7hPASer4TKxm5ps","type":"assistant","uuid":"0c62db61-ddef-4df0-81fd-eafd7fe9298e","timestamp":"2026-08-18T20:32:00.498Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"f507d58c-285f-4d11-b1d0-201f2a5e172d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"de272aad-c620-4d71-bbdd-27dd2d3dc8af","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"quizzical-sniffing-quasar"}
{"parentUuid":"0c62db61-ddef-4df0-81fd-eafd7fe9298e","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_011CeArDk8o61fZNgfe32vYT","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01GiiyeziAnWmXGTf8P9YWst","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Re-verify cli fix pass","subagent_type":"general-purpose","model":"opus","prompt":"ADVERSARIAL RE-REVIEW, round 2. Default: WRONG until proven. READ-ONLY, use rtk. /Users/suhaan/devenv/cli-keystone (entireio/cli, branch feat/checkpoint-entity-deltas, commits e8432d01d + f57e55479 off origin/main). Round 1 found 14 defects in the old synchronous design; a fix pass replaced it with: post-commit hook writes a job file + execx.SpawnDetached child (`entire __entity_deltas <job>`) → RunEntityDeltasBackfill → producer (120s cap, Setpgid+pgid-kill, 8MB output cap) → new SessionEntityDeltas write request (api/checkpoint/interfaces.go:80) implemented in persistent/refs/fs/routing stores → entity_deltas.json into the already-committed checkpoint, per-repo flock serializing backfills.\n\nYour job: attack the NEW architecture — it is new code that round 1 never saw.\n\nHUNT:\n1. The backfill mutates an ALREADY-COMMITTED checkpoint. Trace exactly how each store applies SessionEntityDeltas (persistent_write.go:20, refs_store.go:122, fsstore.go:120, routing_store.go:254): amend? new commit on the checkpoint branch/ref? Does the result stay consistent with what condense wrote (tree layout, trailers, ref advance semantics, OPF/pre-push interaction)? Could a concurrent condense (next commit, same session) race the backfill's ref CAS and lose one side silently?\n2. Job file lifecycle: where written, what's in it, when deleted. Leak on child crash? Consumed twice (double backfill)? Any path/argument injection via the job file contents (it's fed to a hidden command)? Stale job from an old binary version parsed by a new one?\n3. SpawnDetached child environment: does the child re-check the gate (settings+env) or trust the job? Does it inherit the right HOME/config dir (hook context vs user shell)? What happens when `entire` re-execs itself but argv[0]/PATH resolves a DIFFERENT entire version?\n4. The per-repo flock in the child: blocking or non-blocking? Can a wedged backfill make every later backfill queue forever / pile up processes? Is there any TTL/cleanup?\n5. Hook-path cost now: prove the ONLY added sync work is job-write+spawn (no producer exec, no git walk). Any error path in scheduleEntityDeltas that can still propagate into CondenseSession's error return?\n6. Spot-check 5 of the round-1 fixes survived intact by reading the code (producer_version key, before_start_line fallback, old_name any-type, file-level old_path, session-file filtering incl. old_path matching), and confirm the fixture testdata/entity_deltas_producer_diff.json actually matches the real producer keys (compare against /Users/suhaan/devenv/graph-keystone internal/sem/model.go JSON tags).\n7. Tests honest? Would TestCondenseAndBackfill_WritesEntityDeltasIntoCheckpointTree fail if the backfill never ran (async race: does it deterministically run the child inline in-test or poll)? Flaky-prone sleeps?\n8. Run: `go build ./... && go test ./cmd/entire/cli/strategy/ ./cmd/entire/cli/settings/ ./api/checkpoint/... ./cmd/entire/cli/checkpoint/...` — full pass/fail.\n\nReport caveman-ultra: per hunt item REFUTED-A-DEFECT (file:line + concrete failure scenario) or VERIFIED-OK (evidence), test results, ship/no-ship. Max 35 lines."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2441,"cache_read_input_tokens":178778,"output_tokens":2094,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":534},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2441,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{