{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-08-18T20:34:26.165Z","sessionId":"de272aad-c620-4d71-bbdd-27dd2d3dc8af","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>ae0dd9676e127e1ad</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_01L4zzTVVRdTzHjo1qzmgbJN</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-suhaan-devenv/f507d58c-285f-4d11-b1d0-201f2a5e172d/tasks/ae0dd9676e127e1ad.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Audit entity deltas tests honesty\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>1. TestCondenseAndBackfill_WritesEntityDeltasIntoCheckpointTree (strategy/entity_deltas_test.go:370-409). Spawn substitution at L374 via captureEntityDeltasJobs (L72-83): `entityDeltasSpawn = func(_, jobPath string) { job,_:=readEntityDeltasJob(jobPath); *jobs=append(*jobs,job) }` — captures job, does NOT fork. Backfill run SYNCHRONOUSLY inline at L384: `runEntityDeltasBackfill(context.Background(), (*jobs)[0])`. Verdict: COVERED, not weak — L386-388 `file, err := tree.File(...); require.NoError(t, err, \"entity_deltas.json must land in the session directory\")` is a hard failing assertion (not if-present-then-correct); it would FAIL if backfill never ran. Bonus: L380-381 proves the pre-backfill tree has NO deltas file (condense path alone doesn't write it).\n\n2. NO time.Sleep/goroutine/flock/eventually-loop in any of the 3 test files (grep zero hits). Only \"sleep\" is inside a shell producer-stub body: L270 `installEntityDeltasProducer(t, \"sleep 10\\n\")` for TestComputeEntityDeltas_ProducerHangIsKilled — real subprocess exec+kill, gated `entityDeltasTimeout=200ms` (L274), asserts `elapsed &lt; 2s` (L283). POSIX-only (installEntityDeltasProducer skips windows, L54-56). Low flake risk but real-subprocess timing test — no polling/eventually pattern used.\n\n3. Fake producer only: installEntityDeltasProducer (L52-61) writes shell stub to temp dir, prepends PATH. Real `entire-graph` never invoked. `emitFixtureBody` (L64-67) makes the stub `cat` out `testdata/entity_deltas_producer_diff.json` verbatim — comment at L29-31 states this is the REAL captured `entire-graph diff --json` output, not hand-written. Negative-path tests (error/badjson/hang/oversized, L230/239/270/291) use small ad-hoc hand-written bodies, but only for narrow failure-injection, not for schema-mapping assertions (those use the real fixture exclusively, L488-547).\n\n4. ABSENT (direct test). No test proves scheduleEntityDeltas doesn't exec synchronously via an argv/exec recorder. Only indirect evidence: item 1's L380-381 (post-condense, pre-backfill tree has no deltas file) implies the schedule path didn't run the producer inline, but no schedule-specific test installs an argv-capturing or invocation-counting stub the way TestComputeEntityDeltas_ProducerArgv (L250-263) does for computeEntityDeltas. WEAK.\n\n5. flock serialization (concurrent backfills): ABSENT — zero \"flock\" references in any of the 3 test files (source has it: strategy/entity_deltas.go:438). 8MB cap: WEAK — TestComputeEntityDeltas_OversizedOutputSkips (L289-302) overrides `entityDeltasMaxOutputBytes` to 512, never tests the real default (source L89: `8 &lt;&lt; 20`). 120s timeout: WEAK — TestComputeEntityDeltas_ProducerHangIsKilled overrides `entityDeltasTimeout` to 200ms (L273-274), asserts against that shortened var + a 2s wall-clock slack bound (L283), never exercises/asserts the real 120s default (source L82).\n\n6. Job-file lifecycle: COVERED for write+delete-after-valid-read — TestScheduleEntityDeltas_JobFileIsConsumed (L160-177): writes, `require.FileExists`, `readEntityDeltasJob`, then `assert.NoFileExists`. ABSENT for \"deleted even on malformed JSON\" — no test writes a malformed job JSON file and checks it's still deleted after a failed read.\n\n7. COVERED — TestWriteSessionEntityDeltas_UnknownSessionErrorsWithoutMovingTheRef (checkpoint/persistent_entity_deltas_test.go:98-120): checkpoint exists, SessionID \"session-does-not-exist\"; `require.Error(err)` + `require.NotErrorIs(err, ErrCheckpointNotFound)` + branch-hash unchanged.\n\n8. strategy/entity_deltas_test.go: 26 total `func Test...`. 9 use `t.Parallel()`: TestEntityDeltasFromDiff_RealProducerOutput(L488), _FiltersToSessionFiles(L551), _NeverNil(L575), TestEntityDeltaFromChange_NameAndPathFallbacks(L583), _OldFieldsFollowTheValues(L599), _StartLineFallsBackToBefore(L623), _FileOldPathReachesEntities(L637), TestNormalizeEntityChange(L652), TestCappedBuffer(L671) — all pure-mapping tests per file's own header comment (L25-27) explaining the other 17 can't parallelize (t.Setenv/t.Chdir/package-var swaps).</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>91986</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>4</tool_uses><duration_ms>73391</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
