{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-08-18T20:34:39.485Z","sessionId":"de272aad-c620-4d71-bbdd-27dd2d3dc8af","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>a3f02abe88fd97282</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>REDACTED</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-suhaan-devenv/f507d58c-285f-4d11-b1d0-201f2a5e172d/tasks/a3f02abe88fd97282.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Verify fixture vs producer tags\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>Confirmed exact line citations. Now compiling the final report.\n\n## Verdict: fixture MATCHES the real producer schema (field-by-field), with only test-annotation noise as drift.\n\n**A) Fixture keys** (`cli-keystone/cmd/entire/cli/strategy/testdata/entity_deltas_producer_diff.json`)\n- Top-level: `_capture_recipe, _comment, _covers, _producer_commit, base, files, head, producer_version, schema_version`\n- `files[].changes[]` union (14): `after_start_line, before_start_line, dependents_count, kind, name, new_name, new_path, new_signature, old_name, old_path, old_signature, reconciliation, similarity, type`\n\n**B) Real producer** (`graph-keystone/internal/sem/model.go`)\n- `Result` (L82-98): `checkpoint,omitempty` `base` `head` `files` `warnings,omitempty` `schema_version` `producer_version,omitempty`\n- `FileChange` (L74-79): `path` `old_path,omitempty` `status` `language,omitempty` `changes`\n- `EntityChange` (L54-71): `type kind name old_name,omitempty new_name,omitempty old_signature,omitempty new_signature,omitempty old_path,omitempty new_path,omitempty before_start_line,omitempty after_start_line,omitempty dependents_count similarity(float64),omitempty reconciliation,omitempty`\n- `ProducerVersion` set centrally in `internal/cli/root.go:839` (`printResult`); marshaled via `json.MarshalIndent` to `opts.Stdout` at `root.go:824,826`.\n\n**C) Strict diff**\n- Fixture-only (not real fields): `_comment, _capture_recipe, _covers, _producer_commit` — test-doc annotations, harmless (Go unmarshal ignores unknown fields) but not producer output. DRIFTED (annotation only).\n- Producer-only, absent in fixture: `checkpoint`, `warnings` — both `omitempty`, legitimately absent. MATCHES.\n- Type mismatch: none real. `similarity` is Go `float64`; fixture shows `1` not `1.0` — Go's encoder prints whole floats without a decimal point, so `1` is exactly what the real producer emits too. MATCHES.\n- `type` enum in code (`analyze.go:384,478,488,508,545,547,549,557,567`): `moved, signature_changed, body_changed, renamed, added, removed` — exactly 6, exactly the fixture's set. MATCHES. Note: `RECONCILED_FROM` mentioned only in a comment (`model.go:70`), never actually assigned anywhere in code — not a real emitted value.\n\n**D) `before_start_line` on removals**: YES — `removedChange()` at `analyze.go:557,560` sets `BeforeStartLine: oldEntity.StartLine`, no `AfterStartLine`. MATCHES fixture (`LegacyConfig`/`LegacyConfig.A` removed entries).\n`old_name` on `type:\"moved\"`: YES, conditionally — `analyze.go:394-397`: `OldName`/`NewName` only set `if r.entity.Name != a.entity.Name`. Fixture's \"Relocated\" moved-only entry correctly omits old_name/new_name; \"ShiftedRenamed\" (moved+renamed) correctly includes them. MATCHES exactly.\n\n**E) CLI flags/output** (`graph-keystone/internal/cli/root.go`): `--base`/`--head` parsed in `parseDiffFlags` (L744,750); `--repo` in `parseCommonFlags` (L632); `--json` in `parseCommonFlags` (L618). Command dispatch is flat — `diff` is a top-level verb (`root.go:69-70`), not nested under a `graph` parent inside the binary itself. JSON written to `opts.Stdout` via `fmt.Fprintln` (`root.go:826`). So `&lt;bin&gt; diff --base B --head H --repo D --json` is exactly correct for the `entire-graph` binary; the `entire graph diff ...` form seen in `stats_test.go:672` is the `entire` wrapper delegating to it. MATCHES.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>63937</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>13</tool_uses><duration_ms>98741</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
