{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-08-18T20:36:44.882Z","sessionId":"de272aad-c620-4d71-bbdd-27dd2d3dc8af","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>a292fd00d944eee90</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_01GiiyeziAnWmXGTf8P9YWst</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-suhaan-devenv/f507d58c-285f-4d11-b1d0-201f2a5e172d/tasks/a292fd00d944eee90.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Re-verify cli fix pass\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>## ADVERSARIAL RE-REVIEW ROUND 2 — cli-keystone `feat/checkpoint-entity-deltas`\n\n**H1 REF RACE — REFUTED-A-DEFECT (severe, ship-blocking).** `setPrimaryRef` (checkpoint/store.go:115) is an unconditional `Storer.SetReference` — **no CAS**. `backfillEntityDeltas` (persistent.go:978-1017) does read-tip → build tree → `CreateCommit(parent=tip)` → force-set. `writeSession` force-sets the same ref (persistent.go:123). The new `entire-entity-deltas.lock` (entity_deltas.go:429-445) is taken **only by backfill children**; condensation serializes on the *per-session* state lock (session_state.go:592-610, `stateLockPath(sessionID)`). Different lock files ⇒ zero mutual exclusion. Scenario: post-commit condenses sessions A then B in one hook run; A's child spawns, producer returns in &lt;1s, child reads tip T; B's `writeSession` force-sets v1=T+1; child force-sets v1=commit(parent=T) → **session B's entire checkpoint is orphaned, silently**. Same shape eats the combined-attribution backfill (manual_commit_hooks.go:1171). Tree layout/trailers/redaction are fine (`RedactBlobBytes`; `content_hash.txt` is transcript-only, persistent.go:2124 — unaffected). git-refs backend mostly safe (per-checkpoint refs) but same force-set at refs_store.go:203.\n**H1b OPF — REFUTED-A-DEFECT (user-visible).** `atomicSetV1Ref` (opf_rewrite.go:809-826) *does* CAS → a child landing during pre-push rewrite returns `V1RefMovedError` → manual_commit_push.go:169-176 **aborts the user's push**. The child can land up to ~4 min after any commit, so this is now reachable at random. Fix exists in-tree: `CheckAndSetReference` (gitrepo/reftable.go:224) + retry.\n\n**H2 JOB LIFECYCLE — VERIFIED-OK (one minor leak).** `os.CreateTemp(\"\")` 0600 (entity_deltas.go:243-263); `readEntityDeltasJob` (308-320) `os.Remove` **before** decode ⇒ deleted even on malformed JSON, single-use ⇒ no double backfill. No shell anywhere (`exec.CommandContext` argv array), jobPath is process-generated ⇒ no path/arg injection. Leak: `SpawnDetached` is fire-and-forget (execx:99-126, silent on `os.Executable`/`Start` failure) ⇒ job file left for the OS reaper. Job has no version field; a binary upgraded between fork and exec parses an old job with silent zero-defaults — theoretical, low.\n\n**H3 CHILD ENV — VERIFIED-OK.** Gate re-checked in the child (entity_deltas.go:331). `SpawnDetached` uses `os.Executable()`, **not PATH/argv[0]** (execx:103) ⇒ the \"different entire version\" hazard does not exist. `cmd.Env = os.Environ()` (execx:116) ⇒ HOME/ENTIRE_CONFIG_DIR/ENTIRE_ENTITY_DELTAS inherited identically to the parent; `cmd.Dir=repoDir`; logging guarded on `WorktreeRoot` (entity_deltas_cmd.go:32).\n\n**H4 FLOCK — VERIFIED-OK.** `AcquireContext` with a 2-min deadline ⇒ takes the **bounded** 25ms-poll non-blocking branch (flock_unix.go:20,59-78), never the indefinite kernel path. A wedged holder makes later backfills **drop work, not queue forever**. flock is released by the kernel on process exit ⇒ a killed child cannot wedge it; no TTL needed. Worst child lifetime ≈120s producer +120s wait; children block idle, not spin.\n\n**H5 HOOK COST — VERIFIED-OK (return path), PARTIAL (cost claim).** `scheduleEntityDeltas` returns nothing (entity_deltas.go:186), call site ignores it (manual_commit_condensation.go:441), every branch is a bare `return` — no error can reach `CondenseSession`. But sync work is not *only* job-write+spawn: also `settings.Load` (file read + flock, settings.go:859), a full `exec.LookPath` $PATH scan (entity_deltas.go:222), `os.CreateTemp`, fork+exec, and `repo.Head()` when `headCommitHash==\"\"`. No producer exec, no git walk. Gate is first, so a disabled repo pays only `settings.Load`.\n\n**H6 ROUND-1 FIXES — ALL 5 VERIFIED-OK.** producer_version top-level (entity_deltas.go:141); before_start_line fallback (583-586); old_name value-gated not type-gated (600-602); file-level old_path→entities (606-611); session filtering incl. old_path match (556-564). **Fixture MATCHES the real producer field-for-field** vs graph-keystone `internal/sem/model.go:54-98`: all 6 emitted `type` values present; producer-only `checkpoint`/`warnings` are `omitempty` and legitimately absent; only drift is 4 `_`-prefixed test annotations (ignored by Unmarshal). Producer really emits `before_start_line` on removals (analyze.go:557) and `old_name` on `moved` when names differ (analyze.go:394-397). Flags `diff --base --head --repo --json` all real, top-level, JSON to stdout (root.go:69,618,632,744,750,826).\n\n**H7 TESTS — HONEST.** `TestCondenseAndBackfill_...` swaps `entityDeltasSpawn` for a job-capturing stub and calls `runEntityDeltasBackfill` **inline** — deterministic, no async race; `require.NoError(tree.File(entity_deltas.json))` **hard-fails if the backfill never ran**, and it first asserts the pre-backfill tree lacks the file. Zero sleeps/goroutines/polling in the 3 test files (only a `sleep 10` shell stub for the kill test, asserted against the shortened deadline var). Fake producer `cat`s the real fixture verbatim. Gaps: **no flock/concurrency test** (precisely where H1 lives), no argv-recorder proving schedule never execs, oversize/timeout tests only exercise shrunk vars, no malformed-job-deletion test.\n\n**H8 BUILD/TEST — PASS.** `go build ./...` clean; `go test ./cmd/entire/cli/strategy/ ./cmd/entire/cli/settings/ ./api/checkpoint/... ./cmd/entire/cli/checkpoint/...` → **1738 passed, 0 failed, exit 0**.\n\n**VERDICT: NO-SHIP.** The async redesign fixed the round-1 latency/error-propagation class cleanly, but it introduced an **out-of-band, unsynchronized, non-CAS writer to `entire/checkpoints/v1`** — which the old synchronous design structurally could not have. That is silent checkpoint loss plus random push aborts. Required before ship: CAS the backfill's ref advance (`CheckAndSetReference` + retry-on-`ErrReferenceHasChanged`, primitive already in `gitrepo/reftable.go:224`), or make the child contend on the same lock the v1 writers hold; then add the missing concurrent-backfill-vs-condense test. Everything else is clean.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>97381</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>26</tool_uses><duration_ms>265375</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
