{"parentUuid":"77dc55e7-9d87-4587-afc3-4f9cba75ec3f","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_011CeArbwUYEN4UGfcEqzqqa","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Brain fixer is done — window cursors, verify compatibility, session scoping, non-blocking tick, cache-poisoning fix, contract fixes, honest history, all landed with 5/5 mutations killed and a fresh live e2e pass. It even caught one extra real bug on its own (backfill-backwards was answering history newest-first; chronology now enforced with a test).\n\nSame discipline as the cli: the fixes created new surface — spawning its round-2 skeptic now, focused hardest on the `verify` changes since that's a *shipped* user surface being modified."}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2604,"cache_read_input_tokens":183707,"output_tokens":2007,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":166},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2604,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2007,"cache_read_input_tokens":183707,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2604,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2604},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CeArbsgq8ekVtVvHSbCZ3","type":"assistant","uuid":"3b04322b-8198-4e8e-90a8-566595d90c04","timestamp":"2026-08-18T20:36:53.248Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"f507d58c-285f-4d11-b1d0-201f2a5e172d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"de272aad-c620-4d71-bbdd-27dd2d3dc8af","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"quizzical-sniffing-quasar"}
{"parentUuid":"3b04322b-8198-4e8e-90a8-566595d90c04","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_011CeArbwUYEN4UGfcEqzqqa","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_013xkxqEXeodtjSCdV9PC4RS","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Re-verify brain fix pass","subagent_type":"general-purpose","model":"opus","prompt":"ADVERSARIAL RE-REVIEW, round 2. Default: WRONG until proven. READ-ONLY, use rtk. /Users/suhaan/devenv/p0p1/brain-keystone (entire-brain, branch feat/entity-checkpoint-index, 3 commits off origin/main: 78d02685 factgitmeta → edf3a69a entityindex → 97a487dc cli; +5418/−28). Round 1 killed the original design (single HWM, verify regression, cache poisoning, blocking flock); a fix pass replaced it. Attack the NEW code round 1 never saw.\n\nNew design under test: contiguous indexed window {floor,tip} persisted as one git-meta blob (doc.go:48,153; build.go readWindow:274 w/ ancestor check, extendWindow:340 forward tip..head walk + budget-bounded backward floor pull; checkpoints-only moves no cursor); verify_cmd.go:427 now accepts any session-owned checkpoint via checkpointSnapshot.SessionCheckpoints (export.go:3421) with per-checkpoint transcript resolution; provenance scoped to same session+branch, multi-checkpoint commits skipped, byPath distinct-path ambiguity guard, %cI dates; MetaStore.TryLock/TryUpdate (LOCK_NB) used by the freshness tick only; cache rebuild aborts without persisting on git failure (partitionPresentCommits separates pruned from failed); join sorts occurrences by commit date.\n\nHUNT:\n1. WINDOW ancestor check (readWindow:274): what happens when the branch is force-moved/rebased so the stored tip is NOT an ancestor of head — reset? partial? Can floor/tip invert? Can extendWindow double-index or skip commits when forward and backward extensions run in the same pass? Empty repo / single-commit / floor==root edge cases.\n2. VERIFY (the shipped surface — highest risk): diff verify_cmd.go against origin/main line by line. For a fact anchored at LatestCheckpoint (100% of existing facts), is behavior byte-identical in ALL branches (VERIFIED/STALE/ORPHANED paths)? Can sessionOwnsCheckpoint mis-accept a checkpoint from a DIFFERENT session that shares a commit? SessionCheckpoints filled in BOTH snapshot builders — any third builder or cached snapshot path that leaves it empty (nil → what happens: panic, false STALE, or silent accept)?\n3. TryLock: correct on both unix+windows stubs? Does ErrLockBusy from TryUpdate leave any partial state? Does the BLOCKING path (backfill CLI) still behave exactly as before? Freshness tick with NonBlocking: skip = truly silent-and-cheap (no git walk BEFORE the lock attempt)?\n4. partitionPresentCommits: how does it distinguish \"commit pruned/GC'd\" from \"git failed\"? A pruned checkpoint commit (git gc after ref deletion) must NOT abort rebuilds forever — can the cache get permanently stuck refusing to rebuild? Conversely can a transient failure still slip through as \"pruned\" and poison?\n5. sortOccurrencesByCommitDate: same-second commits (common in tests/CI) — stable? Deterministic across runs?\n6. Provenance: multi-checkpoint-commit skip — does it skip the COMMIT or the whole session? Branch guard sessionBranchByID — facts distilled on a branch later merged: does the guard wrongly refuse sharpening after merge?\n7. Tests honest: would TestBuildTickWalksOnlyTheNewCommits fail if the tick re-walked everything (what does it actually count)? Would TestVerifySharpenedAnchorOnAnEarlierCheckpointVerifies pass if verify just accepted ANY checkpoint (is there a negative control — the foreign-checkpoint STALE test — and does it share the same code path)?\n8. Run: `go build ./... && go vet ./...`, then `go test ./internal/entityindex/ ./internal/cli/ ./internal/factgitmeta/ ./internal/factsync/ ./internal/factmerge/`; if time allows the full `go test ./...`. Report pass/fail counts.\n\nReport caveman-ultra: per item REFUTED-A-DEFECT (file:line + concrete scenario) or VERIFIED-OK (evidence), test results, ship/no-ship. Max 35 lines."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2604,"cache_read_input_tokens":183707,"output_tokens":2007,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":166},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2604,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2007,"cache_read_input_tokens":183707,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2604,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2604},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CeArbsgq8ekVtVvHSbCZ3","type":"assistant","uuid":"3f691fb9-e7fd-4d8a-959e-0d4a9cd60611","timestamp":"2026-08-18T20:37:14.780Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"f507d58c-285f-4d11-b1d0-201f2a5e172d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"de272aad-c620-4d71-bbdd-27dd2d3dc8af","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"quizzical-sniffing-quasar"}
