{"parentUuid":"c70f96d0-3cba-4888-85b3-4bc2690c0a7f","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_011CeAre7pwXyauBxJrVw8wM","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_018KpkMkxJ31Q4T9eDEEhQgq","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Fix cli ref-race defect","subagent_type":"general-purpose","model":"opus","prompt":"TARGETED FIX in /Users/suhaan/devenv/cli-keystone (entireio/cli, branch feat/checkpoint-entity-deltas, commits e8432d01d+f57e55479). Use rtk. Round-2 adversarial review confirmed ONE severe defect plus small gaps in the entity-deltas backfill feature. Fix exactly these; touch nothing else.\n\nTHE DEFECT: the detached backfill child advances `entire/checkpoints/v1` with an unconditional force-set — `backfillEntityDeltas` (persistent.go:978-1017) read-tip→CreateCommit(parent=tip)→`setPrimaryRef` (checkpoint/store.go:115, plain SetReference, no CAS). The child holds only `entire-entity-deltas.lock`; condensation serializes on the per-session state lock (session_state.go:592-610) — different locks, zero mutual exclusion. Proven scenario: hook condenses sessions A,B; A's child reads tip T; B's writeSession sets v1=T+1; child sets v1=commit(parent=T) → B's checkpoint silently orphaned. Also: a child landing during the pre-push OPF rewrite makes `atomicSetV1Ref` (opf_rewrite.go:809-826, DOES CAS) fail → manual_commit_push.go:169-176 aborts the user's push.\n\nREQUIRED OUTCOMES (mechanism is yours, primitives exist in-tree):\n1. The backfill can NEVER orphan another writer's checkpoint: make the child's v1 advance compare-and-swap — `CheckAndSetReference` (gitrepo/reftable.go:224) — and on ErrReferenceHasChanged/moved-tip, RE-READ the tip and REBUILD the delta commit on the new parent, bounded retries (say 5) then drop with a log line. Apply the same to the git-refs backend's force-set (refs_store.go:203) if it can race.\n2. The child must not create NEW user-visible push failures: prevent the child from landing mid-rewrite — e.g. the OPF pre-push rewrite path takes the entity-deltas lock for its duration (cheap, bounded) OR the child detects an in-progress rewrite and parks/retries. Do NOT change existing push semantics for other movers; pick the least invasive mechanism after reading opf_rewrite.go's locking.\n3. Add the missing tests: (a) concurrent condense-vs-backfill — simulate the proven scenario deterministically (move v1 between the child's tip-read and its set; assert BOTH checkpoints survive and deltas land on the new tip); (b) backfill-during-rewrite (whatever mechanism you chose: assert no push abort / child parks); (c) malformed job file is deleted and skipped; (d) MUTATION: revert the CAS to plain SetReference → test (a) must FAIL. State the mutation result.\n4. Two nits while there: add a `v` version field to the job file (child rejects unknown versions with a log line, tolerates absent as v1); on SpawnDetached failure the job file currently leaks — best-effort os.Remove when spawn errors.\n\nVERIFY: `mise run check` green. Amend/extend the branch's commits as fits (keep history clean, honest messages, NO AI footers). Do NOT push.\n\nReport caveman-ultra: mechanism chosen for outcome 2 (one line why), per-item done+file:line, test names, mutation result, check result, final shas. Max 20 lines."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5526,"cache_read_input_tokens":186311,"output_tokens":2506,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":988},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5526,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2506,"cache_read_input_tokens":186311,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5526,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5526},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CeAre3xGrFmVATrTEUjsW","type":"assistant","uuid":"96f49339-7f76-47e8-8547-b713f0466174","timestamp":"2026-08-18T20:37:50.394Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"f507d58c-285f-4d11-b1d0-201f2a5e172d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"de272aad-c620-4d71-bbdd-27dd2d3dc8af","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"quizzical-sniffing-quasar"}
