{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-08-18T20:45:36.898Z","sessionId":"de272aad-c620-4d71-bbdd-27dd2d3dc8af","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>ad947d2d6f2bd0db6</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_013xkxqEXeodtjSCdV9PC4RS</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-suhaan-devenv/f507d58c-285f-4d11-b1d0-201f2a5e172d/tasks/ad947d2d6f2bd0db6.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Re-verify brain fix pass\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>Full suite green. Writing up.\n\n**ROUND-2 ADVERSARIAL RE-REVIEW — brain-keystone @97a487dc**\n\n**1. WINDOW — VERIFIED-OK, 2 minor defects**\n- Force-move/rebase: `readWindow` build.go:290 drops window whole → re-cover from head. Correct.\n- Inversion impossible: build.go:419-428 floor only descends; `tip` set from `\"\"` only when window was empty, and then `commits[0]`=head. Single-commit → `{head,head}`; floor==root → `git log floor` returns [floor], dropped, no-op; empty repo → `revParse` errors at build.go:174.\n- No double-index/skip: forward (`Tip..head`) and backward (ancestors-of-`Floor`) are disjoint; `b.indexed` memo (build.go:463,540) dedupes regardless.\n- **DEFECT (minor)** build.go:341: forward walk uses `maxWalkCommits`, not `walkBudget()`, contradicting the Limit doc at build.go:79 (\"never lists more history than it could index\"). `Limit:10` tick after a 5000-commit fast-forward materializes 5000 commitInfo w/ full bodies to index 10. Perf only.\n- **DEFECT (latent)** build.go:420: window is head-anchored — if HEAD itself is undiffable, `covered[head]=false` breaks the floor loop, window stays empty *forever*, so every tick re-walks the whole budget and never claims coverage.\n- Caveat: ancestor check is full-ancestry but the claim is first-parent. Reset onto a merge reaching old tip via 2nd parent keeps a floor off head's chain → transiently false `{floor,tip}`. Only consumer is a printf (entities_cmd.go:215) and backfill converges to root. Not shipping-blocking.\n\n**2. VERIFY — VERIFIED-OK (byte-identical for LatestCheckpoint), 1 real defect**\n- verify_cmd.go:425 returns *before* the new branch when `CheckpointID==\"\"` or `==LatestCheckpoint`; the prefix branch is gated on `!=LatestCheckpoint` (:500). All VERIFIED/STALE/ORPHANED paths for existing facts unchanged.\n- `sessionOwnsCheckpoint` needs an exact (SessionID,CheckpointID) pair built per-session from tree metadata (export.go:2168-2203); a shared commit cannot fake it. Rejected pairs (empty session id, cross-checkpoint mismatch) return `false` and never enter `members`.\n- Only 2 non-test builders (export.go:1635,1861), both fill it. 4 test literals leave nil → `sessionCheckpoint` guards nil + ranges nil slice → false → STALE (pre-change behavior). **No panic**; neither loader ever returns `(nil,_,nil)`.\n- **DEFECT** verify_cmd.go:429-442: `bySession[0]` is manifest-order dependent when `factBranch==\"\"` and one session ID spans branch rows — previously it only tagged STALE, now it is returned as **VERIFIED** and its `LatestCheckpoint`/`TranscriptPath` drive the downstream transcript check.\n- Caveat: prefix rule assumes append-only transcripts; the v2 path is `\"compact\"` (verify_cmd.go:607) and compaction rewrites → sharpened anchors read STALE there. False-negative only, never launders.\n\n**3. TryLock — VERIFIED-OK on both stubs; DEFECT in ordering**\n- unix `LOCK_EX|LOCK_NB` (EWOULDBLOCK/EAGAIN/EINTR→busy) and windows `LOCKFILE_FAIL_IMMEDIATELY` (ERROR_LOCK_VIOLATION/IO_PENDING→busy) both correct; busy path closes the fd, `releaseFunc` unlocks *and* closes (flock is per-OFD).\n- ErrLockBusy leaves zero partial state: `TryUpdate` returns before `updateLocked` (store.go:183); Build resets Indexed/Entities/NewCommits/Window (build.go:249-261). Blocking path is the extracted-verbatim old loop — unchanged.\n- **REFUTED-A-DEFECT** build.go:205 vs :231 — `extendWindow` (git walk + one `entire graph diff` subprocess per new commit) runs **before** the lock is attempted. Under contention a session-end/watch tick burns up to `entitiesFreshnessCommits=10` diffs bounded only by `entitiesFreshnessTimeout=90s`, discards all of it, reports `Indexed=0` silently. The skip is neither cheap nor silent-and-free — only the *no-new-commits* case is (early return at build.go:218). Fix: TryLock first, hold across the pass.\n\n**4. partitionPresentCommits — VERIFIED-OK, 1 minor**\n- entities_cmd.go:681: `absent==0`→git failed→error; `present==0`→probe failed→error; else retry `present`, second failure errors. Cache never persisted on failure. A GC'd commit lands in `absent`, retry succeeds → **cannot get permanently stuck**.\n- **Minor**: a *transient* per-sha `cat-file` failure is misread as pruned, that sha silently drops from the join, and the cache IS persisted keyed on the current MetaTip. Bounded: the occurrence loses CheckpointIDs/SessionIDs → provenance skips it → coarse anchor. Full ctx-cancel is caught (all probes fail → `present==0`).\n\n**5. sortOccurrencesByCommitDate — VERIFIED-OK**\n`SliceStable` + a valid strict weak ordering (both-nil→false; dated&lt;undated; undated stay last in input order). Ties preserve `snapshot.Commits()` order = `SortListEntries` by `MakeEntryName(ts,value)` (types.go:225), a total deterministic order — and `applyBatch` (state.go:73) nudges colliding timestamps to `max+1`, so list timestamps are unique anyway. Deterministic across runs.\n\n**6. Provenance — VERIFIED-OK, 1 real determinism defect**\n- entities_provenance.go:95 skips the **occurrence** (one commit × one entity key), not the session; the session's other occurrences still register.\n- Branch guard (:174-178) fails *closed* to fallback, never to a wrong anchor, and fails *open* when the session is absent from the manifest (session scoping still holds). Post-merge re-distill: `record.Branch=feat` vs manifest-resolved `main` → sharpening silently refused, coarse anchor stands. Loss of sharpening, not a wrong anchor.\n- `anchorFor` overrides only Commit+CheckpointID (property 3 honored); Transcript/Line still point at the exported latest transcript — which is precisely what forces the verify prefix relaxation.\n- **REFUTED-A-DEFECT** entities_provenance.go:84 + :146-149: `newEntityProvenanceResolver` iterates `view.cache.Entries` (a **map**) and `observe` keeps *first-seen* on a timestamp tie. `%cI` is second-resolution, and `byPath` deliberately collapses basenames (`cmd/a/main.go` + `cmd/b/main.go` → token `\"main.go\"`; likewise same-named funcs in different files). Two such keys committed in the same second by one session ⇒ the winning commit/checkpoint is **Go map-iteration-order dependent** — identical distill input yields different anchors run to run. No test covers a tie; the three provenance tests all use distinct timestamps and pass at `-count=20`.\n\n**7. Tests honest — BOTH HONEST**\n- `TestBuildTickWalksOnlyTheNewCommits` (entityindex_test.go:501) counts the exact `tip..head` walk ==1 **and** asserts no `git log` call ends with the head sha — a real negative control that fires if the tick re-walked the branch. Also pins `Indexed==1` and the window.\n- `TestVerifySharpenedAnchorOnAnEarlierCheckpointVerifies` has its negative control: `TestVerifyAnchorOnAForeignCheckpointIsStale` (verify_cmd_test.go:199), same full-CLI `verify` path, same snapshot loader — checkpoint owned by `sess2`, anchor claims `sess1`, pins `session`→STALE. Fails if verify accepted any checkpoint. The positive test also asserts *every* check verified, exercising the prefix branch.\n\n**8. RESULTS** — `go build ./...` exit 0. `go vet ./...` exit 0. Targeted (entityindex, cli, factgitmeta/…, factsync, factmerge): **2425 pass, 6 pkgs, 0 fail**. Full `go test ./...`: **2468 pass, 12 pkgs, 0 fail**, exit 0.\n\n**VERDICT: SHIP after fixing #3 (take TryLock before `extendWindow`) and #6 (deterministic tie-break in `observe` — break on commit sha, not map order).** Round 1's four kills are genuinely dead: single-HWM → checkable `{floor,tip}` range; verify regression → gated so LatestCheckpoint anchors are byte-identical; cache poisoning → `partitionPresentCommits` aborts rather than persisting an empty join; blocking flock → `TryUpdate`. Neither remaining defect corrupts stored data — one wastes bounded work, one makes anchors non-reproducible under same-second ties. Items 1, 2 (core), 4, 5, 7 verified clean.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>148334</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>40</tool_uses><duration_ms>502064</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
