{"parentUuid":"f3dbb05a-8a76-421d-91ef-fb802b77b1d4","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_011CeAsH6SNrK9MaFnFztpGx","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The brain round-2 verdict is **SHIP after two fixes** — the four round-1 kills are confirmed genuinely dead, and the remaining defects don't corrupt data: the tick does its git-walk and graph-diff work *before* attempting the lock (so a contended tick burns 90s of work and discards it), and provenance anchors are map-iteration-order dependent on same-second timestamp ties. Plus three cheap hardening items worth folding in (a verify manifest-order case that can return arbitrary-row VERIFIED, a walk-budget violation, and a latent head-undiffable window stall).\n\nDispatching the final targeted brain fix:"}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3964,"cache_read_input_tokens":194743,"output_tokens":2755,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1344},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3964,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2755,"cache_read_input_tokens":194743,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3964,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3964},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CeAsH3Un61ihgArrSptCj","type":"assistant","uuid":"ba106602-9d8b-4803-8417-568648c71597","timestamp":"2026-08-18T20:46:03.563Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"f507d58c-285f-4d11-b1d0-201f2a5e172d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"de272aad-c620-4d71-bbdd-27dd2d3dc8af","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"quizzical-sniffing-quasar"}
{"parentUuid":"ba106602-9d8b-4803-8417-568648c71597","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_011CeAsH6SNrK9MaFnFztpGx","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01R7Tc3dtHj7qhQe5XoUebmj","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Final brain fix: lock+ties","subagent_type":"general-purpose","model":"opus","prompt":"TARGETED FIX in /Users/suhaan/devenv/p0p1/brain-keystone (entire-brain, branch feat/entity-checkpoint-index @97a487dc). Use rtk. Round-2 adversarial review says SHIP after these; fix exactly these, nothing else.\n\nREQUIRED (the two ship-gates):\n1. Lock-ordering: build.go:205 runs `extendWindow` (git walk + one `entire graph diff` subprocess per new commit) BEFORE the TryLock at :231 — a contended freshness tick burns up to 10 diffs/90s then discards everything. Take the lock (TryLock for NonBlocking, blocking otherwise) BEFORE extendWindow and hold it across the pass. Test: hold the lock externally, run a NonBlocking build with a fake runner, assert ZERO producer invocations and prompt return.\n2. Provenance tie determinism: entities_provenance.go:84 iterates the cache map + observe (:146-149) keeps first-seen on %cI second-resolution ties, and byPath collapses basenames — identical input yields different anchors run to run. Add a total deterministic order: on equal timestamps break by commit sha (then checkpoint id if needed); make iteration order irrelevant. Test: two same-second commits matching one locus token, run resolution repeatedly (and with shuffled entry insertion), assert the same anchor every time. MUTATION: revert the tie-break → test must fail (state result).\n\nHARDENING (cheap, do all three):\n3. verify_cmd.go:429-442: when factBranch==\"\" and one session ID spans multiple branch rows, `bySession[0]` is manifest-order dependent and its row is now returned as VERIFIED (previously this case only tagged STALE). Make the selection deterministic and conservative: prefer the row whose LatestCheckpoint equals the anchor's CheckpointID or whose SessionCheckpoints own it; if no row matches exactly, preserve the pre-change STALE outcome. Test the spanning case.\n4. build.go:341: forward walk uses maxWalkCommits instead of walkBudget(), contradicting the Limit doc at build.go:79 — a Limit:10 tick after a 5000-commit fast-forward materializes 5000 full commit bodies. Use the budget.\n5. Latent stall: window is head-anchored (build.go:420) — if the head commit itself fails to diff, covered[head] stays false, the window never establishes, and every tick re-walks the full budget forever. Bound it: treat a commit whose diff persistently fails as covered-with-empty-deltas after recording the failure (log once), OR anchor the window at the newest diffable commit — your choice, but the invariant is: repeated ticks against an undiffable head must converge to O(new-commits) work. Test it with a fake runner that always fails on head.\n\nVERIFY: full `go test ./...` green, gofmt/vet clean, re-run the live e2e. Amend the branch's 3 commits in place (honest messages, NO AI footers). Do NOT push.\n\nReport caveman-ultra: per item done+file:line, test names, mutation result, suite result, final shas. Max 18 lines."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3964,"cache_read_input_tokens":194743,"output_tokens":2755,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1344},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3964,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2755,"cache_read_input_tokens":194743,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3964,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3964},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CeAsH3Un61ihgArr