{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-08-18T21:04:20.105Z","sessionId":"de272aad-c620-4d71-bbdd-27dd2d3dc8af","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>a7c580d802d3d5af6</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>REDACTED</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-suhaan-devenv/f507d58c-285f-4d11-b1d0-201f2a5e172d/tasks/a7c580d802d3d5af6.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Fix cli ref-race defect\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>Done. Clean tree, both commits amended, nothing pushed.\n\n**MECHANISM (outcome 2):** OPF pre-push rewrite takes the *existing* entity-deltas flock for its whole duration (fail-soft, 30s bound) — least invasive: no new lock, no new state, other v1 movers keep identical semantics; child parks (nobody waits on it) instead of aborting a user push.\n\n**DONE**\n1. CAS+rebuild, git-branch: `checkpoint/store.go:115` `casPrimaryRef` + `writeWithRefRaceRetry` (5 attempts, Warn on drop); `persistent.go:978` `backfillEntityDeltas` → retry loop + `tryBackfillEntityDeltas` (re-reads tip each attempt).\n2. CAS+rebuild, git-refs: `refs_store.go:210` `casRef`; `refs_store.go:335` backfill → same retry loop.\n3. Lock-out: `manual_commit_opf_rewrite.go:258` acquires via `lockOutEntityDeltasBackfills` (`entity_deltas.go:395`, `entityDeltasRewriteLockWait=30s`, fail-soft log-and-proceed). Lock path now resolved from the **worktree path** both sides (`entityDeltasLockPath`) so child + rewrite agree byte-for-byte (was cwd-based).\n4. Job `v` field + child rejects unknown version (Info line), absent=v1 (`entity_deltas.go:170,340`).\n5. Spawn failure removes job file: `execx.SpawnDetachedErr` added (`SpawnDetached` delegates, contract unchanged), `scheduleEntityDeltas` `os.Remove` on error.\n\n**TESTS** (all new, all green)\n- `TestBackfillEntityDeltas_TipMovedUnderTheWrite_KeepsBothCheckpoints` (a; `refRaceStorer` interposes another checkpoint write on the first ref-set — no production seam)\n- `TestRefsStore_BackfillEntityDeltas_TipMovedUnderTheWrite_KeepsBothSessions`\n- `REDACTED` (b), `..._HeldBackfillLockStillRewrites` (b, fail-soft)\n- `REDACTED` (c), `..._UnknownJobVersionIsRefused`, `TestScheduleEntityDeltas_SpawnFailureRemovesTheJobFile`\n\n**MUTATIONS**\n- CAS → plain `setPrimaryRef`: test (a) FAILS on \"the checkpoint that won the race must survive the backfill\". Restored, green.\n- Bonus: removing the rewrite's lock makes (b) FAIL with the real `V1RefMovedError` push abort. Restored, green.\n\n**CHECK:** `mise run check` green (lint 0 issues, unit+integration 56/56, canary e2e 4/4).\n**SHAS:** `f14ff2fe6` (store-side CAS) → `d8a5713f3` (child + lock + job version + spawn cleanup), branch `feat/checkpoint-entity-deltas`, not pushed.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>214922</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>99</tool_uses><duration_ms>1589656</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
