{"parentUuid":"fbf284d2-cfa0-4440-a2fb-4da3c3a79b53","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"total_tokens_reminder","text":"<total_tokens>14909661 tokens left</total_tokens>"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"b7a1855e-cbbe-4f73-862d-236b398993d6","timestamp":"2026-08-18T21:11:51.308Z","session_id":"f507d58c-285f-4d11-b1d0-201f2a5e172d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/p0p1/brain-keystone","sessionId":"de272aad-c620-4d71-bbdd-27dd2d3dc8af","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"quizzical-sniffing-quasar"}
{"parentUuid":"b7a1855e-cbbe-4f73-862d-236b398993d6","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_011CeAuHAyTqn2CpgHb7gSJR","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**The keystone — the part between P1 and P2 — is done and shipped as three PRs**, all open for review, nothing merged:\n\n| PR | What it delivers |\n|---|---|\n| [entire-graph #114](https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/pull/114) | `schema_version` + `producer_version` stamped on diff output (additive, the COR-781 schema freeze) |\n| [cli #2041](https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2041) | `entity_deltas.json` written into each checkpoint's tree — gated **off by default**, computed by a detached child so the git hook only pays a process spawn, CAS-protected ref advance (COR-782) |\n| [entire-brain #87](https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/87) | The index + query: `entities backfill/history/show`, MCP tool `brain_entity_history`, contiguous-window coverage cursors, and facts now anchored to the checkpoint that actually made the change (COR-783/784) |\n\nHow it got here, in one paragraph: three builders worked in parallel against one frozen schema; two adversarial review rounds then killed the first cli and brain designs outright (a measured 3.5s hook stall and a checkpoint-orphaning ref race on the cli; a permanent index-gap poisoning and a shipped-`verify` regression on the brain) — every defect was fixed, and every fix is pinned by a mutation check (10+ across the campaign, each proven to fail its test when reverted). The live e2e ran a real repo against the real graph binary, not a fake. The doctrine killed roughly half of what the builders initially claimed, which is exactly its job.\n\nDeferred by your call: COR-785 (transparency-log causality) — it's platform work that should follow the P1 merge.\n\nTwo housekeeping items left that only you can do: the Linear issues COR-781..784 sit **Canceled** and need reactivating to track these PRs, and the roadmap doc's keystone row can move from \"Planned\" to \"In review.\" Merge order when you're ready: graph #114 first (both others' producer), then brain #87 and cli #2041 in either order."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1349,"cache_read_input_tokens":212852,"output_tokens":705,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1349,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":705,"cache_read_input_tokens":212852,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1349,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1349},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CeAuH7e3ZcGV2DiFhmxw7","type":"assistant","uuid":"7f510f8e-580b-4de7-8022-420e98b6b35a","timestamp":"2026-08-18T21:12:03.272Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"f507d58c-285f-4d11-b1d0-201f2a5e172d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/p0p1/brain-keystone","sessionId":"de272aad-c620-4d71-bbdd-27dd2d3dc8af","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"quizzical-sniffing-quasar"}
