{"type":"pr-link","sessionId":"de272aad-c620-4d71-bbdd-27dd2d3dc8af","prNumber":2041,"prUrl":"https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2041","prRepository":"entireio/cli","timestamp":"2026-08-18T21:15:50.349Z"}
{"parentUuid":"1524c4db-543c-435b-b3de-7486fafceb3a","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_011CeAuapTS2fMDnHagasSof","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":33,"cache_read_input_tokens":214906,"output_tokens":820,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":153},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":33,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":820,"cache_read_input_tokens":214906,"cache_creation_input_tokens":33,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":33},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CeAuakNNC9e8sY9vm4dvi","type":"assistant","uuid":"8e79a0fe-ad7d-4350-835c-073eeaf0d812","timestamp":"2026-08-18T21:15:54.840Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"f507d58c-285f-4d11-b1d0-201f2a5e172d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/p0p1/brain-keystone","sessionId":"de272aad-c620-4d71-bbdd-27dd2d3dc8af","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"quizzical-sniffing-quasar"}
{"parentUuid":"8e79a0fe-ad7d-4350-835c-073eeaf0d812","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_011CeAuapTS2fMDnHagasSof","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Simply put: **it gives the repo a memory of *what code meant*, not just what lines changed.**\n\nToday git can tell you \"these files changed in this commit.\" It cannot cheaply tell you \"the function `verifyToken` was modified\" — and definitely not \"show me every AI session that ever touched `verifyToken`.\" Answering that today means re-parsing the whole history every time.\n\nWhat the three PRs do together:\n\n1. **Graph PR (#114):** the diff tool's output gets a version stamp so it's safe to store long-term. (Plumbing.)\n\n2. **CLI PR (#2041):** every time an agent session gets checkpointed, a small file rides along in the checkpoint saying *which functions/classes/types that session changed* — e.g. \"this checkpoint modified `ChargeCard` and added `RefundHelper`.\" Computed in the background, costs the commit nothing.\n\n3. **Brain PR (#87):** builds the reverse lookup — an index from *entity → every checkpoint that ever touched it* — and exposes it three ways:\n   - `entire brain entities history ChargeCard` → instantly lists every checkpoint/session that changed that function, oldest first\n   - the same thing as an MCP tool, so **agents can ask it mid-task** (\"who touched this function before, and in which session?\") and pull that session's context\n   - distill uses it so facts get pinned to the *exact* checkpoint that made a change, instead of \"whatever the latest checkpoint happened to be\"\n\n**Why it matters for the roadmap:** it's the hinge everything after P1 stands on. P3's \"two agents claiming the same function\" needs to know entity→history. Reasoning capture needs \"this decision changed *these entities*.\" P5's \"who succeeds on what kind of code\" needs the entity-level record. This is what ties meaning to git history permanently — hence \"keystone.\"\n\nConcretely, the question it unlocks that nobody could ask before: *\"show me every session that ever modified this function, and what they learned\"* — answered from an index in milliseconds, no re-parsing."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":33,"cache_read_input_tokens":214906,"output_tokens":820,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":153},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":33,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":820,"cache_read_input_tokens":214906,"cache_creation_input_tokens":33,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":33},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CeAuakNNC9e8sY9vm4dvi","type":"assistant","uuid":"5394c3ce-0083-4f12-b2cc-66a1746db2fe","timestamp":"2026-08-18T21:16:05.549Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"f507d58c-285f-4d11-b1d0-201f2a5e172d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/p0p1/brain-keystone","sessionId":"de272aad-c620-4d71-bbdd-27dd2d3dc8af","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"quizzical-sniffing-quasar"}
