{"parentUuid":"e6ea907a-233e-4928-9506-9ec20b85c76b","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_011CeAxxs796ihcyDeaiNhfC","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":163,"cache_read_input_tokens":216182,"output_tokens":3701,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":2176},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":163,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3701,"cache_read_input_tokens":216182,"cache_creation_input_tokens":163,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":163},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CeAxxmtMjNwZ9wSc7tULJ","type":"assistant","uuid":"160d3247-821d-4b70-82eb-e3234ce248ee","timestamp":"2026-08-18T22:00:43.909Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"f507d58c-285f-4d11-b1d0-201f2a5e172d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/graph-keystone","sessionId":"de272aad-c620-4d71-bbdd-27dd2d3dc8af","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"quizzical-sniffing-quasar"}
{"parentUuid":"160d3247-821d-4b70-82eb-e3234ce248ee","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_011CeAxxs796ihcyDeaiNhfC","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Short honest answer: **yes, but the token-savings story is the *weakest* of the brain's stories — I've measured it to death and have the receipts. The winning stories are the class gaps (speed, ingest cost) and a new one the keystone just unlocked.** Let me give you the honest inventory, because we've been burned on this exact question before.\n\n## What we already know (measured, adversarially audited)\n\n**Graph token savings — real but modest, don't oversell:**\n- The replicated number is **+8.6% tokens** on the same 50 instances; out-of-sample it's **+7.2% tokens / +2.5% cost** with a CI spanning zero and a *negative median*. The exhaustively-mapped fair ceiling is ~15%. 25-35% is unreachable — every route was quantified and closed.\n- Mechanism: the graph deletes *locate* turns, so savings scale with session length — and it's a 1:1 substitute (each graph call displaces ~0.98 regular tool calls), which is why usage count isn't the lever.\n- Two mandatory caveats we learned the hard way: **wall-clock is slower** (tokens −6%, time +8% — always quote both), and much of the raw saving was actually the *frugality prompt*, not the tool (unclamped: −25.8% → −0.9%). Any public claim must survive that decomposition.\n\n**Memory benchmarks — this is where the brain actually wins:**\n- **LME: 95.1 vs mem0's managed 94.4 — a win**, fair and reproducible, with zero-LLM ingest. (Retrieval was never the wall — 100% recall; all gains were answerer-side.)\n- **LOCOMO: 94.74 vs 93.83 — statistically a tie** (p=0.125 same-window). Parity, claimable as \"matches the leader.\"\n- **BEAM: we lose, 0.53 vs 0.64** — it rewards LLM-synthesized consolidation, which is exactly what zero-LLM ingest doesn't buy. Consolidation-v2 narrows it (+0.022) but can't win deterministically. Don't lead with BEAM.\n- **The class gap is the headline: ingest ~7s vs mem0's ~14 hours, at zero LLM cost.** That's not a percentage, it's a category. (Honest footnote: mem0 is more context-efficient per character — 43 vs 6 pts/1k chars — that's the price of free ingest.)\n\n## What's genuinely unmeasured — and it's the best story\n\nEverything above measured the **graph**. Nobody has measured the **facts/memory layer's** token effect on real coding sessions — and the keystone just made two new benchmarks possible:\n\n1. **\"Second session reuses the first session's knowledge.\"** Paired design: agent does task A then related task B, with brain memory vs without. Measure tokens, turns, wall-clock, correctness on task B. This is the compounding-memory thesis as a number — and per the session-length law (r=0.947 between message-delta and token-delta), if memory deletes re-derivation turns, it *will* show up in tokens. This is the flagship benchmark I'd build.\n2. **Entity-history tasks.** \"Which sessions changed `ChargeCard` and why?\" — baseline agent greps and reads for minutes; brain answers in one indexed tool call. Huge per-query delta, extremely demo-able, and *nobody else has the capability at all* — that's a differentiation demo, not a percentage fight.\n\n## How to run it credibly (the doctrine, or it dies in review)\n\nThe harness exists (GraphMark 3-arm). Non-negotiables from the ledger: paired on identical instances; both-arms-success gate with symmetric drops; n≥30 with bootstrap CI **and median** (MDE is ~25pts at n=30 — never read subgroups); add instances, never replicate; no arm-asymmetric instructions; pre-register the *mechanism* metric (turns deleted) as primary — that's what caught our one false headline; and audit the harness before believing any number, since every withdrawn headline here died of a harness bug.\n\n## What I'd actually show people\n\nLead with: **ingest instant + $0 vs hours + $$ · LME win · LOCOMO parity · entity-history demo (unique capability)**. Support with: +7% tokens / +2.5% cost, quoted with CI and the wall-clock caveat. Skip: BEAM, and any 20%+ token claim — we've proven those can't survive an audit.\n\nWant me to spec the session-2-reuse benchmark as a prereg (design, gates, n, primary metric) so it's ready to run?"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":163,"cache_read_input_tokens":216182,"output_tokens":3701,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":2176},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":163,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3701,"cache_read_input_tokens":216182,"cache_creation_input_tokens":163,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":163},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CeAxxmtMjNwZ9wSc7tULJ","type":"assistant","uuid":"a29a128c-9090-431d-8920-d48b5f42247a","timestamp":"2026-08-18T22:01:05.229Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"f507d58c-285f-4d11-b1d0-201f2a5e172d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/graph-keystone","sessionId":"de272aad-c620-4d71-bbdd-27dd2d3dc8af","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"quizzical-sniffing-quasar"}
