{"type":"pr-link","sessionId":"de272aad-c620-4d71-bbdd-27dd2d3dc8af","prNumber":114,"prUrl":"https://github.com/entireio/entire-graph/pull/114","prRepository":"entireio/entire-graph","timestamp":"2026-08-18T22:04:46.675Z"}
{"parentUuid":"486933ab-e212-4c69-bbca-c3e8ba2c5f9d","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_011CeAyKEnvRbpDCtbofibh5","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":34,"cache_read_input_tokens":220046,"output_tokens":2334,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1376},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":34,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2334,"cache_read_input_tokens":220046,"cache_creation_input_tokens":34,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":34},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CeAyKAJYnkEbPKNcozJcv","type":"assistant","uuid":"d38c063e-43c7-451b-a012-3553b45ceff4","timestamp":"2026-08-18T22:05:10.645Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"f507d58c-285f-4d11-b1d0-201f2a5e172d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/graph-keystone","sessionId":"de272aad-c620-4d71-bbdd-27dd2d3dc8af","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"quizzical-sniffing-quasar"}
{"parentUuid":"d38c063e-43c7-451b-a012-3553b45ceff4","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_011CeAyKEnvRbpDCtbofibh5","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Cost depends on which of the two benchmarks, and the expensive one is the agentic session benchmark. Here's the honest budget math:\n\n## The flagship: session-2-reuse benchmark (agentic, costs real money)\n\nThe design forces 4 sessions per instance: task A then task B, in both arms (task A must run in the brain arm too — that's where the memory gets captured).\n\n| Tier | What it buys | Sessions | Est. cost |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| **Pilot, Sonnet, n=10 pairs** | Harness shakeout only — finding the silent failure modes, not numbers | 40 | **~$25–50** |\n| **Full run, Opus, n=30 pairs** | First real number, CI + median, MDE ~25pts | 120 | **~$250–400** |\n| **Credible headline, Opus, n=50 + 1 replication** | The standard we held the graph number to | 400 | **~$800–1,200** |\n\nAssumptions behind the per-session figure (~$2–3 Opus, ~$0.50–1 Sonnet): our measured cost decomposition (cacheRead ≈49% of spend, output ≈33%), typical SWE-bench-class session lengths from the graph campaign. Add pennies per instance for the brain arm's distill step on a cheap model — and we should *report* that ingest cost as a product line-item, since \"memory costs $0.10 to write, saves $X to read\" is the actual pitch.\n\nWall-clock, not just dollars: at the ~8-way concurrency cap (the load-pressure confound is real — starvation flips signs), 120 sessions ≈ 15–20h on the existing GCP VMs. VM cost is noise next to tokens.\n\n## The cheap ones (mostly already paid for)\n\n- **LOCOMO / LME re-runs**: harness exists on mem0harness-1, ingest is free, cost is answerer-side only — **~$10–30 per full re-run**. If you want fresh numbers for a public post, this is nearly free.\n- **Entity-history demo** (the keystone capability): not a benchmark, a demo — **~$5–20** to record a handful of paired runs (\"agent greps for 4 minutes\" vs \"one brain call\"). Highest persuasion-per-dollar of anything on this list.\n\n## My recommendation\n\n$50 pilot first, always — every withdrawn headline in the campaign died of a harness bug the pilot would have caught, and the both-arms-success gate + arm-fairness audit need to be proven on this new A→B design before any Opus money goes in. Then the $300-ish n=30 run to see if there's an effect worth chasing, and only escalate to the $1k tier if the pilot number and the mechanism metric (re-derivation turns deleted) agree.\n\nPer the standing rule I won't launch any paid run on my own — say go (and which tier) and I'll spec the prereg + kick off the pilot."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":34,"cache_read_input_tokens":220046,"output_tokens":2334,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1376},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":34,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2334,"cache_read_input_tokens":220046,"cache_creation_input_tokens":34,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":34},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CeAyKAJYnkEbPKNcozJcv","type":"assistant","uuid":"e1f63ac5-959f-43a6-acd8-fad47054a32b","timestamp":"2026-08-18T22:05:24.125Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"f507d58c-285f-4d11-b1d0-201f2a5e172d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/graph-keystone","sessionId":"de272aad-c620-4d71-bbdd-27dd2d3dc8af","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"quizzical-sniffing-quasar"}
