{"parentUuid":"b68ab0a5-e452-4c42-98b2-1f62419272cf","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_011CeAyPMmUrEE3VdwECZfXS","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Quick math, with the one big assumption flagged:\n\n**Config mirror**: graph full run = 50 instances × 2 arms, paired. Brain A→B design doubles sessions: 50 × 2 arms × 2 sessions (task A + task B) = **200 sessions per run**.\n\n**Per-session on gpt-5.6**: our measured session profile is ~96% cache-read tokens, and gpt-5-class pricing (~$1.25–1.75/M input, 90% off cached, ~$10–14/M output) is roughly 8–10× cheaper than the Opus sessions the graph numbers came from (~$2–3/session). So **~$0.25–0.45 per session** if prefix caching behaves.\n\n| Scope | Sessions | Est. cost |\n|---|---|---|\n| One full run (50 pairs, 2 arms, A→B) | 200 | **~$50–90** |\n| Graph-campaign discipline (3 replications, same 50) | 600 | **~$150–270** |\n\nDistill in the brain arm adds ~$3–5 total on a cheap model — report it as the product's ingest cost line, don't hide it.\n\nTwo caveats that move the number:\n\n1. **Cache behavior is the whole bill.** Cache-read is ~49% of cost at Anthropic prices and ~96% of tokens; if the codex/gpt-5.6 harness path doesn't get clean prefix-cache hits (fresh process per turn, prompt churn), this can 3–4× to ~$200–350/run. The pilot tells us which world we're in.\n2. gpt-5.6 exact list pricing I'm estimating from the gpt-5 tier — worth a 2-minute check before committing the budget.\n\nSo: **call it ~$75 for one full run, ~$250 for the triple-replication headline discipline** — cheap enough that the $25 Sonnet-tier pilot and the full gpt-5.6 run together stay under ~$100. Still holding until you say go."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":51,"cache_read_input_tokens":222414,"output_tokens":2268,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1620},"server_tool_use":