{"parentUuid":"0e7f88a3-b7b8-42f6-bec0-47bbe7c4e207","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_011CeB2EnkzUMQHVtjRKsVCh","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Goal met — fair, audited, full-n LoCoMo result on the brain with gpt-5.6-terra:**\n\n## 🧠 90.84% overall (1,399/1,540)\n\n| Category | Score |\n|---|---|\n| single-hop | 93.70% |\n| temporal | 90.97% |\n| multi-hop | 88.30% |\n| open-domain | 72.92% |\n\n**Same-protocol comparisons** (identical harness, identical gpt-5 judge, full n=1,540): terra today **90.84** vs terra Aug-12 baseline 90.71 vs terratl 90.65 vs **gpt-5 answerer 90.39**. So terra ≈ gpt-5 as the answerer, +0.45pt — inside the noise band, and stable across three terra runs.\n\n**Why I trust it (the audit):** full 1,540/1,540 evaluations, **zero** questions answered with empty memories, zero empty retrievals, zero missing results — and the config verified in metadata (answerer terra, judge gpt-5, azure_ai, top-k 200, adversarial category dropped).\n\n**Full disclosure on what happened tonight:** you had apparently already run the script manually (22:22 smoke, 22:30 full) — my 22:36 relaunch of the same script then wiped the shared corpus and later killed processes, which is what produced the garbage 1/10 smoke that alarmed me. The 22:30 full run *survived* all of it (its index was in memory and it finished clean before the damage mattered) — that's the run reported above, and the audit is exactly why we can trust it despite the mess. Lesson recorded: never relaunch a corpus-wiping benchmark script without checking for a live instance.\n\n**One caveat for quoting:** this 90.84 is *this harness's* accuracy-under-gpt-5-judge — a different yardstick from the 94.74/93.83 mem0-comparison table (different protocol). Don't mix the columns. Total spend tonight: roughly the cost of one full run + fragments (~$20–30)."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":240,"cache_read_input_tokens":278364,"output_tokens":676,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":240,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":676,"cache_read_input_tokens":278364,"cache_creation_input_tokens":240,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":240},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CeB2Ej129Sddnzu7KdrFK","type":"assistant","uuid":"0388a403-d796-4f3b-bb5b-9cb7f44fd5e7","timestamp":"2026-08-18T22:43:18.097Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"f507d58c-285f-4d11-b1d0-201f2a5e172d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/graph-keystone","sessionId":"de272aad-c620-4d71-bbdd-27dd2d3dc8af","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"quizzical-sniffing-quasar"}
