{"parentUuid":"842e3f53-4c3e-432c-8582-44a568c12416","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_011CeB4ZpSxYnTjepteAP5Bq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"No — **it was not using the latest eg.** Found it:\n\n1. **Apples-to-apples, terra is actually *higher* than eg**: in this same harness with the same base config and judge, eg with gpt-5 answerer = 90.39; terra today = **90.84**. Nothing is \"lower than eg\" in the same column.\n\n2. **The higher eg numbers you remember came from the upgraded config, which tonight's run didn't use.** The Aug-11 runs with the retrieval improvements (`chrono` config, gpt-5.6-sol answerer) hit **92.99** in this harness — and the 94.74 in our table is from the mem0-comparable protocol, a different yardstick entirely.\n\n3. **Tonight's run used the old base setup**: `run_g56terra.sh` sets no `EG_*` flags at all (no profile sidecar, no chrono retrieval), and points at `~/bin/entire-graph` — an **Aug-11 \"dev\" binary** — while the improved runners on the VM use `~/bin/entire-graph-fixed`, a newer build.\n\nSo the honest reading: tonight's 90.84 is \"terra on *base* eg\" — it shows the answerer swap is neutral-to-slightly-positive, but it's not the brain's best foot. The interesting missing number is **terra + latest eg (fixed binary + chrono config)** — if the chrono lift (+2.6pt on sol) carries over, that lands ~93+.\n\nRerunning that is ~$15–25 and I have everything located (fixed binary, chrono corpus dirs, the Aug-11 runner to copy config from). Say go and I'll fire it — same discipline: fresh project name so no stale checkpoints, smoke with a *score* guard this time, full n."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2836,"cache_read_input_tokens":281038,"output_tokens":1990,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1413},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"se