{"parentUuid":"306f128e-4262-4f00-bc9d-1d96a5347e21","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_011CeB54rRpjypsXScMG7pon","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Two explorers are out (harness internals + brain's harness-facing surfaces). Drafting the plan skeleton meanwhile:"}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3472,"cache_read_input_tokens":296250,"output_tokens":828,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":67},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3472,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":828,"cache_read_input_tokens":296250,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3472,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3472},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CeB54nuzMzmTZQvRLdGi5","type":"assistant","uuid":"b6315c56-7ad1-446c-925c-f1a9d63793ec","timestamp":"2026-08-18T23:20:16.620Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"f507d58c-285f-4d11-b1d0-201f2a5e172d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/graph-keystone","sessionId":"de272aad-c620-4d71-bbdd-27dd2d3dc8af","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"quizzical-sniffing-quasar"}
{"parentUuid":"b6315c56-7ad1-446c-925c-f1a9d63793ec","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_011CeB54rRpjypsXScMG7pon","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Y7nTqvYbhFw8MJ11GUHrfB","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/suhaan/.claude/plans/quizzical-sniffing-quasar.md","content":"# BrainMark — flagship benchmark for entire-brain (fair, competitor-comparable)\n\n## Context (draft — exploration in progress)\n\nLoCoMo/LME only measure the brain's retrieval substrate over chat transcripts — no sessions,\nno code, no facts, no entity index. They prove the engine, not the product. The product claim\n(\"memory compounds: a second session reuses what the first learned\") has never been measured.\nThis benchmark is that measurement, built fair enough to publish and comparable against\ncompetitors (mem0 & friends as pluggable memory arms).\n\nTwo tracks:\n- **Track 1 — Session-reuse (A→B), the flagship**: agent does task A (brain captures+distills),\n  then a related task B with memory vs without. Primary mechanism metric: re-derivation turns\n  deleted on B. Secondary: tokens, cost, wall-clock, correctness.\n- **Track 2 — Entity-history**: \"which sessions/checkpoints changed entity X and why\" — brain\n  answers from the keystone index in one call vs agent grepping. Differentiation demo/benchmark.\n\nFairness doctrine (non-negotiable, from graph-bench ledger): symmetric prompts (would this\nsentence help an arm with no tool? then both or neither), both-arms-success + non-empty-patch\ngate with symmetric drops, n≥30 pairs, bootstrap CI + median beside totals, pre-registered\nprimary mechanism metric, add instances never replicate, load cap ~8-way, publish the harness.\n\n## Open design questions (for user)\n- Task source for A→B pairs (SWE-bench same-repo pairs vs curated real-repo commit pairs)\n- Which comp arms in v1 (none / mem0 OSS / mem0 + one more)\n- Budget tier for first real run\n\n## (Sections below filled after exploration + design agents)\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3472,"cache_read_input_tokens":296250,"output_tokens":828,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":67},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3472,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":828,"cache_read_input_tokens":296250,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3472,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3472},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CeB54nuzMzmTZQvRLdGi5","type":"assistant","uuid":"7b5800b6-bfa8-46b2-9375-56b12b7ab7bf","timestamp":"2026-08-18T23:20:26.165Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"f507d58c-285f-4d11-b1d0-201f2a5e172d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/graph-keystone","sessionId":"de272aad-c620-4d71-bbdd-27dd2d3dc8af","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"quizzical-sniffing-quasar"}
{"parentUuid":"7b5800b6-bfa8-46b2-9375-56b12b7ab7bf","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"b1763431-9e4a-4f48-abc3-561327abc891","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Y7nTqvYbhFw8MJ11GUHrfB","type":"tool_result","content":"File created successfully at: /Users/suhaan/.claude/plans/quizzical-sniffing-quasar.md (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"uuid":"f29066ca-3b13-4723-9e11-3b27699fb153","timestamp":"2026-08-18T23:20:26.181Z","toolUseResult":{"type":"create","filePath":"/Users/suhaan/.claude/plans/quizzical-sniffing-quasar.md","content":"# BrainMark — flagship benchmark for entire-brain (fair, competitor-comparable)\n\n## Context (draft — exploration in progress)\n\nLoCoMo/LME only measure the brain's retrieval substrate over chat transcripts — no sessions,\nno code, no facts, no entity index. They prove the engine, not the product. The product claim\n(\"memory compounds: a second session reuses what the first learned\") has never been measured.\nThis benchmark is that measurement, built fair enough to publish and comparable against\ncompetitors (mem0 & friends as pluggable memory arms).\n\nTwo tracks:\n- **Track 1 — Session-reuse (A→B), the flagship**: agent does task A (brain captures+distills),\n  then a related task B with memory vs without. Primary mechanism metric: re-derivation turns\n  deleted on B. Secondary: tokens, cost, wall-clock, correctness.\n- **Track 2 — Entity-history**: \"which sessions/checkpoints changed entity X and why\" — brain\n  answers from the keystone index in one call vs agent grepping. Differentiation demo/benchmark.\n\nFairness doctrine (non-negotiable, from graph-bench ledger): symmetric prompts (would this\nsentence help an arm with no tool? then both or neither), both-arms-success + non-empty-patch\ngate with symmetric drops, n≥30 pairs, bootstrap CI + median beside totals, pre-registered\nprimary mechanism metric, add instances never replicate, load cap ~8-way, publish the harness.\n\n## Open design questions (for user)\n- Task source for A→B pairs (SWE-bench same-repo pairs vs curated real-repo commit pairs)\n- Which comp arms in v1 (none / mem0 OSS / mem0 + one more)\n- Budget tier for first real run\n\n## (Sections below filled after exploration + design agents)\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null,"userModified":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"7b5800b6-bfa8-46b2-9375-56b12b7ab7bf","session_id":"f507d58c-285f-4d11-b1d0-201f2a5e172d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/graph-keystone","sessionId":"de272aad-c620-4d71-bbdd-27dd2d3dc8af","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"quizzical-sniffing-quasar"}
