{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-08-18T23:22:43.117Z","sessionId":"de272aad-c620-4d71-bbdd-27dd2d3dc8af","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>aadd7b2b93079c9fe</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>REDACTED</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-suhaan-devenv/f507d58c-285f-4d11-b1d0-201f2a5e172d/tasks/aadd7b2b93079c9fe.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Explore graphmark-bench harness\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>Findings below. Note: `/Users/suhaan/devenv/graphmark-bench` does not exist — the live harness is `/Users/suhaan/devenv/graphmark/agentic-swebench` (older copies: `/Users/suhaan/graphmark-bench-opus-tx30`, and dead refs to `/Users/suhaan/graphmark-bench`).\n\n```\ngraphmark/agentic-swebench/\n  tasks/pilot_tasks.json (3.4MB, {dataset_id,count,instances[]})  python_tasks.json  multilingual_300.json\n  tools/  run_3arm.sh(1083L, core)  run_cc_one.sh  run_matrix.sh  run_ladder.sh  py_arm.sh eg_*_arm.sh (drivers)\n          eg-q  cmm-q  graph-query (tool wrappers)  netjail/ (network stubs)\n          metrics.py(908L)  report_config.py  score_matrix.py  agg_score.py  grade_tag.sh (swebench docker)\n  measure/ batch.py paired.py pairs.py depceil.py   analysis/ leakaudit|claude-audit|conversion (transcript scans)\n  graphs/&lt;iid&gt;/graph.{symbols,edges}.ndjson   repo-cache/&lt;org__repo&gt;   checkouts/&lt;tag&gt;/&lt;arm&gt;/&lt;iid&gt;   results/&lt;tag&gt;/&lt;arm&gt;/&lt;iid&gt;/\n  .elig_*.txt (instance eligibility lists = the \"cells\")\n```\n\n**1. Run definition.** Instances are SWE-bench-format records in `tasks/pilot_tasks.json` — fields `repo, instance_id, base_commit, patch, test_patch, problem_statement, hints_text, created_at, version, FAIL_TO_PASS, PASS_TO_PASS, environment_setup_commit` (schema visible in `tasks/python_tasks.json`). A run = `(RESULTS_TAG, arm, elig-file of iids)`; entrypoint `tools/run_3arm.sh &lt;arm&gt; &lt;iid&gt;` (`run_3arm.sh:8`), invoked in fan-out loops by `tools/py_arm.sh:10-11`, `eg_robust_arm.sh:13`, `run_matrix.sh` (models × arms × instances, idempotent via `is_done()` at `run_matrix.sh:30`). Config is all env vars: `CC_MODEL, CC_MAX_TURNS(50), CC_TIMEOUT(1400), RESULTS_TAG, ENTIRE_GRAPH, CMM_BIN, SEARCH_ONLY, EG_SWEEP, EG_BATCH, CAPABILITY_ONLY, PROMPT_FAMILY, EXTRA_DISALLOW` (`run_3arm.sh:9-48`, `1053-1062`).\n\n**2. Arms.** Three: `baseline | eg | cmm`. **No MCP anywhere** — `MCP_ARGS=()` is declared at `run_3arm.sh:95` and never used. The tool is injected as a generated shell wrapper the prompt names by path: `$out/eg-q.run` (`run_3arm.sh:127-133`, env-pinned to `$EG`, per-instance graph dump, `EG_TOPK/EG_SNIPPET/EG_MAXBYTES`) and `$out/cmm-q.run` (`:261-274`, after `cmm cli index_repository --mode full`). eg requires a prebuilt graph or skips (`:51-52`). The only cross-arm difference is the prompt's tool block: `tool_block()` `:765-857`, `briefed_tool_block()` `:685`, shared clamp `shared_block()` `:858`, assembled into `PROMPT` at `:982-991` and persisted to `$out/prompt.txt`. A symmetry gate `_assert_prompt_symmetry()` `:1002-1030` hashes shared/tool blocks and hard-aborts if a CAPABILITY_ONLY block smuggles frugality phrasing. Isolation is identical per arm: `--safe-mode --disable-slash-commands`, a fixed `--disallowedTools` list, `netjail` first on PATH (`:1049-1071`).\n\n**3. Metrics.** Primary source is Claude Code's `--output-format json` → `$out/cc_out.json`, parsed in `tools/metrics.py:133-172` (`total_cost_usd`, `usage.{input,cache_creation,cache_read,output}_tokens`, `num_turns`, `subtype`, `is_error`) plus `patch.diff` non-emptiness. `report_config.py:20-30` notes `usage.*` is lossy under compaction and prefers `modelUsage`. Transcript-level metrics (round-trips, tool-call batching, per-call token cost) come from `~/.claude/projects/&lt;slug&gt;/&lt;session_id&gt;.jsonl` joined via `cc_out.json:session_id` — `measure/batch.py:9-38` (`sess_stats`), `analysis/conversion/tx.py`, `analysis/leakaudit/scan.py:248`. Wall-clock is not a first-class metric (timeout kill only, `run_3arm.sh:1055`). **Gates:** per-session gate = `usd &gt; 0 AND patch_nonempty` (`metrics.py:126-129`); both-arms gate = `gated_both` then `clean` (neither side degenerate) at `metrics.py:358-364`; degeneracy reasons at `metrics.py:159-172`. Same gate restated in `report_config.py:9-11`.\n\n**4. Pairing/analysis.** `metrics.py` `Comparison` (`:337`): paired log-ratios `logs()/pairs()` `:366-375`, `paired_block()` `:377-395` (geometric mean, `median_ratio` `:265`, 10% trimmed `:256`, pooled ratio), percentile bootstrap `bootstrap_ci()` `:271-289` (20k draws, seed 20260727), leave-one-out `loo_range()` `:291`, `mcnemar_exact()` `:310`, macro-by-language `macro_block()` `:397`, cost-per-resolved `per_resolved_ratio()` `:428`. Lighter paired deltas in `measure/paired.py` (mean diffs ±1.96 SE over the common set). Multi-tag/model rollups: `tools/score_matrix.py`, `tools/agg_score.py`, `tools/report_config.py`. Grading: `tools/grade_tag.sh:75` runs `swebench.harness.run_evaluation` in Docker over `preds_&lt;tag&gt;.json`.\n\n**5. Agent drivers.** Claude Code only, headless subscription auth: `claude -p \"$PROMPT\" --model --output-format json --max-turns` (`run_3arm.sh:1049-1053`). No codex/cursor/gemini driver in this harness (`competitive-eval/tools/agentic_parity.py` is a separate non-agent scoring path). Sessions run **locally** in a `git worktree` of `repo-cache/&lt;org__repo&gt;` at `base_commit`, under an mkdir lock (`run_3arm.sh:85-89`); Docker is used only for grading. Patch collected by `tools/collect_patch.sh` under the same lock (`:1058`), then the worktree is removed.\n\n**6. Extension surface for a two-session memory arm.** Reusable as-is: instance loading + worktree/lock/checkout (`run_3arm.sh:54-89`), tool-identity provenance (`:66-83`), isolation/netjail/launch block (`:1031-1056`), patch collection, `metrics.py` Session/gate/bootstrap/paired stats, `grade_tag.sh`. New work needed: (a) the runner is hard-wired to **one** `claude -p` call writing one `cc_out.json` per `results/&lt;tag&gt;/&lt;arm&gt;/&lt;iid&gt;/` — you need a phase loop writing e.g. `.../&lt;iid&gt;/s1/` and `.../&lt;iid&gt;/s2/`; (b) `Session`/`load_session` (`metrics.py:133`) reads exactly one `cc_out.json` per dir, so summing or comparing per-phase tokens is new code; (c) task-B definition and its own gate/grading (SWE-bench `FAIL_TO_PASS` grading only covers one patch per instance, and `grade_tag.sh:13-18` infers the arm from the tag name); (d) the state carrier itself. There is **no** existing multi-session, `--resume`/`--continue`, or sequential-task machinery in the harness — the only related asset is the separate LoCoMo conversational-memory bench at `/Users/suhaan/devenv/eg-memharness/bench/memory/` (`run_locomo.sh`, `common/{entire,cmm,graphify}_client.py`, `runmeta.py`), which shares the arm/metering idea but none of the SWE-bench code.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>63451</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>38</tool_uses><duration_ms>160554</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
