{"parentUuid":"ee5d8071-751d-4c80-9b57-95659156b65c","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"PreToolUse:Bash","toolUseID":"toolu_01Y1ApHm1Th3VmZFVg7qFLT8","hookEvent":"PreToolUse","content":"","stdout":"{\"hookSpecificOutput\":{\"hookEventName\":\"PreToolUse\",\"permissionDecisionReason\":\"RTK auto-rewrite\",\"updatedInput\":{\"command\":\"rtk read /Users/suhaan/devenv/p0p1/brain-keystone/benchmarks/agent-brain/temporal-memory/README.md --max-lines 60 2>/dev/null; echo \\\"===CONDITIONS===\\\"; rtk read /Users/suhaan/devenv/p0p1/brain-keystone/benchmarks/agent-brain/CONDITIONS.md --max-lines 50 2>/dev/null\",\"description\":\"Read temporal-memory and conditions docs in agent-brain harness\"}}}\n","stderr":"","exitCode":0,"command":"rtk hook claude","durationMs":19},"type":"attachment","uuid":"3e967a28-c7f8-49a6-90d6-cdefdb47c70f","timestamp":"2026-08-18T23:23:57.074Z","session_id":"f507d58c-285f-4d11-b1d0-201f2a5e172d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/graph-keystone","sessionId":"de272aad-c620-4d71-bbdd-27dd2d3dc8af","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"quizzical-sniffing-quasar"}
{"parentUuid":"ee5d8071-751d-4c80-9b57-95659156b65c","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"7a55e47f-14a0-478c-a660-95949b5cdaa4","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Y1ApHm1Th3VmZFVg7qFLT8","type":"tool_result","content":"# Temporal Memory Phase 0A / 0B\n\nThis lane isolates project memory from present-code retrieval. It materializes\none authentic, temporally frozen Entire session bundle and derives three\nagent-visible conditions from it:\n\n- `raw_history`: indexed history only;\n- `facts_only`: durable facts only;\n- `history_facts`: indexed history plus durable facts.\n\nRaw transcripts, checkpoint refs, semantic indexes, seed context, docs, and\npatterns are absent from every delivered memory condition. `no_brain` receives\nthe same repository snapshot and prompt with no memory source.\n\nThe development task pins the retained source-cache key plus transcript,\nhistory-index, and fact-artifact SHA-256 hashes. A pinned run fails instead of\nredistilling when that exact private source artifact is unavailable or differs.\nThis keeps agent backends on byte-identical memory inputs.\n\nTemporal rows have a hard protocol audit. In the agent-tool lane a memory arm\nis invalid unless its first tool action is exactly one `entire brain search`;\nin every lane all arms are invalid if they inspect raw `.entire`, `.benchmark`,\nor checkpoint-ref artifacts. Claude uses stream JSON and safe mode so tool\nactivity is observable and user hooks, skills, auto-memory, and project\ninstructions are disabled.\n\nThe committed development task is diagnostic, not paper evidence. It was used\nto implement and debug the adapter. Sealed tasks and repeated runs are required\nbefore any channel-attributed claim.\n\n[203 more lines]===CONDITIONS===\n# Entire Brain Benchmark Conditions\n\nThis document is the normative contract for Agent Brain benchmarks. It defines\nwhat each agent may see and use, how implementation comparisons must be run,\nand what evidence makes a result valid. If another benchmark document is\nambiguous, follow this one and update the drift.\n\nThe central comparison is simple:\n\n- **no-Brain** is a normal coding agent with its normal tools, but without\n  `entire`, `entire-graph`, `entire-brain`, or any Entire-managed memory.\n- **Brain** is the same agent with the same normal tools plus the Brain surface\n  selected by the condition.\n- **Neither variant may use information from a previous benchmark run.**\n\nGit history is a normal coding tool. `git log`, `git show`, `git blame`,\n`git diff`, and other ordinary Git commands are allowed in both variants.\nThe harness represents its prepared workspace as a synthetic merge whose first\nparent has the same tree. Agents must not explicitly diff the synthetic second\nparent or request merge-parent patches: that reconstructs harness setup rather\nthan inspecting ordinary source history.\n\n## Non-negotiable rules\n\n1. Use real coding agents on real repository tasks. Do not replace an agent\n[239 more lines]","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"d70ca842-482a-442b-81c0-5b83fbc8bcde","timestamp":"2026-08-18T23:23:57.116Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"# Temporal Memory Phase 0A / 0B\n\nThis lane isolates project memory from present-code retrieval. It materializes\none authentic, temporally frozen Entire session bundle and derives three\nagent-visible conditions from it:\n\n- `raw_history`: indexed history only;\n- `facts_only`: durable facts only;\n- `history_facts`: indexed history plus durable facts.\n\nRaw transcripts, checkpoint refs, semantic indexes, seed context, docs, and\npatterns are absent from every delivered memory condition. `no_brain` receives\nthe same repository snapshot and prompt with no memory source.\n\nThe development task pins the retained source-cache key plus transcript,\nhistory-index, and fact-artifact SHA-256 hashes. A pinned run fails instead of\nredistilling when that exact private source artifact is unavailable or differs.\nThis keeps agent backends on byte-identical memory inputs.\n\nTemporal rows have a hard protocol audit. In the agent-tool lane a memory arm\nis invalid unless its first tool action is exactly one `entire brain search`;\nin every lane all arms are invalid if they inspect raw `.entire`, `.benchmark`,\nor checkpoint-ref artifacts. Claude uses stream JSON and safe mode so tool\nactivity is observable and user hooks, skills, auto-memory, and project\ninstructions are disabled.\n\nThe committed development task is diagnostic, not paper evidence. It was used\nto implement and debug the adapter. Sealed tasks and repeated runs are required\nbefore any channel-attributed claim.\n\n[203 more lines]===CONDITIONS===\n# Entire Brain Benchmark Conditions\n\nThis document is the normative contract for Agent Brain benchmarks. It defines\nwhat each agent may see and use, how implementation comparisons must be run,\nand what evidence makes a result valid. If another benchmark document is\nambiguous, follow this one and update the drift.\n\nThe central comparison is simple:\n\n- **no-Brain** is a normal coding agent with its normal tools, but without\n  `entire`, `entire-graph`, `entire-brain`, or any Entire-managed memory.\n- **Brain** is the same agent with the same normal tools plus the Brain surface\n  selected by the condition.\n- **Neither variant may use information from a previous benchmark run.**\n\nGit history is a normal coding tool. `git log`, `git show`, `git blame`,\n`git diff`, and other ordinary Git commands are allowed in both variants.\nThe harness represents its prepared workspace as a synthetic merge whose first\nparent has the same tree. Agents must not explicitly diff the synthetic second\nparent or request merge-parent patches: that reconstructs harness setup rather\nthan inspecting ordinary source history.\n\n## Non-negotiable rules\n\n1. Use real coding agents on real repository tasks. Do not replace an agent\n[239 more lines]","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"ee5d8071-751d-4c80-9b57-95659156b65c","session_id":"f507d58c-285f-4d11-b1d0-201f2a5e172d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/graph-keystone","sessionId":"de272aad-c620-4d71-bbdd-27dd2d3dc8af","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"quizzical-sniffing-quasar"}
