{"parentUuid":"c6760b7e-72da-4ed4-99fd-a4f06279a6e0","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_011CeB5MQbHWoBN7fDdsTZff","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2575,"cache_read_input_tokens":310402,"output_tokens":2564,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":220},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2575,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2564,"cache_read_input_tokens":310402,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2575,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2575},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CeB5MLmr61kaVE25stbW4","type":"assistant","uuid":"e000663c-5a71-4cf4-87c9-f209c34bc369","timestamp":"2026-08-18T23:24:04.144Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"f507d58c-285f-4d11-b1d0-201f2a5e172d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/graph-keystone","sessionId":"de272aad-c620-4d71-bbdd-27dd2d3dc8af","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"quizzical-sniffing-quasar"}
{"parentUuid":"e000663c-5a71-4cf4-87c9-f209c34bc369","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_011CeB5MQbHWoBN7fDdsTZff","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2575,"cache_read_input_tokens":310402,"output_tokens":2564,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":220},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2575,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2564,"cache_read_input_tokens":310402,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2575,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2575},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CeB5MLmr61kaVE25stbW4","type":"assistant","uuid":"345e20e7-b757-41ea-b4dc-d0ef9728e107","timestamp":"2026-08-18T23:24:04.176Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"f507d58c-285f-4d11-b1d0-201f2a5e172d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/graph-keystone","sessionId":"de272aad-c620-4d71-bbdd-27dd2d3dc8af","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"quizzical-sniffing-quasar"}
{"parentUuid":"345e20e7-b757-41ea-b4dc-d0ef9728e107","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_011CeB5MQbHWoBN7fDdsTZff","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Hfaw3k6AJKNDAvmNfPHRHN","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Design flagship brain benchmark","subagent_type":"Plan","prompt":"Design an implementation plan for BrainMark: the flagship, publishable, competitor-comparable benchmark proving entire-brain's product value — \"a second coding session reuses what the first learned.\" READ-ONLY exploration as needed. You are the architect; output a detailed implementation plan.\n\nGROUND TRUTH FROM EXPLORATION (trust this, verify only where you must):\n\nA. /Users/suhaan/devenv/p0p1/brain-keystone/benchmarks/agent-brain/ — an EXISTING agentic A→B harness (run.py ~490KB): conditions no_brain/raw_history/facts_only/history_facts/full_brain; per-cell disposable worktrees; sandbox-exec read isolation (run.py:5124); memory bundles pinned by SHA-256 (byte-identical inputs across arms); protocol audits (memory arm invalid unless first tool action is exactly one `entire brain search`; all arms invalid if they inspect .entire/.benchmark/checkpoint refs); claude stream JSON + safe mode; MCP wiring for claude (run.py:6815 claude_mcp_config) and codex (run.py:6835); distill driver (run.py:4578); isolation via the 5 ENTIRE_PLUGIN_*/ENTIRE_REPO_ROOT env vars (run.py:3080-3083,5108-5113). temporal-memory/ lane = exactly session-A-memory→session-B-consumption, currently ONE hand-built pinned task (diagnostic, \"sealed tasks and repeated runs required before any channel-attributed claim\"). CONDITIONS.md is the normative fairness contract. docs/agent_benchmark_plan.md exists — read it.\n\nB. /Users/suhaan/devenv/graphmark/agentic-swebench — the graph token-benchmark harness: SWE-bench-format instances in tasks/*.json (fields incl. repo, base_commit, patch, test_patch, problem_statement, FAIL_TO_PASS, created_at); worktree checkout+locking (run_3arm.sh:54-89); netjail; prompt-symmetry hash gate (:1002-1030); metrics.py:337 Comparison = paired log-ratios, geometric mean, median, 20k-draw bootstrap CI (:271-289), McNemar, per-session gate usd>0 AND patch-nonempty (:126-129) + both-arms clean gate (:358-364); Docker SWE-bench grading via tools/grade_tag.sh (swebench.harness.run_evaluation). Hard-wired to ONE claude -p session per instance; no multi-session machinery. Claude Code driver only.\n\nC. Brain surfaces: distill can ingest raw claude-code JSONL by writing <brainDir>/sessions/<branch>/<id>.jsonl + synthesized manifest.json (proven by distill_cmd_test.go:29-61); recall = brain_brief/brain_search/brain_query MCP tools (no ollama needed — embedded Model2Vec, offline); NEW entity index works on plain git commits (needs `entire` binary for graph diff) via entities backfill/history + brain_entity_history MCP.\n\nD. Competitor-arm precedent: /Users/suhaan/devenv/eg-memharness/bench/memory/common/{entire,cmm,graphify}_client.py — pluggable memory clients for the conversational bench (pattern to adapt; mem0 OSS python lib would be a new client).\n\nDESIGN REQUIREMENTS:\n1. Task pairs at scale: mine SWE-bench task JSONs for (A,B) pairs — same repo, temporally ordered (created_at), overlapping patch files (and, better, overlapping entities via `entire graph diff`), B graded by its own FAIL_TO_PASS via the existing Docker grading. Target ≥40 candidate pairs → n≥30 surviving gates. Design the mining script (offline, $0) + a manual seal step (CONDITIONS.md demands sealed tasks).\n2. Arms v1 (each = memory source injected identically): no_brain (baseline), full_brain (product), raw_history (ablation: raw session-A transcript as memory — proves distillation adds value over dumping the transcript), mem0 (competitor: session-A transcript ingested via mem0 OSS, top-k retrieved at B — reuse the injection mechanism identically). Session A runs ONCE per pair per {capture on} and its outputs are pinned by SHA-256, shared across all memory arms (fairness: byte-identical A-derived inputs; also halves cost).\n3. Metrics: PRE-REGISTERED PRIMARY = mechanism metric (re-derivation/locate turns in session B — define precisely from stream-JSON transcripts, e.g. tool calls in {Read,Grep,Glob,Bash-grep-class} before first Edit, plus total turns); secondary = B tokens/cost (modelUsage), B wall-clock, B task success (FAIL_TO_PASS), both-arms gates + symmetric drops, bootstrap CI + median. Reuse graphmark metrics.py where possible.\n4. Fairness: satisfy BOTH contracts (CONDITIONS.md + graphmark symmetry-gate doctrine). Decide how the memory block is delivered so prompts stay symmetric (tool-output difference legitimate; instruction difference not).\n5. Runbook + cost: pilot (Sonnet, ~10 pairs) then full (Opus or user-chosen model, n≥30), concurrency cap ~8, idempotent resume, results layout, report generator.\n\nDECIDE AND JUSTIFY: extend agent-brain's run.py vs a new thin orchestrator importing graphmark's stats; where task-pair mining lives; how session A's claude transcript gets into the brain (raw-JSONL ingest vs entire CLI capture); how mem0 arm stays fair (same injection surface); what \"sealed\" means operationally at n=40.\n\nOUTPUT: a step-by-step implementation plan: components, file paths (new + modified), reused utilities w/ paths, the pair-mining algorithm, arm matrix, metric definitions, gates, runbook with cost tiers, and a verification section (how to prove the harness itself is fair before spending on the full run — include a null-test: brain arm with EMPTY memory must show ~zero delta). Max ~120 lines, dense."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2575,"cache_read_input_tokens":310402,"output_tokens":2564,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":220},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2575,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2564,"cache_read_input_tokens":310402,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2575,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2575},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CeB5MLmr61kaVE25stbW4","type":"assistant","uuid":"167401e1-5fd4-4b71-8c23-94be06809d53","timestamp":"2026-08-18T23:24:35.261Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"f507d58c-285f-4d11-b1d0-201f2a5e172d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/graph-keystone","sessionId":"de272aad-c620-4d71-bbdd-27dd2d3dc8af","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"quizzical-sniffing-quasar"}
{"parentUuid":"167401e1-5fd4-4b71-8c23-94be06809d53","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"7a55e47f-14a0-478c-a660-95949b5cdaa4","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Hfaw3k6AJKNDAvmNfPHRHN","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Async agent launched successfully. (This tool result is internal metadata — never quote or paste any part of it, including the agentId below, into a user-facing reply.)\nagentId: a5209d26bf998e9a7 (internal ID - do not mention to user. Use SendMessage with to: 'a5209d26bf998e9a7', summary: '<5-10 word recap>' to continue this agent.)\nThe agent is working in the background. You will be notified automatically when it completes. You know nothing about its results until that notification arrives — do not report, assume, or predict them; continue other work or respond to the user in the meantime.\nDo not duplicate this agent's work — avoid working with the same files or topics it is using.\noutput_file: /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-suhaan-devenv/f507d58c-285f-4d11-b1d0-201f2a5e172d/tasks/a5209d26bf998e9a7.output\nDo NOT Read or tail this file via the shell tool — it is the full subagent JSONL transcript and reading it will overflow your context. If the user asks for progress, say the agent is still running; you'll get a completion notification."}]}]},"uuid":"3959a6a2-43bf-455b-bb52-5f680475d469","timestamp":"2026-08-18T23:24:35.395Z","toolUseResult":{"isAsync":true,"status":"async_launched","agentId":"a5209d26bf998e9a7","description":"Design flagship brain benchmark","resolvedModel":"claude-fable-5","prompt":"Design an implementation plan for BrainMark: the flagship, publishable, competitor-comparable benchmark proving entire-brain's product value — \"a second coding session reuses what the first learned.\" READ-ONLY exploration as needed. You are the architect; output a detailed implementation plan.\n\nGROUND TRUTH FROM EXPLORATION (trust this, verify only where you must):\n\nA. /Users/suhaan/devenv/p0p1/brain-keystone/benchmarks/agent-brain/ — an EXISTING agentic A→B harness (run.py ~490KB): conditions no_brain/raw_history/facts_only/history_facts/full_brain; per-cell disposable worktrees; sandbox-exec read isolation (run.py:5124); memory bundles pinned by SHA-256 (byte-identical inputs across arms); protocol audits (memory arm invalid unless first tool action is exactly one `entire brain search`; all arms invalid if they inspect .entire/.benchmark/checkpoint refs); claude stream JSON + safe mode; MCP wiring for claude (run.py:6815 claude_mcp_config) and codex (run.py:6835); distill driver (run.py:4578); isolation via the 5 ENTIRE_PLUGIN_*/ENTIRE_REPO_ROOT env vars (run.py:3080-3083,5108-5113). temporal-memory/ lane = exactly session-A-memory→session-B-consumption, currently ONE hand-built pinned task (diagnostic, \"sealed tasks and repeated runs required before any channel-attributed claim\"). CONDITIONS.md is the normative fairness contract. docs/agent_benchmark_plan.md exists — read it.\n\nB. /Users/suhaan/devenv/graphmark/agentic-swebench — the graph token-benchmark harness: SWE-bench-format instances in tasks/*.json (fields incl. repo, base_commit, patch, test_patch, problem_statement, FAIL_TO_PASS, created_at); worktree checkout+locking (run_3arm.sh:54-89); netjail; prompt-symmetry hash gate (:1002-1030); metrics.py:337 Comparison = paired log-ratios, geometric mean, median, 20k-draw bootstrap CI (:271-289), McNemar, per-session gate usd>0 AND patch-nonempty (:126-129) + both-arms clean gate (:358-364); Docker SWE-bench grading via tools/grade_tag.sh (swebench.harness.run_evaluation). Hard-wired to ONE claude -p session per instance; no multi-session machinery. Claude Code driver only.\n\nC. Brain surfaces: distill can ingest raw claude-code JSONL by writing <brainDir>/sessions/<branch>/<id>.jsonl + synthesized manifest.json (proven by distill_cmd_test.go:29-61); recall = brain_brief/brain_search/brain_query MCP tools (no ollama needed — embedded Model2Vec, offline); NEW entity index works on plain git commits (needs `entire` binary for graph diff) via entities backfill/history + brain_entity_history MCP.\n\nD. Competitor-arm precedent: /Users/suhaan/devenv/eg-memharness/bench/memory/common/{entire,cmm,graphify}_client.py — pluggable memory clients for the conversational bench (pattern to adapt; mem0 OSS python lib would be a new client).\n\nDESIGN REQUIREMENTS:\n1. Task pairs at scale: mine SWE-bench task JSONs for (A,B) pairs — same repo, temporally ordered (created_at), overlapping patch files (and, better, overlapping entities via `entire graph diff`), B graded by its own FAIL_TO_PASS via the existing Docker grading. Target ≥40 candidate pairs → n≥30 surviving gates. Design the mining script (offline, $0) + a manual seal step (CONDITIONS.md demands sealed tasks).\n2. Arms v1 (each = memory source injected identically): no_brain (baseline), full_brain (product), raw_history (ablation: raw session-A transcript as memory — proves distillation adds value over dumping the transcript), mem0 (competitor: session-A transcript ingested via mem0 OSS, top-k retrieved at B — reuse the injection mechanism identically). Session A runs ONCE per pair per {capture on} and its outputs are pinned by SHA-256, shared across all memory arms (fairness: byte-identical A-derived inputs; also halves cost).\n3. Metrics: PRE-REGISTERED PRIMARY = mechanism metric (re-derivation/locate turns in session B — define precisely from stream-JSON transcripts, e.g. tool calls in {Read,Grep,Glob,Bash-grep-class} before first Edit, plus total turns); secondary = B tokens/cost (modelUsage), B wall-clock, B task success (FAIL_TO_PASS), both-arms gates + symmetric drops, bootstrap CI + median. Reuse graphmark metrics.py where possible.\n4. Fairness: satisfy BOTH contracts (CONDITIONS.md + graphmark symmetry-gate doctrine). Decide how the memory block is delivered so prompts stay symmetric (tool-output difference legitimate; instruction difference not).\n5. Runbook + cost: pilot (Sonnet, ~10 pairs) then full (Opus or user-chosen model, n≥30), concurrency cap ~8, idempotent resume, results layout, report generator.\n\nDECIDE AND JUSTIFY: extend agent-brain's run.py vs a new thin orchestrator importing graphmark's stats; where task-pair mining lives; how session A's claude transcript gets into the brain (raw-JSONL ingest vs entire CLI capture); how mem0 arm stays fair (same injection surface); what \"sealed\" means operationally at n=40.\n\nOUTPUT: a step-by-step implementation plan: components, file paths (new + modified), reused utilities w/ paths, the pair-mining algorithm, arm matrix, metric definitions, gates, runbook with cost tiers, and a verification section (how to prove the harness itself is fair before spending on the full run — include a null-test: brain arm with EMPTY memory must show ~zero delta). Max ~120 lines, dense.","outputFile":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-suhaan-devenv/f507d58c-285f-4d11-b1d0-201f2a5e172d/tasks/a5209d26bf998e9a7.output","canReadOutputFile":true},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"167401e1-5fd4-4b71-8c23-94be06809d53","session_id":"f507d58c-285f-4d11-b1d0-201f2a5e172d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/graph-keystone","sessionId":"de272aad-c620-4d71-bbdd-27dd2d3dc8af","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"quizzical-sniffing-quasar"}
