{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-08-18T23:29:18.681Z","sessionId":"de272aad-c620-4d71-bbdd-27dd2d3dc8af","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>a5209d26bf998e9a7</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_01Hfaw3k6AJKNDAvmNfPHRHN</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-suhaan-devenv/f507d58c-285f-4d11-b1d0-201f2a5e172d/tasks/a5209d26bf998e9a7.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Design flagship brain benchmark\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>Exploration confirmed all ground-truth anchors: run.py is import-safe (`__main__` guard at :11130), the harness-delivery lane already exists (`&lt;frozen-memory-packet&gt;` injection, policy text at run.py:6724, packet bounding :4731/:5014, delimiter guard :4840, sealed-role bundle schema :3923-3990, pinned distill driver :4578, env sanitization :5108-5113, sandbox :5124, `claude_mcp_config` :6815), phase0b protocol mandates harness delivery, and graphmark's `tools/metrics.py` stats + `tools/grade_tag.sh` + `run_3arm.sh` worktree-lock/symmetry doctrine are reusable as-is. `distill_cmd_test.go:25-75` proves raw-JSONL ingest. eg-memharness clients live at `/Users/suhaan/devenv/eg-memharness/bench/memory/benchmarks/common/*_client.py` (duck-typed `add/search` surface).\n\n# BrainMark Implementation Plan\n\n## Architecture decision\nNew thin orchestrator `benchmarks/agent-brain/brainmark/` in brain-keystone, importing `run.py` **as a library** (unmodified; it has a `__main__` guard) for its fairness primitives, and vendoring graphmark's stdlib-only stats. Justification: run.py encodes CONDITIONS.md in code (packet bounding, delimiter guard, env sanitization, sealed-role schema, pinned distill) — reimplementing risks fairness drift; but grafting SWE-bench Docker execution into a 490KB monolith risks breaking the existing lanes. Graphmark supplies the SWE-bench side (task format, repo-cache worktrees+locks, netjail, grading, paired stats) as patterns/scripts, not a framework. Pair mining lives in brainmark (product repo owns the flagship benchmark); graphmark is a data+stats dependency referenced via `config.json`.\n\n## Components (all new unless noted)\n- `brainmark/config.json` — graphmark root, repo-cache path, model tiers, packet `max_bytes`, mem0 pin (version/extractor/embedder), distill pin (`agent/model/effort` per run.py:4578 schema), concurrency=8, seeds.\n- `brainmark/mine_pairs.py` — offline $0 miner (algorithm below) → `candidates/*.json`.\n- `brainmark/seal.py` — verifies candidates, promotes to `tasks/sealed/`, writes `SEAL-MANIFEST.json` (sha256 per task file + miner commit + PREREGISTRATION.md hash).\n- `brainmark/PREREGISTRATION.md` — primary metric, gates, analysis; hash frozen in the seal manifest.\n- `brainmark/session_a.py` — runs session A once per pair per model tier (`claude -p`, stream-JSON, per-cell `CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR`); harvests the native claude-code JSONL; pins `pinned/&lt;pair&gt;/session_a/{transcript.jsonl,transcript.sha256,cc_out.json,patch.diff}`.\n- `brainmark/memsources/{empty,raw_history,full_brain,mem0_source}.py` — each: pinned-A-bytes in → packet text out, all bounded by run.py `bound_memory_packet` + `packet_contains_reserved_delimiter`; packet sha256-pinned once, reused (pin the PACKET, not the store, so distill nondeterminism can't leak asymmetry).\n  - `full_brain`: write transcript to `&lt;brainDir&gt;/sessions/main/&lt;id&gt;.jsonl` + synthesized manifest (distill_cmd_test.go pattern) → `entire-brain distill` (pinned) + `refresh history` → ONE frozen `entire brain search/brief --json` with query = B's `problem_statement`. Raw-JSONL ingest over `entire` CLI capture: keeps session A pristine/identical for all arms, no capture hooks perturbing A's metrics.\n  - `raw_history`: transcript rendered (tail-truncated to `max_bytes`) into the same envelope — distillation-value ablation.\n  - `mem0_source`: same transcript → messages → `mem0.add()`; retrieval `mem0.search(query=B problem_statement, top_k)` rendered into the identical envelope, same byte budget, same query string as full_brain's frozen retrieval. Client mirrors `entire_client.py`'s duck-typed surface. Prep cost (mem0 extraction, distill) recorded separately per arm, excluded from session-B metrics but reported.\n- `brainmark/prompts.py` — single scaffold for ALL arms incl. no_brain: adapt run.py:6724 policy text but arm-neutral (fixed `source_description`, never names the arm); packet block present in every arm; no_brain gets fixed sentinel \"(no prior-session memory available)\". Symmetry gate: sha256 of prompt with the between-delimiters region replaced by `&lt;PACKET&gt;` must be identical across a pair's arms — enforced at launch (refuse) and at report time (graphmark run_3arm.sh doctrine; only tool-output-class content differs).\n- `brainmark/run_b.py` — B-session driver: repo-cache worktree at `base_commit_B` with mkdir-lock (run_3arm.sh:54-89 pattern, ~15 lines Python), netjail from graphmark, temporal env sanitization + sandbox-exec read isolation imported from run.py, `claude -p` stream-JSON safe mode; results `results/&lt;tag&gt;/&lt;arm&gt;/&lt;pair&gt;/{cc_out.json,stream.jsonl,patch.diff,packet.json,packet.sha256,prompt.txt,prompt_sym.sha256,record.json}`; idempotent resume = skip cell iff `usd&gt;0 &amp;&amp; patch.diff nonempty` (graphmark gate).\n- `brainmark/mechmetrics.py` — PRIMARY metric from stream JSON: `locate_calls_pre_edit` = count of tool_use in {Read, Grep, Glob} ∪ {Bash where command matches `^(rg|grep|egrep|git grep|find|ls|cat|head|tail|ag)\\b`} strictly before the first tool_use in {Edit, Write, MultiEdit, NotebookEdit}; if no edit ever occurs, count over whole session and flag. Ratios computed on (count+1) — pre-registered zero handling. Also `num_turns`.\n- `brainmark/grade.py` — wraps graphmark `tools/grade_tag.sh` (Docker `swebench.harness.run_evaluation`) per arm tag; B graded by its own FAIL_TO_PASS.\n- `brainmark/vendor/graphmark_metrics.py` — pinned copy of `tools/metrics.py` with source-commit provenance header (paired log-ratios, geo mean, median, trimmed, 20k bootstrap CI, LOO, McNemar, Session gates).\n- `brainmark/report.py` + `brainmark/tests/` (see verification).\n\n## Pair-mining algorithm (offline, deterministic, $0)\n1. Load instances from graphmark `tasks/*.json`; group by `repo`; sort by `created_at`.\n2. For each ordered (A,B), `created_at_A &lt; created_at_B`: file overlap = files in `diff --git` lines of `patch_A` ∩ `patch_B`; require ≥1.\n3. Require `git merge-base --is-ancestor base_A base_B` in repo-cache (A's state precedes B's).\n4. Score = Jaccard(files) + symbol overlap from `@@` hunk headers; optional rerank via `entire graph diff` entity overlap when the `entire` binary is present (tie-breaker, not a hard gate).\n5. Leakage screens: normalized patch-body token overlap &lt; 0.8 (A must not BE B's fix); B's FAIL_TO_PASS files not fully contained in A's patch hunks without any new logic — borderline cases flagged for manual seal review.\n6. One A per B (max score); emit ≥40 candidates with full provenance (commits, overlap, ancestor proof, created_at delta).\n7. **Seal (operational)**: human reviews each candidate (real regression, prompt not answer-revealing, no near-duplicate pairs), promotes ~30+ to `tasks/sealed/` with `memory_bundle.role=\"sealed\"` (run.py schema validates), 10 to dev split (disjoint instance ids per CONDITIONS.md); commit `SEAL-MANIFEST.json` + PREREGISTRATION.md **before** the first confirmatory B session; `report.py` refuses to aggregate on hash mismatch or post-seal edits.\n\n## Arm matrix (per pair; session A runs ONCE, sha256-pinned, shared)\n| arm | memory source | packet | ablates/compares |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| no_brain | none | sentinel-empty | baseline |\n| full_brain | distill+history over pinned A JSONL | frozen brain retrieval | product |\n| raw_history | pinned A transcript verbatim | truncated transcript | distillation value |\n| mem0 | mem0 OSS over same bytes | top-k results | competitor |\n\nAll arms harness-delivered through the identical envelope (phase0b's mandated lane — agent self-retrieval makes outcomes hostage to search choice); a `full_brain_mcp` self-retrieval arm is deferred to v2 exploratory.\n\n## Metrics &amp; gates\n- Primary (pre-registered): paired log-ratio of `locate_calls_pre_edit+1`, geo mean + 20k bootstrap CI + median, arm vs no_brain. Secondary: billed_new/total tokens &amp; usd (cc_out.json `modelUsage`/usage), duration, `num_turns`, FAIL_TO_PASS resolve (McNemar exact), per-repo rows.\n- Gates (vendored metrics.py): per-session `usd&gt;0 ∧ patch nonempty`; both-arms gate; degenerate-subtype/zero-cost exclusions symmetric across arms; plus BrainMark gates: prompt-symmetry sha equal, packet.sha256 matches pin, no Entire-family tool in no_brain/raw_history/mem0, no `.entire`/`.benchmark`/checkpoint inspection anywhere (run.py audit), no A-artifact paths readable from B worktree.\n\n## Runbook &amp; cost\n1. `$0`: mine → seal → symmetry/pinning tests. 2. Prep: session A + all packets, pilot tier (Sonnet): 10 dev pairs ≈ 10 A-sessions + distill+mem0 prep ≈ $10–25. 3. Pilot B: 10×4 Sonnet sessions ≈ $25–75; run report; fix harness only (never tasks). 4. Full: n≥30 sealed, A=B model (Opus or user-chosen): ~30 A + 120 B ≈ $500–1200 + prep; concurrency 8, per-repo worktree lock, resume-safe. 5. `grade.py` per tag (Docker, free). 6. `report.py` → REPORT.md/report.json: full_brain vs no_brain (headline), vs raw_history, vs mem0.\n\n## Verification before full spend\n- Miner determinism (two runs byte-identical); seal-hash round-trip.\n- Unit: symmetry sha across stub-packet arms; delimiter-guard rejection; packet re-derivation from pinned transcript → identical sha; mechmetrics against 3 hand-labeled stream fixtures.\n- **Null test (paid, tiny)**: 3 dev pairs × 2 reps, full_brain machinery with EMPTY packet vs no_brain — primary-metric and token geo deltas must have CI straddling 0 (|point| ≲10%): proves the injection machinery itself is inert, so any full-run delta is attributable to memory content.\n- Leakage audit: grep B transcripts for A `instance_id`/pinned paths; confirm sandbox-exec denials logged.\n- One-pair end-to-end smoke including Docker grading.\n\n### Critical Files for Implementation\n- /Users/suhaan/devenv/p0p1/brain-keystone/benchmarks/agent-brain/run.py (import as library: packet bounding :4731/:5014, delimiter guard :4840, policy text :6724, env sanitization :5108, sandbox :5124, bundle schema :3923, distill :4578)\n- /Users/suhaan/devenv/graphmark/agentic-swebench/tools/metrics.py (vendor: paired stats, gates, bootstrap, McNemar)\n- /Users/suhaan/devenv/graphmark/agentic-swebench/run_3arm.sh (worktree locking :54-89, symmetric-prompt doctrine :799-1040) and /Users/suhaan/devenv/graphmark/agentic-swebench/tools/grade_tag.sh (Docker grading)\n- /Users/suhaan/devenv/p0p1/brain-keystone/internal/cli/distill_cmd_test.go (raw-JSONL + synthesized-manifest ingest contract, :25-75)\n- /Users/suhaan/devenv/eg-memharness/bench/memory/benchmarks/common/entire_client.py (duck-typed memory-client surface to mirror for the mem0 arm)</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>78940</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>20</tool_uses><duration_ms>283351</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
