+review (user is thinking NeurIPS-class venues): pre-registered primary metric, sealed tasks,","+external tasks + external grading, released harness."," ","-Two tracks:","-- **Track 1 — Session-reuse (A→B), the flagship**: agent does task A (brain captures+distills),","-  then a related task B with memory vs without. Primary mechanism metric: re-derivation turns","-  deleted on B. Secondary: tokens, cost, wall-clock, correctness.","-- **Track 2 — Entity-history**: \"which sessions/checkpoints changed entity X and why\" — brain","-  answers from the keystone index in one call vs agent grepping. Differentiation demo/benchmark.","+User decisions: **all comp arms** (mem0 + Graphify + cmm + raw_history ablation) ·","+**SWE-bench mined pairs** as task source · **pilot → full** budget path."," ","-Fairness doctrine (non-negotiable, from graph-bench ledger): symmetric prompts (would this","-sentence help an arm with no tool? then both or neither), both-arms-success + non-empty-patch","-gate with symmetric drops, n≥30 pairs, bootstrap CI + median beside totals, pre-registered","-primary mechanism metric, add instances never replicate, load cap ~8-way, publish the harness.","+## Architecture"," ","-## Open design questions (for user)","-- Task source for A→B pairs (SWE-bench same-repo pairs vs curated real-repo commit pairs)","-- Which comp arms in v1 (none / mem0 OSS / mem0 + one more)","-- Budget tier for first real run","+New thin orchestrator **`benchmarks/agent-brain/brainmark/`** (in the entire-brain repo,","+branch off main / on top of keystone), importing the existing `run.py` **as a library**","+(it has a `__main__` guard at run.py:11130 — do not modify it) for its fairness primitives:","+packet bounding (:4731/:5014), delimiter guard (:4840), arm-neutral policy text (:6724),","+sealed-bundle schema (:3923), env sanitization (:5108), sandbox-exec (:5124), pinned distill","+driver (:4578). GraphMark (`/Users/suhaan/devenv/graphmark/agentic-swebench`) supplies the","+SWE-bench side as patterns/data, not a framework: task JSONs, repo-cache worktrees+locks","+(run_3arm.sh:54-89), netjail, Docker grading (tools/grade_tag.sh), and vendored paired stats","+(tools/metrics.py — log-ratios, geo-mean, median, 20k bootstrap CI, McNemar, session gates)."," ","-## (Sections below filled after exploration + design agents)","+## Components (new files under `benchmarks/agent-brain/brainmark/`)","+","+- `config.json` — graphmark root, repo-cache, model tiers, packet max_bytes, per-competitor","+  pins (mem0 version/embedder; graphify + cmm pinned binaries), distill pin, concurrency=8, seeds.","+- `mine_pairs.py` — offline $0 miner (below) → `candidates/*.json`.","+- `seal.py` + `PREREGISTRATION.md` — human-review promotion to `tasks/sealed/` (n≥30) +","+  disjoint 10-pair dev split; `SEAL-MANIFEST.json` = sha256 of every task + miner commit +","+  prereg hash. Report refuses to aggregate on hash mismatch. Seal BEFORE first confirmatory run.","+- `session_a.py` — session A runs ONCE per pair per tier (`claude -p` stream-JSON, isolated","+  CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR); native claude-code JSONL harvested and sha256-pinned. Shared by ALL arms.","+- `memsources/{empty,raw_history,full_brain,mem0_source,graphify_source,cmm_source}.py` — each:","+  pinned-A-bytes in → memory packet out, bounded/guarded by run.py primitives; the PACKET is","+  sha256-pinned (not the store), so ingest nondeterminism can't create arm asymmetry.","+  - `full_brain`: write A transcript to `<brainDir>/sessions/main/<id>.jsonl` + synthesized","+    manifest (contract proven in internal/cli/distill_cmd_test.go:25-75) → pinned","+    `entire-brain distill` + `refresh history` → ONE frozen `brain search/brief --json`,","+    query = B's problem_statement.","+  - `raw_history`: A transcript verbatim, tail-truncated to max_bytes — distillation ablation.","+  - `mem0/graphify/cmm`: same A bytes into each competitor (duck-typed add/search clients —","+    mirror /Users/suhaan/devenv/eg-memharness/bench/memory/benchmarks/common/entire_client.py;","+    graphify+cmm clients exist there to adapt), retrieval with the SAME query string and byte","+    budget, rendered into the IDENTICAL envelope. Prep cost recorded separately, reported.","+- `prompts.py` — one scaffold for all 6 arms; packet block present in every arm (no_brain gets","+  a fixed \"(no prior-session memory available)\" sentinel); symmetry gate = sha256 of prompt","+  with packet region replaced by `<PACKET>` must be identical across a pair's arms; enforced","+  at launch and re-checked at report time.","+- `run_b.py` — B driver: worktree at base_commit_B (graphmark lock pattern), netjail, run.py","+  env-sanitization + sandbox, `claude -p` stream-JSON safe mode; per-cell results dir with","+  cc_out.json, stream.jsonl, patch.diff, packet.sha256, prompt_sym.sha256; idempotent resume","+  (skip iff usd>0 ∧ patch nonempty).","+- `mechmetrics.py` — PRIMARY pre-registered metric: `locate_calls_pre_edit` = tool_use in","+  {Read,Grep,Glob} ∪ {Bash matching ^(rg|grep|egrep|git grep|find|ls|cat|head|tail|ag)\\b}","+  strictly before first {Edit,Write,MultiEdit,NotebookEdit}; no-edit sessions counted whole +","+  flagged; ratios on (count+1). Secondary: tokens/usd (modelUsage), duration, num_turns.","+- `grade.py` — wraps graphmark grade_tag.sh (Docker swebench.harness.run_evaluation); B graded","+  by its own FAIL_TO_PASS. `vendor/graphmark_metrics.py` — pinned metrics.py copy w/ provenance","+  header. `report.py` — REPORT.md/json: full_brain vs no_brain (headline), vs raw_history","+  (distillation value), vs mem0/graphify/cmm (competitor table).","+","+## Pair mining (deterministic, $0)","+","+Group graphmark `tasks/*.json` instances by repo, sort by created_at; for ordered (A,B):","+≥1 overlapping file between patch_A and patch_B (diff --git paths) · `git merge-base","+--is-ancestor base_A base_B` · score = Jaccard(files) + hunk-header symbol overlap (optional","+`entire graph diff` entity rerank when available) · leakage screens: patch-body token overlap","+< 0.8 (A must not BE B's fix), borderline flagged for seal review · one best A per B ·","+emit ≥40 candidates with full provenance.","+","+## Arm matrix (session A once per pair, pinned, shared by all arms)","+","+| arm | memory source | proves |","+|---|---|---|","+| no_brain | sentinel-empty packet | baseline |","+| full_brain | distill+history over pinned A JSONL | the product |","+| raw_history | raw A transcript | distillation > transcript-dumping |","+| mem0 | mem0 OSS over same bytes | vs the named competitor |","+| graphify | graphify over same bytes | vs YC code-memory competitor |","+| cmm | cmm over same bytes | vs codebase-memory-mcp |","+","+All packets harness-delivered through one envelope (phase0b doctrine — self-retrieval arms","+deferred to v2 exploratory).","+","+## Gates (all vendored/enforced)","+","+Per-session usd>0 ∧ patch nonempty · all-arms-clean pair gate, symmetric drops · prompt-symmetry","+sha equal · packet sha matches pin · no Entire-family tools outside full_brain · no","+.entire/.benchmark/checkpoint-ref inspection anywhere (run.py audit) · no A-artifact paths","+readable from B worktree.","+","+## Runbook + cost (6 arms)","+","+1. **$0**: mine → human seal (n≥30 + 10 dev) → prereg freeze → symmetry/pinning/miner-determinism","+   unit tests.","+2. **Null test (~$15, non-negotiable)**: 3 dev pairs × 2 reps, full_brain machinery with EMPTY","+   packet vs no_brain — primary + token deltas must straddle 0. Proves the machinery is inert.","+3. **Pilot (Sonnet, 10 dev pairs)**: 10 A + 60 B + prep ≈ **$60–120**. Fix harness only, never tasks.","+4. **Full (n≥30 sealed, main model)**: 30 A + 180 B ≈ **$700–1,500 on Opus** (or ~$150–300 on","+   gpt-5.6-class via Azure if the user prefers). Concurrency 8, resume-safe.","+5. Docker grading (free) → `report.py`.","+","+## Verification","+","+Miner determinism (byte-identical double run) · seal-hash round-trip · symmetry sha across","+stub-packet arms · delimiter-guard rejection test · packet re-derivation → identical sha ·","+mechmetrics vs 3 hand-labeled stream fixtures · null test (above) · leakage audit (grep B","+transcripts for A instance_ids/paths; sandbox denials logged) · one-pair end-to-end smoke","+including Docker grading — all BEFORE the full spend.","+","+## Critical reused files","+","+- brain-keystone `benchmarks/agent-brain/run.py` (library import; DO NOT modify)","+- brain-keystone `benchmarks/agent-brain/CONDITIONS.md` (normative contract; extend, don't fork)","+- graphmark `agentic-swebench/tools/metrics.py` (vendor), `run_3arm.sh` (patterns),","+  `tools/grade_tag.sh` (grading), `tasks/*.json` (instance pool)","+- brain-keystone `internal/cli/distill_cmd_test.go:25-75` (raw-JSONL ingest contract)","+- eg-memharness `bench/memory/benchmarks/common/*_client.py` (competitor client surface)"]}],"originalFile":"# BrainMark — flagship benchmark for entire-brain (fair, competitor-comparable)\n\n## Context (draft — exploration in progress)\n\nLoCoMo/LME only measure the brain's retrieval substrate over chat transcripts — no sessions,\nno code, no facts, no entity index. They prove the engine, not the product. The product claim\n(\"memory compounds: a second session reuses what the first learned\") has never been measured.\nThis benchmark is that measurement, built fair enough to publish and comparable against\ncompetitors (mem0 & friends as pluggable memory arms).\n\nTwo tracks:\n- **Track 1 — Session-reuse (A→B), the flagship**: agent does task A (brain captures+distills),\n  then a related task B with memory vs without. Primary mechanism metric: re-derivation turns\n  deleted on B. Secondary: tokens, cost, wall-clock, correctness.\n- **Track 2 — Entity-history**: \"which sessions/checkpoints changed entity X and why\" — brain\n  answers from the keystone index in one call vs agent grepping. Differentiation demo/benchmark.\n\nFairness doctrine (non-negotiable, from graph-bench ledger): symmetric prompts (would this\nsentence help an arm with no tool? then both or neither), both-arms-success + non-empty-patch\ngate with symmetric drops, n≥30 pairs, bootstrap CI + median beside totals, pre-registered\nprimary mechanism metric, add instances never replicate, load cap ~8-way, publish the harness.\n\n## Open design questions (for user)\n- Task source for A→B pairs (SWE-bench same-repo pairs vs curated real-repo commit pairs)\n- Which comp arms in v1 (none / mem0 OSS / mem0 + one more)\n- Budget tier for first real run\n\n## (Sections below filled after exploration + design agents)\n","userModified":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"dc8efaad-d1be-458b-b68a-8f9507749e8f","session_id":"f507d58c-285f-4d11-b1d0-201f2a5e172d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/graph-keystone","sessionId":"de272aad-c620-4d71-bbdd-27dd2d3dc8af","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"quizzical-sniffing-quasar"}
