sers/suhaan/devenv/eg-memharness/bench/memory/benchmarks/common/entire_client.py (read the graphify/cmm clients there and adapt; mem0 client written against mem0 OSS pip API, import-guarded so tests pass without the package installed).\n3. Fairness primitives: import benchmarks/agent-brain/run.py AS A LIBRARY (it has a __main__ guard; do NOT modify it). Use its packet bounding, delimiter guard, policy text, env sanitization, sandbox helpers per the plan's line refs. If an import proves impractical for a specific helper, vendor that ONE function with a provenance comment — never fork the file.\n4. RUN THE MINER for real (it's $0): against /Users/suhaan/devenv/graphmark/agentic-swebench/tasks/*.json with repo-cache at .../repo-cache. Report the candidate-pair count per repo and total — this is the go/no-go signal for n≥30. If <40 candidates, still finish the build and report the shortfall prominently; do NOT loosen the mining gates to hit the number.\n5. Tests (offline, all must pass): miner determinism (run twice, byte-identical output); seal-hash round-trip + report refusing on mismatch; prompt symmetry sha identical across all 6 arms with stub packets; delimiter-guard rejection; packet re-derivation → identical sha; mechmetrics against 3 hand-written stream-JSON fixtures (hand-label expected locate_calls_pre_edit incl. a no-edit session); run_b dry-run produces the full results-dir layout with a stubbed claude binary (PATH stub emitting canned cc_out.json + stream).\n6. MUTATION-verify two load-bearing behaviors: (a) break the symmetry gate → its test fails; (b) break the leakage screen in the miner (drop the 0.8 overlap cap) → determinism/fixture test fails or a dedicated screen test fails. State results.\n\nConventions: python3 stdlib only where possible (mem0 import-guarded); no network in tests; everything under benchmarks/agent-brain/brainmark/; make a top-level README.md in brainmark/ with the runbook (incl. the paid tiers you are NOT running). Commit on the branch in 2-3 logical commits, normal messages, NO AI footers/Co-Authored-By. Do NOT push.\n\nReport caveman-ultra: miner candidate counts (per repo + total — LEAD WITH THIS), files+line counts, test summary, mutation results, commit shas. Max 30 lines."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1224,"cache_read_input_tokens":334357,"output_tokens":1714,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1224,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1714,"cache_read_input_tokens":334357,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1224,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1224},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CeB7DA4vbQZGKtbrELqvC","type":"assistant","uuid":"bf5227cf-0622-447b-96c8-662868535fba","timestamp":"2026-08-18T23:48:42.941Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"f507d58c-285f-4d11-b1d0-201f2a5e172d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/graph-keystone","sessionId":"de272aad-c620-4d71-bbdd-27dd2d3dc8af","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"quizzical-sniffing-quasar"}
