{"parentUuid":"2e939ba7-a4b9-421c-a1ce-9db880182fb1","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_011CeB7Gif5KJrzXG2AMpc8G","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Both parts confirmed — and the good news is the design already satisfies the first:\n\n**\"Only one brain chat\"** — yes, the design has exactly that, in all three senses it could mean:\n- **One brain arm** (`full_brain`) — no facts-only/history-only variants cluttering v1; those are v2 ablations if ever.\n- **One session-A chat per pair**, run once, sha256-pinned, shared byte-identical across all six arms.\n- **One frozen brain retrieval** per pair (a single `brain search/brief` call with B's problem statement as query) — the brain doesn't get to iteratively re-query; the packet is pinned. That's also what makes the fairness audit clean.\n\n**NeurIPS-level prestige** — understood as the bar, and it changes what \"done\" means. The current design already carries the hard scientific core (pre-registration frozen before confirmatory runs, sealed external tasks, external Docker grading, bootstrap CIs, mechanism metric, null test, released harness). To be a credible NeurIPS Datasets & Benchmarks submission I'm adding to the deliverable set:\n\n1. **DATASHEET.md** — a proper datasheet for the pair dataset (provenance, mining protocol, seal criteria, licensing — SWE-bench is MIT-derived so redistribution is clean).\n2. **REPRODUCIBILITY.md** — exact pins (models, binaries, seeds, prompts) sufficient for a third party to replicate from a clean machine.\n3. **Multi-model generality** — the full run reported on ≥2 agent models (e.g. Claude + gpt-5.6-class via the codex driver), since single-model results get killed in review.\n4. **Limitations section written by us first** — including the honest ones we already know: memory is harness-delivered not self-retrieved (v2), pairs are same-repo temporal neighbors not arbitrary related work, and the mechanism metric is a proxy.\n5. **Baseline dignity** — competitor arms run with their pinned, documented best configs, not defaults we chose for them (the thing reviewers check first).\n\nThe builder is mid-flight on the $0 stage; I'll fold these into its follow-up pass when it reports, and they're now in the notepad so nothing drops. None of this changes the cost tiers — it's documentation and a second model in the full run (~+$150–300 if we pair Opus with gpt-5.6 on Azure)."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":444,"cache_read_input_tokens":338297,"output_tokens":2158,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1362},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":444,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2158,"cache_read_input_tokens":338297,"cache_creation_input_tokens":444,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":444},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CeB7GeouCpNRc3w4GJLRM","type":"assistant","uuid":"5bbbd07f-f84e-49c6-903c-1fee9ed612e7","timestamp":"2026-08-18T23:49:41.606Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"f507d58c-285f-4d11-b1d0-201f2a5e172d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/graph-keystone","sessionId":"de272aad-c620-4d71-bbdd-27dd2d3dc8af","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"quizzical-sniffing-quasar"}
