{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-08-18T23:54:18.749Z","sessionId":"de272aad-c620-4d71-bbdd-27dd2d3dc8af","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>a4526f536919dc637</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>REDACTED</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-suhaan-devenv/f507d58c-285f-4d11-b1d0-201f2a5e172d/tasks/a4526f536919dc637.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Map entire-brain CLI + manifest schema\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result># ANSWERS — repo /Users/suhaan/devenv/p0p1/brainmark (all live-verified via `go build` + `--help`)\n\n## 1. MANIFEST SCHEMA\n\n`internal/cli/brain.go:12`\n```go\nconst brainManifestSchemaVersion = 3\n```\n\n`internal/cli/export.go:31-32` (filenames written into brainDir):\n```go\nexportManifestFileName = \"manifest.json\"\nexportReadmeFileName   = \"README.md\"\n```\n`writeBrainManifestAndReadme` (`internal/cli/brain.go:280`) writes exactly these two files, atomically, via `writeBrainRelativeFileAtomic(outputDir, exportManifestFileName, ...)` then same for README. JSON is `json.MarshalIndent(manifest, \"\", \"  \")` + trailing `\\n`, mode `0o600`.\n\n`exportManifest` (`internal/cli/export.go:3507-3522`):\n```go\ntype exportManifest struct {\n    SchemaVersion      int             `json:\"schema_version\"`\n    GeneratedAt        time.Time       `json:\"generated_at\"`\n    RepoRoot           string          `json:\"repo_root,omitempty\"`\n    RepoKey            string          `json:\"repo_key,omitempty\"`\n    EntireCLIVersion   string          `json:\"entire_cli_version,omitempty\"`\n    DefaultBranch      string          `json:\"default_branch,omitempty\"`\n    TranscriptMode     string          `json:\"transcript_mode\"`\n    Scope              string          `json:\"scope\"`\n    CheckpointLimit    int             `json:\"checkpoint_limit\"`\n    CheckpointsScanned int             `json:\"checkpoints_scanned\"`\n    Branches           []exportBranch  `json:\"branches,omitempty\"`\n    Sessions           []exportSession `json:\"sessions\"`\n    Warnings           []string        `json:\"warnings,omitempty\"`\n    Sources            *brainSources   `json:\"sources,omitempty\"`\n}\n```\n\n`exportSession` (`export.go:3531-3553`):\n```go\ntype exportSession struct {\n    SessionID            string                `json:\"session_id\"`\n    Branch               string                `json:\"branch,omitempty\"`\n    SourceBranch         string                `json:\"source_branch,omitempty\"`\n    Authors              []exportAuthor        `json:\"authors,omitempty\"`\n    Agent                string                `json:\"agent,omitempty\"`\n    Model                string                `json:\"model,omitempty\"`\n    Kind                 string                `json:\"kind,omitempty\"`\n    ReviewSkills         []string              `json:\"review_skills,omitempty\"`\n    LatestCheckpoint     string                `json:\"latest_checkpoint_id\"`\n    SessionIndex         int                   `json:\"session_index\"`\n    CreatedAt            time.Time             `json:\"created_at\"`\n    TurnID               string                `json:\"turn_id,omitempty\"`\n    IsTask                bool                 `json:\"is_task,omitempty\"`\n    ToolUseID            string                `json:\"tool_use_id,omitempty\"`\n    FilesTouched         []string              `json:\"files_touched,omitempty\"`\n    TokenUsage           *checkpointTokenUsage `json:\"token_usage,omitempty\"`\n    Summary              *checkpointSummary    `json:\"summary,omitempty\"`\n    CheckpointsCount     int                   `json:\"checkpoints_count,omitempty\"`\n    TranscriptPath       string                `json:\"transcript_path\"`\n    SourceTranscriptPath string                `json:\"-\"`  // NOT serialized\n    SourceKey            string                `json:\"-\"`  // NOT serialized\n}\n```\n(`exportBranch` at export.go:3524; `exportAuthor` at 3555 — Name/Email/Commits/LastCommitAt, all omitempty except none-tagged.)\n\n`brainSources` (`brain.go:22-30`):\n```go\ntype brainSources struct {\n    Seed     *seedSourceManifest     `json:\"seed,omitempty\"`\n    Sessions *sessionSourceManifest  `json:\"sessions,omitempty\"`\n    Semantic *semanticSourceManifest `json:\"semantic,omitempty\"`\n    History  *historySourceManifest  `json:\"history,omitempty\"`\n    Facts    *factSourceManifest     `json:\"facts,omitempty\"`\n    Docs     *docSourceManifest      `json:\"docs,omitempty\"`\n    Patterns *patternSourceManifest  `json:\"patterns,omitempty\"`\n}\n```\n\n`sessionSourceManifest` (`brain.go:32-45`):\n```go\ntype sessionSourceManifest struct {\n    GeneratedAt        time.Time       `json:\"generated_at\"`\n    EntireCLIVersion   string          `json:\"entire_cli_version,omitempty\"`\n    DefaultBranch      string          `json:\"default_branch,omitempty\"`\n    TranscriptMode     string          `json:\"transcript_mode\"`\n    Scope              string          `json:\"scope\"`\n    CheckpointLimit    int             `json:\"checkpoint_limit\"`\n    CheckpointsScanned int             `json:\"checkpoints_scanned\"`\n    OldestSessionAt    *time.Time      `json:\"oldest_session_at,omitempty\"`\n    LatestCheckpointID string          `json:\"latest_checkpoint_id,omitempty\"`\n    Branches           []exportBranch  `json:\"branches,omitempty\"`\n    Sessions           []exportSession `json:\"sessions\"`\n    Warnings           []string        `json:\"warnings,omitempty\"`\n}\n```\n(Sibling source manifests, in case needed: `seedSourceManifest` seed.go:67; `semanticSourceManifest` semantic.go:79; `historySourceManifest` history.go:71; `factSourceManifest` facts.go:32; `docSourceManifest` doc.go:29; `patternSourceManifest` episodes.go:40 — all read if you need them, ask.)\n\n**Time format**: plain `time.Time` fields, no custom `MarshalJSON` anywhere in `internal/cli` — encoded via Go stdlib default, i.e. RFC3339 with optional fractional-nanosecond digits, layout `\"2006-01-02T15:04:05.999999999Z07:00\"`. NOT written with a fixed `time.RFC3339` truncation for JSON fields (only used for human-text output like README/status lines). Write `\"...Z\"` for UTC-zero-fraction timestamps and it round-trips fine.\n\nFor a hand-written manifest to pass `writeBrainManifestAndReadme`'s own guard (`brain.go:287`, it calls `loadBrainManifest` first, which round-trips existing bytes through `decodeStrictVersionedJSON` and rejects `version &gt; brainManifestSchemaVersion` or `&lt; 0`), set `\"schema_version\": 3` (or omit — normalized to 1 if 0, but any writer resets it to 3 on save anyway).\n\n## 2. `entire-brain distill` (verified live via `--help`)\n\nPositional: `distill [path]` — optional repo dir arg (`Args: cobra.MaximumNArgs(1)`), defaults to `opts.Env.RepoRoot` else `.`. **Not** a brain-dir arg — it's the repo path; brainDir is derived (see §6).\n\nFlags (all confirmed):\n- `--dry-run` — bool, \"Estimate distill work without calling an agent or writing facts.\" When set, calls `buildDistillDryRunReportContext` and returns a `distillDryRunReport` (schema_version, generated_at, brain_path, branch, force, agent, model, effort, jobs, extraction_jobs_cap, max_chunk_bytes, confidence_threshold, sessions, cached_sessions, sessions_to_distill, missing_transcripts, raw_bytes, preprocessed_bytes, chunks, chunks_if_uncached, ...) — no agent invoked, no facts written.\n- `--agent string` (default `\"auto\"`) — allowed values: `auto | codex | claude-code | ollama | command | none`. `none` errors (\"distillation requires an agent\"). Exact switch is in `internal/cli/distill.go:106` `distillAgentCommandArgs`.\n- `--agent-command stringArray` — exact flag name is `--agent-command` (repeatable). **Required** when `--agent command`; errors \"`--agent-command is required when --agent command`\" if empty.\n- `--model string` — override model for codex/claude-code, or pick Ollama model.\n- `--effort string` — override reasoning effort for codex/claude-code.\n- `--branch`, `--session`, `--force`, `--json`, `--confidence float64` (default 0.75), `--concurrency int` (default 4), `--jobs int` (compat alias, conflicts if != concurrency), `--max-chunk-bytes int` (default 49152).\n- Output: facts written under `&lt;brainDir&gt;/facts/` (`factsDirName = \"facts\"` at `internal/cli/facts.go:20`), taxonomy at `&lt;brainDir&gt;/facts/taxonomy.json` (`factsTaxonomyPath = factsDirName + \"/\" + \"taxonomy.json\"`, facts.go:21-22). Fact-source summary recorded onto `manifest.Sources.Facts` (`factSourceManifest`) and manifest+README rewritten via `writeBrainManifestAndReadme`.\n- `--json` (non-dry-run) prints `json.MarshalIndent(source, \"\", \"  \")` where `source` is `*factSourceManifest`.\n\n## 3. `entire-brain refresh history` — verified live\n\n```\nentire-brain refresh history [path]\n```\n`internal/cli/history.go:250-267`, `newHistoryIndexCommand`. **No flags of its own** (only inherited `-h`). `Args: cobra.MaximumNArgs(1)`, same target resolution as distill (path = repo dir, default `.`/RepoRoot). Errors if target isn't a local path: `\"refresh history requires a local repository path: %s\"`.\n\nReads: exported session transcripts already on disk under the brain (built by `refresh sessions`/`export`). Writes: calls `writeBrainHistoryIndexAndSourceContext(ctx, storage.BrainDir, ...)` → decision/rationale history index (`historySourceManifest`, index file under brainDir, path reported by `source.IndexPath`, printed as `\"indexed %d history records: %s\\n\"`). Also runs history-vector backfill iff env var `ENTIRE_BRAIN_EMBEDDER` is set (opt-in).\n\nNote: `refresh` itself (`entire-brain refresh`, no subcommand) is the umbrella that runs sessions+seed+semantic+history+delta in sequence; `refresh history` is the standalone single-stage form. Sibling stages: `refresh` (export/sessions), `refresh index` (semantic), `refresh delta` (short-term memory), `refresh seed`.\n\n## 4. `entire-brain search` and `entire-brain brief` — verified live\n\n**Top-level commands, NOT nested under `brain`.** Both registered directly on root (`internal/cli/root.go:98,107`): `entire-brain search &lt;query&gt;`, `entire-brain brief &lt;task&gt; | brief --handoff`.\n\n### `search --json` (also applies to `vsearch`, `query` — same `newRetrieveCommand` factory, `internal/cli/retrieve_cmd.go:70-121`)\nFlags: `--json`, `--limit int` (default 10), `-n/--number int` (alias), `--format string` (`json`|`cli`), `--branch`, `--patterns`, `--source string` (`all|fact|history|conversation|doc`), `--after`, `--before`, `--session`, `--agent`, `--concept stringArray` (repeat, max 4), `--include-abstract`.\n\n**JSON shape DOES have `results`** (non-multi-concept path, `retrieve_cmd.go:238`):\n```go\nout := map[string]any{\n    \"query\": query, \"branch\": resolvedBranch,\n    \"results\": compactUnifiedResults(results, query),   // []compactUnifiedResult\n    // optional: \"abstract_previews\", \"abstract_previews_truncated\",\n    //           \"likely_edit_files\", \"likely_test_files\",\n    //           \"action_checklist\", \"related_patterns\", \"blind_spot\"\n}\n```\nPer-result struct `compactUnifiedResult` (`retrieve_cmd.go:17-56`):\n```go\ntype compactUnifiedResult struct {\n    Source  string `json:\"source\"`\n    ID      string `json:\"id\"`\n    Path    string `json:\"path,omitempty\"`\n    Heading string `json:\"heading,omitempty\"`\n    Line    int    `json:\"line,omitempty\"`\n    Text                 string            `json:\"text\"`\n    Excerpt              string            `json:\"excerpt,omitempty\"`\n    Score                float64           `json:\"score,omitempty\"`\n    VerificationRequired bool              `json:\"verification_required,omitempty\"`\n    Caveats              []retrievalCaveat `json:\"caveats,omitempty\"`\n    RelatedIDs           []string          `json:\"related_ids,omitempty\"`\n    EndLine      int      `json:\"end_line,omitempty\"`\n    Branch       string   `json:\"branch,omitempty\"`\n    SessionID    string   `json:\"session_id,omitempty\"`\n    Agent        string   `json:\"agent,omitempty\"`\n    CreatedAt    string   `json:\"created_at,omitempty\"`\n    Truncated    bool     `json:\"truncated,omitempty\"`\n    MatchedTerms []string `json:\"matched_terms,omitempty\"`\n    SessionRef   string   `json:\"session_ref,omitempty\"`\n    Concepts       []string       `json:\"concepts,omitempty\"`\n    ConceptMatches []conceptMatch `json:\"concept_matches,omitempty\"`\n    EvidenceIDs    []string       `json:\"evidence_ids,omitempty\"`\n    WorstRank         int  `json:\"worst_rank,omitempty\"`\n    RankSum           int  `json:\"rank_sum,omitempty\"`\n    Approximate       bool `json:\"approximate,omitempty\"`\n    ResponseTruncated bool `json:\"response_truncated,omitempty\"`\n}\n```\n\n### `brief --json` — **DOES NOT HAVE `results`**, has `facts` instead\nFlags (`agent_surface.go:649-681`): `--json`, `--limit int` (default 3), `--no-semantic`, `--profile-json string`, `--handoff`, `--sessions int` (default 5, only with `--handoff`).\n\nTop-level marshalled type is `brainBriefJSONReport` (`agent_surface.go:246-262`) — emitted via `writeJSON(cmd, brainBriefJSONProjection(report))`:\n```go\ntype brainBriefJSONReport struct {\n    GeneratedAt        time.Time                   `json:\"generated_at\"`\n    Task               string                      `json:\"task\"`\n    Status             brainStatusReport           `json:\"status\"`\n    Semantic           brainBriefJSONSemantic      `json:\"semantic\"`\n    History            brainBriefHistory           `json:\"history\"`\n    Conversation       []brainBriefConversationHit `json:\"conversation,omitempty\"`\n    Facts              []brainBriefJSONFact        `json:\"facts,omitempty\"`\n    FactsLocusDrift    map[string][]string         `json:\"facts_locus_drift,omitempty\"`\n    FactsPendingReview map[string]factReviewNotice `json:\"facts_pending_review,omitempty\"`\n    ActionChecklist    []brainBriefAction          `json:\"action_checklist,omitempty\"`\n    LikelyEditFiles    []string                    `json:\"likely_edit_files,omitempty\"`\n    LikelyTestFiles    []string                    `json:\"likely_test_files,omitempty\"`\n    LikelyFiles        []string                    `json:\"likely_files,omitempty\"`\n    Guidance           []string                    `json:\"guidance\"`\n    Warnings           []string                    `json:\"warnings,omitempty\"`\n}\n```\n**IMPORTANT for your bounder**: if it requires `{\"results\":[...]}`, only `search`/`vsearch`/`query` satisfy that natively. `brief` never emits a `results` key — you'd need to feed it `facts` (or map/rename) instead, or point the bounder at `search --json` output.\n\n## 5. Build — verified\n\n`cmd/entire-brain/main.go` is the ONLY entry point under `cmd/` (single dir `cmd/entire-brain/`, single file `main.go`). Confirmed:\n```\ngo build -o entire-brain ./cmd/entire-brain\n```\nBuilds clean, help output matches source for all commands checked (`search`, `brief`, `refresh history`, `distill`).\n\n## 6. Brain dir location / env vars — NOT a `--brain-dir` flag; NOT `ENTIRE_BRAIN_DIR`\n\n**No `--brain-dir` flag exists anywhere** (grepped all `.Flags()` calls; no persistent flags on root — `internal/cli/root.go` has zero `PersistentFlags()` calls).\n\nResolution chain (`internal/cli/env.go`):\n- Env vars, exact names: `ENTIRE_PLUGIN_CONFIG_DIR`, `ENTIRE_PLUGIN_DATA_DIR`, `ENTIRE_PLUGIN_STATE_DIR`, `ENTIRE_PLUGIN_CACHE_DIR` (`env.go:23-26`).\n- If `ENTIRE_PLUGIN_DATA_DIR` set: used verbatim as data root (must be absolute).\n- Else falls to `$XDG_DATA_HOME/entire` (if `XDG_DATA_HOME` set) else `~/.local/share/entire`, then (only when no host-supplied `PluginDataDir`) appends `/plugins/data/brain` (`pluginDataName = \"brain\"`, env.go:41,102).\n- Final **BrainDir** = `&lt;dataDir&gt;/repos/&lt;key&gt;` (`repoStoreDirName = \"repos\"`, `repoStorageForKey`, env.go:249-255) where `&lt;key&gt;` is derived from repo identity (path-based, resolved via `resolveRepoStorageIdentity`) — i.e. brainDir is per-repo, not directly settable to an arbitrary path via env/flag; you steer it only by controlling `ENTIRE_PLUGIN_DATA_DIR` + which repo path you pass.\n- `distill`, `refresh history`, etc. resolve `storage, err := repoStoragePaths(ctx, opts.Runner, opts.Env, repoDir)` then use `storage.BrainDir` — there is no per-command override flag.\n- `refresh` (top-level, not `refresh history`) DOES have `-o/--output string` (default `defaultExportDir`) but that's documented as \"(default: persistent brain directory)\" — an escape hatch to export to an arbitrary dir, separate from the canonical per-repo brainDir plumbing used by `distill`/`refresh history`/`search`/`brief`.\n\nFull default (typical dev machine, no env vars set): `~/.local/share/entire/plugins/data/brain/repos/&lt;key&gt;`.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>118446</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>44</tool_uses><duration_ms>229598</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"remove","timestamp":"2026-08-18T23:54:22.821Z","sessionId":"de272aad-c620-4d71-bbdd-27dd2d3dc8af","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>a4526f536919dc637</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>REDACTED</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-suhaan-devenv/f507d58c-285f-4d11-b1d0-201f2a5e172d/tasks/a4526f536919dc637.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Map entire-brain CLI + manifest schema\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result># ANSWERS — repo /Users/suhaan/devenv/p0p1/brainmark (all live-verified via `go build` + `--help`)\n\n## 1. MANIFEST SCHEMA\n\n`internal/cli/brain.go:12`\n```go\nconst brainManifestSchemaVersion = 3\n```\n\n`internal/cli/export.go:31-32` (filenames written into brainDir):\n```go\nexportManifestFileName = \"manifest.json\"\nexportReadmeFileName   = \"README.md\"\n```\n`writeBrainManifestAndReadme` (`internal/cli/brain.go:280`) writes exactly these two files, atomically, via `writeBrainRelativeFileAtomic(outputDir, exportManifestFileName, ...)` then same for README. JSON is `json.MarshalIndent(manifest, \"\", \"  \")` + trailing `\\n`, mode `0o600`.\n\n`exportManifest` (`internal/cli/export.go:3507-3522`):\n```go\ntype exportManifest struct {\n    SchemaVersion      int             `json:\"schema_version\"`\n    GeneratedAt        time.Time       `json:\"generated_at\"`\n    RepoRoot           string          `json:\"repo_root,omitempty\"`\n    RepoKey            string          `json:\"repo_key,omitempty\"`\n    EntireCLIVersion   string          `json:\"entire_cli_version,omitempty\"`\n    DefaultBranch      string          `json:\"default_branch,omitempty\"`\n    TranscriptMode     string          `json:\"transcript_mode\"`\n    Scope              string          `json:\"scope\"`\n    CheckpointLimit    int             `json:\"checkpoint_limit\"`\n    CheckpointsScanned int             `json:\"checkpoints_scanned\"`\n    Branches           []exportBranch  `json:\"branches,omitempty\"`\n    Sessions           []exportSession `json:\"sessions\"`\n    Warnings           []string        `json:\"warnings,omitempty\"`\n    Sources            *brainSources   `json:\"sources,omitempty\"`\n}\n```\n\n`exportSession` (`export.go:3531-3553`):\n```go\ntype exportSession struct {\n    SessionID            string                `json:\"session_id\"`\n    Branch               string                `json:\"branch,omitempty\"`\n    SourceBranch         string                `json:\"source_branch,omitempty\"`\n    Authors              []exportAuthor        `json:\"authors,omitempty\"`\n    Agent                string                `json:\"agent,omitempty\"`\n    Model                string                `json:\"model,omitempty\"`\n    Kind                 string                `json:\"kind,omitempty\"`\n    ReviewSkills         []string              `json:\"review_skills,omitempty\"`\n    LatestCheckpoint     string                `json:\"latest_checkpoint_id\"`\n    SessionIndex         int                   `json:\"session_index\"`\n    CreatedAt            time.Time             `json:\"created_at\"`\n    TurnID               string                `json:\"turn_id,omitempty\"`\n    IsTask                bool                 `json:\"is_task,omitempty\"`\n    ToolUseID            string                `json:\"tool_use_id,omitempty\"`\n    FilesTouched         []string              `json:\"files_touched,omitempty\"`\n    TokenUsage           *checkpointTokenUsage `json:\"token_usage,omitempty\"`\n    Summary              *checkpointSummary    `json:\"summary,omitempty\"`\n    CheckpointsCount     int                   `json:\"checkpoints_count,omitempty\"`\n    TranscriptPath       string                `json:\"transcript_path\"`\n    SourceTranscriptPath string                `json:\"-\"`  // NOT serialized\n    SourceKey            string                `json:\"-\"`  // NOT serialized\n}\n```\n(`exportBranch` at export.go:3524; `exportAuthor` at 3555 — Name/Email/Commits/LastCommitAt, all omitempty except none-tagged.)\n\n`brainSources` (`brain.go:22-30`):\n```go\ntype brainSources struct {\n    Seed     *seedSourceManifest     `json:\"seed,omitempty\"`\n    Sessions *sessionSourceManifest  `json:\"sessions,omitempty\"`\n    Semantic *semanticSourceManifest `json:\"semantic,omitempty\"`\n    History  *historySourceManifest  `json:\"history,omitempty\"`\n    Facts    *factSourceManifest     `json:\"facts,omitempty\"`\n    Docs     *docSourceManifest      `json:\"docs,omitempty\"`\n    Patterns *patternSourceManifest  `json:\"patterns,omitempty\"`\n}\n```\n\n`sessionSourceManifest` (`brain.go:32-45`):\n```go\ntype sessionSourceManifest struct {\n    GeneratedAt        time.Time       `json:\"generated_at\"`\n    EntireCLIVersion   string          `json:\"entire_cli_version,omitempty\"`\n    DefaultBranch      string          `json:\"default_branch,omitempty\"`\n    TranscriptMode     string          `json:\"transcript_mode\"`\n    Scope              string          `json:\"scope\"`\n    CheckpointLimit    int             `json:\"checkpoint_limit\"`\n    CheckpointsScanned int             `json:\"checkpoints_scanned\"`\n    OldestSessionAt    *time.Time      `json:\"oldest_session_at,omitempty\"`\n    LatestCheckpointID string          `json:\"latest_checkpoint_id,omitempty\"`\n    Branches           []exportBranch  `json:\"branches,omitempty\"`\n    Sessions           []exportSession `json:\"sessions\"`\n    Warnings           []string        `json:\"warnings,omitempty\"`\n}\n```\n(Sibling source manifests, in case needed: `seedSourceManifest` seed.go:67; `semanticSourceManifest` semantic.go:79; `historySourceManifest` history.go:71; `factSourceManifest` facts.go:32; `docSourceManifest` doc.go:29; `patternSourceManifest` episodes.go:40 — all read if you need them, ask.)\n\n**Time format**: plain `time.Time` fields, no custom `MarshalJSON` anywhere in `internal/cli` — encoded via Go stdlib default, i.e. RFC3339 with optional fractional-nanosecond digits, layout `\"2006-01-02T15:04:05.999999999Z07:00\"`. NOT written with a fixed `time.RFC3339` truncation for JSON fields (only used for human-text output like README/status lines). Write `\"...Z\"` for UTC-zero-fraction timestamps and it round-trips fine.\n\nFor a hand-written manifest to pass `writeBrainManifestAndReadme`'s own guard (`brain.go:287`, it calls `loadBrainManifest` first, which round-trips existing bytes through `decodeStrictVersionedJSON` and rejects `version &gt; brainManifestSchemaVersion` or `&lt; 0`), set `\"schema_version\": 3` (or omit — normalized to 1 if 0, but any writer resets it to 3 on save anyway).\n\n## 2. `entire-brain distill` (verified live via `--help`)\n\nPositional: `distill [path]` — optional repo dir arg (`Args: cobra.MaximumNArgs(1)`), defaults to `opts.Env.RepoRoot` else `.`. **Not** a brain-dir arg — it's the repo path; brainDir is derived (see §6).\n\nFlags (all confirmed):\n- `--dry-run` — bool, \"Estimate distill work without calling an agent or writing facts.\" When set, calls `buildDistillDryRunReportContext` and returns a `distillDryRunReport` (schema_version, generated_at, brain_path, branch, force, agent, model, effort, jobs, extraction_jobs_cap, max_chunk_bytes, confidence_threshold, sessions, cached_sessions, sessions_to_distill, missing_transcripts, raw_bytes, preprocessed_bytes, chunks, chunks_if_uncached, ...) — no agent invoked, no facts written.\n- `--agent string` (default `\"auto\"`) — allowed values: `auto | codex | claude-code | ollama | command | none`. `none` errors (\"distillation requires an agent\"). Exact switch is in `internal/cli/distill.go:106` `distillAgentCommandArgs`.\n- `--agent-command stringArray` — exact flag name is `--agent-command` (repeatable). **Required** when `--agent command`; errors \"`--agent-command is required when --agent command`\" if empty.\n- `--model string` — override model for codex/claude-code, or pick Ollama model.\n- `--effort string` — override reasoning effort for codex/claude-code.\n- `--branch`, `--session`, `--force`, `--json`, `--confidence float64` (default 0.75), `--concurrency int` (default 4), `--jobs int` (compat alias, conflicts if != concurrency), `--max-chunk-bytes int` (default 49152).\n- Output: facts written under `&lt;brainDir&gt;/facts/` (`factsDirName = \"facts\"` at `internal/cli/facts.go:20`), taxonomy at `&lt;brainDir&gt;/facts/taxonomy.json` (`factsTaxonomyPath = factsDirName + \"/\" + \"taxonomy.json\"`, facts.go:21-22). Fact-source summary recorded onto `manifest.Sources.Facts` (`factSourceManifest`) and manifest+README rewritten via `writeBrainManifestAndReadme`.\n- `--json` (non-dry-run) prints `json.MarshalIndent(source, \"\", \"  \")` where `source` is `*factSourceManifest`.\n\n## 3. `entire-brain refresh history` — verified live\n\n```\nentire-brain refresh history [path]\n```\n`internal/cli/history.go:250-267`, `newHistoryIndexCommand`. **No flags of its own** (only inherited `-h`). `Args: cobra.MaximumNArgs(1)`, same target resolution as distill (path = repo dir, default `.`/RepoRoot). Errors if target isn't a local path: `\"refresh history requires a local repository path: %s\"`.\n\nReads: exported session transcripts already on disk under the brain (built by `refresh sessions`/`export`). Writes: calls `writeBrainHistoryIndexAndSourceContext(ctx, storage.BrainDir, ...)` → decision/rationale history index (`historySourceManifest`, index file under brainDir, path reported by `source.IndexPath`, printed as `\"indexed %d history records: %s\\n\"`). Also runs history-vector backfill iff env var `ENTIRE_BRAIN_EMBEDDER` is set (opt-in).\n\nNote: `refresh` itself (`entire-brain refresh`, no subcommand) is the umbrella that runs sessions+seed+semantic+history+delta in sequence; `refresh history` is the standalone single-stage form. Sibling stages: `refresh` (export/sessions), `refresh index` (semantic), `refresh delta` (short-term memory), `refresh seed`.\n\n## 4. `entire-brain search` and `entire-brain brief` — verified live\n\n**Top-level commands, NOT nested under `brain`.** Both registered directly on root (`internal/cli/root.go:98,107`): `entire-brain search &lt;query&gt;`, `entire-brain brief &lt;task&gt; | brief --handoff`.\n\n### `search --json` (also applies to `vsearch`, `query` — same `newRetrieveCommand` factory, `internal/cli/retrieve_cmd.go:70-121`)\nFlags: `--json`, `--limit int` (default 10), `-n/--number int` (alias), `--format string` (`json`|`cli`), `--branch`, `--patterns`, `--source string` (`all|fact|history|conversation|doc`), `--after`, `--before`, `--session`, `--agent`, `--concept stringArray` (repeat, max 4), `--include-abstract`.\n\n**JSON shape DOES have `results`** (non-multi-concept path, `retrieve_cmd.go:238`):\n```go\nout := map[string]any{\n    \"query\": query, \"branch\": resolvedBranch,\n    \"results\": compactUnifiedResults(results, query),   // []compactUnifiedResult\n    // optional: \"abstract_previews\", \"abstract_previews_truncated\",\n    //           \"likely_edit_files\", \"likely_test_files\",\n    //           \"action_checklist\", \"related_patterns\", \"blind_spot\"\n}\n```\nPer-result struct `compactUnifiedResult` (`retrieve_cmd.go:17-56`):\n```go\ntype compactUnifiedResult struct {\n    Source  string `json:\"source\"`\n    ID      string `json:\"id\"`\n    Path    string `json:\"path,omitempty\"`\n    Heading string `json:\"heading,omitempty\"`\n    Line    int    `json:\"line,omitempty\"`\n    Text                 string            `json:\"text\"`\n    Excerpt              string            `json:\"excerpt,omitempty\"`\n    Score                float64           `json:\"score,omitempty\"`\n    VerificationRequired bool              `json:\"verification_required,omitempty\"`\n    Caveats              []retrievalCaveat `json:\"caveats,omitempty\"`\n    RelatedIDs           []string          `json:\"related_ids,omitempty\"`\n    EndLine      int      `json:\"end_line,omitempty\"`\n    Branch       string   `json:\"branch,omitempty\"`\n    SessionID    string   `json:\"session_id,omitempty\"`\n    Agent        string   `json:\"agent,omitempty\"`\n    CreatedAt    string   `json:\"created_at,omitempty\"`\n    Truncated    bool     `json:\"truncated,omitempty\"`\n    MatchedTerms []string `json:\"matched_terms,omitempty\"`\n    SessionRef   string   `json:\"session_ref,omitempty\"`\n    Concepts       []string       `json:\"concepts,omitempty\"`\n    ConceptMatches []conceptMatch `json:\"concept_matches,omitempty\"`\n    EvidenceIDs    []string       `json:\"evidence_ids,omitempty\"`\n    WorstRank         int  `json:\"worst_rank,omitempty\"`\n    RankSum           int  `json:\"rank_sum,omitempty\"`\n    Approximate       bool `json:\"approximate,omitempty\"`\n    ResponseTruncated bool `json:\"response_truncated,omitempty\"`\n}\n```\n\n### `brief --json` — **DOES NOT HAVE `results`**, has `facts` instead\nFlags (`agent_surface.go:649-681`): `--json`, `--limit int` (default 3), `--no-semantic`, `--profile-json string`, `--handoff`, `--sessions int` (default 5, only with `--handoff`).\n\nTop-level marshalled type is `brainBriefJSONReport` (`agent_surface.go:246-262`) — emitted via `writeJSON(cmd, brainBriefJSONProjection(report))`:\n```go\ntype brainBriefJSONReport struct {\n    GeneratedAt        time.Time                   `json:\"generated_at\"`\n    Task               string                      `json:\"task\"`\n    Status             brainStatusReport           `json:\"status\"`\n    Semantic           brainBriefJSONSemantic      `json:\"semantic\"`\n    History            brainBriefHistory           `json:\"history\"`\n    Conversation       []brainBriefConversationHit `json:\"conversation,omitempty\"`\n    Facts              []brainBriefJSONFact        `json:\"facts,omitempty\"`\n    FactsLocusDrift    map[string][]string         `json:\"facts_locus_drift,omitempty\"`\n    FactsPendingReview map[string]factReviewNotice `json:\"facts_pending_review,omitempty\"`\n    ActionChecklist    []brainBriefAction          `json:\"action_checklist,omitempty\"`\n    LikelyEditFiles    []string                    `json:\"likely_edit_files,omitempty\"`\n    LikelyTestFiles    []string                    `json:\"likely_test_files,omitempty\"`\n    LikelyFiles        []string                    `json:\"likely_files,omitempty\"`\n    Guidance           []string                    `json:\"guidance\"`\n    Warnings           []string                    `json:\"warnings,omitempty\"`\n}\n```\n**IMPORTANT for your bounder**: if it requires `{\"results\":[...]}`, only `search`/`vsearch`/`query` satisfy that natively. `brief` never emits a `results` key — you'd need to feed it `facts` (or map/rename) instead, or point the bounder at `search --json` output.\n\n## 5. Build — verified\n\n`cmd/entire-brain/main.go` is the ONLY entry point under `cmd/` (single dir `cmd/entire-brain/`, single file `main.go`). Confirmed:\n```\ngo build -o entire-brain ./cmd/entire-brain\n```\nBuilds clean, help output matches source for all commands checked (`search`, `brief`, `refresh history`, `distill`).\n\n## 6. Brain dir location / env vars — NOT a `--brain-dir` flag; NOT `ENTIRE_BRAIN_DIR`\n\n**No `--brain-dir` flag exists anywhere** (grepped all `.Flags()` calls; no persistent flags on root — `internal/cli/root.go` has zero `PersistentFlags()` calls).\n\nResolution chain (`internal/cli/env.go`):\n- Env vars, exact names: `ENTIRE_PLUGIN_CONFIG_DIR`, `ENTIRE_PLUGIN_DATA_DIR`, `ENTIRE_PLUGIN_STATE_DIR`, `ENTIRE_PLUGIN_CACHE_DIR` (`env.go:23-26`).\n- If `ENTIRE_PLUGIN_DATA_DIR` set: used verbatim as data root (must be absolute).\n- Else falls to `$XDG_DATA_HOME/entire` (if `XDG_DATA_HOME` set) else `~/.local/share/entire`, then (only when no host-supplied `PluginDataDir`) appends `/plugins/data/brain` (`pluginDataName = \"brain\"`, env.go:41,102).\n- Final **BrainDir** = `&lt;dataDir&gt;/repos/&lt;key&gt;` (`repoStoreDirName = \"repos\"`, `repoStorageForKey`, env.go:249-255) where `&lt;key&gt;` is derived from repo identity (path-based, resolved via `resolveRepoStorageIdentity`) — i.e. brainDir is per-repo, not directly settable to an arbitrary path via env/flag; you steer it only by controlling `ENTIRE_PLUGIN_DATA_DIR` + which repo path you pass.\n- `distill`, `refresh history`, etc. resolve `storage, err := repoStoragePaths(ctx, opts.Runner, opts.Env, repoDir)` then use `storage.BrainDir` — there is no per-command override flag.\n- `refresh` (top-level, not `refresh history`) DOES have `-o/--output string` (default `defaultExportDir`) but that's documented as \"(default: persistent brain directory)\" — an escape hatch to export to an arbitrary dir, separate from the canonical per-repo brainDir plumbing used by `distill`/`refresh history`/`search`/`brief`.\n\nFull default (typical dev machine, no env vars set): `~/.local/share/entire/plugins/data/brain/repos/&lt;key&gt;`.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>118446</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>44</tool_uses><duration_ms>229598</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
