{"parentUuid":"9c1834a2-6bdd-430d-b904-a74eeb05d8d2","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_011CeBBKRC9Cpp4rqzcGUGfe","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01RkozNq4Ku8F2z4ckpXdQYc","name":"WebSearch","input":{"query":"NeurIPS datasets benchmarks track common rejection reasons reviewer criteria benchmark paper"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3068,"cache_read_input_tokens":357977,"output_tokens":163,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3068,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":163,"cache_read_input_tokens":357977,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3068,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3068},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CeBBKMYNoSZZXRn2zzRUZ","type":"assistant","uuid":"b07731c1-1df4-4bf4-ab7c-5d422aa4d874","timestamp":"2026-08-19T00:42:14.785Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"f507d58c-285f-4d11-b1d0-201f2a5e172d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"de272aad-c620-4d71-bbdd-27dd2d3dc8af","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"quizzical-sniffing-quasar"}
{"parentUuid":"9c1834a2-6bdd-430d-b904-a74eeb05d8d2","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"d03804f5-4028-4a24-a2b9-46b62188e5f6","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TqQjphej8MUHG4tcGY8QUp","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"NeurIPS 2026 Datasets and Benchmarks track call for papers requirements checklist croissant\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"NeurIPS 2026 Evaluations & Datasets Track Call for Papers\",\"url\":\"https://neurips.cc/Conferences/2026/CallForEvaluationsDatasets\"},{\"title\":\"NeurIPS 2025 Datasets & Benchmarks Track Call for Papers\",\"url\":\"https://neurips.cc/Conferences/2025/CallForDatasetsBenchmarks\"},{\"title\":\"Croissant Baker: Metadata Generation for Discoverable, Governable, and Reusable ML Datasets\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2605.15079\"},{\"title\":\"NeurIPS Datasets & Benchmarks Track: From Art to Science in AI Evaluations – NeurIPS Blog\",\"url\":\"https://blog.neurips.cc/2025/12/05/neurips-datasets-benchmarks-track-from-art-to-science-in-ai-evaluations/\"},{\"title\":\"2026 Conference – NeurIPS Blog\",\"url\":\"https://blog.neurips.cc/category/2026-conference/\"},{\"title\":\"Responsible AI metadata requirements for the Evaluations and Datasets Track NeurIPS 2026 – NeurIPS Blog\",\"url\":\"https://blog.neurips.cc/2026/05/04/responsible-ai-metadata-requirements-for-the-evaluations-and-datasets-track-neurips-2026/\"},{\"title\":\"NeurIPS 2026 Evaluations & Datasets FAQ\",\"url\":\"https://neurips.cc/Conferences/2026/EvaluationsDatasetsFAQ\"},{\"title\":\"NeurIPS 2026 Evaluations & Datasets Hosting Guidelines\",\"url\":\"https://neurips.cc/Conferences/2026/EvaluationsDatasetsHosting\"},{\"title\":\"Introducing the Evaluations & Datasets Track at NeurIPS 2026 – NeurIPS Blog\",\"url\":\"https://blog.neurips.cc/2026/03/23/introducing-the-evaluations-datasets-track-at-neurips-2026/\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here are the key requirements and checklist items for the NeurIPS 2026 Evaluations & Datasets Track regarding Croissant and other submission requirements:\n\n## Croissant File Requirements\n\nDataset submissions are required to include a Croissant file, a standardized, machine-readable metadata format for describing datasets and their structure. Specifically:\n\n- You should submit a Croissant file for every dataset (and check whether they are all valid).\n- You can combine the .json files into a .zip folder and upload that during submission.\n\n## Responsible AI (RAI) Metadata\n\nAll dataset submissions must now include Responsible AI (RAI) metadata as part of the dataset's Croissant file. All submissions that include a dataset as a contribution must provide answers to these RAI fields, at least in the Croissant file.\n\n## Data Availability Requirements\n\nBenchmarks or datasets that include a collection of new or existing datasets must also ensure that the underlying datasets are compliant with the same guidelines (eg, availability, croissant files, etc.) All accepted papers must have their code and datasets documented and publicly available by the camera-ready deadline.\n\n## Code Release Policy\n\nCode release is required at submission when the primary contribution is a reusable executable artifact, such as a benchmark suite, evaluation environment, data generator, or software tool, whose functionality must be inspected in order to evaluate the scientific claims.\n\n## Validation and Desk Rejection\n\nAfter submissions are closed, if your Croissant file is invalid or if your data is not accessible, your submission may be desk-rejected.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"22c456df-380a-4d75-bbda-834e59a5891d","timestamp":"2026-08-19T00:42:22.114Z","toolUseResult":{"query":"NeurIPS 2026 Datasets and Benchmarks track call for papers requirements checklist croissant","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01UZUMqbJDp7ghoPsQR71z2d","content":[{"title":"NeurIPS 2026 Evaluations & Datasets Track Call for Papers","url":"https://neurips.cc/Conferences/2026/CallForEvaluationsDatasets"},{"title":"NeurIPS 2025 Datasets & Benchmarks Track Call for Papers","url":"https://neurips.cc/Conferences/2025/CallForDatasetsBenchmarks"},{"title":"Croissant Baker: Metadata Generation for Discoverable, Governable, and Reusable ML Datasets","url":"https://arxiv.org/pdf/2605.15079"},{"title":"NeurIPS Datasets & Benchmarks Track: From Art to Science in AI Evaluations – NeurIPS Blog","url":"https://blog.neurips.cc/2025/12/05/neurips-datasets-benchmarks-track-from-art-to-science-in-ai-evaluations/"},{"title":"2026 Conference – NeurIPS Blog","url":"https://blog.neurips.cc/category/2026-conference/"},{"title":"Responsible AI metadata requirements for the Evaluations and Datasets Track NeurIPS 2026 – NeurIPS Blog","url":"https://blog.neurips.cc/2026/05/04/responsible-ai-metadata-requirements-for-the-evaluations-and-datasets-track-neurips-2026/"},{"title":"NeurIPS 2026 Evaluations & Datasets FAQ","url":"https://neurips.cc/Conferences/2026/EvaluationsDatasetsFAQ"},{"title":"NeurIPS 2026 Evaluations & Datasets Hosting Guidelines","url":"https://neurips.cc/Conferences/2026/EvaluationsDatasetsHosting"},{"title":"Introducing the Evaluations & Datasets Track at NeurIPS 2026 – NeurIPS Blog","url":"https://blog.neurips.cc/2026/03/23/introducing-the-evaluations-datasets-track-at-neurips-2026/"}]},"Based on the search results, here are the key requirements and checklist items for the NeurIPS 2026 Evaluations & Datasets Track regarding Croissant and other submission requirements:\n\n## Croissant File Requirements\n\nDataset submissions are required to include a Croissant file, a standardized, machine-readable metadata format for describing datasets and their structure. Specifically:\n\n- You should submit a Croissant file for every dataset (and check whether they are all valid).\n- You can combine the .json files into a .zip folder and upload that during submission.\n\n## Responsible AI (RAI) Metadata\n\nAll dataset submissions must now include Responsible AI (RAI) metadata as part of the dataset's Croissant file. All submissions that include a dataset as a contribution must provide answers to these RAI fields, at least in the Croissant file.\n\n## Data Availability Requirements\n\nBenchmarks or datasets that include a collection of new or existing datasets must also ensure that the underlying datasets are compliant with the same guidelines (eg, availability, croissant files, etc.) All accepted papers must have their code and datasets documented and publicly available by the camera-ready deadline.\n\n## Code Release Policy\n\nCode release is required at submission when the primary contribution is a reusable executable artifact, such as a benchmark suite, evaluation environment, data generator, or software tool, whose functionality must be inspected in order to evaluate the scientific claims.\n\n## Validation and Desk Rejection\n\nAfter submissions are closed, if your Croissant file is invalid or if your data is not accessible, your submission may be desk-rejected."],"durationSeconds":7.658705458015204,"searchCount":1},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"9c1834a2-6bdd-430d-b904-a74eeb05d8d2","session_id":"f507d58c-285f-4d11-b1d0-201f2a5e172d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"de272aad-c620-4d71-bbdd-27dd2d3dc8af","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"quizzical-sniffing-quasar"}
{"parentUuid":"b07731c1-1df4-4bf4-ab7c-5d422aa4d874","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"d03804f5-4028-4a24-a2b9-46b62188e5f6","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01RkozNq4Ku8F2z4ckpXdQYc","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"NeurIPS datasets benchmarks track common rejection reasons reviewer criteria benchmark paper\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"NeurIPS Datasets & Benchmarks Track: From Art to Science in AI Evaluations – NeurIPS Blog\",\"url\":\"https://blog.neurips.cc/2025/12/05/neurips-datasets-benchmarks-track-from-art-to-science-in-ai-evaluations/\"},{\"title\":\"Evaluations and Datasets 2026 Reviewing Guidelines\",\"url\":\"https://neurips.cc/Conferences/2026/EvaluationsDatasetsReviewerGuidelines\"},{\"title\":\"NeurIPS 2025 Datasets & Benchmarks Track Call for Papers\",\"url\":\"https://neurips.cc/Conferences/2025/CallForDatasetsBenchmarks\"},{\"title\":\"NeurIPS 2025 Statistics: Datasets & Benchmarks Track - Paper Copilot\",\"url\":\"https://papercopilot.com/statistics/neurips-statistics/neurips-2025-statistics-datasets-benchmarks-track/\"},{\"title\":\"Call For Datasets & Benchmarks 2024\",\"url\":\"https://neurips.cc/Conferences/2024/CallForDatasetsBenchmarks\"},{\"title\":\"Reflecting on the 2025 Review Process from the Datasets and Benchmarks Chairs – NeurIPS Blog\",\"url\":\"https://blog.neurips.cc/2025/09/30/reflecting-on-the-2025-review-process-from-the-datasets-and-benchmarks-chairs/\"},{\"title\":\"Introducing the Evaluations & Datasets Track at NeurIPS 2026 – NeurIPS Blog\",\"url\":\"https://blog.neurips.cc/2026/03/23/introducing-the-evaluations-datasets-track-at-neurips-2026/\"},{\"title\":\"NeurIPS 2026 Reviewing Guidelines\",\"url\":\"https://neurips.cc/Conferences/2026/ReviewerGuidelines\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found comprehensive information about NeurIPS Datasets & Benchmarks track reviewer criteria and common rejection reasons:\n\n## Reviewer Criteria\n\nFor the 2026 E&D Track, reviewers are asked to evaluate submissions along the core NeurIPS dimensions — Quality, Clarity, Significance, and Originality. Additionally, the E&D Track places particular emphasis on responsible data practices, transparency, and reproducibility.\n\n## Common Issues and Rejection Reasons\n\nSeveral key issues emerge from the review process:\n\n1. **Documentation and Metadata Requirements**: Missing fields included license information (11.9 percent), dataset descriptions (4.9 percent) and URLs (3.5 percent).\n\n2. **Hosting and Accessibility Issues**: New datasets should be hosted at one of the hosting sites dedicated to ML datasets, data should be found and obtained without a personal request to the PI, and non-compliance justifies the desk rejection of the paper.\n\n3. **Scope and Problem Formulation**: Papers that present data without clarifying the intended problem formulation, evaluation setup, or interpretive boundaries are unlikely to provide sufficient context for review; simply releasing a large collection of data without specifying the problem setting it addresses would not provide a sufficient basis for review.\n\n4. **Reviewer Concerns**: Concerns included limited reviewer engagement in rebuttals, reliance on AI-generated feedback and emphasis on methodological novelty over real-world impact.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"a6060869-fda4-44d7-bfc1-4d10b04e319a","timestamp":"2026-08-19T00:42:22.116Z","toolUseResult":{"query":"NeurIPS datasets benchmarks track common rejection reasons reviewer criteria benchmark paper","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01Gak5Nvqp2UXqZ3So7eVveQ","content":[{"title":"NeurIPS Datasets & Benchmarks Track: From Art to Science in AI Evaluations – NeurIPS Blog","url":"https://blog.neurips.cc/2025/12/05/neurips-datasets-benchmarks-track-from-art-to-science-in-ai-evaluations/"},{"title":"Evaluations and Datasets 2026 Reviewing Guidelines","url":"https://neurips.cc/Conferences/2026/EvaluationsDatasetsReviewerGuidelines"},{"title":"NeurIPS 2025 Datasets & Benchmarks Track Call for Papers","url":"https://neurips.cc/Conferences/2025/CallForDatasetsBenchmarks"},{"title":"NeurIPS 2025 Statistics: Datasets & Benchmarks Track - Paper Copilot","url":"https://papercopilot.com/statistics/neurips-statistics/neurips-2025-statistics-datasets-benchmarks-track/"},{"title":"Call For Datasets & Benchmarks 2024","url":"https://neurips.cc/Conferences/2024/CallForDatasetsBenchmarks"},{"title":"Reflecting on the 2025 Review Process from the Datasets and Benchmarks Chairs – NeurIPS Blog","url":"https://blog.neurips.cc/2025/09/30/reflecting-on-the-2025-review-process-from-the-datasets-and-benchmarks-chairs/"},{"title":"Introducing the Evaluations & Datasets Track at NeurIPS 2026 – NeurIPS Blog","url":"https://blog.neurips.cc/2026/03/23/introducing-the-evaluations-datasets-track-at-neurips-2026/"},{"title":"NeurIPS 2026 Reviewing Guidelines","url":"https://neurips.cc/Conferences/2026/ReviewerGuidelines"}]},"Based on the search results, I found comprehensive information about NeurIPS Datasets & Benchmarks track reviewer criteria and common rejection reasons:\n\n## Reviewer Criteria\n\nFor the 2026 E&D Track, reviewers are asked to evaluate submissions along the core NeurIPS dimensions — Quality, Clarity, Significance, and Originality. Additionally, the E&D Track places particular emphasis on responsible data practices, transparency, and reproducibility.\n\n## Common Issues and Rejection Reasons\n\nSeveral key issues emerge from the review process:\n\n1. **Documentation and Metadata Requirements**: Missing fields included license information (11.9 percent), dataset descriptions (4.9 percent) and URLs (3.5 percent).\n\n2. **Hosting and Accessibility Issues**: New datasets should be hosted at one of the hosting sites dedicated to ML datasets, data should be found and obtained without a personal request to the PI, and non-compliance justifies the desk rejection of the paper.\n\n3. **Scope and Problem Formulation**: Papers that present data without clarifying the intended problem formulation, evaluation setup, or interpretive boundaries are unlikely to provide sufficient context for review; simply releasing a large collection of data without specifying the problem setting it addresses would not provide a sufficient basis for review.\n\n4. **Reviewer Concerns**: Concerns included limited reviewer engagement in rebuttals, reliance on AI-generated feedback and emphasis on methodological novelty over real-world impact."],"durationSeconds":7.330204291015863,"searchCount":1},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"b07731c1-1df4-4bf4-ab7c-5d422aa4d874","session_id":"f507d58c-285f-4d11-b1d0-201f2a5e172d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"de272aad-c620-4d71-bbdd-27dd2d3dc8af","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"quizzical-sniffing-quasar"}
