{"parentUuid":"4e9b36b5-e1f7-4f32-bc39-1e94831059be","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_011CeBBLGKd4VcchBKZKbUsR","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01JWHusPi5Ho3vF92p5yoo9M","name":"WebFetch","input":{"url":"https://neurips.cc/Conferences/2026/EvaluationsDatasetsReviewerGuidelines","prompt":"Extract the full list of review criteria and questions reviewers must answer for the NeurIPS 2026 Evaluations & Datasets track: quality dimensions, required artifacts (croissant, hosting, license, code), statistical/rigor expectations, what makes a submission strong vs weak, any scoring rubric. Be exhaustive and concrete."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2808,"cache_read_input_tokens":361045,"output_tokens":704,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":270},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2808,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":704,"cache_read_input_tokens":361045,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2808,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2808},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CeBBLBtEERtwvbiADZwJD","type":"assistant","uuid":"a36ff1fa-a8aa-4bab-9e15-af1950188582","timestamp":"2026-08-19T00:42:31.427Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"f507d58c-285f-4d11-b1d0-201f2a5e172d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"de272aad-c620-4d71-bbdd-27dd2d3dc8af","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"quizzical-sniffing-quasar"}
{"parentUuid":"a36ff1fa-a8aa-4bab-9e15-af1950188582","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_011CeBBLGKd4VcchBKZKbUsR","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01S5tbWPcgZ1nWwkZwoYCmPj","name":"WebFetch","input":{"url":"https://blog.neurips.cc/2025/12/05/neurips-datasets-benchmarks-track-from-art-to-science-in-ai-evaluations/","prompt":"Summarize what the NeurIPS chairs say makes AI evaluation/benchmark papers scientific rather than art: statistical rigor expectations, uncertainty quantification, construct validity, contamination, what they want future benchmark submissions to include. Concrete and exhaustive."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2808,"cache_read_input_tokens":361045,"output_tokens":704,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":270},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2808,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":704,"cache_read_input_tokens":361045,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2808,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2808},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CeBBLBtEERtwvbiADZwJD","type":"assistant","uuid":"0baa07ca-2146-4eb4-8fb6-461a2899ed6d","timestamp":"2026-08-19T00:42:32.815Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"f507d58c-285f-4d11-b1d0-201f2a5e172d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"de272aad-c620-4d71-bbdd-27dd2d3dc8af","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"quizzical-sniffing-quasar"}
{"parentUuid":"0baa07ca-2146-4eb4-8fb6-461a2899ed6d","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"d03804f5-4028-4a24-a2b9-46b62188e5f6","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01S5tbWPcgZ1nWwkZwoYCmPj","type":"tool_result","content":"# What Makes AI Evaluation \"Science\" Not \"Art\" According to NeurIPS Chairs\n\nBased on the provided content, the NeurIPS organizers do **not explicitly define** what transforms benchmark evaluation from art to science using the specific frameworks you mentioned (statistical rigor, uncertainty quantification, construct validity, contamination).\n\nInstead, the article emphasizes **infrastructure and standardization** as the path to scientific rigor:\n\n**Current Focus:**\n- Mandatory hosting on persistent repositories with machine-readable metadata (Croissant)\n- Automated compliance checklists and standardized dataset summaries\n- Required licensing documentation and dataset descriptions\n- \"Datasets remain verifiable, accessible, and scientifically impactful over time\"\n\n**Identified Gaps Requiring Development:**\nThe organizers acknowledge that evaluating dataset impact remains underdeveloped. They note: \"dataset and benchmark impact depends on enabling future research\" and propose that \"future iterations could consider requiring a 'demonstrated impact' section\" mapping dataset characteristics to evaluation results.\n\n**The Real Limitation:**\nThe article reveals the track is still \"in a learning phase\" establishing norms for data-centric research evaluation. The organizers have prioritized *reproducibility infrastructure* over defining the *epistemological standards* that distinguish rigorous benchmarking from subjective assessment.\n\nThe \"art to science\" framing in the title is not substantively developed in the content provided."}]},"uuid":"7ea48587-a49f-4ef1-ad50-07e2f4a98d1e","timestamp":"2026-08-19T00:42:38.376Z","toolUseResult":{"bytes":62163,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# What Makes AI Evaluation \"Science\" Not \"Art\" According to NeurIPS Chairs\n\nBased on the provided content, the NeurIPS organizers do **not explicitly define** what transforms benchmark evaluation from art to science using the specific frameworks you mentioned (statistical rigor, uncertainty quantification, construct validity, contamination).\n\nInstead, the article emphasizes **infrastructure and standardization** as the path to scientific rigor:\n\n**Current Focus:**\n- Mandatory hosting on persistent repositories with machine-readable metadata (Croissant)\n- Automated compliance checklists and standardized dataset summaries\n- Required licensing documentation and dataset descriptions\n- \"Datasets remain verifiable, accessible, and scientifically impactful over time\"\n\n**Identified Gaps Requiring Development:**\nThe organizers acknowledge that evaluating dataset impact remains underdeveloped. They note: \"dataset and benchmark impact depends on enabling future research\" and propose that \"future iterations could consider requiring a 'demonstrated impact' section\" mapping dataset characteristics to evaluation results.\n\n**The Real Limitation:**\nThe article reveals the track is still \"in a learning phase\" establishing norms for data-centric research evaluation. The organizers have prioritized *reproducibility infrastructure* over defining the *epistemological standards* that distinguish rigorous benchmarking from subjective assessment.\n\nThe \"art to science\" framing in the title is not substantively developed in the content provided.","durationMs":5558,"url":"https://blog.neurips.cc/2025/12/05/neurips-datasets-benchmarks-track-from-art-to-science-in-ai-evaluations/"},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"0baa07ca-2146-4eb4-8fb6-461a2899ed6d","session_id":"f507d58c-285f-4d11-b1d0-201f2a5e172d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"de272aad-c620-4d71-bbdd-27dd2d3dc8af","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"quizzical-sniffing-quasar"}
