{"type":"bridge-session","sessionId":"de272aad-c620-4d71-bbdd-27dd2d3dc8af","bridgeSessionId":"cse_01Y3eBMHxH1unhhR8ZVDY52y","lastSequenceNum":0,"ownerAccountUuid":"1adeeb49-de49-49d0-b362-b9b5f0bc27ed","ownerOrganizationUuid":"46041b3e-8c7e-4659-a2cb-1751292663c4"}
{"parentUuid":"a36ff1fa-a8aa-4bab-9e15-af1950188582","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"d03804f5-4028-4a24-a2b9-46b62188e5f6","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JWHusPi5Ho3vF92p5yoo9M","type":"tool_result","content":"# NeurIPS 2026 Evaluations & Datasets Review Criteria\n\n## Core Review Dimensions\n\nReviewers must evaluate submissions across four criteria, interpreted contextually by contribution type:\n\n1. **Quality**: \"Is the submission technically sound, and are the claims well-supported by empirical, analytical, or conceptual arguments?\"\n2. **Clarity**: \"Is the submission clearly written, well-organized, and detailed enough to enable reproducibility?\"\n3. **Significance**: \"Are the results impactful for the community? Does it advance our understanding of AI evaluation?\"\n4. **Originality**: \"Does the work provide new insights, deepen understanding, or highlight important properties of existing methods?\"\n\n## Mandatory Artifact Requirements\n\n### Datasets\n- **Croissant metadata**: \"All submissions that contribute datasets are required to provide a valid Croissant file\"\n- **Responsible AI metadata**: Documentation must address data limitations, biases, personal/sensitive information, intended uses, and social impact\n- **Accessibility**: \"Datasets should be available to all reviewers...at the time of submission, and without a personal request\"\n- **Double-blind**: Required unless justified single-blind (e.g., de-anonymization unfeasible)\n\n### Code/Executable Artifacts\n- **Mandatory for tools**: \"If the primary contribution is a reusable executable artifact...code release is mandatory\"\n- **Code URL required**: Must be accessible, executable, anonymized, and properly documented\n- **Encouraged for analytical work**: Code justification field required if omitted\n- **Assessment criterion**: \"Does the paper provide enough detail for you to meaningfully assess validity without code?\"\n\n## Rigor & Statistical Expectations\n\nFor **Evaluation Methodology and Metrics** contributions:\n- \"Assess the statistical soundness, rigor, and validity of proposed evaluation protocols or metrics\"\n- \"Does [the methodology] shift conclusions if applied to existing benchmarks?\"\n\nFor **Reproducibility/Auditing** submissions:\n- \"Findings must be grounded in rigorous, systematic analysis — not superficial observations\"\n- \"If a negative result: is it deep and carefully controlled?\"\n\nFor **Human-Centered Evaluation**:\n- \"Verify that human subject research protocols were followed (e.g., fair wages, IRB accreditation)\"\n- Confirmation of \"fair compensation for all participants\" required\n\n## Contribution-Type Specific Strengths\n\n| Type | Strong Papers Demonstrate |\n|------|--------------------------|\n| **Datasets** | \"Data domain, task coverage, or data collection methodology that enables new evaluative claims\" |\n| **Benchmarks** | Rigor in task design; ability to \"change how we measure progress in this area\" |\n| **Metrics** | Validity advances; \"novel metrics or...different evaluation assumptions lead to different scientific conclusions\" |\n| **Tools** | \"Addresses a genuine gap in the evaluation ecosystem and has potential for broad adoption\" |\n| **Auditing** | \"Meaningful insights about the robustness or limitations of existing evaluations\" |\n| **Human-Centered** | Novel methodologies for \"human-AI interaction, safety, or human evaluation methodology\" |\n\n## Common Weaknesses to Flag\n\n- Missing or placeholder Croissant files → escalate to Area Chair\n- Inaccessible datasets requiring PI request → denied\n- Anonymization violations in tools/methods papers\n- Code unavailability without justified explanation\n- Datasets presented as \"endpoints\" without clear evaluative purpose\n- Incomplete RAI metadata\n- Non-rigorous empirical claims\n\n## Key Reviewing Expectations\n\n- \"Superficial, uninformed reviews without evidence are worse than no review\"\n- Avoid personal language; \"please keep in mind that...reviews...will be made public\"\n- \"Make an effort to update your understanding of the paper when new information is presented\" during author discussion\n- \"Participation in discussions is a critical part of your role\"\n\n## No Scoring Rubric Provided\n\nThe document establishes dimension-based evaluation rather than numerical scoring guidance."}]},"uuid":"c3336a98-8d27-49a8-a6d6-0b7adba0d286","timestamp":"2026-08-19T00:42:46.138Z","toolUseResult":{"bytes":100574,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# NeurIPS 2026 Evaluations & Datasets Review Criteria\n\n## Core Review Dimensions\n\nReviewers must evaluate submissions across four criteria, interpreted contextually by contribution type:\n\n1. **Quality**: \"Is the submission technically sound, and are the claims well-supported by empirical, analytical, or conceptual arguments?\"\n2. **Clarity**: \"Is the submission clearly written, well-organized, and detailed enough to enable reproducibility?\"\n3. **Significance**: \"Are the results impactful for the community? Does it advance our understanding of AI evaluation?\"\n4. **Originality**: \"Does the work provide new insights, deepen understanding, or highlight important properties of existing methods?\"\n\n## Mandatory Artifact Requirements\n\n### Datasets\n- **Croissant metadata**: \"All submissions that contribute datasets are required to provide a valid Croissant file\"\n- **Responsible AI metadata**: Documentation must address data limitations, biases, personal/sensitive information, intended uses, and social impact\n- **Accessibility**: \"Datasets should be available to all reviewers...at the time of submission, and without a personal request\"\n- **Double-blind**: Required unless justified single-blind (e.g., de-anonymization unfeasible)\n\n### Code/Executable Artifacts\n- **Mandatory for tools**: \"If the primary contribution is a reusable executable artifact...code release is mandatory\"\n- **Code URL required**: Must be accessible, executable, anonymized, and properly documented\n- **Encouraged for analytical work**: Code justification field required if omitted\n- **Assessment criterion**: \"Does the paper provide enough detail for you to meaningfully assess validity without code?\"\n\n## Rigor & Statistical Expectations\n\nFor **Evaluation Methodology and Metrics** contributions:\n- \"Assess the statistical soundness, rigor, and validity of proposed evaluation protocols or metrics\"\n- \"Does [the methodology] shift conclusions if applied to existing benchmarks?\"\n\nFor **Reproducibility/Auditing** submissions:\n- \"Findings must be grounded in rigorous, systematic analysis — not superficial observations\"\n- \"If a negative result: is it deep and carefully controlled?\"\n\nFor **Human-Centered Evaluation**:\n- \"Verify that human subject research protocols were followed (e.g., fair wages, IRB accreditation)\"\n- Confirmation of \"fair compensation for all participants\" required\n\n## Contribution-Type Specific Strengths\n\n| Type | Strong Papers Demonstrate |\n|------|--------------------------|\n| **Datasets** | \"Data domain, task coverage, or data collection methodology that enables new evaluative claims\" |\n| **Benchmarks** | Rigor in task design; ability to \"change how we measure progress in this area\" |\n| **Metrics** | Validity advances; \"novel metrics or...different evaluation assumptions lead to different scientific conclusions\" |\n| **Tools** | \"Addresses a genuine gap in the evaluation ecosystem and has potential for broad adoption\" |\n| **Auditing** | \"Meaningful insights about the robustness or limitations of existing evaluations\" |\n| **Human-Centered** | Novel methodologies for \"human-AI interaction, safety, or human evaluation methodology\" |\n\n## Common Weaknesses to Flag\n\n- Missing or placeholder Croissant files → escalate to Area Chair\n- Inaccessible datasets requiring PI request → denied\n- Anonymization violations in tools/methods papers\n- Code unavailability without justified explanation\n- Datasets presented as \"endpoints\" without clear evaluative purpose\n- Incomplete RAI metadata\n- Non-rigorous empirical claims\n\n## Key Reviewing Expectations\n\n- \"Superficial, uninformed reviews without evidence are worse than no review\"\n- Avoid personal language; \"please keep in mind that...reviews...will be made public\"\n- \"Make an effort to update your understanding of the paper when new information is presented\" during author discussion\n- \"Participation in discussions is a critical part of your role\"\n\n## No Scoring Rubric Provided\n\nThe document establishes dimension-based evaluation rather than numerical scoring guidance.","durationMs":14706,"url":"https://neurips.cc/Conferences/2026/EvaluationsDatasetsReviewerGuidelines"},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"a36ff1fa-a8aa-4bab-9e15-af1950188582","session_id":"f507d58c-285f-4d11-b1d0-201f2a5e172d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"de272aad-c620-4d71-bbdd-27dd2d3dc8af","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"quizzical-sniffing-quasar"}
