{"parentUuid":"36fe31d6-9227-461b-bacd-8052ef9d2ac5","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_011CeBBN4N6FjwTBcmmrxVpZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2685,"cache_read_input_tokens":363853,"output_tokens":2907,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":682},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2685,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2907,"cache_read_input_tokens":363853,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2685,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2685},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CeBBMxxuNiynDtwbH41Ka","type":"assistant","uuid":"21b5564a-5c6d-49a3-b957-5d94b4852eaa","timestamp":"2026-08-19T00:43:02.150Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"f507d58c-285f-4d11-b1d0-201f2a5e172d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"de272aad-c620-4d71-bbdd-27dd2d3dc8af","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"quizzical-sniffing-quasar"}
{"parentUuid":"21b5564a-5c6d-49a3-b957-5d94b4852eaa","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_011CeBBN4N6FjwTBcmmrxVpZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01BZiQgrM1drJz7XFzH1pNc7","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Design NeurIPS-grade upgrade plan","subagent_type":"Plan","prompt":"You are designing the gap-closure plan that takes BrainMark (an A→B cross-session memory benchmark for coding agents) from its current state to unambiguous NeurIPS Evaluations & Datasets–track accept-grade rigor. READ the current plan first: /Users/suhaan/.claude/plans/quizzical-sniffing-quasar.md. Also read /Users/suhaan/devenv/p0p1/brainmark/benchmarks/agent-brain/brainmark/README.md and PREREGISTRATION.md and DATASHEET.md if they exist (the $0 harness is already built: miner, seal, 5 arms (no_brain/full_brain/mem0/graphify/cmm), symmetry gates, mechanism metric locate_calls_pre_edit, vendored bootstrap stats, 55 offline tests).\n\nCURRENT STATE FACTS:\n- Task pool: only 303 SWE-bench instances (graphmark's local task JSONs) → 15 verified pairs now, ~83 after repo clones finish. Full SWE-bench has 2,294 (python) + SWE-bench Multimodal/Multilingual/Verified pools; full-scale mining has NOT been attempted.\n- Single agent driver wired (claude -p); codex MCP wiring exists in the parent harness (run.py:6835).\n- Seal = single human review; no inter-rater protocol yet.\n- Primary metric is pre-registered but not construct-validated.\n- No contamination treatment: A/B tasks are public SWE-bench (in model training data) — a memorization confound reviewers WILL raise.\n\nNEURIPS 2026 E&D TRACK REQUIREMENTS (fetched from neurips.cc today — treat as binding):\n- Valid Croissant file + Responsible AI metadata for every contributed dataset; desk-reject if invalid/inaccessible; hosting on persistent ML-dataset repositories, accessible to reviewers without personal request; license documentation.\n- Code release MANDATORY AT SUBMISSION for reusable executable artifacts (benchmark suites): accessible, executable, ANONYMIZED, documented.\n- Double-blind by default → the released harness/dataset must be anonymizable (no entire-brain branding in the submitted artifact!).\n- Review dimensions: Quality (claims well-supported), Clarity (reproducible detail), Significance (\"does it change how we measure progress\"), Originality. Benchmarks judged on task-design rigor.\n- Reviewer red flags: datasets as endpoints without evaluative purpose, non-rigorous empirical claims, placeholder metadata.\n\nEXPERT GAP LIST TO FOLD IN (address every item; add your own):\n1. SCALE + POWER: n≈30-80 pairs is weak. Design full-pool mining (all SWE-bench variants + multilingual) targeting 150-300 sealed pairs; a power analysis from pilot variance choosing final n; justify n statistically in the paper.\n2. CONTAMINATION: (a) discussion + per-repo breakdowns; (b) a post-training-cutoff FRESH pair subset (SWE-rebench-style mining of recent PRs, or SWE-bench-verified date filtering) as a robustness split; (c) argue why the PAIRED design partially controls memorization (both arms see the same B task; memory delta is the measurand) — but verify this argument holds.\n3. GENERALITY: ≥2 agent backends (claude + codex/gpt-5.6-terra via Azure; the run.py codex wiring exists) and ≥2 reps per cell or a variance-decomposition justification (we have prior evidence run-level noise dominates instance identity).\n4. CONSTRUCT VALIDITY of locate_calls_pre_edit: human-label a sample (~30 B sessions) for \"re-derivation of session-A knowledge\", report correlation; pre-register the validation protocol.\n5. SEAL PROTOCOL: 2 independent raters + Cohen's kappa + documented criteria + adjudication; raters cannot be the harness authors ideally (or disclose).\n6. CONTROLS: add an exploratory \"irrelevant-memory\" control arm (packet from an UNRELATED session A, same size) — distinguishes relevant-memory value from placebo-context effects; null test already planned.\n7. BASELINE DIGNITY: competitor best-config protocol — document each competitor's config selection procedure (their published defaults + one tuning pass on dev split only), pin versions.\n8. ARTIFACTS: croissant + RAI metadata generation script; anonymized release repo (\"BrainMark\" neutral naming, memory systems as pluggable adapters); HF dataset hosting; Zenodo DOI; maintenance/versioning policy; leaderboard plan; MIT licensing chain (SWE-bench is MIT — verify each pool's license).\n9. PAPER SKELETON: contributions framing (first sealed cross-session memory-utility benchmark for coding agents + mechanism metric + N-system comparison), related-work map (LoCoMo, LongMemEval, mem0/Letta evals, SWE-bench family, agent-memory surveys), limitations, ethics, compute disclosure, NeurIPS checklist pass.\n10. TIMELINE/BUDGET: NeurIPS 2027 submission (abstract ~May 2027). Phase the spend: current pilot ladder unchanged; full-scale runs sized for the bigger n and 2 backends — estimate honestly (cheap-model tier vs Opus tier).\n\nOUTPUT: a concrete phased implementation plan (what to build/change in the brainmark/ tree, what new scripts/docs, what runs, what human protocols), each phase with cost + wall-clock + owner (agent-automatable vs needs-human), ordered so $0 items front-load. Include a Verification section (how we know each gap is closed) and an honest \"residual acceptance risks we cannot engineer away\" list. Max ~110 dense lines."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2685,"cache_read_input_tokens":363853,"output_tokens":2907,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":682},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2685,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2907,"cache_read_input_tokens":363853,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2685,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2685},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CeBBMxxuNiynDtwbH41Ka","type":"assistant","uuid":"645c25ee-dbf0-44a8-9af5-874c975eb05f","timestamp":"2026-08-19T00:43:33.483Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"f507d58c-285f-4d11-b1d0-201f2a5e172d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"de272aad-c620-4d71-bbdd-27dd2d3dc8af","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"quizzical-sniffing-quasar"}
