ect":false},{"question":"Include a fresh post-training-cutoff task subset (mining recent GitHub PRs, SWE-rebench style) to kill the contamination objection head-on? It's the strongest possible answer to the #1 expected reviewer attack, but it's the most new engineering (fresh-task miner + test-harness validation for repos with no SWE-bench scaffolding).","header":"Fresh tasks","options":[{"label":"Yes, as a robustness split (Recommended)","description":"~30-50 fresh pairs alongside the main SWE-bench set. Main claims on the big set; fresh split proves the effect survives on never-seen tasks. ~1-2 weeks extra agent-buildable work."},{"label":"No — argue it in the paper","description":"Rely on the paired-design argument (both arms see the same possibly-memorized task B; the memory DELTA is the measurand) + per-repo breakdowns. Cheaper, but leaves the objection alive."}],"multiSelect":false},{"question":"Who are the two independent seal raters? NeurIPS-grade seal protocol needs 2 humans rating each candidate pair with documented criteria + agreement stats — raters ideally not the harness authors.","header":"Seal raters","options":[{"label":"You + one teammate","description":"e.g. you + Thomas/Alisha/James — cleanest for the paper (disclosed non-author or co-author raters), ~2-4 hours each for ~100 candidates with the review UI the plan adds."},{"label":"You + me (disclosed)","description":"You rate, I pre-screen and rate as the second rater with the AI role disclosed in the paper. Weakest optics but zero coordination cost."},{"label":"Decide later","description":"Build the rating UI + criteria now; pick raters when candidates are ready."}],"multiSelect":false}],"answers":{"Full-scale runs (150–300 pairs × 5 arms × 2 agent backends) are the biggest cost driver. What's the budget ceiling for the confirmatory runs?":"Decide after pilot","Include a fresh post-training-cutoff task subset (mining recent GitHub PRs, SWE-rebench style) to kill the contamination objection head-