{"parentUuid":"3c0d8745-f09a-4f3c-9564-b0a3e744c222","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"queued_command","prompt":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>a102d538487b6c8e3</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_01BZiQgrM1drJz7XFzH1pNc7</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-suhaan-devenv/f507d58c-285f-4d11-b1d0-201f2a5e172d/tasks/a102d538487b6c8e3.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Design NeurIPS-grade upgrade plan\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>I have what I need. Here is the gap-closure plan.\n\n# BrainMark → NeurIPS 2027 E&amp;D Accept-Grade: Gap-Closure Plan\n\nAll paths relative to `/Users/suhaan/devenv/p0p1/brainmark/benchmarks/agent-brain/brainmark/` unless absolute. Ordering front-loads $0 work; every paid tier is preceded by the code + protocol that makes its spend interpretable. Owner key: **[A]** agent-automatable, **[H]** needs-human.\n\n## Phase 0 — $0 code + protocol hardening (Sep–Oct 2026, ~2–3 wk wall-clock, [A] except noted)\n\n**0.1 Full-pool miner (Gap 1).** Extend `mine_pairs.py`: new `pool_loaders.py` pulling `princeton-nlp/SWE-bench` (2,294), `SWE-bench_Verified`, `SWE-bench_Multimodal`, `SWE-bench_Multilingual` via HF `datasets` (downloaded once, then offline/deterministic; record dataset revision shas in `candidates/INDEX.json`). New `clone_repos.py` to populate `graphmark/agentic-swebench/repo-cache/` for every repo with ≥2 instances (network+disk, ~50–150 GB; run in background). Gates unchanged. Target ≥300 verified candidates so seal review can reject freely and still land 150–300 sealed + 15–20 dev. Cost $0, ~2–4 days clone wall-clock.\n\n**0.2 Fresh post-cutoff split (Gap 2b).** New `mine_fresh.py`: SWE-rebench-style mining of merged PRs after the newest backend's training cutoff (GitHub API over the already-cached repos; require linked issue, F2P-style test delta, buildable base). Same pair gates. Target 25–40 fresh pairs as a pre-registered **robustness split**, analyzed separately, never pooled. Also add per-pair `created_at`/repo-popularity metadata so `report.py` can regress memory-effect vs task age (contamination probe, Gap 2a).\n\n**0.3 Paired-design contamination argument (Gap 2c).** New PREREGISTRATION section: memorization inflates *both* arms of a pair identically (same B task, same model); the measurand is the within-pair delta, so contamination biases toward **null**, not toward a fake win — verify by checking the argument's failure mode (memorization could floor `locate_calls_pre_edit` in no_brain, compressing the delta) and pre-register the check: report headline stratified by no_brain locate-call floor, and fresh-split concordance.\n\n**0.4 Irrelevant-memory control arm (Gap 6).** New `memsources/irrelevant.py`: packet distilled from a *different pair's* session A (deterministic derangement over sealed pairs, same repo excluded), same byte budget, same envelope. Registered as **exploratory control**, not a competitor. NOTE: the 2026-08-19 user decision was \"no ablation arms\" — this is a placebo control, not a brain ablation, but it changes the arm matrix, so **[H] user sign-off required** before sealing. Symmetry tests extended to 6 arms.\n\n**0.5 Second backend (Gap 3).** Refactor `session_a.py`/`run_b.py` behind an `agents/` adapter (claude adapter = current code; codex adapter reuses `run.py` `codex_mcp_config_args`/toml config wiring at run.py:6835 and stream parsing). Map codex tool events into `mechmetrics.py` LOCATE/EDIT taxonomy (new fixture + tests — the metric definition must be backend-neutral or the prereg amends it per-backend, frozen before any codex confirmatory run). Config gains `agent.backends: [claude, codex]`.\n\n**0.6 Reps + power (Gaps 1, 3).** `run_b.py --rep N` with per-rep seeds; new `power_analysis.py`: from pilot per-pair log-ratio variance, compute MDE curves and choose final n (pre-committed rule: smallest n giving 80% power for a 15% locate-call reduction, capped by sealed supply); variance decomposition (pair/arm/rep) using the prior evidence that run-level noise dominates. Final n frozen as a dated prereg amendment **before** confirmatory spend.\n\n**0.7 Seal protocol v2 (Gap 5).** Extend `seal.py`: `REVIEW.json` → two independent attributed reviews per pair + `adjudication` field; compute and store Cohen's kappa in `SEAL-MANIFEST.json`; refuse promotion if kappa unreported. New `SEAL_PROTOCOL.md`: written accept/reject criteria (genuine dependence, leakage, triviality), rater instructions, disclosure that raters are project-affiliated if no external rater is recruited. **[H]** recruit 1 rater who is not a harness author (colleague/contractor, ~10–15 hr at final scale).\n\n**0.8 Construct-validity protocol (Gap 4).** New `validity/` with `LABEL_PROTOCOL.md` (unit: each pre-edit locate call in a sampled B session, label \"re-derives session-A knowledge: yes/no/unclear\"), `render_session.py` (transcript → labeling sheet), `analyze_validity.py` (Spearman ρ between `locate_calls_pre_edit` and human-labeled re-derivation count; per-rater agreement). Sampling frame pre-registered: ~30 B sessions stratified by arm × outcome, drawn from **pilot**, labeled blind to arm. Freeze in PREREGISTRATION before pilot transcripts are viewed.\n\n**0.9 Baseline dignity (Gap 7).** New `COMPETITORS.md`: per competitor — published default config, the one permitted tuning pass (dev split only, before seal of confirmatory analysis), and version pins. Fix `config.json` graphify/cmm `null` pins to explicit commit shas/binaries; record mem0 embedder/LLM versions in every packet's provenance.\n\n**0.10 Artifacts + anonymization (Gap 8).** New `release/make_release.py`: builds an anonymized tree — neutral \"BrainMark\" naming, `full_brain` → `system_x` pluggable adapter, strip Entire branding/paths (extend the existing parent `PUBLICATION-SANITIZATION.md` + `test_publication_safety.py` patterns; add a grep-gate test for forbidden strings). New `release/croissant_gen.py` emitting Croissant JSON-LD + Responsible-AI metadata from `SEAL-MANIFEST.json`, validated with `mlcroissant` in CI-style test. New `MAINTENANCE.md` (versioning-by-seal, deprecation, leaderboard intake policy). License audit: per-repo license recorded per pair (DATASHEET already covers preact/prometheus; automate for the full pool; verify Multimodal/Multilingual pool licenses — note SWE-bench Multimodal has a distinct license, check before inclusion). Hosting plan: HF dataset (pair metadata only, no upstream content) + Zenodo DOI, uploaded anonymously for review via HF's anonymized link or an anonymous org.\n\n**0.11 Paper skeleton (Gap 9). [A+H]** `paper/OUTLINE.md`: contributions (first sealed cross-session memory-utility benchmark for coding agents; mechanism-primary pre-registered metric; N-system same-bytes comparison; fresh-split contamination treatment), related-work map (LoCoMo, LongMemEval, mem0/Letta evals, SWE-bench family + rebench, agent-memory surveys), limitations, ethics, compute disclosure, NeurIPS checklist mapping each item to a repo artifact.\n\n## Phase 1 — Mining, sealing, freeze (Oct–Nov 2026)\n\nRun 0.1/0.2 miners → candidates. **[H]** dual-rater seal review (150–300 pairs, ~10–15 hr/rater), kappa + adjudication → `tasks/sealed/` + dev split + fresh split sealed separately. Freeze PREREGISTRATION v2 (all Phase-0 additions), record sha in manifest. Cost $0 (API-free); wall-clock dominated by human review, ~2 wk.\n\n## Phase 2 — Cheap paid validation (Nov–Dec 2026, ~$150–300 total)\n\n1. **Null test** (~$15, unchanged, now 6 arms). 2. **Pilot** Sonnet, 10 dev pairs × 6 arms × 2 reps (~$120–200): feeds `power_analysis.py` (freeze n), variance decomposition, and the construct-validity sample. 3. **Codex smoke** (~$40): 3 dev pairs end-to-end on the codex adapter, mechmetrics parity check. 4. **[H]** Construct-validity labeling: 2 raters × ~30 sessions (~8 hr each), then `analyze_validity.py`; if ρ &lt; ~0.5, amend prereg (dated) with a revised primary before confirmatory spend — this is the last legal moment to change it.\n\n## Phase 3 — Confirmatory runs (Jan–Feb 2027)\n\n- **Primary cell**: claude backend, main tier, n from power analysis (assume ~150–200 pairs), 6 arms × 2 reps ≈ 1,800–2,400 B + 300–400 A sessions. Honest estimate: **$1.5–3k Sonnet-tier; $8–15k Opus-tier** — decide tier by pilot effect size ([H] budget sign-off).\n- **Generality cell**: codex/gpt-5.6-terra via Azure, pre-registered 60-pair subset (deterministic draw), 6 arms × 2 reps ≈ 720 B ≈ **$400–900**.\n- **Fresh split**: 25–40 pairs, claude backend, 6 arms × 2 reps ≈ **$300–600**.\n- Docker grading free; ~1–2 wk wall-clock at concurrency 8, resume-safe. [A] throughout, [H] spend approvals.\n\n## Phase 4 — Analysis, artifacts, paper (Mar–May 2027)\n\n`report.py` extensions: per-repo/per-language breakdowns (only for subgroups ≥ n floor), age-vs-effect contamination probe, fresh-vs-main concordance, leave-one-out, variance decomposition table, competitor table with prep-cost column. Run `make_release.py` + `croissant_gen.py`; upload HF + Zenodo; leaderboard stub. **[H]** write paper from `paper/OUTLINE.md`; internal red-team review against the four E&amp;D review dimensions; abstract ~May 2027.\n\n## Verification (gap → closed-when)\n\n1 Scale/power: sealed count ≥ power-analysis n; n-choice rule frozen pre-pilot; MDE table in paper. 2 Contamination: fresh split sealed + analyzed; age-probe in report; paired-argument section survives the floor-compression check. 3 Generality: codex confirmatory cell reported; mechmetrics codex fixtures pass; 2 reps or variance-decomp justification in paper. 4 Construct validity: pre-registered ρ reported with rater agreement. 5 Seal: kappa in SEAL-MANIFEST; `seal.py verify` enforces dual review. 6 Control: irrelevant-memory arm passes symmetry tests; result reported as exploratory. 7 Baselines: COMPETITORS.md + non-null pins; tuning-pass log on dev split only. 8 Artifacts: `mlcroissant` validation green; anonymization grep-gate green; DOI + HF link resolve without login; license table complete. 9 Paper: checklist maps every item to an artifact. 10 Budget: every paid phase has a pre-run estimate and post-run actual in REPORT.json.\n\n## Residual acceptance risks we cannot engineer away\n\n- **Contamination residue**: the paired argument biases toward null, not zero; a skeptical reviewer can still argue memorized-B tasks understate all memory systems. Fresh split is small (25–40) and only claude-cutoff-clean.\n- **Null or tiny effect**: if full_brain ≈ no_brain, the benchmark is still publishable as a measurement instrument, but \"does it change how we measure progress\" scoring weakens.\n- **De-anonymization**: a 5-competitor memory benchmark with one unnamed \"system_x\" is guessable by informed reviewers; we can sanitize strings, not context.\n- **SWE-bench-derivative fatigue**: task-design originality rests on the pairing + mechanism metric, not the tasks; some reviewers discount derivatives regardless.\n- **Backend confound**: claude-vs-codex differences mix harness, model, and scaffold; we report per-backend, never pooled, but generality claims stay qualitative.\n- **Rater independence**: if no external rater is recruited, seal + validity labels are team-affiliated (disclosed, still a critique surface).\n- **Mechanism-primary taste**: some reviewers expect resolved% as primary; the prereg rationale is our only defense.\n\n### Critical Files for Implementation\n- /Users/suhaan/devenv/p0p1/brainmark/benchmarks/agent-brain/brainmark/mine_pairs.py\n- /Users/suhaan/devenv/p0p1/brainmark/benchmarks/agent-brain/brainmark/PREREGISTRATION.md\n- /Users/suhaan/devenv/p0p1/brainmark/benchmarks/agent-brain/brainmark/run_b.py\n- /Users/suhaan/devenv/p0p1/brainmark/benchmarks/agent-brain/brainmark/seal.py\n- /Users/suhaan/devenv/p0p1/brainmark/benchmarks/agent-brain/brainmark/config.json</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>35983</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>8</tool_uses><duration_ms>124497</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>","commandMode":"task-notification","timestamp":"2026-08-19T00:45:38.056Z"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"ae224ca0-be19-40e9-928b-c6dbdb07ba51","timestamp":"2026-08-19T00:45:38.056Z","session_id":"f507d58c-285f-4d11-b1d0-201f2a5e172d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"de272aad-c620-4d71-bbdd-27dd2d3dc8af","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"quizzical-sniffing-quasar"}
