{"parentUuid":"2b732a46-3095-4200-a57e-ee4aeaacf8e3","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_011CeBFWB8pqXd3LC5csJtAo","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The gap-closure design is complete and your three answers are folded in (budget decided after pilot; fresh split yes; seal raters = you + a teammate). Writing the final upgraded plan:"}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7095,"cache_read_input_tokens":369842,"output_tokens":3358,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":405},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":7095,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3358,"cache_read_input_tokens":369842,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7095,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":7095},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CeBFW7Hecnc4qnDcWmFgM","type":"assistant","uuid":"e904692b-8381-4380-a3c7-a531783cef4d","timestamp":"2026-08-19T01:37:18.167Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"f507d58c-285f-4d11-b1d0-201f2a5e172d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"de272aad-c620-4d71-bbdd-27dd2d3dc8af","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"quizzical-sniffing-quasar"}
{"parentUuid":"e904692b-8381-4380-a3c7-a531783cef4d","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_011CeBFWB8pqXd3LC5csJtAo","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01BH7Kw1GfgA3ngrnY9PfBNW","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/suhaan/.claude/plans && python3 - <<'EOF'\np = 'quizzical-sniffing-quasar.md'\ns = open(p).read()\naddendum = '''\n\n---\n\n# PART 2 — NeurIPS 2027 E&D accept-grade upgrade (approved direction: maximize acceptance odds)\n\nHonest framing: no plan guarantees acceptance; this closes every engineerable gap. Verdict on v1:\nstrong scientific core (prereg/seal/gates/CIs/null test) but 4 accept-blockers: SCALE (~83\ncandidates), CONTAMINATION (public SWE-bench tasks), GENERALITY (one backend), ARTIFACT COMPLIANCE\n(2026+ track desk-rejects without valid Croissant + RAI metadata + persistent hosting + anonymized\ncode AT submission). User decisions: budget ceiling decided AFTER pilot · fresh post-cutoff split\nYES · seal raters = user + one teammate (disclosed).\n\n## Phase 0 — $0 hardening (now, agent-automatable)\n- 0.1 FULL-POOL MINER: pool_loaders.py over HF princeton-nlp/SWE-bench + Verified + Multimodal +\n  Multilingual (record dataset revision shas); clone_repos.py fills repo-cache (~50-150GB, days,\n  background). Target ≥300 verified candidates → seal can reject freely and still land 150-300.\n- 0.2 FRESH SPLIT: mine_fresh.py — SWE-rebench-style post-training-cutoff merged PRs over cached\n  repos (linked issue + test delta + buildable). 25-40 pairs, pre-registered ROBUSTNESS split,\n  analyzed separately, never pooled. Per-pair created_at metadata → age-vs-effect contamination probe.\n- 0.3 CONTAMINATION ARGUMENT in PREREGISTRATION: memorization hits both arms of a pair identically\n  → biases the within-pair delta toward NULL, not fake wins; pre-register the floor-compression\n  check (stratify by no_brain locate-call floor) + fresh-split concordance.\n- 0.4 IRRELEVANT-MEMORY placebo control arm (memsources/irrelevant.py: another pair's session-A\n  packet, same size, deterministic derangement). EXPLORATORY control, NOT a brain ablation —\n  distinguishes relevant-memory value from any-context placebo. (Flagged: user vetoed brain\n  ablation arms; this is a placebo control — drop it on request, nothing depends on it.)\n- 0.5 SECOND BACKEND: agents/ adapter split; codex adapter reuses run.py codex wiring (:6835);\n  mechmetrics taxonomy made backend-neutral with codex fixtures; frozen before codex confirmatory.\n- 0.6 REPS + POWER: run_b --rep N; power_analysis.py from pilot variance; pre-committed n rule\n  (80% power for 15% locate-call reduction, capped by sealed supply); frozen as dated prereg\n  amendment BEFORE confirmatory spend.\n- 0.7 SEAL v2: dual independent attributed reviews + adjudication + Cohen's kappa stored in\n  SEAL-MANIFEST (promotion refused without it); SEAL_PROTOCOL.md criteria; raters = user + teammate.\n- 0.8 CONSTRUCT VALIDITY: validity/ protocol — human-label ~30 pilot B sessions (blind to arm,\n  stratified) for \"re-derives session-A knowledge\"; Spearman ρ vs locate_calls_pre_edit; if ρ<0.5,\n  dated prereg amendment of the primary BEFORE confirmatory (last legal moment).\n- 0.9 BASELINE DIGNITY: COMPETITORS.md — published defaults + ONE tuning pass on dev split only +\n  version pins; fix null graphify/cmm pins; mem0 embedder/LLM versions in packet provenance.\n- 0.10 ARTIFACTS: release/make_release.py (anonymized tree, neutral naming, full_brain→system_x,\n  grep-gate test for forbidden strings — extend parent PUBLICATION-SANITIZATION patterns);\n  release/croissant_gen.py (Croissant JSON-LD + RAI metadata from SEAL-MANIFEST, mlcroissant-\n  validated in tests); MAINTENANCE.md (versioning-by-seal, leaderboard intake); per-repo license\n  audit automated (check Multimodal pool license before inclusion); hosting = HF dataset\n  (pair metadata only) + Zenodo DOI, anonymized for review.\n- 0.11 PAPER SKELETON: paper/OUTLINE.md — contributions (first sealed cross-session memory-utility\n  benchmark for coding agents; mechanism-primary prereg; N-system same-bytes comparison; fresh-split\n  contamination treatment), related work (LoCoMo/LongMemEval/mem0/Letta/SWE-bench family), limits,\n  ethics, compute disclosure, checklist→artifact map.\n\n## Phase 1 — Mine + seal + freeze (Oct-Nov 2026, $0 + human time)\nRun miners → dual-rater seal (~10-15h/rater at full scale) → kappa + adjudication → sealed/dev/fresh\nsplits → PREREGISTRATION v2 frozen, sha in manifest.\n\n## Phase 2 — Cheap paid validation (~$150-300 total, EACH RUNG NEEDS USER GO)\nNull test (~$15, 6 arms) → Sonnet pilot 10 dev pairs × 6 arms × 2 reps (~$120-200; feeds power\nanalysis + validity sample) → codex smoke 3 pairs (~$40) → validity labeling (2 raters × ~30\nsessions, ~8h each).\n\n## Phase 3 — Confirmatory (Jan-Feb 2027, tier chosen from pilot; NEEDS USER GO)\nPrimary cell claude backend n≈150-200 × 6 arms × 2 reps (~$1.5-3k Sonnet-tier / $8-15k Opus-tier);\ngenerality cell codex/gpt-5.6-terra 60-pair prereg subset (~$400-900); fresh split (~$300-600).\nDocker grading free. Concurrency 8, resume-safe.\n\n## Phase 4 — Analysis + artifacts + paper (Mar-May 2027)\nreport.py: per-repo/language breakdowns (≥n floor only), age-probe, fresh concordance, LOO,\nvariance decomposition, competitor table w/ prep-cost column. Release + DOI + leaderboard stub.\nPaper written from OUTLINE; internal red-team vs the 4 E&D review dimensions; abstract ~May 2027.\n\n## Verification (gap → closed-when)\nScale: sealed ≥ power-n, n-rule frozen pre-pilot · Contamination: fresh split analyzed + age probe +\nfloor-check survives · Generality: codex cell reported, fixtures pass · Validity: prereg ρ reported ·\nSeal: kappa enforced by seal.py · Control: placebo arm passes symmetry · Baselines: pins + tuning\nlog · Artifacts: mlcroissant green, anon grep-gate green, DOI resolves w/o login, license table\ncomplete · Paper: checklist maps every item to an artifact · Budget: pre-estimate + actual per phase.\n\n## Residual risks we cannot engineer away (state in paper, don't hide)\nContamination residue (fresh split small, claude-cutoff-clean only) · null/tiny effect (still\npublishable as instrument, weaker \"significance\") · de-anonymization guessability (5 named\ncompetitors + system_x) · SWE-bench-derivative fatigue (originality rests on pairing + mechanism\nmetric) · backend confound (report per-backend, never pooled) · rater affiliation (disclosed) ·\nmechanism-primary taste (prereg rationale is the defense).\n'''\nopen(p, 'a').write(addendum)\nprint('appended', len(addendum), 'chars')\nEOF","description":"Append NeurIPS upgrade plan to plan file"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7095,"cache_read_input_tokens":369842,"output_tokens":3358,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":405},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":7095,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3358,"cache_read_input_tokens":369842,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7095,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":7095},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CeBFW7Hecnc4qnDcWmFgM","type":"assistant","uuid":"fe2c256d-bd00-4bfc-848d-e7444b3c81a0","timestamp":"2026-08-19T01:37:48.862Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"f507d58c-285f-4d11-b1d0-201f2a5e172d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"de272aad-c620-4d71-bbdd-27dd2d3dc8af","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"quizzical-sniffing-quasar"}
{"parentUuid":"fe2c256d-bd00-4bfc-848d-e7444b3c81a0","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"d03804f5-4028-4a24-a2b9-46b62188e5f6","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BH7Kw1GfgA3ngrnY9PfBNW","type":"tool_result","content":"appended 6104 chars\nShell cwd was reset to /Users/suhaan/devenv","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"fb8da468-e100-4df7-bbb9-4a144f3442ea","timestamp":"2026-08-19T01:37:48.953Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"appended 6104 chars","stderr":"\nShell cwd was reset to /Users/suhaan/devenv","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"fe2c256d-bd00-4bfc-848d-e7444b3c81a0","session_id":"f507d58c-285f-4d11-b1d0-201f2a5e172d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"de272aad-c620-4d71-bbdd-27dd2d3dc8af","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"quizzical-sniffing-quasar"}
{"parentUuid":"fb8da468-e100-4df7-bbb9-4a144f3442ea","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"total_tokens_reminder","text":"<total_tokens>14975520 tokens left</total_tokens>"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"32410d26-93c3-474d-bcfd-5b84de89ee88","timestamp":"2026-08-19T01:37:48.963Z","session_id":"f507d58c-285f-4d11-b1d0-201f2a5e172d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"de272aad-c620-4d71-bbdd-27dd2d3dc8af","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"quizzical-sniffing-quasar"}
{"parentUuid":"32410d26-93c3-474d-bcfd-5b84de89ee88","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_011CeBFZVYh9rRs1WGucLPam","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01LUmCJscdqLhf7gEDgexqmC","name":"ExitPlanMode","input":{"plan":"# BrainMark — flagship benchmark for entire-brain (fair, all-competitor, publication-grade)\n\n## Context\n\nLoCoMo/LME only measure the brain's retrieval substrate over chat transcripts (tonight's runs:\nbase terra 90.84, chrono sol 92.99, chrono terra 91.90 — engine credibility, not product proof).\nThe product claim — **\"a second coding session reuses what the first learned\"** — has never been\nmeasured. BrainMark is that measurement: agent does task A, memory is derived from A's session,\nagent does related task B with memory vs without vs competitors. Built to survive publication\nreview (user is thinking NeurIPS-class venues): pre-registered primary metric, sealed tasks,\nexternal tasks + external grading, released harness.\n\nUser decisions: **all comp arms** (mem0 + Graphify + cmm; NO ablation arms — one true brain arm only, user 2026-08-19) ·\n**SWE-bench mined pairs** as task source · **pilot → full** budget path.\n\n## Architecture\n\nNew thin orchestrator **`benchmarks/agent-brain/brainmark/`** (in the entire-brain repo,\nbranch off main / on top of keystone), importing the existing `run.py` **as a library**\n(it has a `__main__` guard at run.py:11130 — do not modify it) for its fairness primitives:\npacket bounding (:4731/:5014), delimiter guard (:4840), arm-neutral policy text (:6724),\nsealed-bundle schema (:3923), env sanitization (:5108), sandbox-exec (:5124), pinned distill\ndriver (:4578). GraphMark (`/Users/suhaan/devenv/graphmark/agentic-swebench`) supplies the\nSWE-bench side as patterns/data, not a framework: task JSONs, repo-cache worktrees+locks\n(run_3arm.sh:54-89), netjail, Docker grading (tools/grade_tag.sh), and vendored paired stats\n(tools/metrics.py — log-ratios, geo-mean, median, 20k bootstrap CI, McNemar, session gates).\n\n## Components (new files under `benchmarks/agent-brain/brainmark/`)\n\n- `config.json` — graphmark root, repo-cache, model tiers, packet max_bytes, per-competitor\n  pins (mem0 version/embedder; graphify + cmm pinned binaries), distill pin, concurrency=8, seeds.\n- `mine_pairs.py` — offline $0 miner (below) → `candidates/*.json`.\n- `seal.py` + `PREREGISTRATION.md` — human-review promotion to `tasks/sealed/` (n≥30) +\n  disjoint 10-pair dev split; `SEAL-MANIFEST.json` = sha256 of every task + miner commit +\n  prereg hash. Report refuses to aggregate on hash mismatch. Seal BEFORE first confirmatory run.\n- `session_a.py` — session A runs ONCE per pair per tier (`claude -p` stream-JSON, isolated\n  CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR); native claude-code JSONL harvested and sha256-pinned. Shared by ALL arms.\n- `memsources/{empty,full_brain,mem0_source,graphify_source,cmm_source}.py` — each:\n  pinned-A-bytes in → memory packet out, bounded/guarded by run.py primitives; the PACKET is\n  sha256-pinned (not the store), so ingest nondeterminism can't create arm asymmetry.\n  - `full_brain`: write A transcript to `<brainDir>/sessions/main/<id>.jsonl` + synthesized\n    manifest (contract proven in internal/cli/distill_cmd_test.go:25-75) → pinned\n    `entire-brain distill` + `refresh history` → ONE frozen `brain search/brief --json`,\n    query = B's problem_statement.\n  - `mem0/graphify/cmm`: same A bytes into each competitor (duck-typed add/search clients —\n    mirror /Users/suhaan/devenv/eg-memharness/bench/memory/benchmarks/common/entire_client.py;\n    graphify+cmm clients exist there to adapt), retrieval with the SAME query string and byte\n    budget, rendered into the IDENTICAL envelope. Prep cost recorded separately, reported.\n- `prompts.py` — one scaffold for all 5 arms; packet block present in every arm (no_brain gets\n  a fixed \"(no prior-session memory available)\" sentinel); symmetry gate = sha256 of prompt\n  with packet region replaced by `<PACKET>` must be identical across a pair's arms; enforced\n  at launch and re-checked at report time.\n- `run_b.py` — B driver: worktree at base_commit_B (graphmark lock pattern), netjail, run.py\n  env-sanitization + sandbox, `claude -p` stream-JSON safe mode; per-cell results dir with\n  cc_out.json, stream.jsonl, patch.diff, packet.sha256, prompt_sym.sha256; idempotent resume\n  (skip iff usd>0 ∧ patch nonempty).\n- `mechmetrics.py` — PRIMARY pre-registered metric: `locate_calls_pre_edit` = tool_use in\n  {Read,Grep,Glob} ∪ {Bash matching ^(rg|grep|egrep|git grep|find|ls|cat|head|tail|ag)\\b}\n  strictly before first {Edit,Write,MultiEdit,NotebookEdit}; no-edit sessions counted whole +\n  flagged; ratios on (count+1). Secondary: tokens/usd (modelUsage), duration, num_turns.\n- `grade.py` — wraps graphmark grade_tag.sh (Docker swebench.harness.run_evaluation); B graded\n  by its own FAIL_TO_PASS. `vendor/graphmark_metrics.py` — pinned metrics.py copy w/ provenance\n  header. `report.py` — REPORT.md/json: full_brain vs no_brain (headline), vs mem0/graphify/cmm (competitor table).\n\n## Pair mining (deterministic, $0)\n\nGroup graphmark `tasks/*.json` instances by repo, sort by created_at; for ordered (A,B):\n≥1 overlapping file between patch_A and patch_B (diff --git paths) · `git merge-base\n--is-ancestor base_A base_B` · score = Jaccard(files) + hunk-header symbol overlap (optional\n`entire graph diff` entity rerank when available) · leakage screens: patch-body token overlap\n< 0.8 (A must not BE B's fix), borderline flagged for seal review · one best A per B ·\nemit ≥40 candidates with full provenance.\n\n## Arm matrix (session A once per pair, pinned, shared by all arms)\n\n| arm | memory source | proves |\n|---|---|---|\n| no_brain | sentinel-empty packet | baseline |\n| full_brain | distill+history over pinned A JSONL | the product (the ONLY brain arm) |\n| mem0 | mem0 OSS over same bytes | vs the named competitor |\n| graphify | graphify over same bytes | vs YC code-memory competitor |\n| cmm | cmm over same bytes | vs codebase-memory-mcp |\n\nAll packets harness-delivered through one envelope (phase0b doctrine — self-retrieval arms\ndeferred to v2 exploratory).\n\n## Gates (all vendored/enforced)\n\nPer-session usd>0 ∧ patch nonempty · all-arms-clean pair gate, symmetric drops · prompt-symmetry\nsha equal · packet sha matches pin · no Entire-family tools outside full_brain · no\n.entire/.benchmark/checkpoint-ref inspection anywhere (run.py audit) · no A-artifact paths\nreadable from B worktree.\n\n## Runbook + cost (5 arms)\n\n1. **$0**: mine → human seal (n≥30 + 10 dev) → prereg freeze → symmetry/pinning/miner-determinism\n   unit tests.\n2. **Null test (~$15, non-negotiable)**: 3 dev pairs × 2 reps, full_brain machinery with EMPTY\n   packet vs no_brain — primary + token deltas must straddle 0. Proves the machinery is inert.\n3. **Pilot (Sonnet, 10 dev pairs)**: 10 A + 50 B + prep ≈ **$60–120**. Fix harness only, never tasks.\n4. **Full (n≥30 sealed, main model)**: 30 A + 150 B (5 arms) ≈ **$700–1,500 on Opus** (or ~$150–300 on\n   gpt-5.6-class via Azure if the user prefers). Concurrency 8, resume-safe.\n5. Docker grading (free) → `report.py`.\n\n## Verification\n\nMiner determinism (byte-identical double run) · seal-hash round-trip · symmetry sha across\nstub-packet arms · delimiter-guard rejection test · packet re-derivation → identical sha ·\nmechmetrics vs 3 hand-labeled stream fixtures · null test (above) · leakage audit (grep B\ntranscripts for A instance_ids/paths; sandbox denials logged) · one-pair end-to-end smoke\nincluding Docker grading — all BEFORE the full spend.\n\n## Critical reused files\n\n- brain-keystone `benchmarks/agent-brain/run.py` (library import; DO NOT modify)\n- brain-keystone `benchmarks/agent-brain/CONDITIONS.md` (normative contract; extend, don't fork)\n- graphmark `agentic-swebench/tools/metrics.py` (vendor), `run_3arm.sh` (patterns),\n  `tools/grade_tag.sh` (grading), `tasks/*.json` (instance pool)\n- brain-keystone `internal/cli/distill_cmd_test.go:25-75` (raw-JSONL ingest contract)\n- eg-memharness `bench/memory/benchmarks/common/*_client.py` (competitor client surface)\n\n\n---\n\n# PART 2 — NeurIPS 2027 E&D accept-grade upgrade (approved direction: maximize acceptance odds)\n\nHonest framing: no plan guarantees acceptance; this closes every engineerable gap. Verdict on v1:\nstrong scientific core (prereg/seal/gates/CIs/null test) but 4 accept-blockers: SCALE (~83\ncandidates), CONTAMINATION (public SWE-bench tasks), GENERALITY (one backend), ARTIFACT COMPLIANCE\n(2026+ track desk-rejects without valid Croissant + RAI metadata + persistent hosting + anonymized\ncode AT submission). User decisions: budget ceiling decided AFTER pilot · fresh post-cutoff split\nYES · seal raters = user + one teammate (disclosed).\n\n## Phase 0 — $0 hardening (now, agent-automatable)\n- 0.1 FULL-POOL MINER: pool_loaders.py over HF princeton-nlp/SWE-bench + Verified + Multimodal +\n  Multilingual (record dataset revision shas); clone_repos.py fills repo-cache (~50-150GB, days,\n  background). Target ≥300 verified candidates → seal can reject freely and still land 150-300.\n- 0.2 FRESH SPLIT: mine_fresh.py — SWE-rebench-style post-training-cutoff merged PRs over cached\n  repos (linked issue + test delta + buildable). 25-40 pairs, pre-registered ROBUSTNESS split,\n  analyzed separately, never pooled. Per-pair created_at metadata → age-vs-effect contamination probe.\n- 0.3 CONTAMINATION ARGUMENT in PREREGISTRATION: memorization hits both arms of a pair identically\n  → biases the within-pair delta toward NULL, not fake wins; pre-register the floor-compression\n  check (stratify by no_brain locate-call floor) + fresh-split concordance.\n- 0.4 IRRELEVANT-MEMORY placebo control arm (memsources/irrelevant.py: another pair's session-A\n  packet, same size, deterministic derangement). EXPLORATORY control, NOT a brain ablation —\n  distinguishes relevant-memory value from any-context placebo. (Flagged: user vetoed brain\n  ablation arms; this is a placebo control — drop it on request, nothing depends on it.)\n- 0.5 SECOND BACKEND: agents/ adapter split; codex adapter reuses run.py codex wiring (:6835);\n  mechmetrics taxonomy made backend-neutral with codex fixtures; frozen before codex confirmatory.\n- 0.6 REPS + POWER: run_b --rep N; power_analysis.py from pilot variance; pre-committed n rule\n  (80% power for 15% locate-call reduction, capped by sealed supply); frozen as dated prereg\n  amendment BEFORE confirmatory spend.\n- 0.7 SEAL v2: dual independent attributed reviews + adjudication + Cohen's kappa stored in\n  SEAL-MANIFEST (promotion refused without it); SEAL_PROTOCOL.md criteria; raters = user + teammate.\n- 0.8 CONSTRUCT VALIDITY: validity/ protocol — human-label ~30 pilot B sessions (blind to arm,\n  stratified) for \"re-derives session-A knowledge\"; Spearman ρ vs locate_calls_pre_edit; if ρ<0.5,\n  dated prereg amendment of the primary BEFORE confirmatory (last legal moment).\n- 0.9 BASELINE DIGNITY: COMPETITORS.md — published defaults + ONE tuning pass on dev split only +\n  version pins; fix null graphify/cmm pins; mem0 embedder/LLM versions in packet provenance.\n- 0.10 ARTIFACTS: release/make_release.py (anonymized tree, neutral naming, full_brain→system_x,\n  grep-gate test for forbidden strings — extend parent PUBLICATION-SANITIZATION patterns);\n  release/croissant_gen.py (Croissant JSON-LD + RAI metadata from SEAL-MANIFEST, mlcroissant-\n  validated in tests); MAINTENANCE.md (versioning-by-seal, leaderboard intake); per-repo license\n  audit automated (check Multimodal pool license before inclusion); hosting = HF dataset\n  (pair metadata only) + Zenodo DOI, anonymized for review.\n- 0.11 PAPER SKELETON: paper/OUTLINE.md — contributions (first sealed cross-session memory-utility\n  benchmark for coding agents; mechanism-primary prereg; N-system same-bytes comparison; fresh-split\n  contamination treatment), related work (LoCoMo/LongMemEval/mem0/Letta/SWE-bench family), limits,\n  ethics, compute disclosure, checklist→artifact map.\n\n## Phase 1 — Mine + seal + freeze (Oct-Nov 2026, $0 + human time)\nRun miners → dual-rater seal (~10-15h/rater at full scale) → kappa + adjudication → sealed/dev/fresh\nsplits → PREREGISTRATION v2 frozen, sha in manifest.\n\n## Phase 2 — Cheap paid validation (~$150-300 total, EACH RUNG NEEDS USER GO)\nNull test (~$15, 6 arms) → Sonnet pilot 10 dev pairs × 6 arms × 2 reps (~$120-200; feeds power\nanalysis + validity sample) → codex smoke 3 pairs (~$40) → validity labeling (2 raters × ~30\nsessions, ~8h each).\n\n## Phase 3 — Confirmatory (Jan-Feb 2027, tier chosen from pilot; NEEDS USER GO)\nPrimary cell claude backend n≈150-200 × 6 arms × 2 reps (~$1.5-3k Sonnet-tier / $8-15k Opus-tier);\ngenerality cell codex/gpt-5.6-terra 60-pair prereg subset (~$400-900); fresh split (~$300-600).\nDocker grading free. Concurrency 8, resume-safe.\n\n## Phase 4 — Analysis + artifacts + paper (Mar-May 2027)\nreport.py: per-repo/language breakdowns (≥n floor only), age-probe, fresh concordance, LOO,\nvariance decomposition, competitor table w/ prep-cost column. Release + DOI + leaderboard stub.\nPaper written from OUTLINE; internal red-team vs the 4 E&D review dimensions; abstract ~May 2027.\n\n## Verification (gap → closed-when)\nScale: sealed ≥ power-n, n-rule frozen pre-pilot · Contamination: fresh split analyzed + age probe +\nfloor-check survives · Generality: codex cell reported, fixtures pass · Validity: prereg ρ reported ·\nSeal: kappa enforced by seal.py · Control: placebo arm passes symmetry · Baselines: pins + tuning\nlog · Artifacts: mlcroissant green, anon grep-gate green, DOI resolves w/o login, license table\ncomplete · Paper: checklist maps every item to an artifact · Budget: pre-estimate + actual per phase.\n\n## Residual risks we cannot engineer away (state in paper, don't hide)\nContamination residue (fresh split small, claude-cutoff-clean only) · null/tiny effect (still\npublishable as instrument, weaker \"significance\") · de-anonymization guessability (5 named\ncompetitors + system_x) · SWE-bench-derivative fatigue (originality rests on pairing + mechanism\nmetric) · backend confound (report per-backend, never pooled) · rater affiliation (disclosed) ·\nmechanism-primary taste (prereg rationale is the defense).\n","planFilePath":"/Users/suhaan/.claude/plans/quizzical-sniffing-quasar.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3418,"cache_read_input_tokens":376937,"output_tokens":31,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3418,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":31,"cache_read_input_tokens":376937,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3418,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3418},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CeBFZRhmAZpkSqHG5GaKx","type":"assistant","uuid":"3f0473de-0b92-44a8-9322-680660a5bcc5","timestamp":"2026-08-19T01:37:52.121Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"f507d58c-285f-4d11-b1d0-201f2a5e172d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"de272aad-c620-4d71-bbdd-27dd2d3dc8af","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"quizzical-sniffing-quasar"}
