{"parentUuid":"b6b13871-a9ef-4d8b-8739-ee233c4175fc","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_011CeBFegEGTBjwb6AGgkn4Y","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_016KY6ZjAAVcFTLto6nQPVWW","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Build full-pool + fresh miners","subagent_type":"general-purpose","model":"opus","prompt":"Build the DATA side of BrainMark Phase 0 in /Users/suhaan/devenv/p0p1/brainmark/benchmarks/agent-brain/brainmark/. Use rtk. Read the plan first: /Users/suhaan/.claude/plans/quizzical-sniffing-quasar.md (PART 2, items 0.1, 0.2, 0.9). Read the existing mine_pairs.py/config.json/README.md to match conventions. Two other agents work in this same tree on OTHER files — you may ONLY create/modify: pool_loaders.py, clone_repos.py, mine_fresh.py, COMPETITORS.md, config.json, mine_pairs.py, and new tests named tests/test_pool_*.py / tests/test_fresh_*.py. DO NOT git commit — leave changes in the working tree. DO NOT touch any other file.\n\nTASKS:\n1. (0.1) pool_loaders.py: load SWE-bench pools from HF `datasets` — princeton-nlp/SWE-bench, SWE-bench_Verified, SWE-bench_Multilingual (SKIP Multimodal for now — license unverified, note it in COMPETITORS.md... no, note it in a comment + config flag). Download once into a local cache dir (config key), record each dataset's HF revision sha into candidates/INDEX.json. Loader must work OFFLINE after first download and be deterministic. Import-guard `datasets` (tests pass without it; fixture-based tests use canned instance JSON).\n2. (0.1) clone_repos.py: for every repo with ≥2 instances across loaded pools, ensure /Users/suhaan/devenv/graphmark/agentic-swebench/repo-cache/<owner>_<name> exists — `git clone --filter=blob:none` (commit graph only; ancestry checks work; disk-frugal — we have ~99GB free, do NOT full-clone). Idempotent, resumable, per-clone timeout+skip-on-failure with a summary ledger. Supports --limit and --only-repos.\n3. (0.1) Extend mine_pairs.py to accept the HF pools via pool_loaders (new --pool flags) alongside the existing local task JSONs; gates UNCHANGED; target ≥300 verified candidates once clones exist. Keep byte-determinism (the determinism test must still pass; extend it to cover pool mode with fixtures).\n4. (0.2) mine_fresh.py: SWE-rebench-style fresh-pair miner over ALREADY-CACHED repos: enumerate merged PRs after 2026-01-01 (config key training_cutoff) via `gh api` (import/exec-guard: skip gracefully without gh auth), require linked issue + a test-file delta + same pair gates as mine_pairs (shared-file overlap with an earlier fresh task or an existing instance, ancestry-verified). Emit to candidates/fresh/ with full provenance, NEVER pooled with main candidates. Deterministic given a pinned PR list snapshot (snapshot file committed to candidates/fresh/SNAPSHOT.json on first run; subsequent runs read the snapshot — that's the determinism boundary, document it).\n5. (0.9) COMPETITORS.md: per competitor (mem0, graphify, cmm) — published default config, the ONE permitted tuning pass rule (dev split only), version-pin procedure. Fix config.json's null graphify/cmm pins: locate actual pinned versions/binaries from /Users/suhaan/devenv/eg-memharness/bench/memory/benchmarks/common/*_client.py and the eg-memharness lockfiles; if a true pin is unavailable, write the pin-resolution TODO procedure in COMPETITORS.md rather than inventing one.\n6. RUN what's free: clone_repos.py for the current 303-instance pool's missing repos (another agent may have already added some — clone_repos must detect and skip existing), then mine_pairs in local-JSON mode to refresh the verified count. Do NOT download the full HF pools if >10GB total — check sizes first and report instead.\n\nTests: pool loader fixtures, fresh-miner gates on canned PR fixtures, clone ledger idempotency, extended determinism. All offline.\nReport caveman-ultra: verified candidate count now (lead), files+lines, HF pool sizes (downloaded or deferred+why), clone ledger summary, test results. Max 20 lines."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6740,"cache_read_input_tokens":382437,"output_tokens":6151,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1303},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6740,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":6151,"cache_read_input_tokens":382437,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6740,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6740},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CeBFebYF5w59NgdLaJBnU","type":"assistant","uuid":"3f21f097-71eb-4b6f-9f8b-8c0d8d253196","timestamp":"2026-08-19T01:39:42.661Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"f507d58c-285f-4d11-b1d0-201f2a5e172d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"de272aad-c620-4d71-bbdd-27dd2d3dc8af","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"quizzical-sniffing-quasar"}
