is.py: reads pilot report JSON → per-pair log-ratio variance → MDE curve + smallest n for 80% power at 15% locate-call reduction (pre-committed rule from the plan) + pair/arm/rep variance decomposition; pure stdlib; unit-tested on synthetic data with known answer.\n5. Dry-run proof: run_b full layout via a PATH-stubbed codex binary (like the existing claude stub test) — no paid calls.\nMUTATION-verify: (a) break the codex locate-call mapping → codex fixture test fails; (b) break the derangement (allow same-pair packet) → irrelevant-arm test fails. State results.\nReport caveman-ultra: files+lines, adapter contract summary, fixture/mutation results, test totals. Max 18 lines.","outputFile":"/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-suhaan-devenv/f507d58c-285f-4d11-b1d0-201f2a5e172d/tasks/afa1d69c4343ea541.output","canReadOutputFile":true},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"6139b712-932c-44f6-9d78-1b163f285ac5","session_id":"f507d58c-285f-4d11-b1d0-201f2a5e172d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"de272aad-c620-4d71-bbdd-27dd2d3dc8af","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"quizzical-sniffing-quasar"}
{"parentUuid":"b26a6350-1dee-4bc1-ad1d-db64ef82d5a0","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_011CeBFegEGTBjwb6AGgkn4Y","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_012M9dezxhipGuctHWSsriwf","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Build protocol + artifacts side","subagent_type":"general-purpose","model":"sonnet","prompt":"Build the PROTOCOL/ARTIFACTS side of BrainMark Phase 0 in /Users/suhaan/devenv/p0p1/brainmark/benchmarks/agent-brain/brainmark/. Use rtk. Read the plan first: /Users/suhaan/.claude/plans/quizzical-sniffing-quasar.md (PART 2, items 0.3, 0.7, 0.8, 0.10, 0.11). Read existing seal.py, PREREGISTRATION.md, DATASHEET.md, report.py, tests/ to match conventions. Two other agents work in this tree on OTHER files — you may ONLY create/modify: seal.py, SEAL_PROTOCOL.md, PREREGISTRATION.md, validity/ (new dir), release/ (new dir), MAINTENANCE.md, paper/ (new dir), and new tests named tests/test_seal_v2_*.py / tests/test_release_*.py / tests/test_validity_*.py. DO NOT git commit — leave changes in the working tree. DO NOT touch config.json, mine_pairs.py, run_b.py, prompts.py, mechmetrics.py.\n\nTASKS:\n1. (0.7) seal.py v2: REVIEW.json schema = two independent attributed reviews per candidate (rater id, verdict accept/reject, criteria codes, notes) + adjudication field for disagreements; compute Cohen's kappa across raters, store in SEAL-MANIFEST.json; REFUSE promotion if kappa missing or either review absent. SEAL_PROTOCOL.md: written accept/reject criteria (genuine A→B dependence, leakage, triviality, answer-revealing prompts), rater instructions, disclosure template (raters = user + one teammate, project-affiliated). Tests: dual-review round trip, refusal without second review, kappa computed correctly on a known fixture.\n2. (0.8) validity/: LABEL_PROTOCOL.md (unit = each pre-edit locate call in a sampled B session; label \"re-derives session-A knowledge yes/no/unclear\"; blind-to-arm; stratified sample of ~30 pilot B sessions); render_session.py (stream JSONL → human labeling sheet, markdown); analyze_validity.py (Spearman rho between locate_calls_pre_edit and labeled re-derivation count + per-rater agreement; stdlib only; unit-tested on synthetic labels).\n3. (0.3) PREREGISTRATION.md: add the contamination section — paired-design argument (memorization affects both arms of a pair identically → biases the within-pair delta toward NULL); pre-register the floor-compression check (stratify headline by no_brain locate-call floor) and fresh-split concordance analysis; add the power-rule (n = smallest giving 80% power for 15% locate-call reduction, from pilot variance, capped by sealed supply) and the validity gate (if rho<0.5, dated amendment of primary BEFORE confirmatory). Mark all additions as dated amendments (2026-08-19), never rewrite existing frozen text.\n4. (0.10) release/make_release.py: builds an anonymized copy of the brainmark tree — neutral naming, full_brain→system_x, strip Entire branding/absolute paths/usernames; grep-gate list of forbidden strings (entire, entirehq, entireio, suhaan, devenv, brain — case-insensitive, allowlist for necessary words) enforced by tests/test_release_*.py; look at the parent benchmarks/agent-brain/PUBLICATION-SANITIZATION.md + test_publication_safety.py for existing patterns to extend. release/croissant_gen.py: emit Croissant JSON-LD + Responsible-AI metadata fields from SEAL-MANIFEST.json + DATASHEET.md content; validate with `mlcroissant` if importable else structural self-validation (import-guarded); unit test on a fixture manifest. MAINTENANCE.md: versioning-by-seal, deprecation policy, leaderboard submission intake.\n5. (0.11) paper/OUTLINE.md: contributions, related-work map (LoCoMo, LongMemEval, mem0/Letta evals, SWE-bench family incl. rebench/Verified/Multilingual, agent-memory surveys), limitations (copy the plan's residual-risk list), ethics, compute disclosure, NeurIPS checklist → repo-artifact mapping table.\