{"parentUuid":"884bbb3a-498b-43af-8092-148527466941","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_011CeCBKkRJ8svNYPhsX6ZtA","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01WWoWyBDxWBwa7WE28EGJm3","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Prescreen + seal packets","subagent_type":"general-purpose","model":"opus","prompt":"Free ($0) task in /Users/suhaan/devenv/p0p1/brainmark/benchmarks/agent-brain/brainmark/ (worktree of entire-brain, branch feat/brainmark). Use rtk. Read README.md, SEAL_PROTOCOL.md, seal.py, mine_pairs.py first. You may create/modify ONLY: seal_prescreen.py, review/ (new dir), REVIEWING-QUICKSTART.md, candidates/ (emitting files there), and tests/test_prescreen_*.py. Do NOT commit.\n\nGOAL: get the human seal session fully prepared so the two raters (the user + a teammate) can sit down and review efficiently. Everything deterministic.\n\n1. Run the full-pool mine to emit the complete candidate set (mine_pairs.py --all-pools or equivalent per its --help; ~1,806 expected; candidates/ is gitignored, that's fine).\n2. Build seal_prescreen.py: DETERMINISTIC selection of the review slate from all candidates — rank by miner score, enforce diversity caps (no repo >12% of slate, balance across pools/languages where possible), drop near-duplicate pairs (same A or same B instance appearing >2x), select top 350 for review + propose a 20-pair dev-split candidate list (chosen to span repos/languages, marked separately). Emit review/SLATE.json with full provenance + selection rationale codes. Unit-test the determinism + caps (tests/test_prescreen_*.py).\n3. Generate the human review packets: for each slated pair, a compact markdown sheet (review/sheets/NNN_<pairid>.md) with: problem statements A and B, the overlapping files, the miner's overlap/leakage scores, links/paths to patches, and the SEAL_PROTOCOL criteria checklist inline (accept/reject + criteria codes). Also review/REVIEW-TEMPLATE.json prefilled with the slate ids and empty rater fields matching seal.py v2's REVIEW.json schema exactly (verify against seal.py's parser — a mismatched template would waste the human session).\n4. REVIEWING-QUICKSTART.md: the 1-page instruction for the two raters — how long (~2-3 min/pair), how to fill REVIEW.json (or the sheets), what happens after (kappa, adjudication, promotion), the dev-split rule (disjoint, sealed separately).\n5. Verify: seal.py dry-run accepts the template's shape (fill 3 pairs with synthetic dual reviews in a COPY under /tmp, run the promote path, confirm kappa computed + promotion works + refusal on missing second review still enforced).\nReport caveman-ultra: candidate total emitted, slate size + composition (repos/pools histogram, top-repo share), dev-split proposal size, template-vs-parser verification result, test results. Max 16 lines."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":418537,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":5167,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":2393},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":418537,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":5167,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":418537,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":418537},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":{"cache_miss_reason":{"type":"previous_message_not_found"}}},"requestId":"req_011CeCBKfiX2Rq7Loa14k8ew","type":"assistant","uuid":"9c34eb8b-4c29-4013-95c5-324259feeb64","timestamp":"2026-08-19T13:24:04.629Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"f507d58c-285f-4d11-b1d0-201f2a5e172d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/p0p1/brainmark","sessionId":"de272aad-c620-4d71-bbdd-27dd2d3dc8af","versio