{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-08-19T13:48:04.178Z","sessionId":"de272aad-c620-4d71-bbdd-27dd2d3dc8af","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>ac17a39927dc585b5</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_01WWoWyBDxWBwa7WE28EGJm3</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-suhaan-devenv/f507d58c-285f-4d11-b1d0-201f2a5e172d/tasks/ac17a39927dc585b5.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Prescreen + seal packets\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>Done. All artifacts built, verified, nothing committed.\n\n**MINE** `--all-pools`: 2,594 instances → **1,806 candidates** (was 82 local-only); 110 borderline-flagged; rejects no_shared=502644/not_anc=626/leak=308/not_best=11702; repo-cache complete (0 unverifiable).\n\n**SLATE** 350/350, 36 repos, top = django/django 42 = **12.00%** (cap 12%, respected). Pools swe_bench 144 / verified 127 / local 79. Langs Python 273, JS 14, PHP 12, Rust 12, Go 10, Java 10, C 7, C++ 7, Ruby 5. 25 flagged. Exclusions DROP_DUP_A 299 / DROP_RANK 295 / DROP_REPO_CAP 862. One recorded relaxation (stratum ceiling 140 left it at 346; repo cap never relaxed). Dev proposal **20 pairs / 20 repos / 9 langs**.\n\n**TEMPLATE vs PARSER: MATCH** — generated *by calling* `seal.cmd_review_template`, then byte-diffed against a fresh reference after stripping 5 documented `_` aids. This check caught a real bug: a `_`-prefix strip also ate seal's own `_instructions` (raters would have gotten an instruction-less file). Stripping is now an explicit key list, and a test pins that.\n\n**SEAL DRY-RUN** (/tmp copy, 3 pairs, synthetic): promote → 2 sealed, 1 disagreement adjudicated, **kappa 0.4** (po .6667 / pe .4444, hand-checks), `verify` OK; blank rater_2 verdict → `REFUSES ... missing a review`, exit 1, **no manifest written**.\n\n**TESTS** 54 new (`test_prescreen_selection/template/merge`), full suite **322 OK**. Determinism: two runs byte-identical across 1,525 files incl. changed `PYTHONHASHSEED`. One regression test mutation-verified (fails when the bug is reinstated, green on revert).\n\n**BUGS I FOUND IN MY OWN CODE** — (1) fixpoint repo-cap trim collapsed a concentrated pool (2 repos × 30 → 2-pair slate); replaced with a feasibility test (`sum min(c_r, floor(n·f)) ≥ n`) that trims once when possible and otherwise leaves the slate intact and reports `repo_cap_respected: false`. (2) trimmed pairs appeared twice in `excluded`. (3) markdown fences broke on issue bodies containing ``` (now length-adaptive).\n\n**EXTRAS** (both serve session integrity): per-rater `review/REVIEW-rater_{1,2}.json` copies — one shared file lets rater 2 read rater 1's verdict, which makes kappa agreement-after-anchoring — plus `--merge-reviews A B` to recombine them mechanically, refusing on two-owner/no-owner files and conflicting splits, and *listing* pairs neither rater reached instead of leaving blanks.\n\n**FILES** created: `seal_prescreen.py`, `REVIEWING-QUICKSTART.md`, `review/` (1,525 files, 12M: SLATE.json + template + 3 rater copies + 350 sheets + INDEX.md + patches/statements, sha256 re-verified against the mined candidates), `tests/test_prescreen_{selection,template,merge}.py`.\n\n**CAVEATS** — `candidates/INDEX.json` is git-**tracked** (not ignored despite the .gitignore line) and is now modified, uncommitted; `review/` is untracked and not ignored. 350 pairs × 2–3 min = 12–17h/rater if read exhaustively; the quickstart gives a pre-committed 80–110-pair plan (~3.5–5.5h each) that reaches 30 sealed + 10 dev, dev-proposed pairs first per seal.py's draw-dev-first rule, and flags that sealing the top-ranked accepted pairs is itself a disclosable selection for `DATASHEET.md`.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>230436</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>95</tool_uses><duration_ms>1439452</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
