{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-08-19T14:33:12.184Z","sessionId":"de272aad-c620-4d71-bbdd-27dd2d3dc8af","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>ae6d1dd687a09ed8c</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_01EvdiLqHuGdCzNDPBLNBqRX</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-suhaan-devenv/f507d58c-285f-4d11-b1d0-201f2a5e172d/tasks/ae6d1dd687a09ed8c.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Fix anonymizer + croissant\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>Fix pass complete. Caveman-ultra report:\n\n**1a (make_release.py):** extended `_SUBSTITUTIONS` (L91-207) with `entire-graph→codegraph-tool`, `agent-brain→agent-memory`, `ENTIRE_PLUGIN_*→MEMHOST_*`, `brain_dir/path/env/cfg/repo`-family→`memhost_*`, filename renames (`full_brain.py→system_x.py`, `test_full_brain.py`, `bin/entire-brain`). Rewrote `_WORD_RE` (L436) to alphanumeric-only tokens so `brainmark.foo`/`brainmark_run` decompose instead of failing as one glued blob — this alone killed ~150 false hits. Also excluded `review/` (raw upstream issue text, same false-positive class as pools/, rater-identifying `REVIEW-rater_*.json`).\n**1b:** `build_release()` now drops `src_root`/`dst_root`, records anonymized relative `path` + `sha256` per file (L246-264).\n**1c:** `pools` added to `DEFAULT_EXCLUDE_DIRS` (L96); new `write_fetch_pools_doc()` generates `release/FETCH_POOLS.md` from `pools/*.meta.json` (dataset id + pinned revision sha).\n**Gate result:** real build `--src brainmark`: **0 hits, 0 files** (was 403/48). Verified via both `build` and `check` subcommands.\n\n**2 (croissant_gen.py):** `contentSize` now `str()` (L124); added `_task_file_set()` FileSet + `source: {fileSet, extract.jsonPath}` on `pair_id`/`split` fields (dropped dishonest `sha256` field — no Croissant fileProperty exists for a content hash); added missing `includes`/`jsonPath`/`fileProperty` JSON-LD context terms (root cause of earlier \"property does not exist\" errors). Found+fixed a **real mlcroissant bug**: an all-null `_provenance` dict sends JSON-LD expansion into infinite recursion — now omits unknown hashes, drops key if empty. `_structural_validate` now strict on both defect classes (field-without-source, non-string contentSize) — regression-tested.\n**mlcroissant (real, installed venv) results:** empty manifest `ok=True`; fixture manifest `ok=True` (was: 3-4 errors / RecursionError).\n\n**3:** REPRODUCIBILITY.md — new \"Known gap: grading on Apple Silicon\" section with the flask-5014 evidence (404→resolved after manual `docker pull --platform linux/amd64`).\n\n**Suite:** 331/331 pass, both with mlcroissant (real validation path exercised) and without (structural fallback) — `python3 -m unittest discover -s brainmark/tests -t . -p \"test_*.py\"`.\n\nFiles touched (all in allowed scope): `release/make_release.py`, `release/croissant_gen.py`, `tests/test_release_sanitization.py`, `tests/test_release_croissant.py`, `README.md`, `REPRODUCIBILITY.md`. Nothing committed.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>403480</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>97</tool_uses><duration_ms>3557402</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
