{"parentUuid":"a36c8f71-40a7-47e8-8749-88a67d2fd925","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_011CeCHEBmKdJ6XMnCc37mdH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Here's exactly what comes out the other end, in plain terms:\n\n## The headline number (the \"score\")\n\n**How much less work does the agent do on task B when it has memory?** Measured as the paired ratio of **pre-edit locate calls** — the Reads/Greps/searches the agent burns *re-finding* what session A already knew, counted before its first edit. That's the pre-registered primary because it's the mechanism: memory's job is to delete re-derivation. If it's real, an accepted-style headline reads:\n\n> *\"With brain memory, agents used **X% fewer locate calls** [95% CI] and **Y% fewer tokens** on follow-up tasks, at equal-or-better solve rate — vs Z%/W% for mem0 on identical inputs.\"*\n\n## The full scorecard per arm (vs no-memory baseline)\n\n| Metric | What it tells you |\n|---|---|\n| locate_calls_pre_edit ratio | re-derivation deleted — **primary** |\n| tokens + $ cost ratio | the efficiency claim — yes, **tokens are a first-class output** |\n| turns, wall-clock | speed |\n| resolved % (Docker tests) | did memory *help or hurt* correctness — graded by SWE-bench's own FAIL_TO_PASS tests, not a judge |\n| prep cost | what the memory itself cost to build (brain vs mem0's LLM ingest) |\n\nAll paired per task-pair, geometric mean + bootstrap CI + median, and the same table for each competitor — so it's simultaneously a **product proof** (brain vs nothing) and a **head-to-head** (brain vs mem0 vs graphify vs cmm on byte-identical inputs).\n\n## \"Is it validated?\" — three separate layers, yes by design\n\n1. **The machinery is validated**: the null test must show ~0% deltas with empty memory before any real run counts — proving any effect we later report comes from memory *content*, not the harness.\n2. **The metric is validated**: humans label a sample of sessions for \"is this call re-deriving session-A knowledge?\" and we report the correlation (construct validity) — if it's weak, the pre-registration forces us to amend *before* the confirmatory runs, publicly and dated.\n3. **The comparison is validated**: placebo arm (real-looking but irrelevant memory) separates \"the content helped\" from \"any context helps\"; symmetry gates prove no arm got different instructions; external Docker grading means success isn't our opinion.\n\n**What it does NOT show**, stated up front: it measures memory utility on same-repo follow-up tasks with harness-delivered memory — not self-directed retrieval, not cross-repo, not long-horizon multi-week memory. Those are v2 claims and the paper says so.\n\nSo after the ladder runs, you hold one sentence for the world: *\"On N sealed pairs, brain memory makes the second session cheaper by X% tokens and Y% search effort without hurting correctness — and here's the same number for every competitor.\"*"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":51,"cache_read_input_tokens":447392,"output_tokens":1591,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":611},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":51,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1591,"cache_read_input_tokens":447392,"cache_creation_input_tokens":51,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":51},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CeCHE6RqtapreV3wfytYD","type":"assistant","uuid":"1f69f660-2954-4381-93a0-a5f2c42a3dfa","timestamp":"2026-08-19T14:40:49.589Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"f507d58c-285f-4d11-b1d0-201f2a5e172d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/p0p1/brainmark","sessionId":"d