{"parentUuid":"b77b93a6-a308-4a3e-bafa-c3f99aa4ef51","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_011CeCHjz8AceHhUGsruDaWw","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Standalone tree is fully green. Writing the clean README (plain style, zero em dashes) and publishing:"}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1216,"cache_read_input_tokens":459124,"output_tokens":2403,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":236},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1216,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2403,"cache_read_input_tokens":459124,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1216,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1216},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CeCHjt2K2YPY6zEdGX6Do","type":"assistant","uuid":"7ecf40ee-8655-49ff-bb10-f844ce9df7a3","timestamp":"2026-08-19T14:47:12.545Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"f507d58c-285f-4d11-b1d0-201f2a5e172d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"de272aad-c620-4d71-bbdd-27dd2d3dc8af","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"quizzical-sniffing-quasar"}
{"parentUuid":"7ecf40ee-8655-49ff-bb10-f844ce9df7a3","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_011CeCHjz8AceHhUGsruDaWw","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01A6o9K3M2CCtxsYacMQMjZd","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-suhaan-devenv/de272aad-c620-4d71-bbdd-27dd2d3dc8af/scratchpad/brainmark-repo && mv README.md HARNESS-LANES.md && cat > README.md <<'EOF'\n# BrainMark\n\nA benchmark that measures whether memory makes a coding agent's second session cheaper.\n\nThe question: an agent solves task A, and its work is captured. A related task B in the same\nrepository comes later. Does a memory system built from session A make session B faster,\ncheaper, and at least as correct as starting cold?\n\n## How it works\n\n1. Task pairs (A, B) are mined from SWE-bench: same repository, A strictly before B,\n   overlapping files, leakage-screened, then sealed by two human raters.\n2. Session A runs once per pair. Its raw transcript is pinned by hash and shared by all arms.\n3. Each memory system ingests the identical session A bytes and produces a memory packet.\n   Packets are hash-pinned and delivered through one identical prompt envelope.\n4. Session B runs once per arm. Every arm gets the same task, same code, same instructions.\n   Only the packet contents differ.\n5. Results are graded by the SWE-bench Docker harness (real tests decide correctness).\n\n## The six arms\n\n| arm | memory packet |\n|---|---|\n| no_brain | none (fixed sentinel text) |\n| full_brain | entire-brain: distill of session A, one frozen retrieval |\n| irrelevant | placebo: a real packet from the wrong session, same size |\n| mem0 | mem0 over the same bytes, top-k retrieval |\n| graphify | graphify over the same bytes |\n| cmm | codebase-memory-mcp over the same bytes |\n\n## What it reports\n\nPrimary (pre-registered): locate_calls_pre_edit, the number of search and read tool calls\nsession B spends before its first edit. Memory should delete re-derivation work; this metric\nmeasures exactly that. Backend-neutral definition in brainmark/mechmetrics.py.\n\nSecondary: tokens and dollar cost, turns, wall clock, resolved rate (Docker tests),\nand each system's own preparation cost.\n\nAll results are paired per task pair: geometric mean ratio, bootstrap confidence interval,\nand median, per arm against no_brain.\n\n## Fairness rules\n\n- Session A bytes are byte-identical across every memory arm.\n- Prompt symmetry is enforced by hash: strip the packet region and every arm's prompt must\n  hash identically. Checked at launch and again at report time.\n- A pair counts only if all arms produce a valid session (symmetric drops).\n- A null test (all arms get empty packets) must show zero deltas before any real run counts.\n- The primary metric, gates, and analysis are frozen in PREREGISTRATION.md before\n  confirmatory runs. Amendments are dated and append-only.\n- Tasks are sealed by two independent raters with Cohen's kappa recorded. Sealed task\n  hashes live in SEAL-MANIFEST.json and the report refuses to aggregate on mismatch.\n\n## Repository layout\n\n- run.py, CONDITIONS.md: the underlying agent-brain harness (packet bounding, delimiter\n  guard, sandboxing, environment sanitization). brainmark imports run.py as a library.\n- brainmark/: the benchmark itself. Start with brainmark/README.md.\n  - mine_pairs.py, pool_loaders.py, clone_repos.py: pair mining from SWE-bench pools.\n  - mine_fresh.py: post-training-cutoff pair mining (contamination robustness split).\n  - seal.py, seal_prescreen.py, SEAL_PROTOCOL.md, REVIEWING-QUICKSTART.md: task sealing.\n  - session_a.py, run_b.py, agents/: session drivers (Azure GPT via codex is primary).\n  - memsources/: one module per arm.\n  - mechmetrics.py, power_analysis.py, report.py, grade.py: metrics and analysis.\n  - validity/: construct-validity labeling protocol for the primary metric.\n  - release/: anonymized release builder and Croissant metadata generator.\n  - PREREGISTRATION.md, DATASHEET.md, REPRODUCIBILITY.md, MAINTENANCE.md, paper/.\n\n## Requirements\n\n- python3 with pytest. Optional: the HF datasets package (pool mining), mlcroissant\n  (metadata validation), Docker (grading).\n- The entire-brain binary for the full_brain arm; competitor packages per COMPETITORS.md.\n- Azure OpenAI credentials for the GPT backends (see brainmark/agents/backends.json).\n- Apple Silicon note: pull grading images with --platform linux/amd64 first\n  (details in brainmark/REPRODUCIBILITY.md).\n\n## Run ladder and rough costs\n\n1. Mine and seal: free. 1,806 verified candidates and a 79-pair fresh split exist;\n   the 350-pair review slate and rater packets are in brainmark/review/.\n2. Null test: about 15 dollars. Proves the machinery is inert.\n3. Pilot: 10 dev pairs, 6 arms, 2 reps on gpt-5.6-sol, about 60 to 120 dollars.\n   Feeds the power analysis that fixes the final sample size.\n4. Confirmatory: about 700 to 1,500 dollars all-GPT, sized by the power analysis.\n\n## Status\n\nAll zero-cost work is complete: 326 tests green, miners deterministic, anonymizer output\npasses its own gate, Croissant metadata validates, Docker grading smoke passed with a gold\npatch. Waiting on the human seal session and the paid run ladder.\n\nHistorical context for the surrounding harness lanes is in HARNESS-LANES.md.\nEOF\ngrep -c \"—\\|–\" README.md; git init -q && git add -A && git commit -q -m \"BrainMark: sealed cross-session memory benchmark for coding agents\" && git log --oneline -1 && du -sh .git","description":"Write clean README and create initial commit"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1216,"cache_read_input_tokens":459124,"output_tokens":2403,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":236},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1216,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2403,"cache_read_input_tokens":459124,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1216,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1216},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CeCHjt2K2YPY6zEdGX6Do","type":"assistant","uuid":"b831c7de-d214-4f41-af6b-df2641f6c8a2","timestamp":"2026-08-19T14:47:38.028Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"f507d58c-285f-4d11-b1d0-201f2a5e172d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv","sessionId":"de272aad-c620-4d71-bbdd-27dd2d3dc8af","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"quizzical-sniffing-quasar"}
