{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-08-19T15:11:56.110Z","sessionId":"de272aad-c620-4d71-bbdd-27dd2d3dc8af","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>ac7b2c867cae42e83</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_011XRy7j6j66ZF6LmPK8FrLk</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-suhaan-devenv/f507d58c-285f-4d11-b1d0-201f2a5e172d/tasks/ac7b2c867cae42e83.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Read report/power/mechmetrics contracts\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>**Dir:** `/Users/suhaan/devenv/p0p1/brainmark/benchmarks/agent-brain/brainmark`\n\n## 1. report.py flags + invocation\n\n- Flags (`report.py:396-407`): `--results` (required), `--config` (default `None`→ `_harness.BRAINMARK_DIR/config.json`), `--arms` (comma list, optional), `--out` (default = `--results`), `--allow-unsealed` (store_true; demotes seal fail to warning; \"not quotable\").\n- `--arms` NOT required: `arms = args.arms.split(\",\") if args.arms else list(config[\"arms\"])` (`report.py:410`).\n- No `grading.json` required: `grading = json.loads(...) if grading_path.is_file() else None` (`report.py:356-357`); absent → `resolved`/McNemar keys just don't appear in `compare()` output.\n- Concrete invocation:\n  `python3 report.py --results results/B/pilot/rep0 --allow-unsealed`\n  (repo has no `SEAL-MANIFEST.json`/`results/` today, so a fresh pilot run WILL fail seal unless `--allow-unsealed` is passed or `seal.py` is run first — `seal.verify()` returns `False, [\"SEAL-MANIFEST.json not found -- the task set was never sealed\"]`, `seal.py:503-505`.)\n- Per-cell files (from `report.py` `collect`/`check_integrity` + `run_b.py:9-19` layout contract):\n  - HARD requirement to be included at all: `meta.json` (`report.py:126-128`, skipped if missing).\n  - HARD requirement to pass the clean gate: `meta.json` with `result_event.total_cost_usd&gt;0` AND non-empty `patch.diff` (`report.py:135,139,142`).\n  - Optional, used if present: `packet.txt`+`packet.sha256` (sha pin recheck, `report.py:85-94`), `prompt.txt` (symmetry recheck, `report.py:96-99`), `stream.jsonl` (fallback source for `mechmetrics` if `meta.json[\"mechmetrics\"]` absent, `report.py:130-133`).\n- **Pooling reps: NOT built into report.py.** `run_b.py:20-27` docstring: `--rep N` writes `rep0..repN-1` under `--out`; each `rep&lt;k&gt;/` is \"itself a complete, valid results root that report.py and grade.py consume with no change at all\" — i.e. you point `report.py --results` at ONE rep dir at a time; there is no multi-rep union/pool flag in `report.py` itself. (`power_analysis.py` DOES pool across reps — see Q5 — but `report.py` does not.)\n\n## 2. Primary metric + full key list + symmetry recheck\n\n- PRIMARY metric name: `\"locate_calls_pre_edit\"` (`report.py:196-198,203`, echoed `mechmetrics.py:3`).\n- Full `compare()` output keys per arm-pair (`report.py:201-261`): `treatment, control, n, primary_metric, ratio_offset, bootstrap_draws, bootstrap_seed, geomean_pct, median_pct, mean_delta, median_delta, bootstrap_ci_pct, straddles_zero, bootstrap_valid_draws, loo_range_pct, cost_geomean_pct, cost_median_pct, cost_n, tokens_geomean_pct, tokens_median_pct, tokens_n, duration_geomean_pct, duration_median_pct, duration_n, turns_geomean_pct, turns_median_pct, turns_n, resolved{treatment,control,...mcnemar}, prep_seconds_median, prep_seconds_total` (+ `error` if no clean pairs).\n- packet-sha recheck: `report.py:85-94` inside `check_integrity`. FAIL text: `f\"{pair_dir.name}/{arm}: packet.sha256 mismatch (pinned {expected[:12]}, on disk {actual[:12]})\"`.\n- prompt-symmetry recheck: `report.py:96-108`, re-derives via `prompts.symmetry_sha(prompt_file.read_text(...))` (`prompts.py:122`) — NEVER trusts a recorded sha file. FAIL text: `f\"{pair_dir.name}: PROMPT SYMMETRY VIOLATION -- \" + \"; \".join(f\"{s[:12]}={a}\" for s,a in groups)`. Triggers when `len(set(shas.values())) &gt; 1` across arms in a pair (`report.py:101-108`).\n\n## 3. Ratio/CI method + output shape\n\n- Paired log-ratios on `(count+1)` (`RATIO_OFFSET=1`, `mechmetrics.py:113`), geometric mean via vendored `graphmark_metrics.geo()`, median via `median_ratio()` (both return fractions, ratio-1) (`report.py:191-215`).\n- Bootstrap: `gm.bootstrap_ci(lambda idx: gm.geo([logs[i] for i in idx]), len(logs), BOOTSTRAP_DRAWS=20000, seed=20260815)` — 20k resamples over pair indices, seeded (`report.py:164,217-219`). `straddles_zero = lo&lt;=0&lt;=hi`.\n- Leave-one-out: `gm.loo_range(logs, gm.geo)` → `loo_range_pct` (`report.py:227-231`).\n- Secondary metrics (`cost, tokens, duration, turns`) get their own paired log-ratio geomean/median, each with its own `n` (skips pairs where control value ≤0, `report.py:167-179,233-243`).\n- Resolved (McNemar): only if `\"resolved\"` key present on both arms for every clean pair (i.e. `grading.json` was supplied) → `gm.mcnemar_exact(...)` (`report.py:245-254`).\n- Top-level `build_report()`/`main()` output shape (written to `REPORT.json`, `report.py:363-393,416`): `arms, pairs_collected, n_clean, clean_pairs, seal_ok, problems, warnings, refused, provenance{config_sha256, prompts_sha256, mechmetrics_sha256, vendored_metrics_sha256, results_dir}`, then if not refused: `headline` (full_brain vs no_brain), `competitors` (full_brain vs each non-baseline/headline arm), `arm_vs_baseline` (each arm vs no_brain). Also writes `REPORT.md` via `render_markdown()` and prints it; exit code `1 if refused else 0` (`report.py:412-419`).\n\n## 4. mechmetrics `locate_calls_pre_edit` (codex)\n\n- Def (`mechmetrics.py:439-449`): count of calls with `kind==\"locate\"` among calls strictly BEFORE the index of the first call with `kind==\"edit\"` (`first_edit(\"kind\")`); if no edit call exists (`no_edit=True`), horizon = full call list.\n- Codex tool call = ONE item; `item.started`+`item.completed` for same id collapsed IN PLACE preserving original order (`mechmetrics.py:314-355`, comment references `run.py:7887`).\n- Codex event/item types read (`mechmetrics.py:116-123,271-311`):\n  - `item.started`/`item.completed`/`item.updated` (`CODEX_ITEM_EVENTS`), plus `turn.completed` for the terminal result event.\n  - `item_type` (or `itemType`) values: `command_execution|local_shell_call|shell_call` → Bash, classified LOCATE/OTHER via `effective_shell_command` + `LOCATE_BASH` regex `^(rg|grep|egrep|git grep|find|ls|cat|head|tail|ag)\\b`; `file_change|patch_apply|apply_patch` → EDIT (\"FileChange\"); `mcp_tool_call` → OTHER (`mcp__&lt;server&gt;__&lt;tool&gt;`); `web_search` → OTHER (\"WebSearch\"); anything else (reasoning/agent_message/todo_list/error) → skipped, not a tool call.\n  - Legacy schema: event has `msg` dict + top-level `id` → `_legacy_type` from `msg[\"type\"]`; prefixes `exec_command*|shell_command*` → shell/LOCATE-check, `patch_apply*|apply_patch*` → EDIT (`CODEX_LEGACY_SHELL`, `CODEX_LEGACY_EDIT`, `mechmetrics.py:122-123,289-295`).\n  - Shell wrapper unwrap: `[\"bash\",\"-lc\",\"rg foo\"]` → `\"rg foo\"` (`effective_shell_command`, `mechmetrics.py:161-180`).\n- Full `session_metrics()` return keys (`mechmetrics.py:474-495`): `backend, locate_calls_pre_edit, locate_ratio_basis, locate_calls_pre_edit_extended, no_edit, first_edit_call_index, tool_calls_total, tool_calls_pre_edit, locate_calls_total, edit_calls_total, tool_histogram, num_turns, duration_ms, total_cost_usd, subtype, is_error, tokens{input_tokens,output_tokens,cache_read_input_tokens,cache_creation_input_tokens,total_tokens,source,cache_read_is_subset_of_input}, has_result_event`.\n\n## 5. power_analysis.py\n\n- Flags (`power_analysis.py:449-462`): mutually exclusive `--report` (pilot/observations JSON) XOR `--results` (results root to `rglob` for `meta.json`); `--treatment` (default `full_brain`), `--control` (default `no_brain`), `--reps` (int, default 1, informational only), `--sealed-n` (int, caps `n`), `--reduction` (float, default `0.15`), `--out`.\n- Invocation for required n: `python3 power_analysis.py --results results/B/pilot --reps 2 --sealed-n 30` (docstring example, `power_analysis.py:38-42`); this one DOES walk ALL `rep*/` subdirs under the given root via `root.rglob(\"meta.json\")` (`observations_from_results`, `power_analysis.py:143-172`) — i.e. it natively pools reps, unlike `report.py`.\n- Input consumed: recorded `meta[\"mechmetrics\"][\"locate_calls_pre_edit\"]` only — never recomputed from `stream.jsonl` (`power_analysis.py:145-149`). `--report` accepts `report.py`'s REPORT.json only if it happens to carry per-pair observations (it currently doesn't — docstring `power_analysis.py:49-51` says results tree is \"the reliable input\").\n- Prints (stdout + optional `--out` file, `power_analysis.py:471-474`): full `analyze()` JSON — `primary_metric, ratio_offset, treatment, control, n_pairs_with_both_arms, pre_committed_rule, observed{mean_log_ratio,median_log_ratio,sd_log_ratio,observed_reduction_pct}, required_n{rule,sd_log_ratio,reduction,delta_log,alpha,power,z_sum,n_exact,n,n_t_corrected,approximation,[sealed_supply,n_capped,underpowered,power_at_sealed_n]}, mde_curve[...], variance_decomposition{...}, sd_by_reps{1..4}, required_n_by_reps{1..4}`.\n\n## 6. sealed/dev pair list + arm-count requirement\n\n- `report.py`: needs `SEAL-MANIFEST.json` only via `seal.verify()` (`report.py:71-74`, `seal.py:500-505`) — a blocking problem unless `--allow-unsealed`. No sealed/dev PAIR LIST is consumed directly by report.py; it just re-hashes `tasks/` against the manifest.\n- `grade.py`: does NOT touch seal/dev pair lists at all — its own `eligible_ids()` all-arms-clean gate (`grade.py:69-86`) derives eligibility purely from the results tree (usd&gt;0 + non-empty patch.diff per arm), independent of `seal.py`.\n- **No hard requirement that all 6 arms be present.** Both `report.py`'s `collect()`/`compare()` and `grade.py`'s `eligible_ids()`/`run()` operate over whatever `arms` list is passed (`--arms` or `config[\"arms\"]`); the \"all-arms-clean\" gate (`report.py:145-148`, `grade.py:84-86`) is `all(cells.get(arm,{}).get(\"clean\") for arm in arms)` — evaluated only over the arms IN THAT LIST. Passing `--arms no_brain,full_brain,mem0` runs report/grade over exactly those 3; the config's default 6-arm list (`config.json:99-106`: `no_brain, full_brain, mem0, graphify, cmm, irrelevant`) is just the default, not enforced.\n\n## 7. Hardcoded `/Users/` paths (will break on Linux VM)\n\nReal code/config hazards (excluding SWE-bench issue-body text in `pools/*.json`, `review/sheets/*.md`, `candidates/fresh/SNAPSHOT.json` which are just dataset content, not paths the tool executes):\n\n- `config.json:4` — `\"graphmark_root\": \"/Users/suhaan/devenv/graphmark/agentic-swebench\"` — consumed by `grade.py:90` (`graphmark_root = pathlib.Path(config[\"graphmark_root\"])`) to locate `grade_tag.sh`. Breaks `grade.py` on any other machine.\n- `config.json:5` — `\"repo_cache\": \"/Users/suhaan/devenv/graphmark/agentic-swebench/repo-cache\"`.\n- `config.json:161` — `\"path\": \"/Users/suhaan/devenv/eg-memharness/bench/memory/patches/0005-cmm-v0.9.0-markdown-sections.patch\"`.\n- `memsources/_competitor.py:167-169` — hardcoded `root = pathlib.Path(\"/Users/suhaan/devenv/eg-memharness/bench/memory/benchmarks/common\")` inside `load_memharness_client()` — used to import mem0/graphify/cmm reference clients at runtime; fails loudly (\"competitor client ... not found\") if absent, so mem0/graphify/cmm arms are dead on a fresh VM until this path exists.\n- `pools/CLONE-LEDGER.json` — many `\"dir\": \"/Users/suhaan/devenv/graphmark/agentic-swebench/repo-cache/&lt;repo&gt;\"` entries (repo clone locations for the mined pool).\n- `review/SLATE.json:59` — `\"candidates_dir\": \"/Users/suhaan/devenv/p0p1/brainmark/benchmarks/agent-brain/brainmark/candidates\"`; also `SLATE.json:31048,31056,31064` — absolute paths to the three `pools/swe_bench*.json` files.\n- `candidates/INDEX.json:4284,4295,4306` — absolute paths under this exact checkout.\n- `vendor/graphmark_metrics.py:4` — comment only: `# Source repo : /Users/suhaan/devenv/graphmark (graphmark)` (provenance note, not executed).\n- `bin/entire-brain` — **not a `/Users/` string bug but worse**: `file bin/entire-brain` → `Mach-O 64-bit executable arm64` (darwin-arm64). This binary will not RUN AT ALL on a Linux VM regardless of any path fix.\n- Not bugs (intentional): `release/make_release.py:206-207` are the sanitizer's OWN regexes that scrub `/Users/...` → `&lt;REPO_ROOT&gt;`/`&lt;HOME&gt;` for release output; `tests/test_release_sanitization.py` just exercises that sanitizer with sample `/Users/` fixtures.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>114526</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>25</tool_uses><duration_ms>151880</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
