{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-08-19T16:44:38.512Z","sessionId":"de272aad-c620-4d71-bbdd-27dd2d3dc8af","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>a9a7a65b9e3bcb8d9</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_01EEk1EgXuyossbyiX5tqmB9</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-suhaan-devenv/f507d58c-285f-4d11-b1d0-201f2a5e172d/tasks/a9a7a65b9e3bcb8d9.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"VM: null test + 3-arm pilot\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>All phases complete. Full ladder ran to the end, well inside budget.\n\n**COST (estimated — codex reports no provider cost; backends.json rates are `UNVERIFIED_PLACEHOLDER`)**\n| phase | cells | usd |\n|---|---|---|\n| smoke (1 cell) | 1 | 0.040 |\n| null v0 (discarded, see below) | 12 | 0.558 |\n| null (final) | 12 | 0.609 |\n| session A | 10 | 0.861 |\n| packets (distill; mem0 not instrumented) | – | 0.149 |\n| pilot B | 60 | 4.018 |\n| **TOTAL** | | **$6.24** vs $120 stop |\n\n**NULL VERDICT — PASS.** Pooled n=6 (pair,rep), full_brain-with-empty-packet vs no_brain: primary −10.91% CI[−41.12,+54.31]; tokens −8.85% CI[−35.17,+19.57]; usd −7.53%; tool_calls_pre_edit −1.94%; duration −2.23%. All five straddle zero, 0 dropped. Per-rep the sign flips (rep0 −45%, rep1 +44%) — run-level noise, which is why pooled is the readout.\n\n**PILOT (n=20 pair-reps, 0 dropped, 0 missing, 60/60 success, 0 empty patches)**\n| vs no_brain | locate_calls_pre_edit [CI] | median | tokens [CI] | median | resolved | prep/pair |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| full_brain | −17.80% [−37.82,+8.03] | 0.0% | −2.29% [−18.29,+15.33] | +0.29% | 14/20 | 3.0 s |\n| mem0 | −1.35% [−20.81,+23.84] | 0.0% | +0.02% [−13.24,+17.47] | −7.57% | 14/20 | 58.8 s |\n| no_brain | — | — | — | — | 15/20 | 0 |\n\nEvery interval includes zero. Exploratory locate-*segments* metric agrees directionally: full_brain 5.70 vs no_brain 6.35 vs mem0 6.65. Grading is saturated — 7/10 instances solved by all three arms in both reps, 2 by nobody, 1 (fmt-3750) by no_brain rep0 only. No correctness headroom here.\n\n**POWER.** Required n = 99 pairs (t-corrected 101) at 1 rep for a 15% reduction, 80% power; 46 at 2 reps, 31 at 3, 23 at 4. Sealed supply of 30 gives power 0.34 — underpowered as designed.\n\n**GATES.** Null ✅. Session A 10/10 valid ✅. Packet gate ✅ (10/10, cross-arm symmetry + build-time pin + sha re-verify). Concurrency held at 12, constant across arms; **0 genuine rate-limit events in 2,079 stream events** (the \"429\" strings in my first audit were grep line numbers in agent output), so no fallback to 8. Netjail blocked 27 `git log` attempts, 0 absolute-path-git bypasses.\n\n**Six blockers found and fixed — five were silent:**\n1. `backends.json` Azure URL 404s on this Foundry resource; correct shape is `&lt;endpoint&gt;/openai/v1`, no `api-version`.\n2. Azure has **no** `gpt-4o-mini` and **no embedding deployment at all**, so mem0's pinned published defaults are undeployable. Forced (not tuning) deviation: extractor `gpt-5.6-sol` (stronger than its default, charitable), embedder local MiniLM-384. Disclosed in config.\n3. entire-brain's distill shells out to `codex` with zero Azure plumbing under `--ignore-user-config` — it would have billed public OpenAI. Fixed with a PATH shim that injects the provider config only when the caller supplied none.\n4. **Neither** entire-brain's distill parser **nor** brainmark's competitor ingest understands codex's ThreadEvent JSONL — both memory arms would have been silent null arms. Fixed by one canonicalization of the pinned A transcript, byte-identical to every arm, raw stream re-pinned beside it.\n5. `mechmetrics` read `item.item_type`; codex 0.148 emits `item.type`, and reports the shell command as the string `/usr/bin/bash -lc '…'`. Both bugs made `locate_calls_pre_edit` identically 0 — the primary metric was dead.\n6. **Fairness defect:** worktrees lived at `&lt;pair&gt;/&lt;ARM&gt;/worktree`, so each agent could read its own arm name from `pwd` (observed in session output), and sibling arms' packets sat two levels up with macOS-only read isolation inert on Linux. Fixed to opaque hashed paths outside the results tree; the null was **re-run** from scratch afterwards (the discarded v0 is the $0.558 line).\n\n**Caveats to carry.** All usd figures are placeholder-priced. mem0 exposes no token counters, so its ingest LLM cost is uninstrumented — 229 messages, 588 s wall-clock total is what can be reported (~20× full_brain's prep). `num_turns` is null for codex, so report.py's turns column is empty. Tasks were gold-stripped before shipping, so no gold patch existed on the VM during sessions. Reports required `--allow-unsealed` (no SEAL-MANIFEST). Nothing was committed or pushed.\n\n**Paths on mem0harness-1:** `~/brainmark-runs/{pilot,null,A,packets}` (pilot has `POOLED_PILOT.json`, `POWER.json`, `AUDIT.json`, `rep{0,1}/REPORT.{json,md}`, `rep{0,1}/grading.json`); `~/bmscripts/` drivers; `~/bmscripts/patches/*.diff` plus `*.orig` beside each patched file for the exact VM-local deltas; `~/graphmark/logs/run_evaluation/` official SWE-bench reports.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>341169</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>148</tool_uses><duration_ms>5918755</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
