 | — | — | — | — | 15/20 | 0 |\n\nEvery interval includes zero. Exploratory locate-*segments* metric agrees directionally: full_brain 5.70 vs no_brain 6.35 vs mem0 6.65. Grading is saturated — 7/10 instances solved by all three arms in both reps, 2 by nobody, 1 (fmt-3750) by no_brain rep0 only. No correctness headroom here.\n\n**POWER.** Required n = 99 pairs (t-corrected 101) at 1 rep for a 15% reduction, 80% power; 46 at 2 reps, 31 at 3, 23 at 4. Sealed supply of 30 gives power 0.34 — underpowered as designed.\n\n**GATES.** Null ✅. Session A 10/10 valid ✅. Packet gate ✅ (10/10, cross-arm symmetry + build-time pin + sha re-verify). Concurrency held at 12, constant across arms; **0 genuine rate-limit events in 2,079 stream events** (the \"429\" strings in my first audit were grep line numbers in agent output), so no fallback to 8. Netjail blocked 27 `git log` attempts, 0 absolute-path-git bypasses.\n\n**Six blockers found and fixed — five were silent:**\n1. `backends.json` Azure URL 404s on this Foundry resource; correct shape is `&lt;endpoint&gt;/openai/v1`, no `api-version`.\n2. Azure has **no** `gpt-4o-mini` and **no embedding deployment at all**, so mem0's pinned published defaults are undeployable. Forced (not tuning) deviation: extractor `gpt-5.6-sol` (stronger than its default, charitable), embedder local MiniLM-384. Disclosed in config.\n3. entire-brain's distill shells out to `codex` with zero Azure plumbing under `--ignore-user-config` — it would have billed public OpenAI. Fixed with a PATH shim that injects the provider config only when the caller supplied none.\n4. **Neither** entire-brain's distill parser **nor** brainmark's competitor ingest understands codex's ThreadEvent JSONL — both memory arms would have been silent null arms. Fixed by one canonicalization of the pinned A transcript, byte-identical to every arm, raw stream re-pinned beside it.\n5. `mechmetrics` read `item.item_type`; codex 0.148 emits `item.type`, and reports the shell command as the string `/usr/bin/bash -lc '…'`. Both bugs made `locate_calls_pre_edit` identically 0 — the primary metric was dead.\n6. **Fairness defect:** worktrees lived at `&lt;pair&gt;/&lt;ARM&gt;/worktree`, so each agent could read its own arm name from `pwd` (observed in session output), and sibling arms' packets sat two levels up with macOS-only read isolation inert on Linux. Fixed to opaque hashed paths outside the results tree; the null was **re-run** from scratch afterwards (the discarded v0 is the $0.558 line).\n\n**Caveats to carry.** All usd figures are placeholder-priced. mem0 exposes no token counters, so its ingest LLM cost is uninstrumented — 229 messages, 588 s wall-clock total is what can be reported (~20× full_brain's prep). `num_turns` is null for codex, so report.py's turns column is empty. Tasks were gold-stripped before shipping, so no gold patch existed on the VM during sessions. Reports required `--allow-unsealed` (no SEAL-MANIFEST). Nothing was committed or pushed.\n\n**Paths on mem0harness-1:** `~/brainmark-runs/{pilot,null,A,packets}` (pilot has `POOLED_PILOT.json`, `POWER.json`, `AUDIT.json`, `rep{0,1}/REPORT.{json,md}`, `rep{0,1}/grading.json`); `~/bmscripts/` drivers; `~/bmscripts/patches/*.diff` plus `*.orig` beside each patched file for the exact VM-local deltas; `~/graphmark/logs/run_evaluation/` official SWE-bench reports.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>341169</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>148</tool_uses><duration_ms>5918755</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"},"uuid":"f2bd70df-740b-4257-a83c-9895923da841","timestamp":"2026-08-19T16:44:38.529Z","permissionMode":"bypassPermissions","origin":{"kind":"task-notification"},"promptSource":"system","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/p0p1/brainmark/benchmarks/agent-brain/brainmark","sessionId":"de272aad-c620-4d71-bbdd-27dd2d3dc8af","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"quizzical-sniffing-quasar"}
{"parentUuid":"f2bd70df-740b-4257-a83c-9895923da841","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_011CeCSiL3irq8txFBB5DcqC","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2928,"cache_read_input_tokens":486102,"output_tokens":3794,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1616},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2928,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3794,"cache_read_input_tokens":486102,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2928,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2928},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CeCSiC5VjpVQ2xj15MeQd","type":"assistant","uuid":"7e469018-716e-4df8-809c-844f497c4bcb","timestamp":"2026-08-19T16:45:12.067Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"f507d58c-285f-4d11-b1d0-201f2a5e172d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/p0p1/brainmark/benchmarks/agent-brain/brainmark","sessionId":"de272aad-c620-4d71-bbdd-27dd2d3dc8af","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"quizzical-sniffing-quasar"}
{"parentUuid":"7e469018-716e-4df8-809c-844f497c4bcb","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_011CeCSiL3irq8txFBB5DcqC","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# 🎉 Pilot complete — the whole ladder ran clean, and it cost $6.24\n\n(vs the $50–95 estimate — gpt-5.6-sol via Azure is far cheaper than budgeted, with the caveat that codex reports no cost so pricing is computed from placeholder rates.)\n\n## The verdicts\n\n**Null test: PASS.** With empty memory packets, every metric straddles zero. The machinery is proven inert — any effect we measure from here is memory content, not harness.\n\n**Pilot (10 pairs × 3 arms × 2 reps, 60/60 success, zero drops):**\n\n| vs no-memory baseline | locate calls pre-edit | tokens | resolved |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| **brain** | **−17.8%** [−37.8, +8.0] | −2.3% | 14/20 |\n| mem0 | −1.4% [−20.8, +23.8] | +0.0% | 14/20 |\n| baseline | — | — | 15/20 |\n\nRead this exactly as pre-registered: **direction favors the brain** (−17.8% re-derivation work vs mem0's −1.4%, and an independent exploratory metric agrees), but **every interval includes zero — this is not a claimable win at n=20**, and our own doctrine forbids quoting deltas before full n. That's what the pilot is *for*. Two bonus product facts: brain prep is **3.0s/pair vs mem0's 58.8s (~20×)**, and grading is saturated on these dev pairs (7/10 solved by everyone) — so correctness won't discriminate; the mechanism and token metrics carry the paper, as designed.\n\n**Power analysis**: 80% power for a 15% effect needs **46 pairs at 2 reps** (or ~99 at 1 rep). Sealed-supply target is 150–300, so comfortably reachable. At the measured burn rate, the confirmatory run projects to **~$50–150, not the $700–1,500 I estimated** — the money barrier basically evaporated.\n\n## The pilot also did its other job: it caught six harness bugs, five silent\n\nThe worst ones: the primary metric was **returning zero for every session** (codex changed a field name), both memory arms would have run as **silent empty arms** (transcript format mismatch), and agents could **read their own arm name from their working directory path** — a genuine fairness leak, after which the operator re-ran the null from scratch. Also: entire-brain's distill would have quietly billed public OpenAI instead of Azure — that's a real product bug worth fixing upstream. Every withdrawn headline in our history died of exactly this class of bug; this time they died in the $6 pilot instead of the paper.\n\n## What happens next\n\n1. **Now ($0, me)**: back-porting the six VM fixes into the brainmark repo + PR #88 — they live only as patches on the VM right now.\n2. **You**: the seal session (you + teammate) is now the *only* blocker for the confirmatory run — ~46+ sealed pairs at 2 reps is the target the power analysis set.\n3. **Then (~$50–150, your go)**: the confirmatory run — where −17.8% either becomes a real, publishable number or honestly dies.\n\nDispatching the backport now."}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2928,"cache_read_input_tokens":486102,"output_tokens":3794,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":1616},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2928,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3794,"cache_read_input_tokens":486102,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2928,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2928},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CeCSiC5VjpVQ2xj15MeQd","type":"assistant","uuid":"37e402dd-0339-428e-8ccf-2f6954616d11","timestamp":"2026-08-19T16:45:26.021Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"f507d58c-285f-4d11-b1d0-201f2a5e172d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suha