{"parentUuid":"a382615a-5f61-4947-a9a5-fa3a416ae618","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_011CeCU7Uzzcyg4KE7JnVMZs","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01RBMkdPyDEZAnm5fnPKsHtZ","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Build brain setup onboarding","subagent_type":"general-purpose","model":"opus","prompt":"Build the brain onboarding feature in /Users/suhaan/devenv/p0p1/brain-onboarding (worktree of entire-brain, branch feat/brain-setup-onboarding, clean, off origin/main). Use rtk. This is a real product feature with an agreed UX plan — implement it COMPLETELY.\n\nTHE PROBLEM (from the CEO): brain onboarding is confusing — three separate setup paths (brain without agent, with agent, facts extraction); the agent pass is O(sessions) so it always runs long; people forget to run it.\n\nTHE AGREED PLAN — one command `entire-brain setup` (also reachable as `entire brain setup` via the plugin):\n1. INSTANT PHASE (blocking, seconds, $0): build the deterministic core — semantic/graph index + session export/overlay (the existing deterministic refresh path that `watch` calls with seed agent \"none\"). Brain is immediately queryable when this returns. Print a clean, friendly progress line per step.\n2. BACKGROUND BACKFILL: kick off fact extraction (distill) over past sessions NEWEST FIRST, detached (setsid/nohup pattern or the repo's existing background convention), so the prompt returns immediately. Token work must respect the existing gates: cheap --model/--effort defaults, --budget cap, persisted cursor (never re-spend). If no agent CLI is on PATH or sessions are absent, skip gracefully with one clear line.\n3. DAEMON (the piece the user explicitly wants): register the repo into a workspace (create default workspace if none; `workspace create`/`workspace add` exist — workspace.go:279,305) and ensure ONE `workspace watch` daemon is running machine-wide (workspace.go:332 \"Keep every repo in a workspace fresh automatically\"). Build the install glue: `setup` writes + loads a launchd plist on darwin (~/Library/LaunchAgents/io.entire.brain-watch.plist) / a systemd user unit on linux (~/.config/systemd/user/entire-brain-watch.service), pointing at `entire-brain workspace watch <ws>` with the token-frugal flags (deterministic refresh free; distill gated by --distill-every/--budget). Idempotent: re-running setup detects the existing daemon and repo registration. Also `setup --no-daemon` opt-out and a `setup --uninstall-daemon`.\n4. SESSION-END HOOK: already built (hook_cmd.go `hook session-end`) — setup should wire/verify whatever host-agent hook registration exists (check how the plugins/hooks get registered — .claude/settings.json wiring in the repo README/docs) and report its status rather than duplicating it.\n5. PROGRESS: extend the status/dash surface (find the existing status command; there is doctor.go + dash.go) so `entire-brain status` (or the closest existing verb — do NOT create a duplicate) shows backfill progress as \"facts: <distilled>/<total> sessions distilled\" + daemon health (running/not, last tick) + instant-phase component freshness. Doctor stays the deep health check.\n\nEXISTING CODE TO REUSE (verified anchors): watch.go (watchCommandOptions, defaultWatchOptions, cursor, gating — deterministic refresh free / agent steps gated); workspace.go (create/add/watch); hook_cmd.go:76 session-end; distill_cmd.go (distill --session, agent selection); doctor.go. Follow the repo's cobra command idiom, test isolation conventions, and options plumbing.\n\nNEWEST-FIRST BACKFILL: distill's session selection must run newest sessions first so the most useful facts land early — check how distill orders sessions today; if oldest-first or unordered, add the ordering (bounded change, flag-gated default for setup's invocation if changing global default is risky).\n\nVERIFY (non-negotiable):\n- Unit tests for: setup instant-phase orchestration (fake runner), idempotent re-run, daemon plist/unit generation (golden file, both platforms via GOOS-independent codepaths), workspace registration, --no-daemon, backfill kick-off (stubbed agent), status progress counters (fixture brain dir with N sessions / M distilled).\n- LIVE smoke on THIS machine (darwin, $0): run `setup --no-daemon` (and then with daemon incl. launchctl load + verify + uninstall) inside a THROWAWAY temp git repo with isolated ENTIRE_PLUGIN_* env dirs — never touch the real user config/daemon. Prove: instant phase < 60s on the small repo, queryable immediately after, status shows sane counters. Keep any launchctl labels test-unique and clean them up.\n- MUTATION-verify 2 behaviors: (a) break idempotence (setup re-registers/duplicates daemon) → test fails; (b) break newest-first ordering → its test fails. State results.\n- `go build ./... && go test ./...` green; gofmt/vet clean.\nCommit on the branch in logical commits (NO AI footers/Co-Authored-By). Do NOT push.\nReport caveman-ultra: files+lines, command UX transcript of the live smoke (the actual printed lines), test totals, mutation results, shas. Max 25 lines."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1658,"cache_read_input_tokens":496520,"output_tokens":1902,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1658,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1902,"cache_read_input_tokens":496520,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1658,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1658},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CeCU7MjBYyqiaBqEiv5Lp","type":"assistant","uuid":"86ee049c-0599-484f-b238-5d8dc44c53f3","timestamp":"2026-08-19T17:03:32.526Z","eff