{"parentUuid":"89053850-78c9-41c8-8697-eddc0204f7f9","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"88e62cb7-7512-4953-baa2-36775df0a95b","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>a23740e1de548c5ff</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>REDACTED</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-suhaan-devenv/f507d58c-285f-4d11-b1d0-201f2a5e172d/tasks/a23740e1de548c5ff.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Backport VM pilot fixes\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>All six fixes ported, both repos green and pushed.\n\n```\nVM patches: 4 diffs + 5 drivers fetched. All 6 mapped. Skipped VM-env-only: bmenv.sh, mkconfig.py\npaths, grade_tag.sh.vm, pipsetup/clone10 (apt/venv/VM paths).\n\n1 Azure URL   PORTED  backends.json:23 /openai/v1 + send_api_version:false (:18-20);\n              codex_adapter.py:125,155,167. Explicit opt-out, not the VM's fake-env-name hack —\n              a stray AZURE_AI_API_VERSION would else re-404.\n2 mem0 dev.   PORTED  config.json:133-160 (_llm/_embedder_forced_deviation); COMPETITORS.md:94\n              \"Forced deviations\" + pin table + tuning-log carve-out; mem0_source.py:79\n              provider_block, :50 expand_env (${VAR}, hard-fail), :250 observed_provenance.\n3 distill shim PORTED agents/codex_provider_shim.py (new, documented helper, not a script hack);\n              full_brain.py:79 install_distill_provider_shim, invoked at :283. Drift test caught a\n              REAL BUG: shim quoted provider key inside the TOML path (model_providers.\"azure\".name).\n4 transcript  PORTED  transcript_canon.py (new) :204 canonicalize, :120 translate, :262\n              canonicalize_dir (post-hoc, idempotent, pin-verified); session_a.py:149 wiring.\n              Reuses mechmetrics.effective_shell_command — one unwrap definition, not two.\n5 mechmetrics PORTED  mechmetrics.py:315 item.type fallback (_legacy-guarded), :177 string\n              \"/usr/bin/bash -lc\" unwrap. Fixture codex_stream_0148_shape.jsonl (both defects).\n              MUTATION-VERIFIED: reverting either fix alone reddens the suite.\n6 fairness    PORTED  run_b.py:377 worktree_path / :367 worktree_key (sha256[:16]),\n              :416 call, :438-439 meta. MUTATION-VERIFIED (in-cell layout → 6 failures).\n\nNew tests: Codex0148ShapeTest{test_primary_metric_is_nonzero_on_a_0148_stream,\ntest_item_kind_is_read_from_item_dot_type, test_string_bash_wrapper_is_unwrapped, +2};\nRunBDryRunTest.test_worktree_path_leaks_neither_the_arm_name_nor_the_results_root (asserts the cwd\nthe stub OBSERVED, not just meta); WorktreePathTest (5); test_codex_provider_shim.py (10, shim really\nexecuted vs fake codex); test_transcript_canon.py (15, checked against BOTH consumers' parse rules);\nMem0ForcedDeviationTest (6); 2 new Azure-shape tests.\n\nSuites: entire-brain 331 → 376 passed (+45). standalone 326+5skip → 371 passed +5 skip (+45; the 5\nskips are entire-brain-binary tests, absent there).\nSHAs: entire-brain feat/brainmark b7717b7a, 904eddab (pushed).\n      entirehq/brainmark main 97b9832c, 095a8054 (pushed).\n```\n\nTwo things worth flagging: the shim's one-source-of-truth test caught a genuine defect the VM version also has (`model_providers.\"azure\".name` — codex fails that by falling back, not erroring), so the VM's shim was likely running distill unconfigured; and fix 1 is deliberately not a byte-port — I used an explicit `send_api_version: false` rather than the VM's `AZURE_AI_API_VERSION_UNUSED` sentinel, since that hack breaks the moment a real resource wants an api-version.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>217383</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>131</tool_uses><duration_ms>1284169</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"},"uuid":"07d4a997-41fe-4bd3-8577-415603937ba8","timestamp":"2026-08-19T17:07:06.631Z","permissionMode":"bypassPermissions","origin":{"kind":"task-notification"},"promptSource":"system","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/p0p1/brainmark","sessionId":"de272aad-c620-4d71-bbdd-27dd2d3dc8af","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"quizzical-sniffing-quasar"}
