{"parentUuid":"a2296df8-3d69-4af4-8436-8b04489c9b19","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_011CeCWjrvLxW9dzN2qF3vbm","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":954,"cache_read_input_tokens":506634,"output_tokens":1064,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":63},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":954,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1064,"cache_read_input_tokens":506634,"cache_creation_input_tokens":954,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":954},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CeCWjkMTKkUhNvqiiYwgp","type":"assistant","uuid":"66d23a4e-61b4-4799-bb97-10317dd27c4c","timestamp":"2026-08-19T17:37:36.907Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"f507d58c-285f-4d11-b1d0-201f2a5e172d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/p0p1/brainmark","sessionId":"de272aad-c620-4d71-bbdd-27dd2d3dc8af","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"quizzical-sniffing-quasar"}
{"parentUuid":"66d23a4e-61b4-4799-bb97-10317dd27c4c","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_011CeCWjrvLxW9dzN2qF3vbm","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Plain explanations of both:\n\n## entire-api #242 — the brain gets a server (P1's whole server side)\n\nToday the brain lives only on your laptop. This PR adds everything the *hosted* brain needs inside the per-jurisdiction api cells:\n\n- **A store for brain artifacts**: content-addressed blobs, each encrypted with its own fresh key (AES-256-GCM, KMS-wrapped). Retract a fact and its key is destroyed — \"crypto-shred,\" meaning the data is provably unreadable afterwards.\n- **The sync endpoint**: your laptop's brain pushes/pulls the shared fact-set under compare-and-swap on a branch head. Two teammates racing? Loser gets a 412, re-reads, re-merges. The merge always happens on the client — the server only stores bytes and moves pointers.\n- **The proposal queue**: the shared review workflow (one member proposes a fact change, another settles it), stored as one CAS'd blob per branch — this is the wire we reconciled and live-round-trip-verified against #85.\n- **Remote query**: a teammate's agent can query the shared brain over HTTP with no local clone.\n- **Auth/tenancy**: org→project→repo SpiceDB checks, fail-closed twice; migrations are additive-only.\n\nMerged, it ships **dormant** — every endpoint returns 503 until `ENTIRE_BRAIN_HOSTED_ENABLED=true` is set, and rollback is unsetting one env var. What it unlocks: *one person's agent learns something, every teammate's agent knows it.* That's P1, and P2's gate.\n\n## cli #2041 — checkpoints learn *what code they changed* (keystone write path)\n\nToday a checkpoint knows which *files* changed. This PR makes each checkpoint also record which **functions/classes/types** changed — a small `entity_deltas.json` riding inside the checkpoint tree.\n\n- At checkpoint time, the cli spawns a detached background child; the git hook itself only pays a process-spawn (measured — the earlier synchronous design cost 3.5s per commit and we killed it).\n- The child runs `entire-graph diff` between the session's base and head, filters to the session's own files, and backfills the result into the already-committed checkpoint — with a compare-and-swap ref advance so it can *never* clobber a concurrent checkpoint, and a lock handshake so it never aborts a user's push.\n- **Off by default** (settings/env gate), silently skips if the graph binary isn't installed, capped at 8MB, and structurally unable to fail checkpoint creation.\n\nWhat it unlocks: entity deltas travel *with* the checkpoint to the server, so the hosted side can answer \"which checkpoints changed `verifyToken`?\" without anyone's laptop — feeding brain #87's index today and P3's entity-claims/conflict-detection later.\n\nIn one line each: **#242 = the brain becomes shared infrastructure; #2041 = every checkpoint starts carrying its meaning.**"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":954,"cache_read_input_tokens":506634,"output_tokens":1064,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":63},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":954,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1064,"cache_read_input_tokens":506634,"cache_creation_input_tokens":954,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":954},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CeCWjkMTKkUhNvqiiYwgp","type":"assistant","uuid":"e9bc9940-253c-4f9c-8255-9237aec12199","timestamp":"2026-08-19T17:37:51.671Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"f507d58c-285f-4d11-b1d0-201f2a5e172d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/p0p1/brainmark","sessionId":"de272aad-c620-4d71-bbdd-27dd2d3dc8af","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"quizzical-sniffing-quasar"}
