{"parentUuid":"21cbb84a-7634-4dcc-b8e8-0ef0fe8c50b6","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_011CeCXEoHNprjVUW5xtPZwA","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":402,"cache_read_input_tokens":525003,"output_tokens":1468,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":445},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":402,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1468,"cache_read_input_tokens":525003,"cache_creation_input_tokens":402,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":402},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CeCXEdWW42Za3sASAykXz","type":"assistant","uuid":"cef23a3b-9c32-4028-885f-9db2f454b7d8","timestamp":"2026-08-19T17:44:14.649Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"f507d58c-285f-4d11-b1d0-201f2a5e172d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/p0p1/brainmark","sessionId":"de272aad-c620-4d71-bbdd-27dd2d3dc8af","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"quizzical-sniffing-quasar"}
{"parentUuid":"cef23a3b-9c32-4028-885f-9db2f454b7d8","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_011CeCXEoHNprjVUW5xtPZwA","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Noted on the roadmap status, I'll treat the repo and PR state as the only truth. Here are the two messages, clean, no em dashes, ready to paste:\n\n**Message 1, for the cli PR (#2041):**\n\n> Hey, could you review and merge cli PR #2041 when you get a chance?\n> https://github.com/entireio/cli/pull/2041\n>\n> It records which code entities (functions, classes, types) each checkpoint changed, as an entity_deltas.json inside the checkpoint tree. This is the write-path half of the semantic index work: it lets us answer \"which checkpoints touched this function\" without re-parsing history, and it feeds the entity index in entire-brain.\n>\n> Safety properties, since this touches the checkpoint path:\n> - Off by default. Gated behind a settings key plus an env override, so nothing changes for anyone until it is explicitly enabled.\n> - Nothing runs in the git hook. The hook only spawns a detached background child; the compute happens after the hook returns. Measured hook cost is a process spawn.\n> - The backfill advances the checkpoint ref with compare-and-swap plus bounded retries, so it can never orphan a concurrent checkpoint, and it takes a lock during the OPF pre-push rewrite so it can never abort a push.\n> - Any failure (graph binary missing, timeout, bad output) is a silent skip. Checkpoint creation cannot fail because of it.\n> - mise run check is green (lint, unit plus integration with race, canary e2e), and the race and rewrite interactions have dedicated deterministic tests.\n>\n> Happy to walk through any part of it.\n\n**Message 2, for the api PR (#242):**\n\n> Hey, could you review and approve entire-api PR #242? It needs one approval to merge.\n> https://github.com/entirehq/entire-api/pull/242\n>\n> This is the server side of the hosted brain (P1): the encrypted fact store with per-object keys and crypto-shred, compare-and-swap fact sync per branch, the shared proposal queue, remote query, and SpiceDB tenancy checks.\n>\n> Why it is safe to merge now:\n> - It ships completely dormant. Every endpoint fails closed with 503 until ENTIRE_BRAIN_HOSTED_ENABLED=true is set on a cell, and rollback is unsetting that one flag.\n> - Migrations are additive only.\n> - No new bucket, key, IAM policy, or credentials. It reuses the session-share cipher, bucket, and KMS that are already live.\n> - The wire contract is verified end to end: the real entire-brain client binary ran a full round trip against this server (sync, CAS advance, proposal read) in an automated test, not just against fakes.\n> - The client PR on the brain side is ready and merges independently; neither breaks anything while waiting for the other.\n>\n> Happy to demo the round trip or answer anything.\n\nBoth are self-contained and make no claims that depend on the roadmap doc. Want any tone or length changes, or should I also draft the matching one-liner for whoever merges the graph PR #114?"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":402,"cache_read_input_tokens":525003,"output_tokens":1468,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":445},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":402,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1468,"cache_read_input_tokens":525003,"cache_creation_input_tokens":402,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":402},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CeCXEdWW42Za3sASAykXz","type":"assistant","uuid":"1f7288e7-48b2-41d5-97a6-1b8d18d4b6db","timestamp":"2026-08-19T17:44:28.836Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id"