{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-08-19T17:47:42.548Z","sessionId":"de272aad-c620-4d71-bbdd-27dd2d3dc8af","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>ae88f396e6c3675e7</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>REDACTED</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-suhaan-devenv/f507d58c-285f-4d11-b1d0-201f2a5e172d/tasks/ae88f396e6c3675e7.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Skeptic: onboarding review\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>All green: `go build` 0, `go vet` 0, `go test ./...` **11 pkgs ok, 0 fail, exit 0** (internal/cli 156s).\n\n**1 DAEMON GLUE — REFUTED-A-DEFECT (×5)**\n- `setup.go:494` `--budget 1` + `workspace.go:377` `agentCalls := 0` outside the loop + `watch.go:362` `agentCalls &gt;= budget` ⇒ the machine-wide daemon distills **once, for one repo, ever**. KeepAlive/Restart=always means it never exits, so the counter never resets. Core claim \"keeps every member fresh\" is false for facts. `setup.go:52-54` comment (\"one per --distill-every window\") contradicts `watch.go:114`.\n- `setup.go:479` `LogPath` is **per-repo** but the plist/label is machine-wide ⇒ every new repo's `setup` renders different Contents → `Current=false` → unload+load, restarting the live daemon; repo A's `status` then reports the daemon not-current. Ping-pong.\n- `workspace.go:525-559` `runWorkspaceAdd` = load→modify→write with **no lock**. Two concurrent `setup`s = lost update; one repo silently absent from the workspace while setup reports success.\n- ENTIRE_PLUGIN_* isolation does **not** cover the daemon: unit path comes from `os.UserHomeDir()`/`XDG_CONFIG_HOME` (`setup_daemon.go:106,114`) and `launchctl load -w` runs for real. A sandboxed/smoke run still installs+reloads the user's real daemon.\n- `setup_daemon.go:77` `launchdLabel` is not injective (`foo` and `entire-foo` → same label+path) despite the one-to-one comment; `setup_daemon.go:202,208` WorkingDirectory/StandardOutput unquoted while ExecStart/Environment are.\n- VERIFIED-OK: missing launchctl/systemctl → warning, file left, self-heals next run; dead-binary plist → Contents mismatch → rewritten; `--uninstall-daemon` intentionally leaves workspace membership (by design, not orphaning state it owns).\n\n**2 BACKFILL — mixed**\n- VERIFIED-OK: `setup_spawn_unix.go:13` Setsid + stdio→log/devnull + `Release()`; ordering reaches selection (`distill_cmd.go:744` sorted once → straight into `startSessionPrefetch`, no re-sort; budget enforced in the single dispatcher at `:283` **after** skip/cached, never dispatches deferred).\n- REFUTED-A-DEFECT: no gate vs. concurrent distill. `setup.go:253` spawns the detached pass, then `:276` installs a `--distill` daemon whose **first tick spends immediately** (zero cursor). Brain write lock only wraps the flush (`distill_cmd.go:880,1053`), so both read the same `prevCache` and **make duplicate agent calls on the same sessions**. Setup creates this by construction.\n- REFUTED-A-DEFECT: `runSetupBackfill` (`setup.go:355`) never consults `readSetupBackfillState`/`processAlive` (both exist, used only by status) ⇒ re-running `setup` mid-backfill spawns a **second** one. Violates \"every phase is idempotent\" (`setup.go:37`).\n- `--backfill-budget` defaults to **0 = whole corpus** (`setup.go:181`): bare `setup` starts an unattended, uncapped LLM pass with no confirmation. Not \"budget-gated\"; only re-spend is cache-gated.\n\n**3 CONCURRENCY FIX — VERIFIED-OK mechanically, REFUTED on disclosure**\n`watch.go:551` clamps `jobs&lt;=0→1`; `hook_cmd.go:145` sets 4. No zero reaches the pipeline; `sem` only built when &gt;1, `workAhead` floored at 2 — no divide/deadlock. But it is a **live token-spend activation**: both callers previously died at `distill_cmd.go:598` before any agent call. Existing `watch --distill` users and every wired session-end hook now spend (hook at concurrency 4). **Zero docs**: `git diff origin/main..HEAD -- README.md docs/` is empty, no CHANGELOG exists.\n\n**4 STATUS — one defect** `setup_status.go:277` `hookSettingsDeclareSessionEnd` returns true for **any** SessionEnd hook with a non-empty command — never checks it is entire's. A user with any other SessionEnd hook gets \"already wired\" and is never told to run `entire enable`. `entire` CLI absence is never probed. Counters at sessions=0 / manifest-missing / mid-flight: VERIFIED-OK (`Pending()` clamp, dead-pid test real). Minor: pid-reuse false positive; `Running` forced false once `Pending()==0`.\n\n**5 IDEMPOTENCE — one defect** `setup.go:626-631` compares to the default **value** instead of `Flags().Changed` ⇒ `setup --workspace default` on a repo recorded as `team` silently keeps `team` (same for `--daemon-name`). Also: interval/distill-every/model/effort are not recorded, so a bare re-run silently reverts a customized daemon; and changing `--daemon-name` writes a new unit without unloading the old one → **two** daemons.\n\n**6 TESTS — honest overall, 4 gaps** `TestSetupInstallsExactlyOneDaemonAcrossRuns` is **not** vacuous (asserts `==1` twice plus the \"already running\" line; real install covered separately by `TestInstallDaemonWritesUnitAndLoadsItIdempotently`, which counts unload/load `==2` each on real files). `TestRunDistillMaxSessionsDefersRatherThanSkips` is strong (real run, real cache, follow-up asserts only `old`). Gaps: `TestSetupChildEnvCarriesPluginDirs` tests `setupPluginEnv`, never `setupChildEnv`'s `os.Environ()` merge; `TestInProcessDistillOptionsPassTheConcurrencyGuard` covers only `watchDistillOptions`, not the hook literal it names; `TestSetupRemembersItsIdentitiesForLaterReads` tests \"explicit wins\" only with a non-default value — dodging the §5 bug; `TestBrainWatchDaemonArgsStayTokenFrugal` mirrors the implementation strings and cannot catch the budget-1 semantics. Suite isolation is clean (`t.Setenv(\"HOME\", tmp)` + all daemon steps injected — nothing touches real launchd).\n\n**VERDICT: NO-SHIP.** Blockers: budget-1 one-shot daemon (§1), setup-induced concurrent double-distill (§2), re-entrant backfill spawn (§2), unlocked workspace manifest (§1), undocumented token-spend activation (§3). Fix-first set is small: raise/replace `--budget`, guard the backfill on a live pid + a distill-level lock, lock `runWorkspaceAdd`, move `LogPath` out of the per-repo dir, switch record defaults to `Flags().Changed`, tighten the SessionEnd matcher, and write the docs.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>169606</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>49</tool_uses><duration_ms>457856</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
