{"parentUuid":"0ce8b62d-af79-48c9-829f-de75d4ab8d45","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_011CeCXXFwT1pZnoZveLUrN5","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The onboarding skeptic came back **NO-SHIP with five blockers** — all real, all fixable, and two would have burned actual money or broken the core promise: the machine-wide daemon had `--budget 1` with a never-resetting counter (it would distill **once, ever, for one repo** — the exact opposite of \"keeps every repo fresh\"), and `setup` itself creates a duplicate-spend race (detached backfill + the daemon's first tick both distill the same sessions). Plus: bare `setup` starts an *uncapped* LLM pass by default, concurrent setups can lose workspace registrations, and the pre-existing-bug fix silently *activates* token spending for existing hook users with zero documentation.\n\nDispatching the fix pass:"}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4462,"cache_read_input_tokens":525405,"output_tokens":2711,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":651},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4462,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2711,"cache_read_input_tokens":525405,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4462,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4462},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CeCXX8yjtTqnZ6tK13DBW","type":"assistant","uuid":"6dc80325-dc73-4997-a8f9-573ef1c823de","timestamp":"2026-08-19T17:48:03.789Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"f507d58c-285f-4d11-b1d0-201f2a5e172d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/p0p1/brainmark","sessionId":"de272aad-c620-4d71-bbdd-27dd2d3dc8af","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"quizzical-sniffing-quasar"}
{"parentUuid":"6dc80325-dc73-4997-a8f9-573ef1c823de","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_011CeCXXFwT1pZnoZveLUrN5","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_016HysH8SCY7UqTsYt89h7CB","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Fix onboarding blockers","subagent_type":"general-purpose","model":"opus","prompt":"FIX PASS in /Users/suhaan/devenv/p0p1/brain-onboarding (entire-brain, branch feat/brain-setup-onboarding, 5 commits). Use rtk. An adversarial review confirmed these defects; fix ALL, do not re-litigate. Files: setup.go, setup_daemon.go, setup_status.go, setup_spawn*.go, workspace.go, watch.go, distill_cmd.go, docs.\n\nBLOCKERS:\n1. Daemon one-shot bug: setup.go:494 passes --budget 1 and watch.go:377 counts agentCalls process-lifetime (KeepAlive daemon never exits → never resets) → machine-wide daemon distills once ever. Fix semantics: the daemon must allow one gated agent run per --distill-every window per repo, forever. Either make the budget window-scoped in the watch loop (reset agentCalls when the distill-every window rolls — check cursor semantics) or drop --budget from the daemon args and rely on --distill-every + cursor (the durable anti-re-spend guard per watch.go's own docs). Update the misleading comment at setup.go:52-54. TEST: simulated daemon loop over 3 windows × 2 repos asserts 6 gated runs, not 1.\n2. Setup-induced double-distill: setup.go:253 spawns the detached backfill AND :276 installs a --distill daemon whose first tick spends immediately; brain write lock only wraps the flush → duplicate agent calls on the same sessions. Fix: a distill-level cross-process guard — e.g. a distill lockfile per brain dir held for the whole pass (TryLock semantics: second comer skips with a log line), used by BOTH the backfill child and watch's distill step. TEST: two concurrent distill passes over one brain dir → exactly one spends, other skips cleanly.\n3. Re-entrant backfill: runSetupBackfill (setup.go:355) never checks readSetupBackfillState/processAlive → rerunning setup mid-backfill spawns a second pass. Fix: consult state+pid first; if alive, report progress and skip. TEST included.\n4. Uncapped default spend: --backfill-budget default 0 = whole corpus on bare `setup`. Change default to a sane cap (e.g. 25 sessions) with --backfill-budget 0 meaning explicit unlimited, and print what the cap did + how to lift it.\n5. Unlocked workspace manifest: workspace.go:525-559 read-modify-write with no lock → concurrent setups lose registrations. Add the same lockfile discipline used elsewhere in the repo (look at factgitmeta's lock or state locks). TEST: two concurrent adds both persist.\n6. Daemon churn: setup.go:479 per-repo LogPath inside a machine-wide plist → every new repo's setup sees Contents!=Current → unload/load restart ping-pong + status false-negatives. Move the daemon log to a machine-level location (state dir, not per-repo), so plist contents are repo-independent. TEST: render for two repos → byte-identical unit.\n7. Token-spend activation disclosure: the concurrency fix (172fe971) makes previously-dead watch --distill and session-end distill paths actually spend. Document loudly: README section for setup + a note in the command help + CHANGELOG.md entry (create if absent) describing the behavior change and the gates that bound it.\n\nSMALLER (all): status hook matcher must verify the SessionEnd command is entire's (setup_status.go:277) and probe entire CLI presence; identity record: use Flags().Changed not value-vs-default comparison (setup.go:626-631), record interval/distill-every/model/effort so re-runs don't silently revert customizations (unchanged unless flag passed), and changing --daemon-name unloads the old unit before writing the new; launchdLabel injectivity (setup_daemon.go:77) — hash-suffix the label; quote WorkingDirectory/StandardOutput in the systemd unit (:202,208); daemon unit path should respect the plugin/state env override so sandboxed runs cannot touch the real user's LaunchAgents even with real HOME (add an env knob + use it in tests/smoke); close the 4 test gaps named in review (setupChildEnv os.Environ merge, hook literal guard coverage, explicit-default flag case, budget-semantics test replacing the string-mirror).\n\nVERIFY: full `go test ./...` green, gofmt/vet clean; re-run the live smoke (isolated HOME + env knob) proving: one daemon, no restart on second repo setup, backfill skip-if-running, capped default backfill. MUTATIONS: re-introduce budget-1 → window test fails; remove the distill lock → concurrency test fails. Amend into the existing commit structure (honest messages, NO AI footers). Do NOT push.\nReport caveman-ultra: per blocker done+file:line, test names, mutation results, suite tally, smoke transcript lines, final shas. Max 22 lines."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4462,"cache_read_input_tokens":525405,"output_tokens":2711,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":651},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4462,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2711,"cache_read_input_tokens":525405,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4462,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4462},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CeCXX8yjtTqnZ6tK13DBW","type":"assistant","uuid":"7b43fe96-6fbe-4bee-bf61-bc87531000aa","timestamp":"2026-08-19T17:48:28.315Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"f507d58c-285f-4d11-b1d0-201f2a5e172d","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan/devenv/p0p1/brainmark","sessionId":"de272aad-c620-4d71-bbdd-27dd2d3dc8af","version":"2.1.233","gitBranch":"main","slug":"quizzical-sniffing-quasar"}
