{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-08-19T17:54:51.222Z","sessionId":"de272aad-c620-4d71-bbdd-27dd2d3dc8af","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>a4c4da3d1f4cfbfb0</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_0146oc5ZN72dQ3KscxxPQ6nu</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-suhaan-devenv/f507d58c-285f-4d11-b1d0-201f2a5e172d/tasks/a4c4da3d1f4cfbfb0.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Verify systemd path quoting\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>Have all evidence needed. Verdict confirmed by source code (config_parse_working_directory / config_parse_exec_output in load-fragment.c) — neither calls extract_first_word(EXTRACT_UNQUOTE); only unit_path_printf() (specifier expansion, no dequoting) runs on the raw rvalue.\n\n**QUOTE BREAKS.**\n\n1. No unquote for these 3. `EXTRACT_UNQUOTE` in `extract_first_word()` is what strips quotes (used by list/cmdline parsers: ExecStart, Environment, ReadWritePaths, etc — grep hits at load-fragment.c:4257,4323,4396,4470...). `config_parse_working_directory` (L2656) and `config_parse_exec_output` (L1329, handles `append:`/`file:`/`truncate:` prefixes) call **only** `unit_path_printf()` (specifier `%`-expansion) on raw rvalue — never extract_first_word/unquote_first_word/cunescape.\n2. Man page caveat is exact: systemd.syntax(7) says \"For **settings where quoting is allowed**...\" — these 3 aren't in that set per source above.\n3. Quotes land literally in the path string → `\"/opt/some dir\"` becomes a path starting with `\"`, fails `PATH_CHECK_ABSOLUTE` in `path_simplify_and_warn()` → warning + setting/unit rejected.\n4. Unquoted spaces DO work: whole rest-of-line (after `=`, trimmed only at ends) is taken verbatim as the single value — `WorkingDirectory=/opt/some dir` is correct/valid.\n5. Escaping needed: `%` → `%%` (specifier escape, systemd.unit.xml specifier table incl. literal `%%`); C-style backslash escapes are NOT processed here (no EXTRACT_CUNESCAPE call) except a trailing `\\` for line-continuation merge (systemd.syntax §Quoting/line-continuation).\n\nSources:\n- https://github.com/systemd/systemd/blob/main/man/systemd.syntax.xml (Quoting section, L136-141: \"For settings where quoting is allowed...\")\n- https://github.com/systemd/systemd/blob/main/src/core/load-fragment.c (`config_parse_working_directory` L2656-2712, `config_parse_exec_output` L1329- , both use `unit_path_printf` only)\n- https://github.com/systemd/systemd/blob/main/src/core/unit-printf.c (`unit_path_printf`→`unit_full_printf_full` L253, L179 — specifier expansion only, no unquote)\n- https://github.com/systemd/systemd/blob/main/man/systemd.unit.xml (specifier table incl. `%%`)\n- https://www.freedesktop.org/software/systemd/man/latest/systemd.exec.html (StandardOutput=/StandardError=/WorkingDirectory= docs — rendered man page; freedesktop.org blocked WebFetch with 403 but GitHub XML source above is authoritative and matches)</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>62523</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>17</tool_uses><duration_ms>109449</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
