{"parentUuid":"7fa3d96d-06be-4385-8fbc-7a5989916043","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_011CeCaZung8Mp39kPHuLq65","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Found it — three sources, all transient, **no daemon installed** (launchctl is clean; the onboarding smoke cleaned up after itself properly):\n\n1. **`entire-brain memory worker --once`** at ~84% CPU — a one-shot memory-consolidation worker spawned by tonight's test/smoke work (running from my scratchpad copy of the binary, not your real install). `--once` means it exits when its pass finishes.\n2. **`sem.test` processes** (~80% + two smaller) — Go test binaries for entire-graph's `internal/sem` package. That's likely the *other* Claude agent's (graph-bench) work or a leftover long-running probe test — not from my current pipeline, so I won't kill it without you saying so.\n3. **My onboarding fix pass** — it runs entire-brain's full suite repeatedly (the `internal/cli` package alone takes ~2.5 min of multi-core each pass). This is the legitimate cost of the validation you asked for and stops when the fixer finishes (soon).\n\nSo: nothing persistent got installed on your machine, and it all self-terminates. Options if the fans are annoying right now: I can kill the memory worker (safe, it's a scratch artifact), or pause the onboarding fixer until later — say which, or let it ride for the ~15–30 min the fixer needs."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":508,"cache_read_input_tokens":534813,"output_tokens":1357,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":919},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":508,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1357,"cache_read_input_tokens":534813,"cache_creation_input_tokens