{"type":"queue-operation","operation":"enqueue","timestamp":"2026-08-19T18:49:06.638Z","sessionId":"de272aad-c620-4d71-bbdd-27dd2d3dc8af","content":"<task-notification>\n<task-id>ad97b67e1834783ac</task-id>\n<tool-use-id>toolu_016HysH8SCY7UqTsYt89h7CB</tool-use-id>\n<output-file>/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-suhaan-devenv/f507d58c-285f-4d11-b1d0-201f2a5e172d/tasks/ad97b67e1834783ac.output</output-file>\n<status>completed</status>\n<summary>Agent \"Fix onboarding blockers\" finished</summary>\n<note>A task-notification fires each time this agent stops with no live background children of its own. The user can send it another message and resume it, so the same task-id may notify more than once.</note>\n<result>All blockers fixed, verified, and committed. Not pushed.\n\n**BLOCKERS (file:line, final tree)**\n1. Daemon one-shot: dropped `--budget` from `brainWatchDaemonArgs` (setup.go:530-552); `watch.go:44-49,114` docs corrected; setup.go:52-65 comment rewritten. Tests `TestDaemonBudgetSemanticsAllowOneRunPerWindow` (6 runs, 3 windows × 2 repos, shared counter, parses the real installed argv) + `TestDaemonBudgetGateStillHoldsInsideAWindow`.\n2. Double-distill: try-only `withDistillPassLock` (brain.go:107-142) wired into `runDistill` (distill_cmd.go:648-668) — covers backfill child, watch, hook, human. Tests `TestDistillPassLockLetsExactlyOneSpend|IsReleasedForTheNextPass|SurvivesAFailedPass`.\n3. Re-entrant backfill: state+`processAlive` check (setup.go:387-400). Tests `TestSetupSkipsBackfillWhileOneIsStillRunning`, `TestSetupRestartsTheBackfillWhenTheRecordedProcessIsDead`.\n4. Uncapped spend: `setupDefaultBackfillBudget=25`, 0=explicit unlimited, cap disclosed (setup.go:54-60,432-447). Tests `TestSetupCapsTheDefaultBackfillSpend|ReportsWhatTheCapDidAndHowToLiftIt|BackfillBudgetZeroIsExplicitlyUnlimited`.\n5. Workspace lock: `addWorkspaceRepoLocked` (workspace.go:557-624), sole mutation path. Tests `TestConcurrentWorkspaceAddsAllPersist` (8), `TestConcurrentSetupRegistrationsAllPersist` (6), `TestWorkspaceAddReportsCreatedAndAlready`.\n6. Daemon churn: log moved to `&lt;state&gt;/logs/watch.log` (setup.go:508-529). Tests `TestBrainWatchDaemonPlanIsRepoIndependent`, `TestSetupSecondRepoDoesNotRestartTheDaemon`.\n7. Disclosure: README §3b (phase/cost table + 4 gates) + `--budget` caveat, command Long help, new CHANGELOG.md.\n\n**SMALLER** — hook matcher now requires an Entire hook command + PATH probe (`entireSessionEndHookCommand`, setup_status.go:257-330); `Flags().Changed` + interval/distill-every/model/effort recorded (setup.go:665-728); rename retires old unit, guarded by \"was this repo ever set up\" so a first run can't kill another repo's daemon; launchd label hash-suffixed (`io.entire.brain-watch.a2d3fd66`); daemon unit path honours `ENTIRE_BRAIN_DAEMON_DIR`; 4 test gaps closed.\n\n**ONE DEVIATION (verified, not re-litigated)** — the review asked to *quote* systemd `WorkingDirectory`/`StandardOutput`/`StandardError`. Confirmed against systemd source: those are parsed by `config_parse_working_directory`/`config_parse_exec_output`, which never call `extract_first_word(EXTRACT_UNQUOTE)`, so quotes land inside the path and `path_simplify_and_warn` rejects it — quoting breaks the unit. Implemented the correct hardening instead: `%`→`%%` specifier escaping on those settings (+ `Environment=`), newline values refused, quoting kept only on the settings systemd does unquote. `TestSystemdSingleValueSettingsAreNotQuoted`, `TestSystemdEscapesSpecifiers`, `TestPlanBrainWatchDaemonRejectsNewlineValues`.\n\n**MUTATIONS** — budget-1 reintroduced → `TestDaemonBudgetSemanticsAllowOneRunPerWindow` FAIL (got 1, want 6). Distill lock removed → `TestDistillPassLockLetsExactlyOneSpend` FAIL (got 2). Also: workspace lock removed → 1 of 8 persist; per-repo log path restored → repo-independence FAIL.\n\n**SUITE** — `go test ./...` 2507 passed / 11 packages; `-race` on the concurrency+setup subset green; gofmt and vet clean; all three new commits build individually.\n\n**SMOKE** (real `$HOME`, sandboxed store, `ENTIRE_BRAIN_DAEMON_DIR`, stubbed launchctl/codex) — `unit bytes: IDENTICAL across repos`; `service-manager calls during repo B setup: 1 -&gt; launchctl list …` / `daemon restart: NONE (probe only)`; both repo keys present in the manifest; `fact backfill capped at 25 of 200 pending session(s)`; `fact backfill: already running (pid …, 0/200 sessions distilled so far)`; `real ~/Library/LaunchAgents: UNCHANGED throughout`.\n\n**COMMITS** (branch `feat/brain-setup-onboarding`, not pushed, no AI footers): `b5468e40` distill lock, `43564caf` setup fixes, `cacf42e5` docs. Prior 5 commits intact; I added three scoped `fix`/`docs` commits (the branch's existing pattern) rather than splitting intertwined same-file hunks across earlier commits, which would have left non-building intermediates — say the word if you want them folded instead.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>294161</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>148</tool_uses><duration_ms>3638137</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>"}
