{"parentUuid":"3bc3db12-d93e-4858-9f7b-52cd0e3ed38a","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_011CeCcGN5CrAwLdtAwnrQX6","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Done — the onboarding feature is [PR #89 on entire-brain](https://github.com/entireio/entire-brain/pull/89)**, built, adversarially reviewed (round-1 NO-SHIP with 5 blockers → all fixed and mutation-verified), and live-smoked on this machine with real launchd.\n\nWhat Thomas's complaint turns into: `entire-brain setup` — brain queryable in ~400ms, past sessions distilling in the background (newest first, capped at 25 by default, never double-spends thanks to a new cross-process lock), and the single machine-wide daemon you wanted keeping every repo fresh — with `status` finally answering \"facts: 143/200 sessions distilled.\" Along the way it fixed a real shipped bug: the daemon/hook distill paths were silently dead for everyone, which is exactly why \"the agent stuff never seems to run\" felt true.\n\nFull board now:\n\n| Open PR | State |\n|---|---|\n| #85, #87 (brain, P1 + keystone) | mergeable, your click |\n| #114 (graph) | ready for review |\n| #2041 (cli), #242 (api) | need reviewer approval — messages drafted for you to send |\n| **#89 (brain, onboarding)** | **new, ready for review** |\n| #88 (BrainMark) | parked per your call |\n\nNothing left in flight — every builder and skeptic has landed. Remaining moves are all human: merges, the two review-request messages, and (whenever you're ready) the BrainMark seal session."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":582,"cache_read_input_tokens":542033,"output_tokens":503,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":582,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available"