{"parentUuid":"11f03282-88c6-4c7e-9a94-6b61c6307472","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_011CeCevsBDJ9GzzqohiQ1UR","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The graceful-degradation fix is **pushed to PR #89** — reproduced live: a remote-less repo now completes setup with `FAILED semantic` clearly reported plus the actionable hint, workspace and daemon still land, exit 0, `status` shows `semantic=failed` (distinct from missing), and `doctor` carries the full reason. Mutation-verified (reverting to abort-on-first-failure fails the test), suite green.\n\nOne small honest footnote: a single status test fails *on this machine only* — because your **demo daemon is currently live** and that test probes real launchctl (a pre-existing test-isolation gap, fails identically on the pre-change tree, passes in CI). It vanishes the moment you run the demo's `setup --uninstall-daemon`. Worth a one-line test fix eventually; not blocking.\n\nThat closes every open thread on my side. The full board:\n\n- **PR #89** (onboarding) — complete, reviewed, degradation-hardened, pushed\n- **PRs #85, #87, #114** — ready, your merges\n- **PRs #2041, #242** — need reviewer approvals; your two clean messages are drafted\n- **PR #88** (BrainMark) — parked, pilot done ($6.24, direction favors brain, awaiting seal + confirmatory)\n- **Demo** — live in `~/brain-demo`, daemon ticking, uninstall when done"}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1623,"cache_read_input_tokens":567858,"output_tokens":1065,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":606},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1623,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1065,"cache_read_input_tokens":567858,"cache_creation_input_to