{"parentUuid":"e16c7726-e5c2-4850-9f9c-7423c7c2a650","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-fable-5","id":"msg_011CeCnCGpzevfgziWDiCKC3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_018pcPUR6og73zN4XBd3wCzV","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Fix onboarding windows CI","subagent_type":"general-purpose","model":"opus","prompt":"Fix the failing Windows CI on entireio/entire-brain PR #89. Worktree: /Users/suhaan/devenv/p0p1/brain-onboarding (branch feat/brain-setup-onboarding). Use rtk.\n\nFailing job: test (windows-latest), run 32292859258. Failing tests: TestSetupContinuesWhenTheSemanticComponentFails, TestSetupInstallsExactlyOneDaemonAcrossRuns, TestSetupReinstallsADriftedDaemon, TestSetupRenamingTheDaemonRetiresTheOldUnit, TestSetupSecondRepoDoesNotRestartTheDaemon, TestPlanBrainWatchDaemonHonorsXDGConfigHome, TestPlanBrainWatchDaemonDarwinGolden, TestPlanBrainWatchDaemonLinuxGolden.\n\n1. Pull exact failure output: `gh run view 32292859258 --repo entireio/entire-brain --log-failed | grep -B2 -A15 \"FAIL: TestPlanBrainWatchDaemonDarwinGolden\"` etc. Likely causes: (a) golden tests render darwin/linux units on Windows where filepath.Join produces backslashes inside the rendered paths → golden mismatch — the daemon PLAN code takes GOOS as an arg but path construction probably uses filepath (OS-dependent) instead of path or explicit separators; (b) setup daemon-flow tests assume unix service managers/env (HOME vs USERPROFILE, XDG on windows); (c) the product behavior question: on windows there is NO launchd/systemd — `setup` should cleanly skip the daemon phase with one line (\"background watcher: not supported on windows yet — skipped\") rather than pretend.\n2. Fix properly: make unit RENDERING platform-pure (target-OS paths derived with path/template logic keyed by the GOOS arg, never host filepath semantics), make setup's daemon phase a documented no-op on windows (tests assert the skip line), and keep the golden tests running on ALL host OSes (that's the point of GOOS-as-arg).\n3. ALSO fix the known local test-isolation gap while you're here: TestBuildBrainOnboardingStatusReportsBackfillAndDaemon probes the REAL launchctl and fails on machines with a live daemon — inject the service-manager probe in that test (the injection seam exists for other daemon tests).\n4. You cannot run Windows locally: compile-check with `GOOS=windows go vet ./...` + `GOOS=windows go build ./...`, run the full darwin suite green, and reason the windows paths carefully; write the golden expectations so they are host-independent (prove by running the goldens under `GOOS=` env permutations if the tests allow).\n5. Commit (no AI footers), push (updates PR #89), then watch `gh pr checks 89 --repo entireio/entire-brain` until the windows job rechecks (cap 30 min) and report its outcome.\nReport caveman-ultra: root cause per test class, fixes w/ file:line, local+cross-compile results, windows CI outcome, sha. Max 14 lines."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1184,"cache_read_input_tokens":577440,"output_tokens":3428,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":311},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1184,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":3428,"cache_read_input_tokens":577440,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1184,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1184},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null},"requestId":"req_011CeCnCAbgvcZunJZEfokqx","type":"assistant","uuid":"77aadda3-eaaf-4ab0-ad0e-f8cbe914e33c","timestamp":"2026-08-19T21:01:00.653Z","effort":"xhigh","session_id":"de272aad-c620-4d71-bbdd-27dd2d3dc8af","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/suhaan